hadiths[1148]{hadithnumber,text}:
"13780","(13774) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us from what he recited to Mālik, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yazīd, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyān, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, that Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥafs irrevocably divorced her (ṭalāq al-battah) while he was absent. She mentioned the hadith, until she said: \When I became lawful (i.e."," my waiting period ended)"," I mentioned to him\""—meaning the Prophet ﷺ—\""that Muʿāwiyah and Abū Jahm had proposed to me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'As for Abū Jahm"," he does not put down his staff from his shoulder'\""—i.e."," he beats women or is always travelling—\""'and as for Muʿāwiyah"," he is a destitute man with no wealth. Marry Usāmah ibn Zayd.' She said: 'I disliked him.' Then he said: 'Marry Usāmah.' So I married him"," and Allah placed goodness in him"," and I was envied on account of him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1480]"""
"13781","(13775) Al-Sayyid Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-ʿAlawī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn al-Ḥakam al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid narrated to me: my father narrated to me: ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah narrated to me — he said: I heard my father Buraydah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Indeed"," the measure of worth (ḥasab) of the people of this world is this wealth.\""\n\nAnd likewise it was narrated by Zayd ibn al-Ḥubāb and ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq from al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid. [Ḥasan]"""
"13782","(13776) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Munādī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Muḥammad al-Mu'addib narrated to us: Salām ibn Abī Muṭīʿ narrated to us: from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Al-ḥasab (lineage/nobility of status) is wealth"," and al-karam (true nobility) is taqwā (God-consciousness).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13783","(13777) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Maslamah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us — he said: It was read to ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad, who was Ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Raqāshī, and my father narrated to us — they said: Muslim ibn Khālid narrated to us: from al-ʿAlāʾ, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The nobility (karam) of a person is his religion (dīn)"," his manliness (murūʾah) is his intellect (ʿaql)"," and his lineage/status (ḥasab) is his character (khuluq).\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh. And in the narration of Ibn Yūsuf is not found: \""wa murūʾatuhu ʿaqluhu (and his manliness is his intellect).\""\n\nAnd something similar has been narrated from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) as his own statement. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13784","(13778) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: Asad ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us: from Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O Banū Bayāḍah"," give Abū Hind in marriage (to your women) and marry (your women) to his people.\"" He (the narrator) said: And he was a cupper (ḥajjām). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13785","(13779) And Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated it with the same meaning (bi-mithlih)."
"13786","(13780) And among what Abū Dāwūd mentioned in al-Marāsīl, from ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān and Kathīr ibn ʿUbayd, from Baqiyyah — al-Zubaydī narrated to me: al-Zuhrī narrated to me regarding this incident, that they said: \O Messenger of Allah"," we marry our daughters to our freed slaves (mawālīnā).\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {Indeed"," We created you from a male and a female and made you peoples and tribes that you may know one another} [al-Ḥujurāt 13]. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13787","(13781) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad al-Nasawī informed me: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Wakīʿ narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to us: from Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm al-ʿAdawī, who said: I heard Fāṭimah bint Qays say: \Her husband divorced her irrevocably (three times)"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not assign her any lodging or maintenance.\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: \""When you become lawful (i.e."," your ʿiddah ends)"," inform me.\"" So I informed him"," and then Muʿāwiyah"," Abū Jahm"," and Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with them) proposed to me. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""As for Muʿāwiyah"," he is a man who has no wealth; and as for Abū Jahm"," he is a man who beats women frequently; but (marry) Usāmah.\"" She said: She gestured with her hand"," \""Usāmah"," Usāmah.\"" He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to her: \""Obedience to Allah and obedience to His Messenger is better for you.\"" She said: \""So I was married to him"," and I was delighted with him.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah.\n\nAnd Fāṭimah bint Qays was a Qurashī woman from Banū Fahr — she is Fāṭimah bint Qays ibn Khālib ibn Wahb ibn Thaʿlabah ibn Wāʾilah ibn ʿAmr ibn Shaybān ibn Muḥārib ibn Fihr. And Usāmah is Ibn Zayd ibn Ḥārithah ibn Sharāḥīl al-Kalbī"," the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13788","(13782) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn al-Layth narrated to me: Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Sarī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Aʿyan al-Ḥarrānī narrated to us: Ḥafṣ ibn Sulaymān al-Asadī narrated to us: from al-Kumayt ibn Zayd al-Asadī, who said: Madhkūr, the freed slave of Zaynab bint Jaḥsh, narrated to me, from Zaynab bint Jaḥsh (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \Several of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) proposed to me"," so I sent my sister to him (the Prophet) to consult him about that. He said: 'Where is she from among those who will teach her the Book of her Lord and the Sunnah of her Prophet?' She said: 'Who?' He said: 'Zayd ibn Ḥārithah.' She became angry and said: 'You would marry your paternal aunt's daughter to your freed slave!' Then she came to me and informed me of that. I said something even harsher than her words and became even angrier than her. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {It is not for a believing man or a believing woman"," when Allah and His Messenger have decided a matter"," that they should have any choice in their affair} [al-Aḥzāb 36]. She said: I sent to him (the Prophet): 'Marry me to whomever you wish.' She said: So he married me to him (Zayd). I took him to task with my tongue (i.e."," I was sharp-tongued with him)"," so he complained to the Prophet (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: 'Hold on to your wife and fear Allah.' Then I again took him to task with my tongue"," and he complained to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: 'Should I divorce her?' So he divorced me"," and my divorce became irrevocable (bāʾin). When my ʿiddah ended"," I was unaware until the Prophet (ﷺ) came to me while my hair was uncovered. I said: 'This is a matter from the heavens.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," without any formal proposal (khuṭbah) or witnesses?' He said: 'Allah is the One Who arranged the marriage"," and Jibrīl is the witness.'\""\n\nAnd although its chain of narration is not one by which a definitive proof can be established"," it is well-known (mashhūr) that Zaynab bint Jaḥsh — who was from Banū Asad ibn Khuzaymah"," and whose mother was Umaymah bint ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib ibn Hāshim"," the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — was married to Zayd ibn Ḥārithah until he divorced her"," and then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married her. And in the ḥadīth it says \""ibnata ʿammika (your paternal aunt's daughter)","\"" but the correct wording is \""ibnata ʿammatik (your paternal aunt's daughter)\"" — i.e."," she was the daughter of his (the Prophet's) paternal aunt. [Ḍaʿīf Jiddan]"""
"13789","(13783) And Abū ʿAmr al-Bisṭāmī al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us: Hārūn ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated to us: from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to Ḍuʿāʿah bint al-Zubayr ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib and said to her: 'It seems you intend to perform Ḥajj.' She said: 'I feel unwell.' He said to her: 'Perform Ḥajj and stipulate the condition that my place of exiting iḥram is wherever you detain me.' And she was married to al-Miqdād ibn al-Aswad.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Abū Kurayb"," both from Abū Usāmah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 6089]"""
"13790","(13784) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd al-Narsī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us: from Sufyān, from Jābir, from al-Shaʿbī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \I arranged the marriage of al-Miqdād and Zayd so that the most honorable among you in the sight of Allah would be the one with the best character among you.\""\n\nThis is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected in the chain)"," and what precedes it is sufficient. And al-Miqdād is Ibn ʿAmr ibn Thaʿlabah ibn Mālik"," an ally of al-Aswad"," a man from Banū Zuhrah"," so he was attributed to them"," though he was not from their direct lineage. And Ḍuʿāʿah bint al-Zubayr ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib ibn Hāshim was married to him. [Ḍaʿīf Jiddan]"""
"13791","(13785) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us that ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us that Abū al-Yamān informed us that Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah narrated on the authority of al-Zuhrī, who informed me that ʿUrwah narrated on the authority of ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that Abū Ḥudhayfah ibn ʿUtbah ibn Rabīʿah ibn ʿAbd Shams — who was among those who witnessed Badr alongside the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him — adopted Sālim and married him to his niece Hind bint al-Walīd ibn ʿUtbah, who was a freed slave woman of a woman from the Anṣār, just as the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, had adopted Zayd. And he mentioned the hadith in its entirety.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī, may Allah have mercy on him, in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. Thus, this was a Qurayshī woman from Banū ʿAbd Shams ibn ʿAbd Manāf who was married to a freed slave. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4000]"
"13792","(13786) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us that ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Ibn Makhlad narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAtīq narrated to us that ʿĀṣim ibn Yūsuf narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated on the authority of Abī al-Ḥasan, who narrated on the authority of Ḥanẓalah ibn Abī Sufyān al-Jumaḥī, who narrated on the authority of his mother, who said: I saw the sister of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf married to Bilāl. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī 207]"
"13793","(13787) And among what Abū Dāwūd mentioned in al-Marāsīl, on the authority of Hārūn ibn Zayd, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hishām ibn Saʿd, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, as a mursal narration: that the Banū Bukayr came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: \Marry our sister to so-and-so.\"" He said: \""What is your opinion about Bilāl?\"" They returned and he repeated it three times"," so they married her to him. He said: And the Banū Bukayr were among the Muhājirūn from Banū Layth.\n\nAbū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad informed us of it; Abū al-Ḥusayn al-Fasawī informed us; Abū ʿAlī al-Luʾluʾī narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13794","(13788) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Zāhid al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Qāḍī narrated to us that ʿĀrim ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Maymūn narrated to me that my father informed me: that a brother of Bilāl, who claimed lineage among the Arabs and considered himself one of them, proposed marriage to a woman from the Arabs. They said: \If Bilāl comes"," we will marry her to you.\"" So Bilāl came and said: \""I am Bilāl ibn Rabbāḥ"," and this is my brother"," who is a wicked man of bad character and religion. If you wish"," marry her to him"," and if you wish"," leave it.\"" They said: \""Whose brother he may be"," we will marry her to him.\"" So they married her to him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13795","(13789) Abū Sahl Muḥammad ibn Naṣrūyah ibn Aḥmad al-Marwazī narrated to us that Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar ibn Ḥamdān al-Qaṭīʿī narrated to us that Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us that ʿAmr ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Shuʿbah narrated on the authority of ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, on the authority of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah, on the authority of his father, that a woman was married for a pair of sandals. She was brought to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and he said to her: \Are you pleased"," regarding yourself and your wealth"," with a pair of sandals?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" So the Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," permitted it.\n\nAnd there are other narrations on this subject"," the place of which is the Book of the Mahr (Dowry). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13796","(13790) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Tamīmī informed us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me that my father narrated to me that Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated on the authority of Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd, on the authority of al-Ḥasan, regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: \Do not prevent them from marrying their (former) husbands\"" (2:32). He said: Maʿqil ibn Yasār al-Muzanī narrated to me that this verse was revealed concerning him. He said: I had married my sister to a man"," and he divorced her. When her waiting period elapsed"," he came to propose to her again. I said to you: I married you to her"," gave you the bedding"," and honored you"," yet you divorced her"," and now you come to propose to her again? No"," by Allah"," she will never return to you. He said: And the man was not a bad man"," and his wife wished to return to him. So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed this verse. I said: Now I will do it"," O Messenger of Allah. So I married her to him.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 1530]"""
"13797","(13791) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥamdān narrated in Hamadhān that Muḥammad ibn al-Jahm al-Simmārī narrated to us that Abū ʿĀṣim al-Ḍaḥḥākh ibn Makhlad narrated to us that Ibn Jurayj narrated to me. He said: I heard Sulaymān ibn Mūsā say: al-Zuhrī narrated to us. He said: I heard ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr say: I heard ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardians"," her marriage is invalid"," her marriage is invalid"," her marriage is invalid. If he has consummated the marriage"," then she is entitled to the mahr for what he has consummated. If they dispute"," then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us on the authority of Mujāld"," on the authority of al-Shaʿbī"," on the authority of ʿAlī"," ʿAbd Allāh"," and Sharīḥ"," who said: There is no marriage except with a guardian"," except when a woman is prevented by her guardian and she comes to the ruler or the judge.\n\nAnd on the authority of Ziyād ibn ʿIlāqah"," who said: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," wrote: \""If he is a suitable match"," then say to her father to marry her to him. If he refuses"," then marry her to him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. See al-Arwāʾ 1340]"""
"13798","(13792) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us that Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī narrated to us that al-Qāsim, meaning Ibn Zakariyyā, narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Manīʿ and Ibn Samurah al-Aḥmasī both narrated to us that Asbāṭ narrated to us that al-Shaybānī narrated on the authority of ʿIkrimah, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās. Al-Shaybānī said: And ʿAṭāʾ Abū al-Ḥasan al-Suwāʾī mentioned it, and I do not think he mentioned it except on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, regarding this verse: \It is not lawful for you to inherit women against their will"," and do not prevent them\"" (4:19). He said: When a man died"," his heirs had more right over his wife than her own guardians. If some of them wished"," they would marry her themselves; if they wished"," they would marry her off to others; and if they wished"," they would not marry her off at all. So this verse was revealed concerning that.\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr"," from Asbāṭ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4579]"""
"13799","(13793) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs and Abū Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī both narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us that Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated on the authority of Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf, on the authority of Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān, regarding His Most High words: \O you who believe! It is not lawful for you to inherit women against their will\"" (4:19). He said: When a man died in the Jāhiliyyah"," the close relative of the deceased would go to his wife and throw a garment over her"," thereby inheriting her marriage"," and thus he would have more right over her. So Allah revealed this verse. And His words: \""And do not prevent them in order to take back part of what you have given them\"" (4:19) — referring to the mahr — is about a man who prevents his wife"," detaining her while he has no need of her"," intending that she ransom herself from him. That is His words: \""And do not prevent them\"" — meaning"," do not detain them — \""in order to take back part of what you have given them\"" — meaning"," what you gave them — \""unless they commit a clear immorality\"" (4:19) — meaning"," clear disobedience"," which is nushūz (recalcitrance). In that case"," Allah has permitted beating and abandonment. If she refuses"," then ransom is permissible for him. The completion of this topic will come"," if Allah the Most High wills"," in the Book of Division"," where we have transmitted the words of al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," regarding this verse. [Ḥasan]"""
"13800","(13794) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us that Abān narrated to us that Qatādah narrated on the authority of al-Ḥasan, on the authority of ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When two guardians perform a marriage contract"," it is for the first of them. And when a man sells something to two men"," it is for the first of them.\"" [Munkar]"""
"13801","(13795) Abū Bakr ibn Furak informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Hishām narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundab, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When two guardians perform a marriage contract"," the marriage belongs to the first of them"," and when a man sells merchandise to two men"," it belongs to the first of them.\""\n\nThus is the narration of the group"," and it is the preserved version.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī"," raḥimahullāh"," said: \""The marriage of two guardians cannot be considered equivalent so that the marriage belongs to the first of them"," except through a power of attorney from one of them"," along with the appointment of the Prophet ﷺ as agent — for he appointed ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī"," and he married him to Umm Ḥabībah bint Abī Sufyān.\"""""
"13802","(13796) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Isḥāq, who said: Abū Jaʿfar narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent ʿAmr ibn Umayyah al-Ḍamrī to al-Najāshī, and he married him to Umm Ḥabībah bint Abī Sufyān, and he paid on his behalf four hundred dīnārs.\n\nAnd we have narrated regarding the marriage of Umm Kulthūm bint ʿAlī to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā, that ʿAlī said to Ḥasan and Ḥusayn, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhum: \Marry your uncle","\"" and they married him to her. [Weak]"""
"13803","(13797) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us that Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us that Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Ibn al-Mubārak informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from Umm Ḥabībah, that she was married to ʿUbaydullāh ibn Jaḥsh, and he died in the land of Abyssinia, so al-Najāshī married her to the Prophet ﷺ, and he paid her dowry on his behalf of four thousand, and he sent her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with Sharḥabīl ibn Ḥasanah. [Authentic]"
"13804","(13798) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān narrated from ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus, from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, who said: \It reached me that the one who acted as her guardian in the marriage was her paternal cousin"," Khālid ibn Saʿīd ibn al-ʿĀṣ.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," raḥimahullāh"," said: \""He is the son of her father's paternal cousin"," for she is Umm Ḥabībah bint Abī Sufyān ibn Ḥarb ibn Umayyah"," and al-ʿĀṣ is the son of Umayyah.\""\n\nAnd it has also been said that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu"," was the one who acted as her guardian in the marriage. [Weak]"""
"13805","(13799) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me that ʿAmr ibn Khālid and Ḥassān narrated from Ibn Lahīʿah, from Abū al-Aswad, from ʿUrwah, who said: \ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu"," married her to him in the land of Abyssinia.\""\n\nAnd al-Zuhrī said the same"," and his narration has already been mentioned. And ʿUthmān is ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ ibn Umayyah"," the son of her father's paternal cousin. Whichever of them married her"," the guardianship is valid"," except that there is a third point of difference regarding it. [Weak]"""
"13806","(13800) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Birtī narrated to us that Mūsā ibn Masʿūd narrated to us that ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us that Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb and Abū ʿAmr al-Faqīh both said: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm al-ʿAnbarī and Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf both said: al-Naḍr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us that ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us that Abū Zuml narrated to me that Ibn ʿAbbās, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, said: \The Muslims would not look at Abū Sufyān nor sit with him"," so he said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'O Prophet of Allah"," three things I have been given.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I have the most beautiful and fairest of the Arabs — Umm Ḥabībah bint Abī Sufyān — I marry her to you.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And Muʿāwiyah — make him a scribe before you.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And appoint me as a commander so that I may fight the disbelievers as I used to fight the Muslims.' He said: 'Yes.'\"" Abū Zuml said: \""Were it not that he asked the Prophet ﷺ for that"," he would not have given it to him"," for he would not ask for anything except that he would say: 'Yes.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-ʿAbbās ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAẓīm and Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar.\n\nThis is one of the matters in which al-Bukhārī and Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj differed: Muslim included it and al-Bukhārī omitted it"," for al-Bukhārī did not use ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār as evidence in his book al-Ṣaḥīḥ"," saying: \""He did not have a written book"," so his hadith became confused.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," raḥimahullāh"," said: \""This hadith regarding the story of Umm Ḥabībah"," raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā"," the people of maghāzī have unanimously agreed upon its contradiction"," for they do not differ that the marriage of Umm Ḥabībah"," raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā"," took place before the return of Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib and his companions from the land of Abyssinia"," and they returned in the time of Khaybar. So the marriage of Umm Ḥabībah took place before that"," and the Islam of Abū Sufyān ibn Ḥarb took place at the time of the Conquest of Makkah"," two or three years after her marriage. How then can it be correct that her marriage took place at his request? Even if his first request to him occurred during one of his journeys to Madīnah while he was a disbeliever"," when he heard of the death of Umm Ḥabībah's husband in the land of Abyssinia"," and the second and third requests occurred after his acceptance of Islam — if the hadith is preserved"," nothing else is possible. And Allah"," the Most High"," knows best.\"" [Denounced — Muslim 2501]"""
"13807","(13801) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us that al-Shāfiʿī, raḥimahullāh, informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm, known as Ibn ʿUlayyah, narrated from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When two guardians perform a marriage"," the first has greater right.\"" Thus did al-Shāfiʿī"," raḥimahullāh"," narrate it in the book Taḥrīm al-Jamʿ and in the Imlāʾ"," and he added in the Imlāʾ: \""And when two sellers make a sale"," the first has greater right.\"" [Denounced — previously mentioned under number 13794]"""
"13808","(13802) And he narrated it in the book Aḥkām al-Qurʾān, as Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us in another place in the Musnad, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us with its chain and its text in its entirety, except that he said: \From al-Ḥasan"," from a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ"," from the Prophet ﷺ.\"""""
"13809","(13803) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us that Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that Abū al-Khaṭṭāb narrated to us that Abū Baḥr al-Bakrāwī narrated to us that Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us that Qatādah narrated from al-Ḥasan, from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir al-Juhanī, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Any woman whose marriage is performed by two guardians"," the marriage belongs to the first of them.\"" [Denounced]"""
"13810","(13804) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us in the book al-Mustadrak that al-Ḥasan ibn Yaʿqūb al-ʿAdl narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾ informed us that Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundab, raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Any man who sells a sale to two men"," it belongs to the first of them"," and any woman whose marriage is performed by two guardians"," it belongs to the first.\"" [Weak]"""
"13811","(13805) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah ibn Dāʿāmah al-Sadūsī, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah — or from ʿUqbah. Saʿīd said: \I think it is from ʿUqbah\"" — the doubt being from Saʿīd. He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Any woman whose marriage is contracted by two guardians"," the marriage belongs to the first of the two.\"" [Weak. Previously mentioned.]"""
"13812","(13806) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz narrated to us: Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah or ʿUqbah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \When two guardians contract a marriage"," the first has the greater right; and when two authorized persons make a sale"," the first has the greater right.\"" This discrepancy occurred from Ibn Abī ʿArūbah in the isnād of this hadith. Abān al-ʿAṭṭār followed him from Qatādah in his statement \""from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir","\"" but the correct narration is from the one who narrated it from Samurah ibn Jundub. [Weak.]"""
"13813","(13807) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Manṣūr al-Ḥārithī narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us: my father narrated from Qatādah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr informed us: Hammām narrated from Qatādah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Qatādah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us: Abū al-Jamāhir narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Bashīr narrated from Qatādah, from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Any woman whose marriage is contracted by two guardians"," the marriage belongs to the first; and any two men who make a sale"," the sale belongs to the first of the two.\"" The wording is from the hadith of Hishām"," and the narrations of the others convey the same meaning. Likewise"," Ashʿath ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated it from al-Ḥasan. [Weak. Previously mentioned.]"""
"13814","(13808) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him: Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī al-Wazīr informed us: Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Anṣārī narrated to me: Ashʿath ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated from al-Ḥasan, from Samurah, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \When two authorized guardians contract a marriage"," the first has the greater right.\"" [Weak. Previously mentioned.]"""
"13815","(13809) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated from Saʿīd, from Qatādah, from Khilās, that a woman's guardians married her to ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Ḥurr in al-Jazīrah, and her family married her again afterwards in al-Kūfah. They brought the matter to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), so he separated her from her second husband and returned her to her first husband, assigned her dower based on what had been consummated from her private part, and commanded her first husband not to approach her until her ʿiddah had expired. [Hasan due to supporting narrations.]"
"13816","(13810) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed us: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us: Abū al-Yamān informed us: Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr used to narrate that he asked ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) about the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls, then marry those that please you of [other] women, two or three or four. But if you fear that you will not be just, then [marry only] one or those your right hands possess} [al-Nisāʾ 3]. ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \It refers to the orphan girl who is in the care of her guardian. He desires her beauty or her wealth and wishes to marry her for less than the customary dower of women like her. So they were forbidden from marrying them unless they dealt justly with them by completing the dower in full"," and they were commanded to marry other women besides them.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Then the people asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for a ruling"," so Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: {They ask you for a ruling concerning women. Say"," 'Allah gives you a ruling concerning them and what has been recited to you in the Book concerning orphan girls to whom you do not give what is decreed for them and yet you desire to marry them'} [al-Nisāʾ 127].\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Allah"," the Exalted"," clarified in this verse that when the orphan girl possesses beauty and wealth"," they desire to marry her but do not meet the customary dower of women like her; and when she is undesirable due to her lack of wealth"," they leave her and seek other women.\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Just as they left her when they were disinclined toward her"," they have no right to marry her when they desire her unless they deal justly with her and give her the most complete dower.\"" It was narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 3018.]"""
"13817","(13811) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī, and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who informed me: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr asked ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), about the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls, then marry those that please you of [other] women} [al-Nisāʾ 3]. She said: \O son of my sister"," this is the orphan girl who is in the care of her guardian"," sharing in her wealth. Her guardian is impressed by her wealth and her beauty and wishes to marry her without being just in her dower — without giving her what others would give her. So they were forbidden from marrying them unless they dealt justly with them and gave them the highest standard of dower. And they were commanded to marry those women besides them who were pleasing to them.\"" ʿUrwah said: ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""Then the people asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for a ruling after this verse concerning them"," so Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed this verse: {They ask you for a ruling concerning women. Say"," 'Allah gives you a ruling concerning them and what has been recited to you in the Book concerning orphan girls to whom you do not give what is decreed for them and yet you desire to marry them'} [al-Nisāʾ 127].\"" He said: \""And what He mentioned as having been recited to them in the Book is the first verse in which He said: {And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls"," then marry those that please you of [other] women} [al-Nisāʾ 3].\"" ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""And Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said in the other verse: {and yet you desire to marry them} — meaning"," one of you turns away from his orphan girl who is in his care when she possesses little wealth and beauty. So they were forbidden from marrying those orphan girls whose wealth and beauty they desired except with justice"," on account of their previous disinclination toward them.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah"," from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"13818","(13812) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Sarḥ al-Miṣrī — and he is Abū al-Ṭāhir — narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Yūnus narrated something similar to it, and at the end he said: Yūnus said: Rabīʿah said regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls} [al-Nisāʾ 3], he said: \He means: Leave them if you fear [injustice]"," for I have made lawful for you four [wives].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"13819","(13813) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad — al-Ḥāfiẓ al-Naysābūrī — narrated to us: Abū al-Jahm Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qurashī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Abī al-Ḥawārī narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us: Hishām narrated from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), regarding His words: {They ask you for a ruling concerning women. Say, 'Allah gives you a ruling concerning them'} to the end of the verse. She said: \It is the orphan girl in the care of a man"," who shares in his wealth. He is disinclined to marry her but desires to marry her off to someone else"," so that the other man may enter upon him in his wealth. So he withholds her. Thus Allah forbade them from that.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Salām"," from Abū Muʿāwiyah. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim also narrated it through another chain from Hishām"," though there is a difference in its wording from Hishām. The hadith of al-Zuhrī is more complete and better preserved. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"13820","(13814) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ibn Bashshār narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn Khālid, from a man called al-Ḥakam, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \There is no marriage except with four: a guardian"," two witnesses"," and a suitor (one who seeks the marriage).\"" [Weak.]"""
"13821","(13815) And it has a corroborating narration from Ibn ʿAbbās through a broken chain: Abū ʿAlī — Rūḥ ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥīm al-Tamīmī al-Aṣbahānī — Abū Yaʿlā al-Zubayrī — Abū al-ʿAbbās Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Māsarjisī — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā — Ibn al-Mubārak, from Hammām, from Qatādah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \There is no marriage except with four: a suitor (khāṭib)"," a guardian (walī)"," and two witnesses.\"" This chain of narration is sound"," except that Qatādah did not meet Ibn ʿAbbās. It has also been narrated through another weak chain from Ibn ʿAbbās in a marfūʿ (elevated) form. The well-known narration from him is mawqūf (stopped at the Companion's level). That has also been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through another chain. [Weak]"""
"13822","(13816) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū ʿAmr ibn Abī Jaʿfar informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Ṣābūnī the jurist in Naysābūr informed us in the year three hundred; Yaʿqūb ibn al-Jarrāh al-Khwārizmī informed us; al-Mughīrah ibn Mūsā informed us; Hishām, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \There is no marriage except with a guardian"," a suitor"," and two upright witnesses.\"" That has also been narrated through another weak chain from Abū Salamah"," from Abū Hurayrah"," in a marfūʿ form"," and through another weak chain from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," in a marfūʿ form. [Weak]"""
"13823","(13817) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us; Hushaym informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that Ibn ʿUmar married his son to his brother's daughter, and his son was a minor at that time. This is understood to mean that his brother executed the marriage contract, and his paternal uncle accepted it on behalf of his minor son.\n\nAnd it has been narrated regarding this from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, al-Ḥasan, al-Shaʿbī, and al-Nakhaʿī. It has been narrated from al-Ḥasan through a weak chain from the Prophet ﷺ in a mursal (incomplete) form: \When a man gives his son in marriage while the son disapproves"," there is no marriage for him; but when he is married off while he is a minor"," his marriage is valid.\"" It has been narrated from Ibn ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," that he said: \""The dower is the responsibility of the son whom you have married off.\"" It has been narrated from ʿAṭāʾ that he said: \""When a man gives his minor son in marriage"," his marriage is valid"," and he has no right of divorce.\"" And from al-Zuhrī"," who said: \""No divorce is valid from him\"" — meaning from the insane person. [Sound]"""
"13824","(13818) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us; Abū Dāwūd informed us; al-Qaʿnabī, from Mālik, from Abū Ḥāzim ibn Dīnār, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, may Allah be pleased with him, that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have given myself to you.\"" She stood for a long time. Then a man stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," marry her to me if you have no need of her.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do you have anything with which to give her a dower?\"" He said: \""I have nothing but this lower garment of mine.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""If you give her your lower garment"," you will sit without a lower garment. Seek something.\"" He said: \""I find nothing.\"" He said: \""Seek"," even if it be an iron ring.\"" He searched but found nothing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Do you have any portion of the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""Yes"," such-and-such sūrah and such-and-such sūrah\"" — naming certain sūrahs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""I have married her to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf"," from Mālik. Likewise"," Zāʾidah ibn Qudāmah"," Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān"," ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad al-Dārawardī"," and others narrated it from Abū Ḥāzim"," from the Prophet ﷺ: \""I have married her to you.\"" Ibn ʿUyaynah said"," from Abū Ḥāzim"," from Sahl ibn Saʿd"," in one of the two narrations from him: \""I have given her in marriage to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.\"" And in another narration from him: \""I have married her to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.\"" [Sound. Muslim 1425]"""
"13825","(13819) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn Ziyād informed us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar informed us; Sufyān, from Abū Ḥāzim ibn Dīnār, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, who said: \I was with the people in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he mentioned this narrative"," but he did not mention the lower garment. He said: A man stood and said: 'Give her in marriage to me.' And at the end of it he said: 'I have given her in marriage to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.'\"" Both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Sound. Preceded above]"""
"13826","(13820) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burhān informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah, from Abū Ḥāzim, who heard Sahl ibn Saʿd say: \I was among the people in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ. A woman stood and he mentioned the narrative. He said: A man from the people stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," marry her to me.' And at the end of it he said: 'Go"," for I have married her to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.'\"" [Sound. Preceded above]"""
"13827","(13821) Abū ʿAmr al-Bisṭāmī al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, that a woman came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. He mentioned the narrative, and in it: \A man from his Companions ﷺ stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," if you have no need of her"," marry her to me.' And at the end of it he said: 'Go"," for I have given her into your possession with what you have of the Qurʾān.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," without citing the full text of the narration. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," from Yaʿqūb and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim"," from Abū Ḥāzim"," from Sahl ibn Saʿd"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," in this ḥadīth: \""Go"," for I have given her into your possession with what you have of the Qurʾān.\"" Then he said: \""This is the ḥadīth of Ibn Abī Ḥāzim.\"" [Sound. Preceded above]"""
"13828","(13822) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd informed us; Yaʿqūb ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Abī Ḥāzim, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd. He mentioned the narrative and in it: \Go"," for I have given her into your possession with what you have of the Qurʾān.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it from al-Qaʿnabī"," from Ibn Abī Ḥāzim"," and said in the ḥadīth: \""Go"," for I have given her into your possession.\"" Likewise"," he narrated it from ʿĀrim"," from Ḥammād ibn Zayd"," from Abū Ḥāzim. [Sound. Preceded above]"""
"13829","(13823) A group narrated it from Ḥammād, as Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Abū al-Rabīʿ informed us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Sulaymān al-Marwazī informed us; Khalaf ibn Hishām informed us; Ḥammād, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd, that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \A woman has given herself to Allah and His Messenger.\"" He said: \""I have no need of women today.\"" A man from the weak among the Muslims said: \""Marry her to me"," O Messenger of Allah.\"" He said: \""What do you have?\"" He said: \""I have nothing.\"" He said: \""Give her a garment.\"" He said: \""I do not find one.\"" He said: \""Give her"," even if it be an iron ring.\"" He said: \""I do not find one.\"" He said: \""What do you have of the Qurʾān?\"" He said: \""Such-and-such and such-and-such.\"" He said: \""I have married her to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.\"" This is the ḥadīth of Khalaf. In the narration of Abū al-Rabīʿ: \""We have married her to you.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it from Ibn Abī Maryam"," from Abū Ghassān"," from Abū Ḥāzim"," from Sahl"," and said in the ḥadīth: the Prophet ﷺ said: \""We have given her into your possession with what you have of the Qurʾān.\"" (T) And al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad narrated it from Abū Ghassān Muḥammad ibn Muṭarrif"," and said in the ḥadīth: He said: \""I have married her to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.\""\n\nThe narration of the majority is in the wording of tazwīj (marriage)"," except for the shādh (irregular) narration among them. The group is more deserving of being preserved than the single narrator"," and Allah knows best. Some of our companions cited as evidence for this what we have narrated in the Book of Ḥajj"," in the established ḥadīth from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad"," from his father"," from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," in the narrative of the Farewell Pilgrimage"," in which he said: \""Fear Allah regarding women"," for you have taken them as a trust from Allah"," and you have made their private parts lawful by the word of Allah.\"" He said: Our companions said: \""That is the word of nikāḥ (marriage) and tazwīj"," both of which are mentioned in the Qurʾān.\"" [Sound. Preceded above]"""
"13830","(13824) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burhān in Baghdad informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us; Mālik ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd ibn Miqsam — and he is Ibn Ḍabbah — informed me. He said: My paternal aunt Sārah bint Miqsam informed me, from Maymūnah bint Kardam, who said: \I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah upon his she-camel"," and I was with my father"," and in the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a whip like the whip of the scribes. I heard the Bedouins and the people saying: 'Al-ṭabṭabīyah"," al-ṭabṭabīyah' (the clapping of the feet). So my father drew near to him and held his foot"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped for him. She said: I have not forgotten the length of the index toe of his foot compared to the rest of his toes. He said to him: 'I was present at the army of ʿUthrah.' She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recognized that army. Ṭāriq ibn al-Marqaʿ said: 'Who will give me a spear in exchange for its reward?' I said: 'What is its reward?' He said: 'I will give him in marriage the first daughter born to me.' I said: I gave him my spear"," then I left him until he had a daughter who reached maturity. I came to him and said: 'Prepare my family for me (i.e."," send my wife to me).' He said: 'No"," by Allah"," I will not prepare her until you give a dower other than that.' I swore that I would not do so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'With which of the women is she comparable?' I said: 'She has seen the onset of old age.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at me and said: 'Leave her; there is no good in her for me.' That alarmed me"," and he looked at me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You will not sin"," nor will she sin.' And he mentioned the rest of the ḥadīth.\"" [Weak]"""
"13831","(13825) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed me, Ibrāhīm ibn Mayrah informed me that his maternal aunt informed him from a woman — she said, \She is a trustworthy woman"," a truthful woman\"" — she said: \""While we were in a military expedition during the Jāhiliyyah"," they were overcome by intense heat. A man said"," 'Who will give me his sandals"," and I will marry him to the first daughter born to me?' So my father removed his sandals and threw them to him. A girl was then born to him"," and she reached maturity.\"" He mentioned something similar to that"," but he did not mention the account of al-qatīr. And al-qatīr is grey hair (old age). [Weak]"""
"13832","(13826) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated to us, Abū Isḥāq narrated to us, he said: I heard Abū ʿUbaydah ibn ʿAbdullāh narrating from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the Khuṭbat al-Ḥājah (the sermon of need): 'Al-ḥamdu lillāh — or inna al-ḥamda lillāh — nastaʿīnuhu, nastaghfiruhū, wa naʿūdhu billāhi min shurūri anfusinā. Man yahdihillāhu fa lā muḍilla lahū, wa man yuḍlilillāhu fa lā hādiya lahū. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh, wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabdahu wa rasūluhū.' Then recite the three verses: {Yā ayyuhā an-nās ittaqū Rabbakum alladhī khalaqakum min nafs-in wāḥidah wa khalaqa minhā zawjahā} (O mankind, fear your Lord, who created you from one soul and created from it its mate) [al-Nisāʾ: 1]; {Yā ayyuhā alladhīna āmanū ittaqullāha ḥaqqa tuqātihī} (O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared) [Āl ʿImrān: 102] to the end of the verse; then recite {Yā ayyuhā alladhīna āmanū ittaqullāh wa qūlū qawlan sadīdā} (O you who believe, fear Allah and speak words of appropriate justice) [al-Aḥzāb: 70] to the end of the verse. Then speak of your need.\ Shuʿbah said: I said to Abū Isḥāq"," \""Is this for the marriage sermon or for other occasions as well?\"" He said"," \""For every need.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13833","(13827) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj Abū Bisṭām narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from Abū ʿUbaydah — and I think he said — from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ, from ʿAbdullāh, from the Prophet ﷺ, that he would say in the tashahhud of need, and he mentioned something similar to it, but he did not mention the statement of Shuʿbah to Abū Isḥāq. [Its chain has been mentioned previously]"
"13834","(13828) Isrāʾīl ibn Yūnus narrated it from Abū Isḥāq, from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ and Abī ʿUbaydah, that ʿAbdullāh — may Allah be pleased with him — said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the Khuṭbat al-Ḥājah.\"" Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of it"," Abū Muḥammad al-Muzanī narrated to us"," Abū Jaʿfar al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us"," Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Numayr narrated to us"," Wakīʿ narrated to us"," Isrāʾīl narrated it with something similar to it"," except that he said: {Yā ayyuhā an-nās ittaqū Rabbakum alladhī khalaqakum min nafs-in wāḥidah wa khalaqa minhā zawjahā wa baththa minhumā rijālan kathīran wa nisāʾā"," wa ittaqullāha alladhī tasāʾalūn bihi wa al-arḥām"," inna Allāha kāna ʿalaykum raqībā} (O mankind"," fear your Lord"," who created you from one soul and created from it its mate"," and from them spread abroad many men and women"," and fear Allah through whom you ask one another"," and the wombs. Indeed"," Allah is ever"," over you"," an Observer) [al-Nisāʾ: 1]. Then he mentioned the last two verses"," but he did not say"," \""Then he should speak of his need.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain has been mentioned previously]"""
"13835","(13829) Al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Isḥāq, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh, as a mawqūf (stopped) narration. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Qabīṣah narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq, from Abī ʿUbaydah, from ʿAbdullāh, who said regarding the Khuṭbat al-Ḥājah: \Al-ḥamdu lillāhi alladhī naḥmaduhū wa nastaʿīnuhū","\"" and he mentioned something similar to it"," but he did not raise it (to the Prophet). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain has been mentioned previously]"""
"13836","(13830) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Aṣamm in Baghdād narrated to us, Abū Qilābah narrated to us, Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us, ʿImrān narrated from Qatādah, from ʿAbd Rabbih, from Abī ʿIyāḍ, from Ibn Masʿūd — may Allah be pleased with him — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he gave the sermon, would say: \Al-ḥamdu lillāh"," nastaʿīnuhu"," nastaghfiruhū"," wa naʿūdhu billāhi min shurūri anfusinā. Man yahdihillāhu fa lā muḍilla lahū"," wa man yuḍlil fa lā hādiya lahū. Wa ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabdahu wa rasūluhū"," arsalahu bil-ḥaqi bashīran wa nadhīran bayna yaday al-sāʿah. Man yuṭiʿillāha wa rasūlahū fa qada rashada"," wa man yaʿṣihimā fa innahū yaḍurru illā nafsahū"," wa lā yaḍurru Allāha shayʾā.\"" (All praise is due to Allah; we seek His help and His forgiveness"," and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides"," none can mislead"," and whomever He leads astray"," none can guide. I bear witness that there is no deity except Allah"," and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. He sent him with the truth as a bearer of glad tidings and a warner before the Hour. Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has indeed achieved guidance"," and whoever disobeys them harms none but himself"," and he does not harm Allah at all.) [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain has been mentioned previously]"""
"13837","(13831) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdād informed us, Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Ḥurayth narrated from Wāṣil al-Aḥdab, from Shaqīq, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud and the sermon just as he would teach us a sūrah from the Qurʾān. The tashahhud: 'At-taḥiyyātu lillāhi wa al-ṣalawātu wa al-ṭayyibāt. As-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-Nabiyyu wa raḥmatullāhi wa barakātuh. As-salāmu ʿalaynā wa ʿalā ʿibādillāhi al-ṣāliḥīn. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," wa ashhadu anna Muḥammadan ʿabdahu wa rasūluh.' And the sermon: 'Al-ḥamdu lillāh"," naḥmaduhū"," nastaʿīnuhu"," nastaghfiruhū. Ashhadu an lā ilāha illallāh"," waḥdahū lā sharīka lahū"," wa anna Muḥammadan ʿabdahu wa rasūluhū. {Wa ittaqullāha alladhī tasāʾalūn bihi wa al-arḥām"," inna Allāha kāna ʿalaykum raqībā} [al-Nisāʾ: 1]. {Yā ayyuhā alladhīna āmanū ittaqullāh wa qūlū qawlan sadīdā"," yuṣliḥ lakum aʿmālakum wa yaghfir lakum dhunūbakum"," wa man yuṭiʿillāha wa rasūlahū fa qad fāza fawzan ʿaẓīmā} [al-Aḥzāb: 70–71].'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Its chain has been mentioned previously]"""
"13838","(13832) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamzah al-Harawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, one who heard Abū Bakr ibn Ḥafṣ narrating informed me, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, who said: \I met Ibn ʿUmar and proposed to him for his daughter's hand in marriage. Ibn Abī ʿAbdillāh said to me: 'Indeed"," Ibn Abī ʿAbdillāh is worthy of giving in marriage. We praise our Lord and send blessings upon our Prophet. We have married you (her) upon what Allah has commanded — either retaining her in kindness or releasing her in goodness.'\"" [Weak]"""
"13839","(13833) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, that Ibn ʿUmar, when he performed a marriage, would say: \I marry you upon what Allah has commanded — either retaining in kindness or releasing in goodness.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13840","(13834) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us, Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Marwazī Abū Bakr narrated to us, ʿĀṣim — that is, ibn ʿAlī — narrated to us, Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, Abū Ḥāzim narrated to us, Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated to us, who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a woman came to him offering herself to him. He lowered his gaze and raised it"," but he did not desire her. A man from among his Companions said"," 'Marry her to me"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said"," 'Do you have anything (to give as mahr)?' He said"," 'I have nothing"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said"," 'Not even an iron ring?' He said"," 'Not even an iron ring"," but I can tear my cloak in half and give her one half and keep the other half.' He said"," 'No. But do you have anything of the Qurʾān (memorized)?' He said"," 'Yes.' He said"," 'Go"," for I have married her to you with what you have of the Qurʾān (i.e."," by teaching it to her).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn al-Miqdām from Fuḍayl ibn Sulaymān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"13841","(13835) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ — meaning al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī — narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbbās narrated to us: Bundār narrated to us: Badal narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And he said: Abū ʿAlī informed us: ʿAlī ibn Salm narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā al-Zajjāj narrated to us: Badal narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Khālid from a man from Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm from a man from Banī Sulaym, who said: \I proposed to the Prophet ﷺ for Ummāmah bint ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib"," and he married me to her without delivering a sermon.\"" And Ibn Salm said in his ḥadīth: from a man from Banī Tamīm that he proposed to the Prophet ﷺ for Ummāmah bint ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib. He said: \""So he married me to her without delivering a sermon\"" — meaning the khutbah.\n\nThus narrated al-Bukhārī in al-Tārīkh from Bundār"," except that he said: from al-ʿAlāʾ"," the brother of Shuʿayb al-Wazzān. And Abū Dāwūd al-Sijistānī likewise said it from Bundār. [Very Weak]"""
"13842","(13836) And it has been narrated from Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbbād ibn Shaybān, from his father, from his grandfather: \I proposed to the Prophet ﷺ for his aunt"," and he married me to her without delivering a sermon.\""\n\nAbū Bakr al-Fārisī al-Mashshāṭ reported it to us; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī reported it to us; Abū Aḥmad ibn Fāris narrated to us; al-Bukhārī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUqbah al-Sadūsī narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn ʿUmar ibn ʿĀmir al-Sulamī narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl narrated it. And other than this has also been narrated."""
"13843","(13837) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Ḥaywah ibn Sharīḥ informed us that al-Walīd ibn Abī al-Walīd informed him that Ayyūb ibn Khālid ibn Abī Ayyūb al-Anṣārī narrated to him from his father, from his grandfather, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:\n\n\Conceal the proposal"," then perform wuḍūʾ and perform it well"," then pray what Allah has decreed for you"," then praise your Lord and glorify Him"," then say: 'O Allah"," You have power and I have no power"," and You know and I do not know"," and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You see that [such-and-such a woman] — and he should mention her by name — is good for me in my religion"," my worldly life"," and my Hereafter"," then decree her for me. And if other than her is better for me in my religion"," my worldly life"," and my Hereafter"," then decree her for me.'\"" [Weak. Aḥmad 5/4239]"""
"13844","(13838) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\When one of you acquires a woman"," a servant"," or a riding animal"," let him take hold of its forelock"," mention the name of Allah — Mighty and Majestic — and say: 'O Allah"," I ask You for the good of her and the good of what she has been created upon"," and I seek refuge in You from the evil of her and the evil of what she has been created upon.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"13845","(13839) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Shahīd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: Ibn ʿAjlān narrated it in a similar manner, except that he said: \Let him take hold of her forelock"," invoke blessings"," and say…\""\n\nHe narrated it and added: \""And if it is a camel"," let him take hold of the top of its hump.\"" [Ḥasan. Previously mentioned]"""
"13846","(13840) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Thābit from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw traces of yellow [dye] on ʿAbd al-Raḥmān and said: \What is this"," O Abū Muḥammad?\""\n\nHe said: \""I married a woman for a weight of a date-stone in gold.\"" He said: \""May Allah bless you. Hold a walīmah"," even if it be with only one sheep.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Ḥammād ibn Zayd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1427]"""
"13847","(13841) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Dārawardī narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Sawwār and Muḥammad ibn Nuʿaym both said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Suhayl from his father from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that when a person congratulated the Prophet ﷺ upon marrying, he would say: \May Allah bless you and bestow blessings upon you and bring you both together in goodness.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Muqriʾ"," he said: \""When a man married and congratulated him"," the Prophet ﷺ would say…\"" and he mentioned it. [Ḥasan]"""
"13848","(13842) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Tammār narrated to us: Ibn Kathīr informed us: Sufyān narrated from Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd, who said: I heard al-Ḥasan say: \ʿAqīl ibn Abī Ṭālib came to Baṣrah and married a woman from Banī Jusham. They said to him: 'May you enjoy comfort and children.' He said: 'Do not say that"," for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from that and commanded us to say: \""May Allah bless you and bestow blessings upon you.\""'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13849","(13843) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Khalīl narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me: Ismāʿīl ibn al-Khalīl informed us: ʿAlī ibn Mushhir informed us: Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated from his father from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old. We came to Madīnah and stayed among Banī al-Ḥārith ibn al-Khazraj. I fell ill and my hair became dishevelled and fell out until it became like wavy locks. My mother Umm Rūmān came to me while I was on a swing with some companions of mine. She called out to me and I came to her"," not knowing what she wanted with me. She took my hand and made me stand at the door of the house while I was panting until my breathing calmed. Then she took some water and wiped my face and head with it"," then she took me into the house. There were some women of the Anṣār in a room"," and they said: 'For goodness and blessing"," and upon the best of fortune.' My mother handed me over to them"," and they put my affairs in order. Nothing alarmed me except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ coming in the forenoon"," and they handed me over to him"," and I was at that time nine years old.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Farwah ibn Abī al-Maghrāʾ from ʿAlī ibn Mushhir. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"13850","(13844) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us: Hishām ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Ibn Rajāʾ informed us: Hammām narrated from Manṣūr ibn al-Muʿtamir, who narrated to me: Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd narrated from Kurayb from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet ﷺ said:\n\n\Verily"," when one of you intends to come to his wife"," let him say: 'In the name of Allah. O Allah"," keep the Shayṭān away from us and keep the Shayṭān away from what You bestow upon us.' Then if a child is decreed between them"," the Shayṭān will never harm him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl from Hammām"," and both he and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Manṣūr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1434]"""
"13851","(13845) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran the trustworthy narrator in Baghdad informed us that Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Bakhtari al-Razzaz narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Mulā'ib narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us that Sa'id narrated from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri from Salim ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who informed him that a man called Ghaylān ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi had ten wives during the Jāhiliyyah. He embraced Islam and they embraced Islam along with him. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ commanded him to choose four of them. [Munkar]"
"13852","(13846) Abu Nasr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamīrūyah narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us that Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abu 'Ali al-Rūdhabāri informed us that Abu Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abu Dāwūd narrated to us that Musaddad narrated to us that Hushaym narrated from Ibn Abi Laylā from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardal from al-Harith ibn Qays ibn 'Amīrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I embraced Islam and I had eight wives. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Choose four of them.'\"" The wording is that of Musaddad. All the other hadiths mentioned in this chapter are recorded in the chapter concerning the man who embraces Islam while having more than four wives. [Da'īf]"""
"13853","(13847) Abu Zakariyyā ibn Abi Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us that Abu al-Hasan al-Tarā'ifī narrated to us that 'Uthmān ibn Sa'id narrated to us that 'Abdullah ibn Salih informed that Mu'āwiyah ibn Salih narrated to him from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding the words of Allah the Most High: {And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls…} He said: \During the Jāhiliyyah they used to marry ten women from among the orphans"," and they used to regard the matter of the orphan as grave. Then they examined their religion concerning the matter of the orphans and abandoned what they used to marry during the Jāhiliyyah. Allah the Most High said: {And if you fear that you will not deal justly with the orphan girls"," then marry those that please you of [other] women"," two or three or four.} And He prohibited them from what they used to marry during the Jāhiliyyah.\"" [Da'īf]"""
"13854","(13848) Abu 'Abdullah the Ḥāfiẓ and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both said that Abu al-'Abbās Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us that Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us that Abu 'Āmir narrated from Isrā'īl from Simāk from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding the verse: {And [also prohibited to you are] married women except those whom your right hands possess. [This is] the decree of Allah upon you.} He said: \It is not permissible for a Muslim to marry more than four. If he does so"," she is to him like his mother or his sister [i.e."," forbidden].\"" And it has been narrated to us from 'Ubaydah al-Salmānī regarding the words of Allah the Most High: {[This is] the decree of Allah upon you}"," that he said: \""Four wives.\"" And similarly from al-Hasan al-Basrī. [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"13855","(13849) Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us that Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rābī narrated to us that al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbāh al-Za'farānī narrated to us that 'Affān narrated to us that 'Abd al-Wāhid ibn Ziyād narrated to us that Sulaymān ibn al-Qāsim narrated to us that Umm Zaynab narrated that Umm Sa'id, the umm walad of 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to her. She said: \I was pouring water over 'Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," while he was performing wuḍū'"," and he said: 'O Umm Sa'id"," I long to be a bridegroom.' She said: 'So I said: Woe to you! What prevents you"," O Amīr al-Mu'minīn?' He said: 'After four?' She said: 'So I said: Divorce one of them and marry another.' He said: 'Divorce is something ugly; I detest it.'\"" [Da'īf]"""
"13856","(13850) Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrājānī informed us that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated from Rabi'ah ibn Abi 'Abd al-Rahmān that 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and al-Qāsim ibn Muhammad used to say regarding a man who has four wives and irrevocably divorces one of them: that he may marry whenever he wishes and need not wait until her 'iddah has expired. [Ṣaḥīh]"
"13857","(13851) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'rūf the jurist al-Mihrājānī informed us that Abu Sa'id 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhāb al-Rāzī narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ayyūb informed us that Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us that Hishām narrated to us that Qatādah narrated from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab regarding a man who had four wives and divorced one of them: he said: \If he wishes"," he may marry a fifth during the 'iddah.\"" He said: \""And similarly he said regarding two sisters.\"" And Ibn Abi 'Arūbah narrated it from Qatādah from Ibn al-Musayyab regarding the one whose divorce was irrevocable"," similarly.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Hasan"," 'Aṭā' ibn Abi Rabāh"," Bakr ibn 'Abdullah al-Muzanī"," and Khilās ibn 'Amr. [Da'īf]"""
"13858","(13852) Abu 'Abdullah the Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abu 'Amr ibn Maṭar informed us that Yahyā ibn Muhammad narrated to us that 'Ubaydullah ibn Mu'ādh narrated to us that my father narrated to us that Shu'bah narrated from Abi Isḥāq from Sa'id ibn Wahb who said: \A man came to Ibn 'Umar and said: 'My mother has made her slave-girl lawful for me.' Ibn 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'She is not lawful for you except by one of three means: an outright gift"," a sale"," or a marriage.'\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"13859","(13853) Abu Tāhir the jurist informed us that Abu 'Uthmān 'Amr ibn 'Abdullah al-Baṣrī narrated to us that Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhāb informed us that Ya'lā ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated from Ayyūb from Nāfi' who said: \The slaves of Ibn 'Umar used to take slave-wives"," and he would not disapprove of that.\"" [Da'īf]"""
"13860","(13854) And Abu Nasr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abu 'Amr ibn Najīd narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us that Ibn Bukayr narrated to us that Mālik narrated from Nāfi' that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say: \A man shall not cohabit with a slave-girl [as a concubine] unless she is a slave-girl whom he may sell if he wishes"," or give away if he wishes"," or do with her as he wishes.\""\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," said: \""Al-Shāfi'ī"," may Allah have mercy upon him"," prohibited the slave from taking a concubine according to his later opinion"," and he countered the first narration with this. However"," Ibn 'Umar only said this regarding a free man who purchases a slave-girl on the basis of a defective condition.\"" [Ṣaḥīh. It was mentioned before the one before it.]"""
"13861","(13855) It was narrated by ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he used to say: \It is not permissible for a man to have intercourse with a private part except one over which he has ownership — if he wishes"," he may gift it; if he wishes"," he may sell it; and if he wishes"," he may emancipate it. There is no condition attached to it.\"" It was relayed to us by ʿAlī ibn Bishrān"," who reported to us Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār"," who narrated to us Ibn ʿAffān"," who narrated to us Ibn Numayr"," from ʿUbayd Allāh"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"13862","(13856) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh reported to us; Abū ʿUthmān al-Baṣrī reported to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb reported to us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd reported to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Abū Maʿbad, who said: \Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — married his male slave to his female slave"," and the slave divorced her. He (Ibn ʿAbbās) said: 'Take her back.' He refused. He (the narrator) said: Then he (Ibn ʿAbbās) said: 'She is yours; cohabit with her through the right of ownership (milk al-yamīn).'\"" Al-Shāfiʿī — may Allah have mercy upon him — said in al-Jadīd: \""Ibn ʿAbbās only said that to a slave who had divorced his wife"," saying to him: 'You have no authority over divorce.' He commanded him to retain her"," but he refused. So he said: 'She is yours; cohabit with her through the right of ownership","' intending thereby that she is lawful to him through the marriage contract"," and he has no authority over divorce.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13863","(13857) The Shaykh — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: \It is as he said"," for ʿAṭāʾ narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās that he used to say: 'The matter rests with the master — whether he gave him permission or did not give him permission.' And he would recite this verse: {Allāh sets forth a parable: a slave owned (mamlūk)"," who has no power over anything} [Sūrat al-Naḥl: 75].\"" Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ reported to us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh reported to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah reported to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr reported to us; Hushaym reported to us; Manṣūr reported from ʿAṭāʾ"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," and he mentioned it. And something indicative of that has also been narrated in the ḥadīth of Abū Maʿbad from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"," 800.]"""
"13864","(13858) Abū Ḥāzim reported to us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh reported to us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah reported to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr reported to us; Sufyān — that is, Ibn ʿUyaynah — from ʿAmr, from Abū Maʿbad: \A slave of Ibn ʿAbbās divorced his wife twice. Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — said to him: 'Take her back.' He refused. He said: 'She is yours; cohabit with her through the right of ownership (milk al-yamīn).'\"" In this there is an indication that he only commanded him to take her back after two divorces"," and there is no taking back for a slave after two divorces. It is as though he held the belief that the divorce did not take effect"," since the master had not given permission for it. So when he refused"," he said: \""She is yours; cohabit with her through the right of ownership.\"" The position of the majority (jamāʿah) is that his divorce is valid. And Allah knows best. Al-Shāfiʿī — may Allah have mercy upon him — said: \""Allāh only made concubinage (tasarrī) lawful for those who possess ownership"," and a slave is not an owner in any circumstance.\"" Allāh"," the Most High"," said: {Allāh sets forth a parable: a slave owned (mamlūk)"," who has no power over anything} [Sūrat al-Naḥl: 75]. And he mentioned what was narrated to us in the Kitāb al-Buyūʿ from Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — that the Prophet ﷺ said: \""Whoever sells a slave who possesses wealth"," the wealth belongs to the seller"," unless the buyer stipulates it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before the one before it.]"""
"13865","(13859) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān reported to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār reported to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq reported to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Musaddad reported to us — and the wording is that of ʿAlī — Muʿtamir ibn Sulaymān al-Taymī reported to us, from his father, from al-Ḥaḍramī, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr — may Allah be pleased with them both — that there was a woman called Umm Mahzūl, who used to be in Ajyād, and she was a prostitute (musāfiḥah). A man would marry her on the condition that she would provide for his expenses. A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about her: \Should I marry her?\"" The Prophet of Allāh ﷺ then recited"," or this verse was revealed: {The fornicator marries none but a fornicatress} [Sūrat al-Nūr: 3]. [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"13866","(13860) He said: And al-Ṣaffār reported to us; Muḥammad ibn Ghālib reported to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿUbaydah reported to us; Muʿtamir mentioned it with his chain of narration: \There was a woman called Umm Mahzūl"," and she would marry a man on the condition that he permit her fornication and that she would provide for his expenses. Some of them asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to marry her.\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ then recited this verse to its end.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. Preceded before it.]"""
"13867","(13861) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh reported to us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān reported to us; Abū al-Azhar Aḥmad ibn al-Azhar reported to us; Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah reported to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Akhnas reported to us; ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb reported to us, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: \There was a man called Murthad ibn Abī Murthad"," who used to carry captives from Makkah to bring them to Madīnah. He said: In Makkah there was a prostitute called ʿAnāq"," and she was his friend. He had promised a man that he would carry him from among the captives of Makkah. He said: I came until I reached the shade of one of the walls of Makkah on a moonlit night. ʿAnāq came and saw the blackness of my shadow beside the wall. When she approached me"," she recognized me and said: 'Murthad!' I said: 'Murthad.' She said: 'Will you stay with us tonight?' I said: 'O ʿAnāq"," Allāh has forbidden fornication.' She said: 'O people of the tents! This is the man who carries your captives!' Eight men followed me"," and I entered the Khandamah until I reached a cave or a grotto"," and I entered it. They came and passed over my head and urinated. Their urine fell upon my head"," and Allāh blinded them until they departed. I returned to my companion and carried him — he was a heavy man — until I reached the Idhkhar. I unfettered his shackle and began to carry him"," and he assisted me"," until I arrived in Madīnah. I came to the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," shall I marry ʿAnāq?' The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ was silent and did not reply to me with anything until this sūrah was revealed: {The fornicator marries none but a fornicatress or a polytheist woman"," and the fornicatress — none marries her except a fornicator or a polytheist"," and that has been forbidden to the believers} [Sūrat al-Nūr: 3]. The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ then said: 'O Murthad"," the fornicator marries none but a fornicatress or a polytheist woman"," and the fornicatress — none marries her except a fornicator or a polytheist.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it. Preceded before it.]"""
"13868","(13862) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ reported to us by recitation, and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī reported verbally; they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib reported to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ reported to us; Ibn Jurayj reported from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: \There were well-known prostitutes in the Jāhiliyyah — the prostitute of the family of so-and-so and the prostitute of the family of so-and-so.\"" Allāh"," the Most High"," said: {The fornicator marries none but a fornicatress or a polytheist woman"," and the fornicatress — none marries her except a fornicator or a polytheist"," and that has been forbidden to the believers} [Sūrat al-Nūr: 3]. He said: \""So Allāh prohibited through Islam the practice of the Jāhiliyyah.\"" Ibn Jurayj said: \""It was said to ʿAṭāʾ: 'Did you receive that from Ibn ʿAbbās?' He said: 'Yes.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"13869","(13863) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd reported to us; they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us; Yaḥyā reported to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb reported to us; Saʿīd reported from Qatādah, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, who said regarding this verse: {The fornicator marries none but a fornicatress or a polytheist woman} [Sūrat al-Nūr: 3]: \There were well-known prostitutes in Madīnah whose status was recognized. So Allāh forbade the believers from marrying them.\"" And this is the statement of Qatādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"13870","(13864) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ reported to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī reported to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn reported to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās reported to us; Warqāʾ reported from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, who said: \There were men who intended to marry certain women who were well-known"," openly practicing prostitutes in the Jāhiliyyah. It was said to them: 'This is unlawful.' So this verse was revealed concerning them"," and Allāh forbade marrying them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ for other than it.]"""
"13871","(13865) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd: that he asked Ibn ʿAbbās about the verse {The fornicator shall not marry save a fornicatress or an idolatress} — he said: \That is a ruling between them.\"" Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: and it has been narrated from ʿIkrimah that he said: \""The fornicator does not commit fornication except with a fornicatress or an idolatress"," and the fornicatress is not approached in fornication save by a fornicator or an idolater.\"" He understood the word *yankiḥu* (shall marry) to mean *yuṣībuhā* (to have intercourse with). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13872","(13866) The Imam Abū al-Fath informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Firās narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Daybulī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Shubrumah, from ʿIkrimah, regarding the words of the Most High {The fornicator shall not marry save a fornicatress or an idolatress} — he said: \He does not commit fornication except with a fornicatress.\"" The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: and this meaning has been narrated through another chain from Ibn ʿAbbās. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13873","(13867) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Abū al-Azhar narrated to us; Rūḥ narrated to us; al-Thawrī narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrat narrated to us; Khallād ibn Yaḥyā and ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Ḥassān both said: Sufyān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, from Ḥabīb ibn Abī ʿAmrah, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the verse {The fornicator shall not marry save a fornicatress or an idolatress} — he said: \It does not refer to marriage (*nikāḥ*); rather it refers to sexual intercourse (*jimāʿ*). None has intercourse with her save a fornicator or an idolater.\"" The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbd Allāh. In the narration of al-Faqīh it reads: \""But none has sexual intercourse with her save a fornicator or an idolater.\"" And ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālah narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās with the same meaning"," and he said regarding {And that has been forbidden to the believers}: \""That is"," fornication has been forbidden to the believers.\"" And with the same meaning it has been narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr"," Mujāhiḍ"," and al-Ḍaḥḥāk. Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And what seems most likely"," and Allah knows best"," is what Ibn al-Musayyab said.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13874","(13868) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Ibn al-Musayyab, regarding the words of the Most High {The fornicator shall not marry save a fornicatress} — the verse: he said: \It is abrogated (*mansūkhah*); it was abrogated by {And marry the unmarried among you} — so they were among the unmarried Muslim women.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13875","(13869) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-ʿAlawī and ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Najjār al-Muqriʾ in Kūfah both said: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Qabīṣah narrated from Sufyān, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, regarding the words of the Most High {Indeed, He is ever Forgiving to those who repeatedly repent}: he said: \He sins"," then repents"," then sins"," then repents.\"" He said: \""And I heard him say regarding {The fornicatress — none shall marry her save a fornicator or an idolater}: it was abrogated by {And marry the unmarried among you"," and the righteous among your male slaves and your female slaves}.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13876","(13870) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī narrated to us; Abū Khālid Yazīd ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥammād al-ʿUqaylī narrated to us; Abū ʿUmar al-Ḍarīr narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn Abī al-Mukhāriq and Hārūn ibn Riʾāb al-Asadī informed us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr al-Laythī. Ḥammād said: one of them said, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him: A man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have a beautiful cousin of mine"," and she does not repel the hand of anyone who touches her.\"" He said: \""Divorce her.\"" He said: \""I cannot bear to be apart from her.\"" He said: \""Then keep her.\"" And Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated it from Hārūn ibn Riʾāb as a *mursal* narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13877","(13871) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd said: al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth al-Marwazī wrote to me.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār al-Wazzān narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥurayth narrated to us; al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqiḍ narrated from ʿUmārah ibn Abī Ḥafṣah, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \My wife does not repel the hand of anyone who touches her.\"" He said: \""Separate from her (*gharribhā*).\"" He said: \""I fear that my soul may follow her.\"" He said: \""Then enjoy her.\"" The narration of Abū Dāwūd does not contain the word *idhan* (\""then\""). [Munkar]"""
"13878","(13872) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān ibn Saʿīd al-Thawrī narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm, who said: Abū al-Zubayr narrated to me, from a freedman of Banī Hāshim, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \My wife does not repel the hand of anyone who touches her.\"" He said: \""Divorce her.\"" He said: \""She is dear to me.\"" He said: \""Then enjoy her.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13879","(13873) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir al-Ṣāʾigh narrated to us; Abū Shaykh al-Ḥarrānī ʿAbd Allāh ibn Marwān narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAmr al-Raqqī narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm ibn Mālik, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have a wife who does not repel the hand of anyone who touches her.\"" He said: \""Divorce her.\"" He said: \""I love her and she is beautiful.\"" He said: \""Then enjoy her.\"" And similarly it has been narrated from Maʿqil ibn ʿUbayd Allāh"," from Abū al-Zubayr"," from Jābir"," may Allah be pleased with them both. [Munkar]"""
"13880","(13874) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Khalīfah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣalt Abū Yaʿlā al-Tūzī narrated to us; Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from Maʿqil ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from the Prophet ﷺ: that a man came to him and said: \I have a wife who does not repel the hand of anyone who touches her.\"" He said: \""Separate from her.\"" He said: \""I cannot bear to be apart from her.\"" He said: \""Then enjoy her.\"" And similarly Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Wazīr narrated it from Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth. [Munkar. It has been mentioned before.]"""
"13881","(13875) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Sufyān informed us: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd narrated to me from his father that a man married a woman who had a daughter from another husband, and he had a son from another wife. The young man committed fornication with the young girl, and she became pregnant. When ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived in Makkah, the matter was brought before him. He questioned them both, and they confessed. So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) had the ḥadd punishment carried out upon both of them, and he desired to bring them together in marriage, but the young man refused. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"13882","(13876) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: al-Shaybānī narrated from al-Shaʿbī that a young girl committed fornication and the ḥadd punishment was carried out upon her. Then they presented the matter to the Emigrants. The young girl repented, and her repentance was sound, and her condition was good. She would receive proposals of marriage, which were referred to her paternal uncle, but he disliked marrying her off until he disclosed what had been her affair, and yet he also disliked spreading that about her. Her matter was mentioned to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said to him: \Marry her off as you marry off your righteous young women.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding a virgin man who committed fornication with a woman"," and both confessed: he had them each flogged one hundred lashes"," then he married one to the other in his place"," and he exiled them for one year. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"," 866]"""
"13883","(13877) Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Sufyān narrated to me: ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd said: I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about a man who commits fornication with a woman—may he marry her? He said: \Yes"," that is when he obtains her through the lawful means.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Ibn Manṣūr"," 886]"""
"13884","(13878) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bishr narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah from Qatādah from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding a man who commits fornication with a woman and then marries her afterwards. He said: \The first was fornication and the last was marriage; the first was unlawful and the last was lawful.\""\n\nAnd from Saʿīd from Qatādah from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr regarding a man who commits fornication with a woman and then marries her"," they said: \""There is no harm in that"," provided they both repent and reform"," and they detest what they did.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13885","(13879) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a man who commits fornication with a woman and then marries her. He said: \The first was fornication and the last was marriage. There is no harm in it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded earlier]"""
"13886","(13880) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬāʾ informed us: Saʿīd narrated from Ayyūb from Saʿīd ibn Abī al-Ḥasan that Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) came out to them with his head dripping, having told them that he was fasting. He said: \It was a good woman I had intended"," and I was going to judge her case another day. I saw a slave-girl of mine who pleased me"," so I lay with her. I will further inform you that she had been a fornicatress"," and I wished to purify her through marriage.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abū Mijlaz from Ibn ʿAbbās that he said: \""Know that Allah accepts the repentance of both of them together just as He accepts it from them when they are apart.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \""If their repentance does not benefit them together"," it will not benefit them when they are apart.\"" And he recited: {Indeed"," Allah is the One who accepts repentance from His servants.} [Weak]"""
"13887","(13881) As for the ḥadīth: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Tamīmī narrated to us: the Imam Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Bishr ibn Muʿādh al-ʿAqadī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us: Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim narrated: A man from the people of Kūfah came to ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb and said: \Are you not astonished that al-Ḥasan says: 'The fornicator who has been flogged may only marry a flogged fornicatress like himself'?\"" ʿAmr said: \""What astonishes you about that? Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated it to us from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him).\""\n\nAnd ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with him) used to proclaim it publicly. Thus did ʿAmr narrate it. And it has been narrated from his father from his grandfather regarding the reason for the revelation of the verse"," which indicates that the prohibition was against marrying those prostitutes.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr through another chain that indicates the prohibition against marrying them was either due to their associating partners with Allah or due to their condition of continuing in fornication. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13888","(13882) As for that which Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us of: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: al-ʿAwwām ibn Ḥawshab narrated to us: al-ʿAlāʾ ibn Badr narrated that a man married a woman and then committed fornication, so the ḥadd punishment was carried out upon him. He was then brought to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) separated him from his wife. Then he said to the man: \Do not marry except a flogged woman like yourself.\"" This narration is munqaṭiʿ (discontinuous).\n\nAnd Ḥanash ibn al-Muʿtamir narrated that a group of people came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) disputing regarding a man who married a woman"," and one of them committed fornication before consummating the marriage. He said: \""So he separated them.\"" And Ḥanash is not strong (in narration). [Weak. Jāmiʿ al-Taḥṣīl"," 599]"""
"13889","(13883) As for that which Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī informed us of, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us: Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd from his father from Ibn Masʿūd, who said: \They are both fornicators as long as they remain together.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13890","(13884) Through this chain of narration: Saʿīd informed us from Ibn Sīrīn from Yaḥyā ibn al-Jazzār from Ibn Masʿūd that he said: \They are both fornicators as long as they do not separate.\"" And it has been narrated from Ibn Masʿūd that which indicates permissibility. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13891","(13885) Alqamah ibn Qays reported that a man came to 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: \A man committed zina with a woman"," then both of them repented and reformed. Is it permissible for him to marry her?\"" He then recited this verse: *\""Then indeed"," your Lord"," for those who committed evil in ignorance and then repented after that and reformed — indeed"," your Lord"," after that"," is Forgiving and Merciful\""* [al-Nahl 119]. He repeated it to him several times until the man thought that he had been granted a concession regarding it. [Da'if]"""
"13892","(13886) Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas narrated from his father: I recited during the night: *\And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds and knows what you do\""* [al-Shura 25]. I was uncertain and did not know how to recite it — *taf'alun* (you do) or *yaf'alun* (they do). So I went to 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud in the morning"," intending to ask him how he recited it. While I was sitting with him"," a man came and asked him about a man who commits zina with a woman and then wishes to marry her. He recited to him: *\""And it is He who accepts repentance from His servants and pardons misdeeds and knows what you do\""* [al-Shura 25]. [Da'if]"""
"13893","(13887) Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayyah al-Kalbi narrated this story and said: \Should he marry her?\"" 'Abd Allah recited the verse and said: \""Let him marry her.\"" Ibrahim ibn Muhajir also narrated from al-Nakha'i from Hammul ibn al-Harith from 'Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud regarding a man who commits fornication with a woman and then wishes to marry her"," he said: \""There is no harm in that.\"" [Da'if]"""
"13894","(13888) 'Amir said that 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said regarding a man who commits fornication with a woman and then marries her: \They will continue to be fornicators.\"" Ibn 'Abbas was asked about that and he said: \""This is fornication (sifah) and this is marriage (nikah).\"" It is also narrated from al-Bara' ibn 'Azib something similar to the saying of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). The saying of Ibn 'Abbas was cited in response to the saying of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," just as the saying of Ibn 'Abbas was cited in response to his own saying. And with those who granted permission are the evidences from the Book and the Sunnah. And success is through Allah alone. [Hasan]"""
"13895","(13889) Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib reported from a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from the Ansar, whose name was Basrah: \I married a virgin woman in her period of seclusion. When I entered upon her"," I found her to be pregnant. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to me: 'She is entitled to the mahr (dower) by virtue of what you have made lawful of her private part"," and the child will be your slave. When you give birth to it"," flog her.'\"" [Munkar]"""
"13896","(13890) The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This hadith was taken by Ibn Jurayj from Ibrahim ibn Abi Yahya from Safwan ibn Sulaym, and Ibrahim is differed upon regarding his reliability. 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated from Ibn Jurayj from Safwan ibn Sulaym something similar to it, but he did not mention \whose name was Basrah.\"" 'Abd al-Razzaq said: \""The hadith of Ibn Jurayj from Safwan ibn Sulaym is [actually] Ibn Jurayj from Ibrahim ibn Abi Yahya from Safwan ibn Sulaym.\"" [Munkar; previously referenced]"""
"13897","(13891) Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib reported from Basrah ibn Abi Basrah al-Ghifari: He married a virgin woman and consummated the marriage with her, only to find her pregnant. He mentioned this to the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he separated between them and said: \When she gives birth"," fling the prescribed punishment (hadd) upon her"," and she is entitled to her mahr by virtue of what you have made lawful of her private part.\"" Ishaq ibn Idris similarly narrated from Abu Ishaq al-Aslami"," who is Ibrahim ibn Muhammad. [Very Da'if]"""
"13898","(13892) This hadith has been narrated through other routes from Ibn al-Musayyib from the Prophet (peace be upon him) in a mursal form. Qatadah narrated from Sa'id ibn Yazid from Ibn al-Musayyib. Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated from Yazid ibn Nu'aym from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, and 'Ata' al-Khurasani narrated from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib — they both sent it as mursal. In the hadith of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: \That Basrah ibn Aktham married a woman.\"" All of them said in their hadith: \""He made the child his slave.\"" [Sahih]"""
"13899","(13893) Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib reported that a man called Basrah ibn Aktham married a woman. He mentioned its meaning and added: \And he separated between them.\"" And the hadith of Ibn Jurayj is more complete. [Da'if]"""
"13900","(13894) Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib reported that a man married a woman. When he had intercourse with her, he found her pregnant. He brought the matter before the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he separated between them, assigned her the mahr, and had her flogged one hundred lashes. This is a mursal hadith. The evidences have already been established regarding the permissibility of marrying a Muslim woman who has committed fornication, and that it is not annulled by zina. Allah, the Most High, has prescribed the waiting period ('iddah) in marriage, and the Prophet (peace be upon him) established the requirement of istibra' (waiting to ascertain the womb's freedom) through ownership. The scholars have unanimously agreed that the child of fornication born to a free woman is free. It is possible that this hadith, if authentic, is abrogated. And Allah knows best. [Da'if; previously referenced]"
"13901","(13895) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan — informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — informed us: al-Shafi'i — informed us: Sufyan — from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, mawla of the family of Talhah — from Sulayman ibn Yasar — from 'Abd Allah ibn 'Utban — from 'Umar ibn al-Khattaab (may Allah be pleased with him), that he said: A slave may marry two women and may issue two divorces, and a slave-girl shall observe the waiting period ('iddah) of two menstrual cycles; if she does not menstruate, then two months, or one month and a half. Sufyan said: and he was trustworthy. [Sahih]"
"13902","(13896) Abu Haazim al-Haafiz — informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Khumayruwayh — informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah — informed us: Sa'id ibn Mansur — informed us: Sufyan — informed us: Ayyub — from Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said upon the minbar: \Do you know how many women a slave may marry?\"" A man stood up before him and said: \""I know.\"" He asked: \""How many?\"" He said: \""Two.\"" Others added more to that"," but 'Umar remained silent. Then a man from the Ansaar stood up. [Sahih in other than this chain]"""
"13903","(13897) And Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr — informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — informed us: al-Shafi'i — informed us: Ibn Abi Yahya — from Ja'far ibn Muhammad — from his father — that 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A slave may marry two women and shall not exceed that. And Sufyan al-Thawri similarly narrated it from Ja'far ibn Muhammad. [Da'if]"
"13904","(13898) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Haafiz — informed us by way of ijazah: Abu al-Walid — informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan — informed us: Abu Bakr — informed us: al-Muharibi — from Layth — from al-Hakam, who said: The Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be blessings be upon him) reached a consensus that a slave shall not gather more than two women in marriage. [Da'if]"
"13905","(13899) Abu 'Amr — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Adib — informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili — informed us: al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya — informed us: Ya'qub — informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id and Ibn Mahdi — (h) And Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi — informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr — informed us: Ibn Mahdi — informed us: Sufyan — from Habib — from Sa'id ibn Jubayr — from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \Seven relations are forbidden to you by lineage and seven by marriage tie — {Forbidden to you are your mothers and your daughters…} [al-Nisa' 23] to the end of the verse.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Hanbal from Yahya ibn Sa'id. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari included it under the chapter \""What is Permissible of Women\""]"""
"13906","(13900) Abu Nasr — 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah — informed us: Abu Mansur — al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Dabbi — informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah — informed us: Sa'id ibn Mansur — informed us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim — from Sa'id al-Jurayri — from Hayyan ibn 'Umayr, who said: Ibn 'Abbas said: \Seven by marriage tie and seven by lineage are forbidden"," and what is forbidden by nursing is likewise forbidden by lineage.\"" [Sahih. Previously cited]"""
"13907","(13901) Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan — informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman — informed us: al-Shafi'i — informed us: Malik — from 'Abd Allah ibn Dinar — from Sulayman ibn Yasar — from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr — from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be blessings be upon him) said: \What is forbidden by nursing is forbidden by birth.\"" [Sahih. Muslim 1445]"""
"13908","(13902) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Haafiz — informed us: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani — informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf — informed us: Malik — from 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr — from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman — that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be blessings be upon him), informed her that the Messenger of Allah (peace be blessings be upon him) was with her when she heard the voice of a man seeking permission to enter the house of Hafsah. 'A'ishah said: \O Messenger of Allah"," a man is seeking permission to enter your house.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be blessings be upon him) said: \""I see him as so-and-so"," the paternal uncle of Hafsah by nursing.\"" 'A'ishah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," if so-and-so were alive"," the paternal uncle of Hafsah by nursing"," would he be able to enter upon me?\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace be blessings be upon him) said: \""Yes. Indeed"," nursing forbids what birth forbids.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf"," and Muslim narrated it from Yahya ibn Yahya from Malik — may Allah have mercy upon him. [Sahih. Al-Bukhari 2646"," 5239]"""
"13909","(13903) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad — informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustawayh — informed us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan — informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari — informed us: 'Abd al-Razzaq — informed us: al-Thawri — from Abu Furwah — from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani — from Ibn Mas'ud, that a man from Banu Shamkh of Fazarah married a woman and then saw her mother and was captivated by her. He sought a ruling from Ibn Mas'ud regarding that, and he ordered him to separate from the woman and marry her mother. So he married her and she bore him children. Then Ibn Mas'ud came to Madinah and asked about that, and he was told that she was not lawful for him. When he returned to Kufah, he said to the man: \She is forbidden to you; she is not appropriate for you. Separate from her.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by 'Abd al-Razzaq 10811]"""
"13910","(13904) And Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl — informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far — informed us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan — informed us: Sa'id ibn Mansur — informed us: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah — from Abu Ishaq — from Sa'id ibn Iyyas, who is Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani — from a man who married a woman from Banu Shamkh and then saw her mother and was captivated by her. He went to Ibn Mas'ud and said: \I married a woman and have not consummated the marriage with her"," and then her mother captivated me. Should I divorce the woman and marry her mother?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So he divorced her and married her mother. Then 'Abd Allah came to Madinah and asked the Companions of the Prophet (peace be blessings be upon him)"," and they said: \""This is not permissible.\"" Then he returned and came to Banu Shamkh and said: \""Where is the man who married the mother of the woman who was under his care?\"" They said: \""Here he is.\"" He said: \""Let him separate from her.\"" They said: \""She has already borne him children.\"" He said: \""Let her separate from him"," for she is forbidden by Allah"," the Almighty"," the Majestic.\"" And Israel narrated it with this meaning from Abu Ishaq. [Sahih]"""
"13911","(13905) Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Hammad informed us: al-Hajjaj informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani, that a man asked Ibn Mas'ud about a man who had divorced his wife before consummating the marriage — could he marry her mother? He said: \Yes.\"" So he married her"," and she bore him a child. Then he came to 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him. He said: \""Separate between them.\"" He said: \""She has already borne a child.\"" He said: \""Even if she had borne ten [children].\"" So he separated between them. [Da'if]"""
"13912","(13906) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Farwah al-Hamdani, who said: I heard Abu 'Amr al-Shaybani say: \Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) used to permit a man who had married a wife and she died before he consummated the marriage to marry her mother.\"" He said: \""Then he came to Madinah and it was as though he met 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)"," so he retracted.\"" This is how Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Farwah"," mentioning death. But Sufyan al-Thawri contradicted him"," narrating it from Abu Farwah with mention of divorce. When Sufyan and Shu'bah differ"," the ruling follows the narration of Sufyan"," for he is more precise and more knowledgeable in jurisprudence. Alongside Sufyan's narration is the narration of Abu Ishaq from Abu 'Amr. [Hasan]"""
"13913","(13907) Abu Sa'id ibn Abu 'Amr informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Malik informed us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, who said: Zayd ibn Thabit was asked about a man who married a woman and separated from her before consummating the marriage — would her mother be lawful for him? Zayd ibn Thabit said to him: \No. The mother is unambiguous (mubhamah); there is no condition regarding her. The condition applies only to the step-daughters (al-raba'ib).\"" This is munqati' (disconnected). It has also been narrated from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib that Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""If she died and he inherited from her"," then her mother is not lawful for him. But if he divorced her"," then he may marry her if he wishes.\"" And the statement of the majority (qawl al-jama'ah) is more worthy of being followed. [Da'if]"""
"13914","(13908) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that he said: \She is unambiguous (mubhamah)","\"" and he disliked it. It is also narrated from Qatadah"," from al-Hasan"," from 'Imran ibn Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him)"," that he said regarding a man who married a woman and then divorced her before consummating the marriage"," or she died — her mother is not lawful for him"," whether she died or he divorced her. This is the position of al-Hasan and Qatadah. [Hasan]"""
"13915","(13909) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, regarding the words of Allah, the Mighty and Majestic: {And [also prohibited to you are] the mothers of your wives} — he said: \What Allah has left unspecified"," leave it unspecified; and what He has made explicit"," follow it.\"" Then he recited: {And [also prohibited to you are] your step-daughters who are under your care"," born to your wives with whom you have consummated the marriage. But if you have not consummated the marriage"," there is no sin upon you.} He said: \""This He left unspecified"," and this He made explicit.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is the position of 'Ata'"," 'Ikrimah"," and others. A musnad hadith has also been narrated concerning it. [Hasan]"""
"13916","(13910) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Mu'alla narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Muthanna narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn 'Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \When a man marries a woman and then divorces her before consummating the marriage"," he may marry her daughter"," but he may not marry her mother.\"" Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah is not strong (in narration). [Da'if]"""
"13917","(13911) 'Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah followed him in this narration from 'Amr. Abu Tahir al-Faqih and Abu Sa'id ibn Abu 'Amr informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Any man who marries a woman — whether he has consummated the marriage or not — it is not lawful for him to marry her mother. And any man who marries a woman and has consummated the marriage with her"," it is not lawful for him to marry her daughter. But if he has not consummated the marriage with her"," then he may marry her daughter if he wishes.\"" [Da'if]"""
"13918","(13912) Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu al-Hasan al-Tarifi narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn 'Abbas, regarding His words: {And do not marry those [women] whom your fathers married} and His words: {And [also prohibited are] the wives of your sons} — he said: \Every woman whom your father or your son has married — whether he consummated the marriage or not — she is forbidden to you.\"" [Da'if]"""
"13919","(13913) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abu 'Amr informed us, both saying: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, from Abu Hurrah, from al-Hasan, that he was asked about a man who married a woman and divorced her before consummating the marriage — could her father marry her? Al-Hasan said: \No.\"" He said: Allah"," the Most High"," said: {And [also prohibited are] the wives of your sons who are from your loins.} The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: He said — and Allah knows best — \""from your loins\"" so that the wives of adopted sons would not be included in it. This is like the words of Allah"," the Most High"," to His Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): {And when Zayd had no longer any need of her"," We married her to you"," so that there would not be any difficulty for the believers regarding the wives of their adopted sons.} Thus"," the wife of a grandson"," however far down the line"," and the wife of a son through breastfeeding are both included in the prohibition. This is the meaning of the statement of al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) in the book on breastfeeding. [Da'if]"""
"13920","(13914) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed me: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtawayh informed us: 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us that Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to them: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar informed us: Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to us: Salim narrated to me, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that Zayd ibn Harithah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we used to call him only \Zayd ibn Muhammad\"" until the Qur'an was revealed: {Call them by [the names of] their fathers; it is more just in the sight of Allah.} Al-Bukhari (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated it in the Sahih from Mu'alla ibn Asad"," and Muslim narrated it through two other chains from Musa. [Sahih. Bukhari 4732]"""
"13921","(13915) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: 'Abdullah ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us: Thabit narrated from Anas, who said:\n\nThis verse was revealed: **{And you concealed within yourself that which Allah was to bring to light}** — concerning the matter of Zaynab bint Jahsh. Zayd had come complaining and intending to divorce her, and he came to seek the Prophet's ﷺ counsel regarding that. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: **{Keep your wife and fear Allah, and you concealed within yourself that which Allah was to bring to light}** — the verse. He said: **{Then when Zayd had fulfilled his need from her, We married her to you, so that there would be no difficulty for the believers regarding the wives of their adopted sons when they have fulfilled their need from them.}**\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the *Sahih* from two other routes from Hammad ibn Zayd. [Sahih]\n\n---"
"13922","(13916) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad al-Hafiz informed me: Muhammad ibn Ishaq Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from 'Irak ibn Malik that 'Urwah informed him:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a marriage proposal to Abu Bakr regarding 'A'ishah — may Allah be pleased with them both. Abu Bakr said: \Am I not your brother?\"" He ﷺ said: **\""You are my brother in the religion of Allah and in His Book"," and she is lawful for me.\""**\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the *Sahih* from 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf from al-Layth"," thus as a *mursal* narration. [Sahih. Bukhari 5081]\n\n---"""
"13923","(13917) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abdullah al-Harawi informed us: Hushaym informed us: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated from 'Adiyy ibn Thabit al-Ansari, who said:\n\nWhen Abu Qays ibn al-Aslat died, his son Qays proposed marriage to his father's wife. She went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," Abu Qays has passed away"," and his son Qays — one of the best of the living — has proposed marriage to me. I said to him: 'I never regarded you except as a son"," and I am not one to precede the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in any matter.'\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent regarding her"," and this verse was revealed: **{And do not marry those women whom your fathers married}** [al-Nisa': 22].\n\nThis is a *mursal* narration"," and others among the scholars of *tafsir* have mentioned its meaning. [Da'if]\n\n---"""
"13924","(13918) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakim ibn Nafi' informed us: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated from al-Zuhri: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me: Yazid ibn al-Bara' narrated from his father, who said:\n\nI met my uncle while he had raised a banner. I said: \Where are you heading?\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to a man who married his father's wife"," to strike his neck and seize his wealth.\"" [Sahih]\n\n---"""
"13925","(13919) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us of that: Abu al-Hasan al-Tara'ifi narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbas — may Allah be pleased with them both — that he said regarding the words of the Almighty: **{From your women whom you have entered upon}**: \Al-Dukhul (entering) means *nikah* (marriage)"," and by *nikah* is meant sexual intercourse (*jima'*).\"" And he said regarding *al-mass* (touching)"," *al-lams*"," and *al-ifda'*: \""It is similar to that.\""\n\nAnd it has reached me that Tawus said: \""Al-Dukhul means sexual intercourse.\"" [Da'if]\n\n---"""
"13926","(13920) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajani informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik informed us — that it reached him:\n\nThat 'Umar ibn al-Khattab — may Allah be pleased with him — gave his daughter a slave-girl as a gift and said to her: \Do not touch her"," for I have already had intercourse with her.\"" [Da'if]\n\n---"""
"13927","(13921) With his *isnad*, he said: Malik narrated from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mujabbir that he said:\n\nSalim ibn 'Abdullah gave his son a slave-girl as a gift and said to him: \Do not approach her"," for I had intended her but did not touch her.\"" [Da'if]\n\n---"""
"13928","(13922) With his *isnad*, he said: Malik narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id that Abu Nahshal al-Aswad said to al-Qasim ibn Muhammad:\n\n\I saw my slave-girl uncovered in the moonlight"," and I sat with her in the position a man sits with his wife. She said: 'I am menstruating.' So I did not touch her. I gifted her to my son so that he may have intercourse with her.\"" Al-Qasim forbade him from that.\n\n---"""
"13929","(13923) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakim ibn Nafi' informed us: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated from al-Zuhri: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Abi Salamah — and her mother was Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ — informed him that Umm Habibah bint Abi Sufyan informed her that she said:\n\n\O Messenger of Allah"," marry my sister Zaynab bint Abi Sufyan.\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\""Would you like that?\""** She said: I said: \""Yes"," I am not one to begrudge you"," and I would love for my sister to share in any good that comes to me.\"" She said: The Prophet ﷺ said: **\""That is not lawful for me.\""** She said: I said: \""By Allah"," O Messenger of Allah"," we have been told that you intend to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\"" He said: **\""The daughter of Umm Salamah?\""** She said: I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: **\""By Allah"," even if she were not my foster-daughter under my care"," she would not be lawful for me"," for she is the daughter of my foster-brother. Thuwaybah nursed me and Abu Salamah.\""** So do not offer your daughters or your sisters to me.\""\n\n'Urwah said: Thuwaybah was a freed slave-girl of Abu Lahab. Abu Lahab had manumitted her"," and she nursed the Prophet ﷺ. When Abu Lahab died"," one of his family members saw him in a dream in a wretched state and said to him: \""What have you encountered?\"" Abu Lahab said: \""I have not found any ease after you"," except that I was given to drink in this\"" — and he pointed to the space between the thumb and the finger next to it — \""because of my manumission of Thuwaybah.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the *Sahih* from Abu al-Yaman"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from al-Zuhri. [Sahih. Muslim 1449]\n\n---"""
"13930","(13924) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us: 'Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated to us: Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from 'Uqayl from Ibn Shihab that he said: 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Zaynab bint Umm Salamah informed him that Umm Habibah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said:\n\n\O Messenger of Allah"," marry my sister"," the daughter of Abi Sufyan.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\""And would you like that?\""** She said: \""Yes"," I am not one to begrudge you"," and I would love for my sister to share in any good that comes to me.\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\""That is not lawful for me.\""** She said: I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," we have been told that you intend to marry Durrah bint Abi Salamah.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: **\""The daughter of Umm Salamah?\""** She said: I said: \""Yes.\"" He said: **\""By Allah"," even if she were not my foster-daughter under my care"," she would not be lawful for me"," for she is the daughter of my foster-brother. Thuwaybah nursed me and Abu Salamah.\""** So do not offer your daughters or your sisters to me.\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the *Sahih* from Yahya ibn Bukayr"," and Muslim narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rumh from al-Layth. [Sahih. Preceded before it]"""
"13931","(13925) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us that al-Rabīʿ reported that al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy upon him, said in the Book of Fosterage: The eldest son of a man used to succeed his father regarding his father's wife, and a man used to marry two sisters simultaneously. So Allah, the Most High, forbade that any of them should combine two sisters in marriage during his lifetime, or marry those whom his fathers had married, except what had already occurred in the pre-Islamic period of ignorance before they came to know of its prohibition. It was not that He permitted to them what they had already combined before Islam.\n\n[Sound. Al-Shāfiʿī said in al-Umm 5/26]"
"13932","(13926) Abū Isḥāq — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm — informed us that ʿAbd al-Khāliq ibn al-Ḥasan informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Thābit narrated to us from his father, from al-Hudhayl, from Muqātil ibn Sulaymān, who said: Allah, the Almighty, said {except what had already passed} (al-Nisāʾ 22) referring to the wives of fathers, because the Arabs used to marry the wives of their fathers. Then He prohibited lineage and in-law relations. He did not say {except what had already passed} regarding lineage and in-law relations because the Arabs did not marry on the basis of lineage and in-law ties. And He said regarding the two sisters {except what had already passed} because they used to combine them both, so combining them was prohibited altogether, except what had already occurred before the prohibition. {Indeed, Allah is ever Forgiving and Merciful} for what had taken place of combining the two sisters before the prohibition.\n\n[Weak]"
"13933","(13927) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Ḥasan — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs — and Abū Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī both said that Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah informed us that Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us from Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf, from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān, who said: When a man died in the pre-Islamic period of ignorance, the next of kin of the deceased would go to his wife and cast a garment over her, thereby inheriting her marriage, and he would have greater right over her. When Abū Qays ibn al-Aslat died, his son Qays went to his father's wife and married her, but had not yet consummated the marriage. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. So Allah revealed regarding Qays: {And do not marry those whom your fathers married, except what has already passed} (al-Nisāʾ 22) — before the prohibition — until He mentioned the prohibition of mothers and daughters, until He said: {And [do not] combine two sisters, except what has already passed} (al-Nisāʾ 23) — before the prohibition. {Indeed, Allah is ever Forgiving and Merciful} for what had transpired before the prohibition.\n\n[Weak]"
"13934","(13928) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us from Muṭarrif, from Abū al-Jahm, from Abū al-Akḍar, from ʿAmmār, that he considered disliked regarding female slaves what he considered disliked regarding free women, except for the number [i.e., the restriction on number]. Al-Shāfiʿī said: And this is from the statement of ʿAmmār, if Allah wills, in accordance with the meaning of the Qurʾān, and upon this we act.\n\n[Weak]"
"13935","(13929) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us that Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn informed us that Ibn Sawwār narrated to us from Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, who said: ʿAbd Allāh — that is, Ibn Masʿūd, may Allah be pleased with him — said: What is prohibited regarding free women is also prohibited regarding female slaves, except for the number.\n\n[Weak]"
"13936","(13930) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that Mālik narrated — (ḥ) and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from Qabīṣah ibn Dhuʾayb, that a man asked ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, about two sisters from among those whom the right hand possesses — whether they could be combined in marriage. ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, said: One verse permits them and another verse prohibits them, but I do not like to do this. He [Qabīṣah] said: He left his presence and met a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who said: If I had any authority, and I found anyone who did that, I would make him an example [of punishment]. Mālik, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: Ibn Shihāb said: I think he was ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him.\n\nMālik said: And it has reached me that al-Zubayr ibn al-ʿAwwām said the same.\n\n[Sound. Reported by Mālik 1144]"
"13937","(13931) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us that ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk informed us that Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bukayr informed us that al-Layth narrated to us from Yūnus, from Ibn Shihāb, that he was asked about combining two sisters from among those whom the right hand possesses. He said: Qabīṣah ibn Dhuʾayb informed me that Niyār al-Aslamī asked a man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about two sisters from among those whom the right hand possesses. He said to him: One verse permits them and another verse prohibits them, and I would not do that. Niyār left that man's presence and met another man from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: What did your companion, the one you asked for a ruling, tell you? He informed him, and he said: I forbid you from them both. If you were to combine them both and I had authority over you, I would punish you with a severe exemplary punishment.\n\n[Sound. Previously reported]"
"13938","(13932) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that Mālik narrated — (ḥ) and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us that al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about a woman and her daughter from among those whom the right hand possesses — whether one could be taken after the other. ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I do not like to permit them both together. In the narration of Abū Aḥmad: I do not permit them.\n\n[Sound. Reported by Mālik 1143]"
"13939","(13933) Abū Bakr and Abū Zakariyyā both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Sufyān narrated to us from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from his father, who said: ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, was asked about a mother and her daughter from among those whom the right hand possesses. He said: I do not like to permit them both together. ʿUbayd Allāh said: My father said: I wish ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, had been more severe in that than he was. The Shaykh, may Allah have mercy upon him, said: Al-Muzannī, may Allah have mercy upon him and us, made an error in this, for he said: Ibn ʿUmar said, \I wish.\"" But it is Ibn ʿUtbah"," without any doubt.\n\n[Sound. Reported by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 4/4]"""
"13940","(13934) Abū Bakr and Abū Zakariyyā both said that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Muslim and ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Ibn Abī Mulaykah narrate that Muʿādh ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Maʿmar came to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and said to her: I had a concubine with whom I had intercourse, and she has borne a daughter who is my slave girl. May I take her daughter as a concubine? She said: No. He said: By Allah, I will not leave this unless you say that Allah has made it unlawful. She said: No one from my family has done this, nor anyone who obeys me.\n\n[Sound. Reported by al-Shāfiʿī, as in his Musnad 1/290]"
"13941","(13935) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; Abū Qaṭan ʿAmr ibn al-Haytham — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — from Abī ʿAwn — from Abī Ṣāliḥ — from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Regarding the two slave-girls who are sisters"," one verse renders them lawful and another verse renders them unlawful. I neither command nor forbid"," neither declare lawful nor unlawful"," and I do not practise it"," nor do any of my household.\"""""
"13942","(13936) Abū Muḥammad — informed us; ibn al-Aʿrābī — said: al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; ʿAffān — narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah — informed us; Simāk — from Ḥanash — that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a man who has two slave-girls who are sisters, and he has intercourse with one of them — may he then have intercourse with the other? He said: \One verse renders them lawful and another verse renders them unlawful"," and I have forbidden myself and my offspring from it.\""\n\nAnd it is narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding a slave-girl and her daughter a similar ruling. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13943","(13937) Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī — informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Firās — narrated to us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Daybulī — narrated to us; Abū ʿUbayd Allāh al-Makhzūmī — narrated to us; Sufyān — from ʿAmr — from ʿIkrimah, who said: \The statement of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the two sisters from among those whom one's right hand possesses was mentioned in the presence of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him). They said: 'Indeed ʿAlī said: One verse renders them lawful and another verse renders them unlawful.'\"" Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him) said at that point: \""One verse renders them lawful and another verse renders them unlawful. Those whom I am now forbidden are so due to the kinship relation I have with them"," and the kinship of some of them with others does not render them forbidden upon me"," by the word of Allah the Most High: {And [also prohibited to you are] married women except those whom your right hand possesses} (al-Nisāʾ 24).\"""""
"13944","(13938) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; from Abī al-Walīd — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib — narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿĪsā — from ibn al-Mubārak — from Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah — from his paternal uncle — from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): \A man asked him: 'I have two slave-girls who are sisters; I have had intercourse with one of them and now wish to have intercourse with the other.' He said: 'Not until you remove her from your ownership.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13945","(13939) The noble Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī — informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Shuraīḥ — narrated to us; Abū al-Qāsim al-Baghawī — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Jaʿd — informed us; Sharīk — from ʿAbd al-Karīm, i.e. al-Jazarī — from Nāfiʿ, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) had two slave-girls who were sisters. He had intercourse with one of them and then wished to have intercourse with the other"," so he removed the one with whom he had had intercourse from his ownership.\""\n\nAnd al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh narrated from Maymūn ibn Mihrān that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""When a man has two slave-girls who are sisters and he has intercourse with one of them"," let him not approach the other until he removes the one with whom he had intercourse from his ownership.\"" [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by Ibn al-Jaʿd"," 2258]"""
"13946","(13940) And al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī said: \Until he removes her from his ownership or marries her off.\"" Ibn Burhān — informed us of it; Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Saʿdān — narrated to us; Muʿādh — from al-Ashʿath — from al-Ḥasan"," and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī"," 5109"," 5111]"""
"13947","(13941) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram — narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar — narrated to us; Yūnus —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh — informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Dārabirdī — in Marw — narrated to us; Abū al-Muwajjih — informed us; ʿAbdān — informed us; ʿAbd Allāh — informed us; Yūnus — from al-Zuhrī — from Qabīṣah ibn Dhuʾayb — that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade combining a woman with her paternal aunt"," and a woman with her maternal aunt.\"" The wording is from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Yūnus ibn Yazīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"13948","(13942) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār — in Baghdad — informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān — narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ — narrated to us; Shabābah — narrated to us; Warqāʾ — from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār — from Abī Salamah — from Abī Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) — from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \A woman shall not be combined with her paternal aunt"," nor a woman with her maternal aunt.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"13949","(13943) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī — narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd — narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā — informed us; Shaybān — from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr — narrated to me; Abī Salamah — that he heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A woman shall not be married along with her maternal aunt"," nor a woman along with her paternal aunt.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Ḥātim from Shabābah"," and Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"13950","(13944) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī, and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān — informed us; al-Shāfiʿī — informed us; Mālik —\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Maslamah — narrated to us; Mālik — from Abī al-Zinād — from al-Aʿraj — from Abī Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A woman shall not be combined with her paternal aunt"," nor a woman with her maternal aunt.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) said.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from al-Qaʿnabī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"13951","(13945) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us — al-Muʿallā, meaning Ibn Manṣūr, narrated to us — al-Layth ibn Saʿd from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb from ʿIrāk from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade combining four women in marriage — a woman and her paternal aunt, and a woman and her maternal aunt. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rumḥ from al-Layth. [Authenticated; previously referenced.]"
"13952","(13946) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr ibn Ḥabīb al-Sahmī narrated to us — Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to us — from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman shall not be married while her paternal aunt is [already] married [to the same man]"," nor while her maternal aunt is [already] married [to the same man].\"" Muslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn Ḥassān. [Authenticated; previously referenced.]"""
"13953","(13947) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said — al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Muḥāḍir ibn al-Mawriʿ narrated to us — ʿĀṣim ibn Sulaymān narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī narrated to us — Abū al-Muwajjih narrated to us — ʿAbdān informed us — ʿAbd Allāh informed us — ʿĀṣim from al-Shaʿbī that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, saying: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a woman be married while her paternal aunt — or he said, her maternal aunt — is [already] married [to the same man]. The wording is that of the ḥadīth of Ibn al-Mubārak. And in the narration of Muḥāḍir from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman shall not be married while her paternal aunt is [already] married [to the same man]"," nor while her maternal aunt is [already] married [to the same man].\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān. al-Bukhārī said"," and Dāwūd and Ibn ʿAwn narrated from al-Shaʿbī from Abū Hurayrah. [Authenticated; al-Bukhārī extracted it"," no. 5108.]"""
"13954","(13948) As for the ḥadīth of Dāwūd: Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ narrated to us — Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us — Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us — from Dāwūd from al-Shaʿbī from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \A woman shall not be married while her paternal aunt is [already] married [to the same man]"," nor while her maternal aunt is [already] married [to the same man]; nor shall a paternal aunt be married while her brother's daughter is [already] married [to the same man]"," nor shall a maternal aunt be married while her sister's daughter is [already] married [to the same man] — neither the younger upon the elder"," nor the elder upon the younger.\"" [Authenticated.]"""
"13955","(13949) As for the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAwn: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Aḥmad the Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿArūbah narrated to us — Bundār and Yaḥyā ibn Ḥakīm said — Ibn Abī ʿAdī narrated to us — from Ibn ʿAwn from al-Shaʿbī from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: [the Prophet ﷺ] forbade that a man marry — meaning, a woman — while her paternal niece or her maternal niece is [already] married [to the same man]. [Authenticated.]"
"13956","(13950) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm: al-Rabīʿ informed me — al-Shāfiʿī mentioned the ḥadīth of al-Aʿraj from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, as has preceded, then said: \And upon this we take [our position]"," and it is the opinion of every muftī I have met — there is no difference among them"," to my knowledge. And the scholars of ḥadīth have not narrated [anything] from the Prophet ﷺ on this from any face [i.e."," chain] except from Abū Hurayrah. And it has been narrated from a ḥadīth that the scholars of ḥadīth do not establish from another face. And in this there is a proof against whoever rejects the ḥadīth"," and against whoever takes the ḥadīth once and leaves it another time.\"" And he spoke at length on this"," and excelled"," may Allah be pleased with him. And as for what he mentioned regarding its being narrated from other than the face of Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," then as he said"," for it is narrated from ʿAlī"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās"," ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," and Anas ibn Mālik"," may Allah be pleased with them all"," and from the women"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her — all of them from the Prophet ﷺ. However"," all of these narrations are not of the condition of the two Ṣaḥīḥ authors"," al-Bukhārī and Muslim. Rather"," they and those before them and those after them among the imāms of ḥadīth agreed only upon establishing the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah in this chapter"," as al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said. And al-Bukhārī extracted the narration of ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal from al-Shaʿbī from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," except that they [i.e."," al-Bukhārī and Muslim] consider it erroneous"," and the correct position is the narration of Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAwn from al-Shaʿbī from Abū Hurayrah"," may Allah be pleased with him. And Allah knows best. [Authenticated; al-Shāfiʿī said this in al-Umm"," 4/6.]"""
"13957","(13951) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us — ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar narrated to us — Yūnus narrated to us — from al-Zuhrī, who said: more than one [narrator] informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar combined [in marriage] the daughter of ʿAlī and the wife of ʿAlī. Then one of the daughters of ʿAlī died, and he married another daughter of ʿAlī. And Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated it from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mihrān from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar in a similar manner. [Authenticated.]"
"13958","(13952) Abū Ḥāzim the Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Jarīr ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd narrated to us — Mughīrah narrated to us — from Qutham, mawlā of the family of al-ʿAbbās, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar combined [in marriage] Laylā bint Masʿūd al-Nahshaliyyah, who was the wife of ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, and Umm Kulthūm bint ʿAlī, daughter of Fāṭimah, may Allah be pleased with her, so the two were his wives. And it is mentioned from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn that a man from the people of Egypt who was known as Jabalah, who was a companion [of the Prophet], combined [in marriage] the wife of a man and the man's daughter by another woman. And from Ayyūb that he said: \I was informed that Saʿd ibn Qarḥāʾ"," a man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," combined [in marriage] the wife of a man and the man's daughter by another woman.\"" [Authenticated; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr extracted it"," no. 1011.]"""
"13959","(13953) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us — al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm: al-Rabīʿ informed me — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated to us — from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār that he heard al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad saying: \The son of my paternal uncle combined [in marriage] the two daughters of his paternal uncle"," and the women became confused"," not knowing where to go.\"" Aḥmad"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Meaning"," the two daughters of his two paternal uncles.\"" [Authenticated; al-Shāfiʿī extracted it in al-Umm"," 4/6.]"""
"13960","(13954) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us — ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawarīrī narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us — from Qatādah from Ṣāliḥ, Abū al-Khalīl, from Abū ʿAlqamah from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an army on the day of Ḥunayn to Awṭās. They encountered an enemy and fought them, overcame them, and took captives. Some of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ felt uneasy about coitus with them on account of their polytheist husbands [still being alive]. So Allah, exalted is His majesty, revealed concerning that: {And [also prohibited to you are all] married women except those your right hands possess} [al-Nisāʾ 24:24] — meaning, they are lawful for them when their waiting period (ʿiddah) has expired. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qawarīrī. [Authenticated; Muslim, no. 1456.]"
"13961","(13955) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ya'qub ibn Yusuf al-'Adl informed us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Abu Husayn from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said regarding this verse: **\And [also prohibited to you are] married women except those whom your right hands possess\""** (al-Nisa' 24): He said: \""Every woman who has a husband"," approaching her is fornication"," except one who has been taken captive.\"" [Sahih]"""
"13962","(13956) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi informed us; Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us; Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us; Sharik narrated from Salim al-Aftas from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding His, the Most High's, words: **\And [also prohibited to you are] married women except those whom your right hands possess\""** (al-Nisa' 24): He said: \""They are the female captives who have husbands; there is no harm in cohabiting with them after they have undergone istibra' (the waiting period to ascertain the state of the womb).\"" [Da'if]"""
"13963","(13957) And with his isnad, Sharik narrated from 'Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib from Sa'id ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) a similar narration. And al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated with his isnad from 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) with the meaning of the statement of Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"13964","(13958) Abu Ahmad al-Mihrajan informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ja'far informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated from Ibn Shihab from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib that he said: **\And [also prohibited to you are] married women\""** (al-Nisa' 24) — they are those female slaves who have husbands.\n\nAnd this refers to the fact that Allah has forbidden fornication. Al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) used it as evidence that married female slaves are forbidden to anyone other than their husbands"," and that the exception in His statement **\""except those whom your right hands possess\""** is specific to female captives"," because the Sunnah indicates that a slave woman who is not a captive"," when she is sold or freed"," her sale is not a divorce. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave Barirah the choice when she was freed — whether to remain with her husband or separate from him — and Barirah's ownership had lapsed through sale and then she was freed. Thus her ownership lapsed for two reasons"," yet this was not a separation (divorce). He said: \""When the private part of a married woman is not made permissible by the lapse of ownership — if she was not sold — then she is not made permissible by right-hand ownership until her husband divorces her.\"" This was his position in the old opinion. Among those who held this view were 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," 'Uthman ibn 'Affan"," 'Ali ibn Abi Talib"," 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf"," and Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them all). They said: \""The husband's marriage remains valid after the sale.\"" And among those who said that the sale of a slave woman constitutes her divorce were 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud"," Ubayy ibn Ka'b"," 'Imran ibn Husayn"," Jabir ibn 'Abdullah"," Ibn 'Abbas"," and Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with them). The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It is as though they drew an analogy with the female captive"," but the hadith of Barirah prevents this analogy. Furthermore"," there is consensus (ijma') that whoever gives his slave woman in marriage does not have the right to cohabit with her"," and she is among those whom his right hand possesses — and this is the meaning of al-Shafi'i's (may Allah have mercy on him) statement.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Malik in al-Talaq]"""
"13965","(13959) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us; al-Shafi'i informed us; Malik narrated from Rabi'ah from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that she said: \There were three Sunnahs (established practices) regarding Barirah. In one of the Sunnahs"," she was freed and was given the choice regarding her husband.\"" [Both al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it in their Sahih collections. Muslim 1504]"""
"13966","(13960) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Yahya ibn Abi Talib informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' informed us; Sa'id narrated from Qatadah from Yahya ibn Ya'mar from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said regarding a man who commits fornication with his wife's mother or his wife's daughter: \They are two sanctities (hurmatan) that he has transgressed"," and that does not make his wife forbidden for him.\"" And Yahya ibn Ya'mar said: \""The unlawful has never rendered the lawful unlawful.\"" This reached al-Sha'bi"," and he said: \""Nay"," if I were to take a vessel of wine and pour it into a container of water"," that water would become unlawful.\"" And it was al-Sha'bi's opinion that she had become forbidden for him. [Sahih from other chains]"""
"13967","(13961) And Abu 'Abdullah informed us; Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us; Yahya informed us; 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Hisham al-Dastawa'i narrated from Qatadah from Yahya ibn Ya'mar from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: \He transgressed two sanctities.\"" [Sahih. From other chains"," as mentioned before it]"""
"13968","(13962) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf informed us; Abu Sa'id 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Wahhab informed us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Hisham narrated to us; Qatadah narrated from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a man who had intercourse with his wife's mother: He said: \He transgressed two sanctities"," and his wife is not made forbidden for him.\"" And 'Abd al-A'la narrated it from Hisham from Qays ibn Sa'd from 'Ata' from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him). And al-Zuhri narrated from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) a similar statement to ours"," but it is mursal. This was also the position of Ibn al-Musayyib"," 'Urwah"," and al-Zuhri. [Sahih]"""
"13969","(13963) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed me; Abu al-Walid narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Humayd ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me from 'Uqayl from Ibn Shihab, and he was asked about a man who had intercourse with his wife's mother. He said: 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \The unlawful does not render anything of the lawful unlawful.\"" [Da'if]"""
"13970","(13964) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran in Baghdad informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sam narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: **\The unlawful does not render the lawful unlawful.\""** [Da'if]"""
"13971","(13965) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd al-Razzāz reported to us in Baghdad: Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn al-Yamān narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The unlawful does not render the unlawful the lawful.\"" [Very weak. Referred to previously.]"""
"13972","(13966) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Buhlūl al-Anbārī narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ al-Makhzūmī narrated to us: al-Mughīrah ibn Ismāʿīl ibn Ayyūb ibn Salamah narrated from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Zuhrī, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about a man who commits zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse) with a woman — may he then marry her daughter? Or if he commits zinā with a daughter, may he marry her mother? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The unlawful does not render the unlawful the lawful. That which renders unlawful is only a lawful marriage.\"" Isḥāq said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Nāfiʿ said"," and it is by this that we abide. [Very weak. Referred to previously.]"""
"13973","(13967) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Yūnus narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn al-Mughīrah al-Makhzūmī narrated to us: my brother Muḥammad ibn al-Mughīrah narrated from his father, al-Mughīrah ibn Ismāʿīl, from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The lawful is not corrupted by the unlawful. Whoever commits fujūr (fornication) with a woman"," there is nothing preventing him from marrying her mother or her daughter — but as for marriage (nikāḥ)"," then no.\"" This narration is unique to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Waqqāṣī"," and he is weak"," as stated by Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and other imams of ḥadīth. The authentic narration from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī is a mursal"," mawqūf report from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and from him from some of the scholars. And the ḥadīth of ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿUmarī is more reliable. And Allah knows best. [Very weak.]"""
"13974","(13968) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Mihrajānī informed us in Herat: Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Ziyād ibn Qays narrated to us: Abū Salamah Yaḥyā ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us: my brother Muḥammad ibn al-Mughīrah narrated from Muḥammad ibn Fulayḥ, from Yūnus ibn Yazīd, from Ibn Shihāb, that he was asked about a man who commits fujūr with a woman — may he marry her daughter? He said: Some of the scholars said: \Allah does not corrupt the lawful by means of the unlawful.\"" [Weak.]"""
"13975","(13969) As for what is narrated from Ibn Masʿūd, that he said: \The unlawful and the lawful do not combine except that the unlawful overcomes the lawful\"" — it is narrated only by Jābir al-Juʿfī from al-Shaʿbī from Ibn Masʿūd. And Jābir al-Juʿfī is weak"," and al-Shaʿbī's narration from Ibn Masʿūd is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). Others narrated its meaning from al-Shaʿbī as his own statement"," not raised to ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd. And Layth ibn Abī Sulaym narrated from Ḥammād"," from Ibrāhīm"," from ʿAlqamah"," from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd"," who said: \""Allah does not look with mercy upon a man who looks at the private parts of a woman or her daughter.\"" This is also very weak. [Very weak.]\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us"," who said: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This is mawqūf (stopped). And Layth and Ḥammād are both weak. As for what is narrated in this regard from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""When a man looks at the private parts of a woman"," her mother and her daughter become unlawful for him\"" — it is narrated only by al-Ḥajjaj ibn Arṭāh from Abī Hānīʾ or Umm Hānīʾ from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). And this is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)"," majhūl (unknown)"," and weak. Al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh is not used as evidence in what he narrates with a chain"," so how about what he narrates as mursal from one who is not known?"""
"13976","(13970) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Isḥāq ibn Abī Kāmil narrated to us: Yaʿqūb narrated to us: the nephew of Ibn Shihāb narrated from his paternal uncle, who said: ʿUrwah informed me that he heard Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam and al-Miswar ibn Makhramah narrating a report from the reports of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) concerning the expedition of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. Among what ʿUrwah informed me from them was: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote a treaty with Suhayl ibn ʿAmr on the day of al-Ḥudaybiyyah for the agreed period, among the conditions that Suhayl ibn ʿAmr stipulated was that no one from among them would come to you, even if he were upon your religion, except that you would return him to us and leave him alone with us. Suhayl refused to agree to any other terms with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). The believers found this difficult and raised objections and spoke about it. When Suhayl refused to agree to any terms with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) other than this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote the treaty with him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) returned Abū Jandal ibn Suhayl on that day to his father Suhayl ibn ʿAmr. No man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during that period except that he was returned, even if he were a Muslim. Then the believing women came as muhājirāt (emigrants). Umm Kulthūm bint ʿUqbah ibn Abī Muʿayṭ was among those who emigrated to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and she was a free woman. Her family came asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to return her to them, until Allah revealed what He revealed concerning the believing women. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ (4181) from Isḥāq from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm.]"
"13977","(13971) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us: Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated, who said: Maʿmar said: al-Zuhrī said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah and Marwān ibn al-Ḥakam, and he mentioned the story of al-Ḥudaybiyyah in its entirety. He said: Then believing women came, so Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \O you who believe"," when the believing women come to you as emigrants…\"" until His words: \""And hold not to the bonds of disbelievers [al-Mumtaḥanah:10].\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced on that day two wives he had from the period of shirk. One of them was married by Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān"," and the other by Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. Referred to previously.]"""
"13978","(13972) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Nasawī informed us: Ḥammād ibn Shākir narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā narrated to us: Hishām narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ʿAṭāʾ said, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both): Quraybah bint Abī Umayyah was married to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). He divorced her, and then Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān married her. And Umm al-Ḥakam bint Abī Sufyān was married to ʿIyāḍ ibn Ghanm al-Fihrī. He divorced her, and then ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān al-Thaqafī married her. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Ṣaḥīḥ (5287).]"
"13979","(13973) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam narrated to us: Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, concerning the words of Allah, the Most High: \And hold not to the bonds of disbelievers [al-Mumtaḥanah:10].\"" He said: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were commanded to divorce their wives who were disbelievers in Makkah"," who had remained with the disbelievers in Makkah.\n\n(Sh) Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Allah"," whose praise is exalted"," said: \""And do not marry the mushrikāt (polytheist women) until they believe. And a believing slave woman is better than a mushrikah [al-Baqarah:221].\"" It is said concerning this verse that it was revealed regarding the Arab polytheists"," who were the people of idols"," and so marriage with their women was prohibited"," just as their men are prohibited from marrying the believing women. If this is so"," then this verse remains established — there is nothing abrogated in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"13980","(13974) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam narrated to us: Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, concerning the words of Allah, the Most High: \And do not marry the mushrikāt until they believe [al-Baqarah:221].\"" He said: This refers to the mushrikāt women of the people of Makkah. Then the women of the People of the Book were made lawful for them. [Very weak.]"""
"13981","(13975) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, saying: Wakīʿ narrated from Sufyān, from Ḥammād, who said: I asked Saʿīd ibn Jubayr about the statement of the Most High: *\And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe\""* (Qurʾān 2:221). He said: \""The worshippers of idols.\"" The Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: Al-Suddī and Muqātil ibn Sulaymān mentioned the same meaning in tafsīr. Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: It has also been said that this verse was revealed concerning all the polytheists"," and then the concession was revealed thereafter specifically permitting the marriage of free women from among the People of the Book"," just as the concession came regarding the permissibility of the slaughtered animals of the People of the Book. Allah"," the Most High"," said: *\""Lawful to you are [all] good foods"," and [the food of] those who were given the Book is lawful to you and your food is lawful to them. And [lawful to you are] chaste women from among the believers and chaste women from among those who were given the Book before you"," when you have given them their due compensation\""* (Qurʾān 5:5). [Ḥasan]"""
"13982","(13976) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥa, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding the statement of the Most High: *\And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe\""* (Qurʾān 2:221). He said: Then He made an exception for the women of the People of the Book"," saying: *\""And [lawful to you are] chaste women from among those who were given the Book before you\""* (Qurʾān 5:5) — lawful for you — *\""when you have given them their due compensation","\""* meaning their dowers — *\""chaste"," not promiscuous\""* — he said: meaning virtuous"," not fornicators. [Ṣaḥīḥ in its chain"," though not from this source]"""
"13983","(13977) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Al-Qāḍī Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Kāmil narrated to us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Saʿd ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAṭiyya narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, saying: My paternal uncle narrated to me, saying: My father narrated from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding His statement: *\And do not marry polytheistic women until they believe\""* (Qurʾān 2:221). He said: It was abrogated"," and the women of the People of the Book from among the polytheists were made permissible. [Ṣaḥīḥ in its chain"," though not from this source. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"13984","(13978) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlānī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Wahb narrated to me, saying: Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, from Abū al-Zāhiriyya, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, who said: I performed Ḥajj and entered upon ʿĀʾisha, may Allah be pleased with her. She said to me: \O Jubayr"," do you recite al-Māʾida?\"" I said: \""Yes.\"" She said: \""Indeed"," it is the last Sūra to be revealed. Whatever you find in it to be permissible"," then deem it permissible"," and whatever you find in it to be forbidden"," then deem it forbidden.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"13985","(13979) Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, saying: It was read to Ibn Wahb: \Ḥuyayy ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Maʿāfirī informed you.\"" He said: I heard Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥubulī narrating from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr that the last Sūra to be revealed was Sūrat al-Māʾida. Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Whichever it was"," the marriage of free women from among the People of the Book has been permitted therein. And I would prefer that a Muslim not marry them.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"13986","(13980) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: Al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Majīd ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Abū al-Zubayr, that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdillāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, being asked about a Muslim marrying a Jewish or Christian woman. He said: \We married them at the time of the Conquest"," in Kūfa"," along with Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ"," and we could hardly find Muslim women in abundance. When we returned"," we divorced them.\"" And he said: \""They do not inherit from a Muslim"," nor does a Muslim inherit from them. And their women are lawful for us"," while our women are unlawful for them.\"" [Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm"," 4/8]"""
"13987","(13981) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Abū Muḥammad Bakr ibn Sahl ibn Ismāʿīl al-Qurashī al-Dimyāṭī narrated to us in Dimyāṭ, saying: Shuʿayb ibn Yaḥyā al-Tujībī narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd, from ʿUmar, the freedman of Ghufra, that ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Sāʾib from Banī al-Muṭṭalib narrated to him that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, married the daughter of al-Farāfiṣa al-Kalbiyya, and she was a Christian, while she was among his wives. Then she accepted Islam at his hands. [Ḥasan in its chain, though not from this source]"
"13988","(13982) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us, from ʿAmr, the freedman of al-Muṭṭalib, from Abū al-Ḥuwayrith, from Muḥammad ibn Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim, that ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, may Allah be pleased with him, married the daughter of al-Farāfiṣa while she was a Christian. He consummated the marriage contract with her while she was still a Christian, until she embraced Islam when she came to him. ʿAmr said: And he also narrated to me that Ṭalḥa ibn ʿUbaydillāh married a Christian woman from Kalb until she embraced Islam when she came to him. ʿAmr said: And ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, a shaykh from Banī al-Ashhal, narrated to me that Ḥudhayfa ibn al-Yamān married a Jewish woman. [Ḥasan in its chain, though not from this source]"
"13989","(13983) Abū Muḥammad al-Sukkārī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us, saying: Al-Ghilābī narrated to us, saying: Ghundar narrated from Shuʿba, from Abū Isḥāq, from Hubayra, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: \Ṭalḥa"," may Allah be pleased with him"," married a Jewish woman.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"13990","(13984) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī narrated to us, saying: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī narrated to us, saying: Sufyān ibn Muḥammad al-Jawharī narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated from Abū Isḥāq al-Hamdānī, from Hubayra ibn Yarīm, from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Ṭalḥa married a Jewish woman.\"" He said: And Sufyān narrated to us"," saying: Al-Ṣalt ibn Bahrām narrated to us"," saying: I heard Abū Wāʾil say: \""Ḥudhayfa"," may Allah be pleased with him"," married a Jewish woman"," so ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," wrote to him to separate from her.\"" He said: \""I fear that you will leave the Muslim women and marry the fornicators.\"" This from ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was by way of disapproval and deeming it reprehensible. In another narration"," Ḥudhayfa wrote to him: \""Is she forbidden?\"" He said: \""No"," but I fear that you will resort to marrying the fornicators among them.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"13991","(13985) And with this isnad, Sufyan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb say: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to him: \A Muslim man may marry a Christian woman"," but a Christian man may not marry a Muslim woman.\"" [Hasan]"""
"13992","(13986) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulaymad ibn Ahmad al-Lakhmi informed us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Hilali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, al-Nu'man ibn 'Abd al-Salam narrated to us, Sufyan narrated from Khalid al-Hadha' from 'Ikrimah from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," sent Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) with the truth to make it prevail over all religion. Our religion is the best of religions"," our community is above all communities"," and our men are above their women"," and their men are not above our women.\"" Abu al-Qasim said: \""None narrated this from Sufyan except al-Nu'man.\"" Al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""The People of the Book whose free women it is permissible to marry are the two well-known People of the Book — the Torah and the Gospel — and they are the Jews and the Christians from the Children of Israel"," not the Magians.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And this is the well-known athar from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): 'Treat them with the treatment of the People of Book.' The people of knowledge"," along with the corroborating narration of Bijalah"," applied this to the jizyah. Thus"," they are attached to them in the matter of the preservation of blood through the jizyah"," and not otherwise. And Allah knows best.\"" [Sahih]"""
"13993","(13987) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, Abu al-'Abbas al-Asam informed us, al-Rabi' informed us, al-Shafi'i informed us, 'Abd al-Majid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: 'Ata' said: \The Christians of the Arabs are not People of the Book. The People of the Book are the Children of Israel"," to whom the Torah and the Gospel came. As for those who entered among them from other peoples"," they are not from them.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""And we have narrated from 'Umar and 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the Christians of the Arabs with this meaning: that their slaughtered animals are not to be eaten. This will be mentioned in its proper place"," if Allah the Most High wills.\"" [Sahih]"""
"13994","(13988) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Isbahani informed us, Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Mukhtar narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Fayruz narrated from Ma'bad al-Juhani, who said: \I saw the wife of Hudhayfah and she was a Magian woman.\"" This is not established. What is preserved from Hudhayfah is that he married a Jewish woman. And Allah knows best. [Munkar]"""
"13995","(13989) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Ardistani informed us, Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Sufyan narrated, Burd ibn Sinan narrated from 'Ubadah ibn Nusayy from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, who said: A governor of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote: \There are people among us called the Samaritans who observe the Sabbath"," recite the Torah"," and do not believe in the Day of Resurrection. What does the Commander of the Faithful think regarding their slaughtered animals?\"" He wrote back: \""They are a sect of the People of the Book. Their slaughtered animals are the slaughtered animals of the People of the Book.\"" [Hasan. Previously cited under no. 139842]"""
"13996","(13990) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, 'Arim narrated from Mu'tamir from his father, who said: al-Hasan informed us that Ziyad was told that the Sabians pray toward the qiblah and pay the khums. He said: He intended to exempt them from the jizyah. Then it was reported afterward that they worship angels. [Da'if]"
"13997","(13991) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us, Abu al-Hasan al-Tara'ifi narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the words of the Most High: {\And whoever among you cannot afford to marry free believing women"," then from those whom your right hands possess of your believing slave-girls\""} — he said: \""Whoever does not have the means to marry free women should marry from the slave-girls of the Muslims. {'That is for him among you who fears sin'} — and it is fornication. It is not permissible for any free man to marry a slave-girl unless he cannot find a free woman and he fears sin. {'And if you abstain'} from marrying slave-girls"," {'it is better for you.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"13998","(13992) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Warqa' narrated from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid: {\And whoever among you cannot afford\""} — meaning"," whoever among you does not find wealth — he said: \""Whoever does not find the means to marry free believing women should marry a believing slave-girl. {'And if you abstain'} from marrying slave-girls"," {'it is better for you'\""} — and it is permissible. [Sahih]"""
"13999","(13993) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us, Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Abu Bishr narrated from Sa'id ibn Jubayr regarding this verse, he said: \Al-tawl (afford) means wealth. When one does not find the means to marry a free woman"," he should marry a slave-girl.\"" And regarding His words {\""And if you abstain"," it is better for you\""}"," he said: \""From marrying slave-girls.\"" And he said: \""Al-'anat (sin) means fornication.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by Ibn Mansur"," 732]"""
"14000","(13994) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us, Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us, al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us, al-Shafi'i informed us, 'Abd al-Majid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn 'Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: \Whoever finds the means to provide the dowry of a free woman should not marry a slave-girl.\"" [Sahih. Narrated by al-Shafi'i in al-Umm"," 31014]"""
"14001","(13995) Abū Saʿīd narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Ṭāwūs informed me from his father, who said: \It is not permissible for a free man to marry a slave woman when he can afford the dowry of a free woman.\"" I said: \""What if he fears committing zinā (fornication)?\"" He said: \""I do not know of it being permissible for him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī"," 4/30]"""
"14002","(13996) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who said: \ʿAṭāʾ asked Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ — while I was listening — about marriage to a slave woman: 'What do you say about it? Is it permissible?' He said: 'Marriage to slave women is not appropriate in this day and age.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm"," 4/301]"""
"14003","(13997) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr from Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ, who said: \Marriage to slave women is not appropriate in this day and age"," because one has the means (ṭawl) to marry a free woman.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm"," 4/301]"""
"14004","(13998) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAlī Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, Abū Bakr ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, Ḥabīb ibn Abī Ḥabīb narrated from ʿAmr ibn Harim, who said: \Jābir ibn Zayd was asked: 'Is it permissible for a free man to marry a slave woman when he can afford the dowry of a free woman?' He said: 'Only the one who cannot afford the dowry of a free woman and fears falling into hardship (ʿanat) may marry a slave woman.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14005","(13999) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Manṣūr narrated from al-Ḥasan, that he used to dislike marriage to slave women in his time, and he said: \Permission regarding them is only granted when one does not have the means (ṭawl) to marry a free woman.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"," 726]"""
"14006","(14000) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Rāzī narrated to us, Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Haytham narrated to us, Sharīk narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \A free man should not marry more than one slave woman.\"" ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb followed him in narrating from ʿAṭāʾ"," and Khuṣayf from Saʿīd from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with them both. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14007","(14001) Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Isfarāʾinī al-Rāzī narrated to us, Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Sinān narrated to us, Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us, my father narrated to me from ʿĀmir al-Aḥwal from al-Ḥasan, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a slave woman be married while a free man already has a free wife.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14008","(14002) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah narrated to me from one who heard al-Ḥasan say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a slave woman be married while a free man already has a free wife.\"" This is a mursal narration"," except that it carries the meaning of the Book (the Qurʾān)"," and it is supported by the statement of a group of the Companions"," may Allah be pleased with them. [Ḍaʿīf. Preceded earlier]"""
"14009","(14003) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Mihrān al-Sawwāq narrated to us, Abū Yaḥyā Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Ghālib narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Umawī narrated to us, Ḥajjāj narrated from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr from Zirr ibn Ḥubaysh from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \When a free woman is married while a slave woman is already present"," two days are allotted to the free woman and one day to the slave woman. Indeed"," it is not befitting for a slave woman to be married while a free woman is present.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14010","(14004) Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Zāhir ibn Aḥmad narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ḥajjāj narrated to us, Layth narrated to me, Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he said: \A slave woman should not be married while a free man has a free wife"," but a free woman may be married while a slave woman is present. And whoever can afford the dowry of a free woman should never marry a slave woman.\"" This chain of narration is ṣaḥīḥ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14011","(14005) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Mālik informed him, having received the report, that Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) were asked about a man who had a free woman under his marriage and wished to marry a slave woman alongside her; they both disapproved of his combining the two. [Weak]"
"14012","(14006) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Muʿādh ibn Muʿādh narrated to us from Ashʿath from al-Ḥasan regarding a man who married a free woman and a slave woman in a single contract: he said, separation shall be made between him and the slave woman. [Sound]\n\nAnd from al-Ḥasan that he said regarding a man who married two women in a single contract while he already had three wives: he said, separation shall be made between him and the two whom he married in the single contract. And if he married three women in a single contract while he had two wives, separation shall be made between him and the three. [Sound]"
"14013","(14007) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us that Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us, both saying: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Sufyān informed us. ʿAmr said: Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: The marriage of a free woman over a slave woman is the divorce of the slave woman.\n\nIt was also narrated by Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Sammān, and he is weak, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Jābir ibn Zayd from Ibn ʿAbbās who said: The marriage of a free woman over a slave woman is the divorce of the slave woman. Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us that Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Sammān informed us, and he mentioned it. [Sound]"
"14014","(14008) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us that Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us that Sufyān narrated to us from Ibn Abī Khālid from al-Shaʿbī from Masrūq who said: It is of the status of carrion, to which one is compelled. When Allah, the Most High, enriches you from need of it, then free yourself from it. [Sound]"
"14015","(14009) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us that Hushaym informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us from al-Shaʿbī from Masrūq who said: When one marries a free woman over a slave woman, it is the divorce of the slave woman. It is like the one who eats carrion: he eats of it only as compelled by necessity. When he is free from need of it, let him refrain. We only say this because of what has been narrated to us regarding that from ʿAlī and Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with them both). And in Allah lies success.\n\n[Narrated by Ibn Manṣūr, 7332]"
"14016","(14010) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd informed us that Hushaym informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us from al-Shaʿbī from Masrūq that he used to say regarding a slave who has a free woman: if he wishes, he may marry a slave woman over her. [Sound. Narrated by Ibn Manṣūr]"
"14017","(14011) And Jābir al-Juʿfī narrated from al-Shaʿbī from Masrūq from ʿAbdullāh: One should not marry a slave woman over a free woman, except the slave. Abū ʿAbdullāh narrated it by way of ijāzah from Abū al-Walīd, who said: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr informed us that ʿAbdullāh ibn Hāshim informed us that Wakīʿ narrated from Isrāʾīl from Jābir, and he mentioned it. [Sound]"
"14018","(14012) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us that Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍarawī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us that Sufyān narrated to us from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid who said: The marriage of the slave women of the People of the Book is not permissible, because Allah, the Most High, says: {\from among your believing slave women\""} [al-Nisāʾ: 25]. [Sound. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr"," 619]"""
"14019","(14013) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us that Abū Usāmah informed us that Ismāʿīl informed us from al-Ḥasan regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: {\And whoever among you cannot afford\""} up to His words: {\""from among your believing slave women\""} [al-Nisāʾ: 25]. He said: He has not granted us permission regarding the slave women of the People of the Book. [Sound]"""
"14020","(14014) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Baghdādī informed us that Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishr informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us that Ibn Abī Uways informed us that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād informed us from his father, from one of the jurists whom he met whose opinions were followed among them: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, Khārijah ibn Zayd, ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah, and Sulaymān ibn Yasār. He said: They used to say: It is not permissible for a Muslim to marry a Jewish or Christian slave woman. Allah has only permitted the chaste women of those who were given the Book, and a slave woman is not considered chaste (muḥṣanah). [Sound]"
"14021","(14015) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyān, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Fāṭimah bint Qays, that Abū ʿAmr ibn Ḥafṣ divorced her irrevocably (al-battah) while he was absent. His agent sent her some barley, but she was displeased with it. She said: \By Allah"," you have no obligation towards us.\"" She came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him. He said: \""You are not entitled to maintenance from him.\"" He then instructed her to observe her ʿiddah in the house of Umm Sharīk. Then he said: \""That woman is one whom my Companions frequently visit. Observe your ʿiddah at the house of Ibn Umm Maktūm"," for he is a blind man — you may remove your garments without concern. When your ʿiddah is completed"," inform me.\"" She said: \""When my ʿiddah was completed"," I informed him that Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān and Abū Jahm had proposed to me.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""As for Abū Jahm"," he never lays his staff down from his shoulder [i.e."," he is severe in beating]"," and as for Muʿāwiyah"," he is a destitute man with no wealth. Marry Usāmah ibn Zayd.\"" She said: \""I disliked him.\"" Then he said: \""Marry Usāmah.\"" So I married him"," and Allah placed goodness in him"," and I became envied on account of him. Muslim narrated this in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1480]"""
"14022","(14016) Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated it from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Fāṭimah, that the Prophet (ﷺ) sent word to her: \Do not precede me concerning yourself [i.e."," do not finalize a marriage without informing me first].\"" And Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated it from Abū Salamah"," and he said: \""And do not cause us to miss you [by finalizing a marriage without informing us].\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Shaybān narrated from Yaḥyā — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ribḥ narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr informed us — both of them from Abū Salamah"," from Fāṭimah"," and he mentioned the hadith including both wordings. [Ṣaḥīḥ — previously cited]"""
"14023","(14017) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Abū al-Walīd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ḥanẓalah al-Ghasīl narrated to us. He said: My maternal aunt Sukaynah bint Ḥanẓalah narrated to me, and she was in Qubāʾ married to a paternal cousin of hers who had passed away, leaving her a widow. She said: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī came to me while I was in my ʿiddah. He greeted me and then said: \How have you fared this morning"," O daughter of Ḥanẓalah?\"" I said: \""Well"," may Allah keep you well.\"" He said: \""I am one whose closeness to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and my kinship with ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālliib (may Allah be pleased with him)"," my right in Islam"," and my nobility among the Arabs are well known.\"" She said: I replied: \""May Allah forgive you"," O Abū Jaʿfar! You are a man from whom knowledge is taken and narrations are transmitted. Are you proposing to me during my ʿiddah?\"" He said: \""I have not done that. I have only informed you of my standing with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" Then he said: \""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to Umm Salamah bint Abī Umayyah ibn al-Mughīrah al-Makhzūmīyah"," who had been widowed by Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Asad"," who was her paternal uncle's son. He kept reminding her of her status before Allah the Most High"," until the marks of the mat were imprinted on his palm from the intensity of his pressing upon it. That was not a marriage proposal.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14024","(14018) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated from Shuʿbah, from Manṣūr, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the words of Allah the Most High: {There is no blame upon you for that to which you allude concerning a proposal to women} [al-Baqarah 235]. He said: \Alluding (al-taʿrīḍ) is that which is not a direct proposal.\"" Others added: \""Alluding is that which is not explicitly intended as a marriage proposal.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14025","(14019) Abū ʿUmar al-Razjāhī informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me; al-Faḍl ibn al-Ḥubāb narrated to us; Ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Manṣūr, from Mujāhid, from Ibn ʿAbbās, regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: {There is no blame upon you for that to which you allude concerning a proposal to women} — \I intend to marry"," I intend to marry.\"" And al-Bukhārī said: Ṭalq said to me: Zāʾidah narrated to us from Manṣūr"," from Mujāhid"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," regarding {that to which you allude} — he says: \""I intend marriage"," and I wish that a righteous woman might become available to me.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq from Manṣūr]"""
"14026","(14020) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim, from his father, that he used to say regarding the words of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: {There is no blame upon you for that to which you allude concerning a proposal to women} — that a man may say to a woman during her ʿiddah following the death of her husband: \You are dear to me"," and I am indeed desirous of you"," and Allah will bestow upon you goodness and provision","\"" and similar such words. [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated by Mālik 1113]"""
"14027","(14021) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Muslim al-Baṭīn, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, regarding the words of Allah the Most High: {There is no blame upon you for that to which you allude concerning a proposal to women}. He said: \It is the man saying to a woman during her ʿiddah: 'I intend to marry"," and if I marry"," I will treat my wife well.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14028","(14022) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Ādam narrated to us; Warqāʾ narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding this verse. He said: \It is the man saying to a woman during her ʿiddah: 'You are indeed beautiful"," and you are indeed pleasing to me","' while concealing his proposal and not making it explicit to her. All of this is permissible and proper. {But do not make a secret promise to them} — meaning"," he says to her: 'Do not precede me by marrying yourself [to someone else]"," for I will marry you.' This is not permissible.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14029","(14023) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, regarding the words of Allah the Most High: {But do not make a secret promise to them}. He said: \He should not propose to her during her ʿiddah. {Unless you speak a proper word} — he says: 'You are indeed beautiful"," and you are indeed of a [noble] standing"," and you are indeed one in whom interest is taken.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr 382]"""
"14030","(14024) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd informed us, both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr. He said: \He makes a pact with her upon such and such [condition] that she will not marry anyone else. {Unless you speak a proper word} — he says: 'I am indeed desirous of you"," and I hope that we may be united.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14031","(14025) Abū ʿAbdullāh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated from Manṣūr, who said: He narrated from al-Shaʿbī regarding this verse: {But do not make a secret promise to them} — he said: He should not take a covenant from her that she will not marry anyone else. [Weak]"
"14032","(14026) He said: And Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: ʿUmar ibn Ḥabīb al-Qāḍī narrated from ʿImrān ibn Ḥudayr from Abī Mijlaz regarding {But do not make a secret promise to them} — he said: It refers to zinā (unlawful sexual intercourse). He said: Then I asked al-Ḥasan about it as well, and he said: It is zinā. [Weak]"
"14033","(14027) He said: And Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated from Sufyān from al-Suddī from Ibrāhīm regarding {But do not make a secret promise to them} — he said: It refers to zinā. [Sound]"
"14034","(14028) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī and Abū Muḥammad al-Kaʿbī informed us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, saying: Yazīd ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Bukayr ibn Maʿrūf from Muqātil ibn Ḥayyān, who said: It has reached us — and Allah knows best — that what is meant by {But do not make a secret promise to them} is obscene speech, i.e., that a man should not address her with allusions to sexual intercourse from himself. Others say it refers to zinā, and Allah knows best. And it has been narrated to us from al-Ḥasan that he said regarding al-taʿrīḍ (allusive speech): He sends to her during her ʿiddah and says, \Indeed"," I am desirous of you"," and indeed"," I am eager for you. I wished to inform you"," so when your ʿiddah is completed"," you may exercise your own judgment.\"" And from ʿAṭāʾ"," who said: He may allude but not state explicitly. He says"," \""I have a need; so rejoice"," for by Allah"," you are a woman of means.\"" And she says"," \""I have heard what you have said.\"" And from ʿAṭāʾ"," who said: If she made a promise to a man during her ʿiddah and then he married her thereafter"," they would not be separated. [Good]"""
"14035","(14029) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī, who informed me: Ibn al-Musayyab narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \None of you should propose marriage over the proposal of his brother.\"" [Sound. Muslim 1076"," 1413"," 1515]"""
"14036","(14030) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed me, saying: Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who said: Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) the same. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim recorded it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān ibn ʿUaynah, and Muslim narrated it from Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb. [Sound. Preceded above]"
"14037","(14031) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī informed us, saying: Mālik narrated — (ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, saying: Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \None of you should propose marriage over the proposal of his brother"," nor should he sell over the sale of his brother.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And some of the muḥaddithūn added: \""Until he gives permission or abandons it.\"" [Sound]"""
"14038","(14032) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī in Marw informed us, saying: ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us, saying: Makkī narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Nāfiʿ narrating that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade that any of you should sell over the sale of another, and that a man should propose marriage over the proposal of his brother until the suitor before him abandons it or gives him permission. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm. [Sound. Bukhārī 2139]"
"14039","(14033) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Umawī informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān al-ʿĀmirī informed us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated — (ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, saying: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \None of you should sell over the sale of his brother"," nor should he propose marriage over the proposal of his brother"," except with his permission.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd. And in the narration of Yaḥyā: \""Except that he gives him permission.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb and others from Yaḥyā. [Sound. Preceded]"""
"14040","(14034) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, saying: Abū Bakr Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us, saying: Ṣakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them) who said: The Prophet (ﷺ) forbade that a man should propose marriage over the proposal of his brother until the latter rejects it or gives him permission. [Sound. Preceded above]"
"14041","(14035) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Ibn Milḥān narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, Jaʿfar — meaning Ibn Rabīʿah — narrated to me from al-Aʿraj, who said: Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him: \Beware of suspicion"," for suspicion is the most false of speech. Do not spy upon one another"," do not search for one another's faults"," do not bear hatred toward one another"," and do not turn your backs on one another. O servants of Allah"," be brothers. Let no man propose marriage over the proposal of his brother until he marries or withdraws. Do not combine a woman and her paternal aunt in marriage"," nor a woman and her maternal aunt. Let no woman fast [a voluntary fast] while her husband is present except with his permission"," and let no woman admit anyone into his house while he is present except with his permission. Whatever she gives in charity from what he earns"," he shall have half the reward thereof. And let no woman ask for the divorce of her sister [in faith] so as to empty the vessel of her companion and marry [the husband]"," for she shall only have what has been decreed for her.\"" al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr up to his words: \""until he marries or withdraws.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2563]"""
"14042","(14036) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan the Qāḍī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed us, a man and al-Layth ibn Saʿd informed me from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Shumāsah al-Mahriyy, who heard ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir upon the minbar saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The believer is the brother of the believer. It is not permissible for a believer to transact a sale over the sale of his brother until he withdraws"," nor to propose marriage over his proposal until he withdraws.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1414]"""
"14043","(14037) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me, Bakr ibn Muḍar narrated to me, from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, from Bukayr, that Nāfiʿ narrated to him that Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, intended to propose marriage to the daughter of Abū Jahl, while a man had already proposed to her. The man came and said: \Do you propose to the daughter of Abū Jahl?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I have left her.\"" He said: \""You have left her"," and you have no need of her?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""I wish to propose to her.\"" He said: \""Then propose to her"," it is permissible.\"" So he proposed to her"," then it occurred to him [to withdraw] and he left her. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14044","(14038) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd, the mawlā of al-Aswad ibn Sufyān, from Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Fāṭimah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to her during her waiting period from the divorce of her husband: \When you become lawful [i.e."," when your waiting period ends]"," inform me.\"" She said: \""When I became lawful"," I informed him that Muʿāwiyah and Abū Jahl"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," had proposed to me.\"" The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: \""As for Muʿāwiyah"," he is a destitute man who has no wealth. As for Abū Jahl"," he does not lay his staff from his shoulder [i.e."," he beats women severely]. Marry Usāmah.\"" She said: \""I disliked him.\"" He said: \""Marry Usāmah.\"" So I married him"," and Allah placed goodness in him"," and I was filled with joy and contentment on his account.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14045","(14039) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Shuʿbah informed me, Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm narrated to me, saying: I and Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf entered upon Fāṭimah bint Qays during the reign of the family of al-Zubayr, and we asked her about the thrice-divorced woman: does she have a right to maintenance? She mentioned the hadith regarding the story of her divorce, until she said: \When my waiting period ended"," Abū al-Jahm"," a man from Quraysh"," and Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān proposed to me. I came to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'As for Abū Jahl"," he is a man who is harsh with women"," and as for Muʿāwiyah"," he is a man who has no wealth.'\"" She said: \""Then he proposed to me — meaning Usāmah ibn Zayd — so I married him"," and Allah blessed me through Usāmah.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Shuʿbah. (b) And al-Thawrī narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī al-Jahm"," who said in it: \""As for Muʿāwiyah"," he is a man of dust [i.e."," destitute] who has no wealth"," and as for Abū Jahl"," he is a man who beats women severely"," but [marry] Usāmah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated before it]"""
"14046","(14040) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Mālik ibn Mighwal said: I heard Abū Bakr ibn Ḥafṣ say: When Ibn ʿUmar was invited to a marriage, he would say: \Do not crowd us with people. All praise is due to Allah"," and blessings and peace be upon Muḥammad. So-and-so has proposed to you for so-and-so. If you marry him to her"," then all praise is due to Allah"," and if you refuse him"," then glory be to Allah.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14047","(14041) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, al-Thiqah — al-Rabīʿ said: I think he meant Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm — informed us from Maʿmar. (H) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar and Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah said: Maʿmar narrated to us from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, who said: Ghaylān ibn Salamah embraced Islam while he had ten wives. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded him to choose four of them and leave the rest. The wording is that of the hadith of Isḥāq. In the narration of al-Shāfiʿī: \Ghaylān ibn Salamah al-Thaqafī embraced Islam and he had ten wives. The Prophet"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said to him: 'Retain four and separate from the rest.'\"" [Munkar. Previously narrated as no. 13845]"""
"14048","(14042) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ, Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan the Qāḍī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr al-Sahmī narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated to us from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from his father, who narrated to him that a man called Ghaylān ibn Salamah al-Thaqafī had ten wives in the Jāhiliyyah. He embraced Islam and they embraced Islam with him. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded him to choose four of them. And likewise Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ narrated it from Maʿmar. These four — Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm Ibn ʿUlayyah, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar Ghundar, and Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ — are among the ḥuffāẓ of the people of Baṣrah, and they narrated it thus as a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Munkar. Previously narrated before it]"
"14049","(14043) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī said: Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr the Qāḍī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, Abū ʿUbayd informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us from Sufyān, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, that Ghaylān ibn Salamah al-Thaqafī embraced Islam and he had ten wives. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded him to choose four of them. And likewise it was narrated from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muḥammad al-Muḥāribī and ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus from Maʿmar. These three are from Kūfah, and Faḍl ibn Mūsā al-Sīnānī — who is from Khurāsān — also narrated it from Maʿmar thus as a connected (mawṣūl) chain. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14050","(14044) ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated it from Maʿmar and sent it as a mursal [hadith]. Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me, ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar informed us from al-Zuhrī: \Ghaylān ibn Salamah embraced Islam and he had ten wives. The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," commanded him to choose four of them.\"" And likewise Mālik ibn Anas narrated it from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously narrated before it]"""
"14051","(14045) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr — Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq — informed us, they said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Malik informed us, from Ibn Shihab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to a man from Thaqif who had embraced Islam and had ten wives in his marriage: \Retain four and separate from the rest.\"" And similarly"," Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated it from al-Zuhri. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14052","(14046) Yunus ibn Yazid narrated from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Abi Suwayd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to Ghaylan ibn Salamah when he embraced Islam and had ten wives under his care: \Choose four of them and separate from the rest.\"" Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzaz narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated to us: Yunus informed us"," from al-Zuhri"," from Muhammad ibn Abi Suwayd"," and he mentioned it. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14053","(14047) 'Uqayl ibn Khalid narrated from Ibn Shihab, who said: It reached us from 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Suwayd, who said: It reached us that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to Ghaylan ibn Salamah when he embraced Islam and had ten wives under his care: \Choose four of them and divorce the rest.\"" Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Hasan — Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus — informed us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us: 'Abdillah ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Layth informed us"," from 'Uqayl"," and he mentioned it. And similarly"," Ibn Wahb and others narrated it from Yunus"," from al-Zuhri"," from 'Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Suwayd. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14054","(14048) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: I heard Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj saying: \The people of Yemen are more knowledgeable regarding the hadith of Ma'mar than others"," for he narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri"," from Salim"," from his father"," in Basra"," and the Basrans alone transmitted it from him. Thus"," if a trustworthy narrator other than the people of Basra narrates it"," the hadith becomes established; otherwise"," irsal (disconnected transmission) is preferable.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""We have narrated it from other than the people of Basra from Ma'mar"," fully connected"," and Allah"," the Most High"," knows best. And it has been narrated from another route from Nafi' and Salim"," from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both).\"""""
"14055","(14049) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith — both said: Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i in Egypt narrated to us: Abu Burayd 'Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi —\n\nAnd Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil said: 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Najiyah narrated to us: Abu Burayd 'Amr ibn Yazid narrated to us: Sayf ibn 'Ubaydillah al-Jarmi narrated to us: Sarar — Abu 'Ubaydah al-'Anazi — narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi' and Salim, from Ibn 'Umar, that Ghaylan ibn Salamah al-Thaqafi embraced Islam and had nine wives, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded him to choose four of them. This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Najiyah. And in the narration of al-Nasa'i, Sarar ibn Mujashshir said: \Ghaylan ibn Salamah had ten wives"," then he embraced Islam and they embraced Islam with him.\"" Ibn Najiyah added in his narration: \""Then in the time of 'Umar"," he divorced his wives and divided his wealth"," so 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: 'You shall return to your wealth and your wives"," or I shall stone your grave as the grave of Abu Righal was stoned.'\"" Abu 'Ali (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Sarar ibn Mujashshir"," a trustworthy Basran"," is alone in narrating this.\"" [Munkar (Denounced); previously referenced]"""
"14056","(14050) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran in Baghdad informed us: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Khalil narrated to us: al-Waqidi narrated to us: 'Abdillah ibn Ja'far al-Zuhri narrated to us, from 'Abdillah ibn Abi Sufyan, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \Ghaylan ibn Salamah embraced Islam and had ten wives"," so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded him to retain four and separate from the rest.\"" He said: \""And Safwan ibn Umayyah embraced Islam and had eight wives"," so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) commanded him to retain four and separate from the rest.\"" [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14057","(14051) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Ibn Abi Layla — Hushaym said: and al-Kalbi informed me, from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardal, from al-Harith ibn Qays, that he embraced Islam and had eight wives. Ibn Abi Layla said: \So the Prophet (peace be upon him) commanded him to choose four of them.\"" And al-Kalbi said: al-Harith said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have embraced Islam and I have eight wives; they have embraced Islam with me and migrated with me.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""Choose four of them.\"" He said: \""So I would say to the one I wished to retain: 'Come forward (aqbili)","' and to the one I wished to separate from: 'Turn away (adburi).' She would say: 'I adjure you by kinship (al-rahim)"," I adjure you by children (al-walad).'\"" Al-Kalbi said: And Abu Salih narrated to us from al-Harith ibn Qays the same. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14058","(14052) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah informed us: Hushaym informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardal, from al-Harith ibn Qays al-Asadi, who said: \I embraced Islam and had eight wives"," so I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: 'Choose four of them.'\"" Abu Dawud said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us with this hadith"," and he said \""Qays ibn al-Harith\"" in place of \""al-Harith ibn Qays.\"" Ahmad ibn Ibrahim said: \""This is correct"," meaning Qays ibn al-Harith.\"" Abu Dawud said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman"," the judge of Kufah"," narrated to us"," from 'Isa ibn al-Mukhtar"," from Ibn Abi Layla"," from Humaydah ibn al-Shamardal"," from Qays ibn al-Harith"," with the same meaning. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14059","(14053) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Khumayruwayh narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Mughirah informed us, from some of the children of al-Harith ibn Qays ibn 'Umayrah al-Asadi, that al-Harith embraced Islam and had eight wives, so he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace be upon him), and he said to him: \Choose four of them.\"" And Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated it from Hushaym"," from Mughirah"," from al-Rabi' ibn Qays"," that his grandfather al-Harith ibn Qays embraced Islam. And Musa ibn Isma'il narrated it from Abu 'Awanah"," from Mughirah"," from Qays ibn 'Abdillah ibn al-Harith"," who said: \""My grandfather embraced Islam.\"" This corroborates the narration of the majority from Hushaym where they said \""al-Harith ibn Qays","\"" and it corroborates the narration of Ibn Abi Layla"," and Allah knows best. [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14060","(14054) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdhan informed us: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Qays ibn al-Rabi', who said: \My grandfather embraced Islam and had eight wives"," so he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and he said: 'Choose four of them"," whichever of them you wish.'\"" [Da'if (Weak)]"""
"14061","(14055) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us: 'Ali ibn Salm al-Isbahani narrated to us: al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Isbahani narrated to us: Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us: Warqa' narrated from Sulayman al-Shaybani from Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydillah al-Thaqafi from 'Urwah ibn Mas'ud, who said: \I embraced Islam while I had ten women under my marriage bond"," four of whom were from Quraysh"," one of them being the daughter of Abu Sufyan. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'Choose four of them and release the rest.' So I chose four of them"," among whom was the daughter of Abu Sufyan.\"" [Sahih]"""
"14062","(14056) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: Abu al-Shaykh al-Isbahani narrated to us: Hajjaj ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Muhallab narrated to us: Adam narrated it with the same wording."
"14063","(14057) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan both narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: one of our companions narrated from Ibn Abi al-Zinad from 'Abd al-Majid ibn Suhayl ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf from 'Awf ibn al-Harith from Nawfal ibn Mu'awiyah, who said: \I embraced Islam while I had five women under my marriage bond"," so I asked the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he said: 'Separate from one of them and retain four.' So I turned to the eldest among them"," who had been barren for sixty years"," and I separated from her.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14064","(14058) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih narrated to us: Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Hayyan al-Isbahani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Mukram al-Birti narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Madini narrated — Ibn Hayyan said: and al-Sufi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us.\n\n(And) 'Abdhan narrated to us: Bundar and Khalifah narrated, all saying: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us: My father narrated to us, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Ayyub from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu Wahb al-Jayshani from al-Dahhak ibn Fayruz ibn al-Daylami from his father, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have embraced Islam and I have two sisters under my marriage bond.' He said: 'Divorce whichever of them you wish.'\""\n\nAbu 'Isa al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar from Wahb ibn Jarir"," and he said in the hadith: \""Choose whichever of them you wish.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14065","(14059) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Luha'ah narrated from Abu Wahb al-Jayshani from al-Dahhak ibn Fayruz al-Daylami, that his father embraced Islam while he had two sisters under his marriage bond, and the Prophet (ﷺ) commanded him to choose one of them. [Hasan]"
"14066","(14060) Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq both narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: Ibn Abi Yahya narrated from Ishaq ibn 'Abdillah from Abu Wahb al-Jayshani from Abu Khirash from al-Daylami or from Ibn al-Daylami, who said: \I embraced Islam while I had two sisters under my marriage bond"," so I asked the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he commanded me to retain whichever of them I wished and to separate from the other.\""\n\nIshaq ibn 'Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah added in his isnad: Abu Khirash. And Ishaq is not used as a basis for argument"," and the narration of Yazid ibn Abi Habib is more authentic"," and Allah knows best. [Hasan; it was narrated before this with a different isnad]"""
"14067","(14061) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us by dictation: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated from Ibn Ishaq, in the story of Abu al-'As ibn al-Rabi's departure while still upon his state of polytheism, behind Zaynab bint Rasulillah (ﷺ) to Madinah. He said: Yazid ibn Roman narrated to me from 'Urwah from 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \Zaynab called out: 'O people"," I have granted protection to Abu al-'As ibn al-Rabi!'\"" — and he mentioned the hadith until she said: \""Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned away and entered upon his daughter Zaynab and said: 'O my daughter"," honor his dwelling"," and let him not have access to you"," for you are not lawful for him.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"14068","(14062) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us: al-Rabi' narrated to us: al-Shafi'i narrated to us: a group of the people of knowledge from Quraysh and the people of military expeditions and others narrated from a number before them, that Abu Sufyan ibn Harb embraced Islam at Marr while the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had gained ascendancy over it. He was in a land of Islam, and his family's Islam rendered it a land of Islam, while his wife Hind bint 'Utbah was a disbeliever in Makkah, and Makkah at that time was a land of war. Then he came to her and called her to Islam, but she grabbed his beard and said: 'Kill this misguided old man!' She remained for several days before she embraced Islam. Then she embraced Islam and gave bay'ah to the Prophet (ﷺ), and so they remained upon their marriage.\n\nAnd it was reported to us that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Makkah and most of its people embraced Islam, and it became a land of Islam. The wife of 'Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl and the wife of Safwan ibn Umayyah embraced Islam, while their husbands fled in the direction of Yemen by the Yemeni route as disbelievers to a land of disbelief. Then they came after a period and embraced Islam. Safwan witnessed Hunayn as a disbeliever. He entered the land of Islam after having fled from it, and he had left it as a disbeliever, and so they remained upon their marriage. All of this occurred while their wives had been consummated in marriage and their 'iddahs had not yet expired. [Sahih]"
"14069","(14063) Abu Ahmad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Mihrajani narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakka narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah narrated to us: Abu 'Amr ibn Najid narrated to us. Both said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-BushanjI narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Malik narrated from Ibn Shihab, that it reached him that there were women in the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who embraced Islam in their own lands without being emigrants, and their husbands were disbelievers at the time they embraced Islam. Among them was the daughter of al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, who was married to Safwan ibn Umayyah. She embraced Islam on the day of the Conquest, and her husband Safwan ibn Umayyah fled from Islam. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent his cousin Wahb ibn 'Umayer with the cloak of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) as a token of safe conduct for Safwan, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called him to Islam and to come to him. If he was pleased with a matter, he would accept it; otherwise, he would grant him respite for two months. When Safwan came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with his cloak, he called out to him — and he mentioned the hadith regarding his being sent away and his return. He said: Safwan went out with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was a disbeliever, and he witnessed Hunayn and Ta'if as a disbeliever, while his wife was a Muslim. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not separate between him and his wife until Safwan embraced Islam, and his wife remained with him by that marriage. Ibn Shihab said: \The time between Safwan's Islam and his wife's Islam was approximately one month.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14070","(14064) With this same isnad, from Ibn Shihab: that Umm Hakim bint al-Harith ibn Hisham, who was married to 'Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, embraced Islam on the day of the Conquest in Makkah, and her husband 'Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl fled from Islam until he reached Yemen. Umm Hakim set out until she came to him in Yemen and called him to Islam, so he embraced Islam. He came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the year of the Conquest, and when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw him, he leapt toward him in joy, and he had no cloak upon him, until he gave him his bay'ah. Thus they remained upon their marriage. [Da'if]"
"14071","(14065) Through this chain, it is related by Ibn Shihab who said: I have not heard of any woman who emigrated to Allah and His Messenger while her husband remained a disbeliever residing in the abode of disbelief, except that her emigration would be severed between her and her husband—unless her husband emigrated before the completion of her waiting period. Nor have we heard of any woman whose marriage was dissolved between her and her husband when he arrived while she was in her waiting period."
"14072","(14066) It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hafiz, who reported to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Nasawi reported to me: Hammād ibn Sharik reported to us: Muhammad ibn Isma‘il reported to me: Ibrāhīm ibn Mūsā reported to us: Hishām reported to us from Ibn Jurayj, who said: ‘Aṭā’ reported to us from Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The polytheists were of two categories in relation to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and the believers: those of the people of war, who fought against them and they fought against him; and those of the people of covenant, whom they neither fought nor were fought by them. So when a woman from the people of war emigrated, she was not married until she menstruated and purified herself; then, once purified, marriage was permitted to her. If her husband emigrated before she married, she was returned to him. This is related by al-Bukhārī in his Sahīh in this manner. And this indicates that the *dār* (the marital home) did not sever the relationship between them."
"14073","(14067) It was reported to us by Abu Sa‘l: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Mihrānī al-Muzakki reported to us: Ahmad ibn Salmān al-Baghdādī reported to us: al-Hasan ibn Mukram al-Bazzāz reported to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn reported to us: Muhammad ibn Ishāq reported to us from Dāwūd ibn al-Husayn, from ‘Ikrima, from Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) returned his daughter ‘Ā’isha to Abū al-‘Āṣ after two years, following their first marriage. This is related by Abū Dāwūd from al-Hasan ibn ‘Alī from Yazīd."
"14074","(14068) It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qāḍī, and Abu Sa‘īd ibn Abī ‘Amr, and Abu Naṣr: Manṣūr ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Mufassir, said: We were told by Abū al-‘Abbās: Muhammad ibn Ya‘qūb said: He was told by Abū Zur‘a al-Dimashqī, who reported to us: Ahmad ibn Khālid reported to us: Muhammad ibn Ishāq reported to us from Dāwūd ibn al-Husayn, and also: Muhammad ibn Ya‘qūb reported to us: Ahmad ibn al-Jabbār reported to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr reported to us from Ibn Ishāq, who said: Then Dāwūd ibn al-Husayn reported to me from ‘Ikrima, from Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) returned Zaynab, his daughter, to Abū al-‘Āṣ ibn al-Rabī‘ after six years, regarding their first marriage. The wording of the report of Ahmad ibn Khālid is as above, and in the version of Yūnus, nothing further is mentioned after six years. Abū Dāwūd also related it from the report of Salama ibn al-Faḍl and others from Ibn Ishāq. This is because she accepted Islam and emigrated to al-Madīnah, while Abū al-‘Āṣ refrained from accepting Islam; thus, their marriage was not contingent upon the completion of her waiting period until the verse prohibiting Muslim women from marrying polytheists was revealed after the Treaty of al-Hudaybiyyah, and after its revelation, their marriage became contingent upon the completion of her waiting period. She did not delay much beyond that until Abū Baṣīr and others took Abū al-‘Āṣ captive and sent him to al-Madīnah, after which Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her) ransomed him. Then he returned to Makkah, returned what he had of trusts, and declared his Islam. Thus, there was no delay between the contingency of their marriage upon the completion of her waiting period and her acceptance of Islam except a short while."
"14075","(14069) It was reported to us by Abu Bakr: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hārith al-Asbahānī al-Faqīh reported to us: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyān reported to us: Abu Ya‘la al-Mawṣilī reported to us: Abu Khaythama reported to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn reported to us: al-Hajjāj reported to us from ‘Amr ibn Shu‘ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Prophet (peace be upon him) returned his daughter to Abū al-‘Āṣ with a new *mahr* and a new marriage."
"14076","(14070) Abu Bakr ibn al-Hārith said: Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutnī, the Hafiz, said: This is not established, and al-Hajjāj does not cite it. The correct report is that of Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with him). It reached me from Abū ‘Īsā al-Tirmidhī, who said: I asked al-Bukhārī (may Allah have mercy on him) about it, and he said: The report of Ibn ‘Abbās is more authentic in this matter than the report of ‘Amr ibn Shu‘ayb. And Abū ‘Ubayd reported from Yahyā ibn Sa‘īd al-Qaṭṭān that al-Hajjāj had not heard it from ‘Amr, and that it is from the report of Muhammad ibn ‘Ubayd Allah al-‘Arzamī from ‘Amr. This is a weak position, and no one would accept it without knowing what the report actually is."
"14077","(14071) It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hafiz, who reported to us: Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbūbī from Merv reported to us: Sa‘īd ibn Mas‘ūd reported to us: ‘Ubayd Allah ibn Mūsā reported to us: Isrā’īl reported to us from Simāk, from ‘Ikrima, from Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A woman accepted Islam during the lifetime of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and married. Then her husband came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: Indeed, I have accepted Islam with her, and she knows that I have accepted Islam with her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) removed her from her second husband and returned her to her first husband."
"14078","(14072) The Sheikh, the Imam, Abu al-Tayyib: Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Sulaymān (may Allah have mercy on him) reported to us: Muhammad ibn ‘Abdillah ibn ‘Alī al-Daqāq reported to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Sa‘īd al-‘Abdī reported to us: Abu Ja‘far al-Nufaylī reported to us: Makhlad ibn Yazīd reported to us: Isrā’īl, and he mentioned it in a similar manner."
"14079","(14073) It was reported to us by Abu Bakr ibn Furāk, who reported to us: ‘Abdillah ibn Ja‘far reported to us: Yūnus ibn Habīb reported to us: Abu Dāwūd reported to us: Sulaymān ibn Mu‘ādh al-Dabbī reported to us from Simāk, from ‘Ikrima, from Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ‘Ammāh, the aunt of ‘Abdillah ibn al-Hārith, accepted Islam, emigrated, and married, while her husband had already accepted Islam before her. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) returned her to her first husband."
"14080","(14074) It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hafiz, who reported to us: Abu Naḍr al-Faqīh reported to us: Sa‘līḥ ibn Muhammad al-Baghdādī reported to us: ‘Alī ibn al-Ja‘d reported to us: Shu‘bah reported to us from al-Hakam, who said: Hāni‘ ibn Qabīṣah came to al-Madīnah and lodged with Ibn ‘Awf, beneath whom were four Christian women. He accepted Islam, and ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) confirmed their marriage along with him. Shu‘bah said: I asked some of the Banū Shaybān about it, and they said: There has been disagreement among us concerning it."
"14081","(14075) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us; ʿAnbasah ibn Khālid narrated to me; Yūnus ibn Yazīd narrated to me; he said: Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihāb said: ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him: Marriage in the Jāhiliyyah was of four types. One of them was the type of marriage practiced by people today: a man would propose to another man for the hand of his ward, then pay her dower and marry her. And he mentioned the hadith as it has passed. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ. And al-Shāfiʿī, may Allah have mercy on him, used as evidence that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned two Jews who had committed zinā, thereby treating their marriage as constituting iḥṣān (lawful conjugal status). So how can it be lost on us that it does not make her lawful when it does constitute iḥṣān? [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5127]"
"14082","(14076) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Raffāʾ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Nuʿaym narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; al-Madanī narrated to me, from Abī al-Ḥuwayrith, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Nothing from the fornication of the people of the Jāhiliyyah begot me; I was only begotten through marriage"," like the marriage of Islam.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"14083","(14077) The Sharīf Abū al-Fatḥ al-ʿUmarī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Firās informed us; Abū Jaʿfar al-Baṣrī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, regarding the words of the Most High: \There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves; it grieves him that you should suffer; he is deeply concerned for you\"" (al-Tawbah"," 9:128). He said: Nothing from the birth of the Jāhiliyyah touched him. And the Prophet ﷺ said: \""I came forth from marriage"," not from fornication.\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"14084","(14078) The Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: They (his parents) were polytheists, as evidenced by what Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, and the wording is his; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿAffān narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thābit, from Anas: A man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," where is my father?\"" He said: \""In the Fire.\"" When the man turned to leave"," he called him and said: \""Indeed my father and your father are in the Fire.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 203]"""
"14085","(14079) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Sayyārī informed us; Abū al-Muwajjah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh informed me; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, from Yazīd ibn Kaysān, from Abī Ḥāzim, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I sought permission from my Lord to seek forgiveness for my mother"," but He did not grant me permission. And I sought His permission to visit her grave"," and He granted me permission.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbbād. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 976]"""
"14086","(14080) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ: that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, sent a message to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, asking: \May a man have sexual contact with his wife while she is menstruating?\"" She said: \""Let her tie her lower garment tightly around her lower part"," then he may have contact with her if he wishes.\"" This is mawqūf. It has also been narrated as mursal and as mawṣūl from the Prophet ﷺ. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14087","(14081) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us; they said: Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam: that a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \What is lawful for me from my wife when she is menstruating?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Let her tie her lower garment tightly upon herself"," then do as you wish with her upper part.\"" This is mursal. [Ṣaḥīḥ li-ghayrih]"""
"14088","(14082) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us, from Abī al-Naḍr, from Abī Salamah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her: that the Prophet ﷺ was asked what is lawful for a man from a woman—meaning a menstruating woman. He said: \That which is above the lower garment.\"" This is mawṣūl. And we have narrated in the Book of Purification two other chains which corroborate this narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14089","(14083) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Iyādī al-Mālikī in Baghdad informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf ibn Khallād al-Naṣībī narrated to us; ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us; Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Sharīk informed me; ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār informed me, from ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: \I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ under a single blanket"," and I slipped away. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you?' I said: 'I have menstruated.' He said: 'Tie your lower garment around yourself"," then come back in.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"14090","(14084) ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār narrates from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: \I was with the Prophet ﷺ under a single blanket"," and I slipped away. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you?' I said: 'I have menstruated.' He said: 'Tie your lower garment around yourself"," then come back in.'\""\n\nMaimūnah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: \""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wished to be close to his menstruating wife (i.e."," to lie with her)"," he would command her to tie her lower garment tightly.\""\n\nImam al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Lying with a woman during her menses and being near her is a matter of disagreement"," and she should place a cloth over the area of her blood.\"""""
"14091","It was narrated that Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would visit his wives and perform ablution (wudu) once before entering them.\n\nNarrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb through Miskin."
"14092","It was narrated that Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would visit his wives and enter them with a single bath (ghusl).\n\nMarwan said: But we do not doubt that he performed wudu between them."
"14093","It was narrated that Abi Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his family and intends to return [to them again], he should perform wudu.\n\nNarrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Abi Kurayb."
"14094","Shu'bah narrated from 'Asim al-Ahwal, and added to it: For indeed, it is more beneficial for returning. \nIt was narrated that Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Thaher al-Daqaq said: Ahmad ibn Uthman al-Adami narrated to us, and 'Abd al-Karim al-Aquli narrated to us, and Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, and Shu'bah narrated to us from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abi al-Mutawakkil, from Abi Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When one of you intends to return [to his wife], he should perform wudu, for indeed it is more beneficial for him. \nIf al-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) intended this hadith, then this is a sound chain, and perhaps he did not reach its chain."
"14095","Perhaps he intended what was narrated by Abu Ali al-Rudhburi: Abu Bakr ibn Mahmud al-Asqari narrated to us, and 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Usama al-Halabi narrated to us, and Musayyab ibn Wadhih narrated to us, and al-Mu'tamir narrated to us from 'Ubaidullah from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When you come to your family and intend to return, perform wudu as you would for prayer.\n\nThis is how Musayyab ibn Wadhih narrated it, but it is not to be relied upon."
"14096","It was narrated that 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' said: Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaaq narrated to us, and Yousuf ibn Ya'qoub narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, and al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulaiman narrated to us from Lait, from 'Asim, from Abi al-Mushtahil, from 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: When one of you comes to his family and intends to return, let him wash his private parts. This is the most authentic. Lait ibn Abi Sulaim does not have a reputation for hadith, and in the hadith of Abi Sa'id there is sufficiency."
"14097","It has been related in matters of ghusl between these two hadiths a narration that is not strong. 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' narrated to us, and Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaaq narrated to us, and Yousuf ibn Ya'qoub narrated to us, and Sulaiman ibn Harb narrated to us, and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Rafi', from his aunt Salma, from Abi Rafi', that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went to visit his wives on a Friday, and he bathed (ghusl) before each one individually. I said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not make it a single bath? He said: This is purer, cleaner, and more pleasant."
"14098","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he had become junub during the night, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: Perform wudu and wash your private parts, then sleep.\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih from 'Abdullah ibn Yousuf through Malik, and narrated by Muslim from Yahya ibn Yahya."
"14099","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: O Messenger of Allah, I have become junub during the night, so what should I do? He said: Wash your private parts, perform wudu, then sleep."
"14100","It was narrated that Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when he was junub and intended to sleep or eat, would perform wudu.\n\nNarrated by Muslim in his Sahih from various narrations through Shu'bah."
"14101","(14095) Abū Naṣr — ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah — informed us; Abū ʿAlī — Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad al-Raffāʾ — informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — narrated to us; Abū Ghassān — narrated to us; Mindal ibn ʿAlī — narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbd Allāh, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you comes to his wife"," let him be covered"," and let the two of them not strip naked as the two beasts of burden do.\"" [Weak]\n\nMindal ibn ʿAlī is alone in narrating it"," and he is not strong (in ḥadīth). Even though it is not established (as a ḥadīth of the Prophet ﷺ)"," it is praiseworthy in terms of good character.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (raḥimahullāh) said: \""I dislike that he approach her while the other (wife) is watching"," because that is neither modesty nor good character"," nor does it resemble (the command of) kind companionship. He has been commanded to live with her in a good manner.\""\n\n---"""
"14102","(14096) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī — informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — said: Abū ʿUbayd (raḥimahullāh) said regarding the ḥadīth of al-Ḥasan about a man who has intercourse with one wife while the other hears: \They used to dislike the faint sound (al-wajs).\""\n\nIt was narrated to us by ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām"," from Ghālib al-Qaṭṭān"," from al-Ḥasan.\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""Al-wajs is a faint"," quiet sound.\"" He added: \""Something even more emphatic in terms of dislike has been narrated on this topic"," namely that (the sound should not be heard) even by an infant in the cradle.\""\n\nHe also said: \""As for the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿAbbās — that he used to sleep between two slave-girls — I heard ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrate it from Abū Shaybah"," who said: I heard ʿIkrimah narrate from Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) that he used to sleep between two slave-girls.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: \""This"," in my view"," refers to sleeping"," not to intercourse.\"" [Weak]\n\n---"""
"14103","(14097) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī — informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī, in Makkah — narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāh al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Fazārī — narrated from ʿUmar ibn Ḥamzah al-ʿUmarī; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd — narrated to us, saying: I heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," the greatest trust (amānah) before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is that a man goes to his wife and she goes to him"," and then he divulges her secret.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Marwān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1437]\n\n---"""
"14104","(14098) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr — narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ — narrated to us; al-Jurayrī — narrated from Abū Naḍrah; a shaykh from al-Ṭufāwah — narrated to me, saying: I came to Abū Hurayrah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) in al-Madīnah, and I did not see any Companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) more energetic in movement or more hospitable to a guest than him. I heard him say: I walked with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until he reached the place where he prayed. He had with him two rows of men and one row of women, or two rows of women and one row of men. He turned his face toward us and said: \If Satan causes me to forget anything from my prayer"," let the men say 'Subḥān Allāh' and let the women clap.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) then prayed and did not forget anything from his prayer. He then said: \""Sit in your places. There is not one of you who"," when he comes to his wife"," closes his door and draws his curtain — (acting) under the veil of Allah.\"" They said: \""We do that.\"" He then sat and said: \""Then he sits and says: 'I did such-and-such with my wife"," and I did such-and-such.'\"" They fell silent. He said: \""Is there any among you women who does that?\"" The women fell silent. Then a young girl — I think he said"," Kaʿb — knelt on one of her knees and stretched herself out so that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) could see her"," and she said: \""Yes"," by Allah"," O Messenger of Allah! Indeed"," they (the men) do talk about it"," and indeed they (the women) do talk about it.\"" He said: \""Do you know what is the likeness of the one who does that? It is the likeness of a male devil and a female devil who meet one another in a lane and fulfill their need from her while the people are watching.\"" He also said: \""Let no man lie down with a man"," and let no woman lie down with a woman"," except with a child or a parent.\""\n\nHe mentioned a third point"," which he (the narrator) forgot. Then he said: \""Indeed"," the perfume of men is that whose scent is found but whose color does not appear; and indeed"," the perfume of women is that whose color appears but whose scent is not found.\"" [Weak]\n\n---"""
"14105","(14099) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān — informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk — narrated to us; Ḥanbal ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā al-Miṣrī — narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb — narrated from ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith, from Abī al-Samḥ, from Abī al-Haytham, from Abī Saʿīd (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Al-Shiyāʿ is forbidden.\"" Ḥanbal said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh — meaning Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal — said: \""Ibn Luḥayʿah says: al-Shiyāʿ means boasting about intercourse.\"" He also said: Ibn Wahb said: \""Al-Sibāʿ means the skins of predatory animals.\"" [Weak]\n\n---"""
"14106","(14100) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us from memory; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī ʿĪsā — narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym — narrated to us; Sufyān — narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us; Muḥammad ibn Bakr — narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us; Ibn Bashshār — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — narrated to us; Sufyān — narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I heard Jābir say: \Indeed"," the Jews say: When a man has intercourse with his wife from behind her in her private part"," his child is born cross-eyed.\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: \""Your wives are a tilth for you"," so approach your tilth however you wish\"" (Qurʾān 2:223). The wording is that of the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī. In the ḥadīth of Abū Nuʿaym it says: \""The Jews used to say: When he has intercourse with her from behind"," the child is born cross-eyed.\"" Then the verse was revealed"," and he mentioned the verse.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Nuʿaym"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 4528]\n\n---"""
"14107","(14101) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq — narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā), who said: The Jews said: \When a man comes to his wife while she is kneeling (on all fours)"," the child is born cross-eyed.\"" This was mentioned to the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and so there was revealed: \""Your wives are a tilth for you"," so approach your tilth however you wish\"" (Qurʾān 2:223).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," from Wahb ibn Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous ḥadīth.]\n\n---"""
"14108","(14102) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān — narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us; Sufyān — narrated from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā), who said: The Jews used to say: \Whoever comes to his wife in her front (vagina) from behind her"," the child is born cross-eyed.\"" So Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," revealed: \""Your wives are a tilth for you"," so approach your tilth however you wish\"" (Qurʾān 2:223).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah and others. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous ḥadīth.]\n\n---"""
"14109","(14103) Abū al-Ḥasan — ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān — informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us; Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī, Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl, and ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar — all said: Musaddad — narrated to us; Abū ʿAwānah — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Bukhārī — narrated to us; Qays ibn Unayf — narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us; Abū ʿAwānah — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir — narrated from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā), who said: The Jews said: \Cross-eyedness occurs only when a man comes to his wife from behind her.\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed: \""Your wives are a tilth for you"," so approach your tilth however you wish\"" (Qurʾān 2:223) — from in front of her or from behind her — but let him not approach her except in the proper passage (al-maʾtay"," i.e."," the vagina).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous ḥadīth.]\n\n---"""
"14110","(14104) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh — narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Rajāʾ — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr and Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh — both said: Wahb ibn Jarīr — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr — informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah — narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd — Abū Qudāmah — narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarīr — narrated to us; my father — narrated from al-Nuʿmān ibn Rāshid, from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), who said: The Jews said: \When a man comes to his wife while she is on her back with her knees drawn up (mujabbiyah)"," the child is born cross-eyed.\"" So there was revealed: \""Your wives are a tilth for you"," so approach your tilth however you wish\"" (Qurʾān 2:223) — if he wishes"," (he may do so) with her on her back with knees drawn up"," and if he wishes"," otherwise — provided that it is in one passage (i.e."," the vagina).\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Abū Qudāmah. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. See the previous ḥadīth.]"""
"14111","It was narrated that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), said: When the Muhajirun arrived in Medina, they married among the Ansar. The Muhajirun would approach their wives from behind, but the Ansar did not do so. So one woman said to her husband, “I will ask the Prophet (peace be upon him) about this.” She went to him, feeling ashamed, then asked him. He called for her and recited upon her: *\Your wives are a tilth for you"," so go to your tilth as you will\""* [Al-Baqarah 223]—meaning"," enter from one opening only."""
"14112","It was narrated that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him), said: A woman came to her asking the Prophet (peace be upon him) about a man who approached his wife from behind. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) entered, she felt ashamed. He asked about her, and Umm Salamah informed him. He said: *\Your wives are a tilth for you"," so go to your tilth as you will\""*—meaning"," approach them from the front or the back"," but in one private place"," that is"," in the womb for conception."""
"14113","It was narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was troubled by the fact that the Ansar were a people of *wasan* (paganism), and they were like the Jews, who were people of the Book. They used to see themselves as superior and followed much of their conduct. It was the practice of the People of the Book that men should not approach women except from one direction, and this was a cover for what women would do. The Ansar had adopted this practice from them, while the Quraysh had introduced an unnatural and prohibited manner—approaching women from the front, back, or sitting between them—and they took pleasure in it. When the Muhajirun came to Medina, a man from them married an Ansari woman and began to approach her in that manner. She disapproved and said, “We were only given one way; do that, or avoid me until your affair becomes clear.” This reached the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, revealed: *\Your wives are a tilth for you"," so go to your tilth as you will\""*—from the front"," back"," or sitting between them—meaning"," in the place of procreation.\n\nIt was also narrated by Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi from Muhammad ibn Ishaaq"," who heard Aban ibn Sahl narrate it"," mentioning it in similar terms"," and he said: After the private part."""
"14114","It was narrated that Aban ibn Sahl said: I recited the Qur’an twice before Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), and I asked him about this verse: *\Your wives are a tilth for you"," so go to your tilth as you will\""* [Al-Baqarah 223]. He said: Approach them from where it is prohibited for you—that is"," from where menstruation and childbirth occur."""
"14115","It was narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) concerning His statement, the Exalted: *\Your wives are a tilth for you"," so go to your tilth as you will\""* [Al-Baqarah 223]"," that he said: You may approach them from the front or the back"," but in the private part."""
"14116","It was narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) concerning His statement, the Exalted: *\So go to your tilth as you will\""* [Al-Baqarah 223]"," that he said: By \""tilth\"" he meant the womb. He said: Approach it however you wish—from the front or the back—but do not pass beyond the private part"," as Allah says: *\""From where He has commanded you\""* [Al-Baqarah 222]."""
"14117","It was narrated from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) that Muhammad ibn Ka’b said: Approach your tilth from where it grows—that is, from where the fruit is produced, meaning, from where offspring are born."
"14118","The Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: I doubted Khuza’imah ibn Thabit regarding a man who asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) about approaching women from behind or a man approaching his wife from behind. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \It is permissible.\"" When the man turned away"," he called him or ordered him to be called. He was called and asked: \""Which of the two holes—or which of the two openings—or which of the two fissures—do you mean: from behind toward the front"," or from behind toward behind?\"" He said: \""No.\"" Then he said: \""Allah does not feel shy of the truth. Do not approach the women from behind.\""\n\nThe Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: My uncle Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Sa’ib is trustworthy"," and Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn al-Sa’ib is trustworthy. Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Sa’ib told me that the Ansari narrator reported it"," and he spoke well of him. Khuza’imah is among those concerning whom no scholar doubts his trustworthiness. I do not weaken his narration; rather"," I reject it."""
"14119","Muhammad ibn Ali said: I was with Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi when a man came and said: \O Abu ‘Amr"," what do you say about a man approaching a woman from behind?\"" He said: \""This is an old man from the Quraysh"," so ask him—that is"," Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn al-Sa’ib.\"" He said: \""Abd Allah has not heard anything about this.\"" He said: \""O Allah"," this is filth"," even if it is permissible.\"" Then Abd Allah ibn Ali met ‘Amr ibn Uhayha ibn al-Julah and said: \""Have you heard anything about a man approaching a woman from behind?\"" He said: \""I testify that I heard Khuza’imah ibn Thabit"," the Ansari"," whom the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made equal in testimony to two men"," say: 'A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him)...' and he narrated the rest of the hadith in a similar manner.\"" There is another chain of narration for Abd Allah ibn Ali ibn al-Sa’ib in this hadith."""
"14120","It was narrated that Khuza’imah ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: \Allah does not feel shy of the truth"," so do not approach the women from behind.\"""""
"14121","It was reported to us by Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, who narrated to us Ahmad ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi, who narrated to us Abu Usama from Walid ibn Kathir, from 'Ubaid Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn al-Khatmi, from Abd al-Malik ibn Amr ibn Qays al-Khatmi, from Harami ibn Abd Allah, who said: I heard Khuzayma ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: Indeed, Allah does not feel shy of the truth; do not approach women in their private parts."
"14122","It was reported to us by Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah, who said: Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi narrated to us, who narrated to us Ahmad ibn Najdah, who narrated to us Sa'id ibn Mansur, who narrated to us Abd al-'Aziz ibn Muhammad, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usama ibn al-Had, from 'Ubaid Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Husayn, from Harami ibn Abd Allah al-Waqifi, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah does not feel shy of the truth; do not approach women in their private parts. Ibn al-Had shortened it and did not mention Abd al-Malik ibn Amr in it."
"14123","It was reported by Ibn 'Uyaynah from Ibn al-Had, but he erred in its chain of narration. It was reported to him by Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz, who said: Abu Bakr narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Ayyub al-Faqih, who narrated to us Bashir ibn Musa, who narrated to us al-Humaydi, who narrated to us Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from 'Umarah ibn Khuzayma ibn Thabit, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah does not feel shy of the truth; do not approach women in their private parts."
"14124","It was reported to us by Abu Tahir al-Faqih, who said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam say: I heard al-Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, say: Sufyan erred in the hadith of Ibn al-Had. The sheikh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: The basis of this hadith is Harami ibn Abd Allah, and there is no foundation for 'Umarah ibn Khuzayma in it except through the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah, and the people of knowledge in hadith consider it a mistake, and Allah knows best."
"14125","It was reported to us by Abu Ali Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shahan, who said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn al-'Abbas, who narrated to us al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri, who narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami and Muslim ibn Ibrahim, and the wording is by al-Hadrami, who said: We were narrated to us by Wahhib ibn Khalid, the companion of al-Karabis, who narrated to us Humayd ibn Qays, from Harami, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: Have shame, for indeed Allah does not feel shy of the truth; do not approach women in their private parts."
"14126","It was reported to us by Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Yusuf, who said: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us, who narrated to us Sadan ibn Nasr, who narrated to us Abu Mu'awiyah, from Hajjaj, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Abd Allah ibn Harami, from Khuzayma, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah does not feel shy of the truth; do not approach women in their private parts. Hajjaj ibn Artath erred in the name of the man, so he changed his name to his father's name."
"14127","It was reported by Musannaf ibn Sabbah from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Harami ibn Abd Allah, from Khuzayma ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah does not feel shy of the truth; do not approach women in their private parts. Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan reported it to us, who said: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us 'Ubayd ibn Sharik, who narrated to us ibn Ufayr, who narrated to us Yahya ibn Ayyub, from al-Musannaf ibn Sabbah, who mentioned it, and there is another chain of narration for 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb in it."
"14128","It was reported to us by Abu Bakr ibn Furak, who said: Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, who narrated to us Yunus ibn Habib, who narrated to us Abu Dawud, who narrated to us Hammam, from Qatadah, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: This is the lesser Lot; that is, approaching a woman in her private parts."
"14129","It was reported to us by Abu al-Hasan ibn Abdan, who said: Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Saffar narrated to us Tamtam, who narrated to us 'Affan, who narrated to us Wahhib, who narrated to us Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, and it was reported to us by Abu Zakariya Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya, who said: Abu al-Hasan ibn Subayh al-Jauhari narrated to us Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shiruwayh, who narrated to us Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, who reported to us Abd al-Razzaq, who reported to us Ma'mar, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Harith ibn Mukhallad, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), who said: Allah will not look at a man on the Day of Resurrection who approaches a woman in her private parts. In the narration of Wahhib: Allah will not look at a man who approaches his wife in her private parts."
"14130","It was reported to us by Abu Sa'd al-Malini, who said: Abu Ahmad ibn Adi narrated to us Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Musannaf, who narrated to us Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj, who narrated to us Hammad ibn Salamah, from Hakim al-Athram, from Abu Tamimah al-Hujaymi, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Whoever approaches a priest and believes him in what he says, and whoever approaches a woman in her private parts, and whoever approaches a menstruating woman, has indeed freed himself from what Allah has revealed to Muhammad (peace be upon him). Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi followed it from Hammad."
"14131","It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hāfiẓ and Abu Bakr: Ahmad b. al-Hasan and Abu Sa‘īd b. ‘Amr said: Muhammad b. Ya‘qūb related to us, Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad b. Ya‘qūb related to us, Abū Ja‘far b. al-Munādi related to us, Yūnus b. Muhammad related to us, Ya‘qūb al-Qummī related to us from Ja‘far b. Abī al-Mughīra, from Sa‘īd b. Jubayr, from Ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: ‘Umar came to the Messenger of Allah -ﷺ- and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have been destroyed.” He said: “What has destroyed you?” He said: “I went out on my night journey and no obstacle came to me.” Then revelation was sent down to him: {Your wives are as a tilth unto you; so approach your tilth when or where you will, but do some good act for your souls beforehand; and fear Allah. And know that you are to meet Him.} [al-Baqarah 223] So he said: “Go forward or go back, but avoid the back and the menses.”"
"14132","It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hāfiẓ and Abu Sa‘īd b. ‘Amr, who said: Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad b. Ya‘qūb related to us, ‘Asad b. ‘Āṣim related to us, al-Husayn b. Ḥafṣ related to us from Sufyān, from ‘Āṣim al-Aḥwal, from ‘Īsā b. Hiṭṭān, from Muslim b. Sallām, from ‘Alī b. Ṭalq, who said: The Messenger of Allah -ﷺ- forbade men from approaching women in their private chambers, for Allah does not feel shy of the truth."
"14133","It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hāfiẓ and Abu Sa‘īd b. ‘Amr, who said: Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad b. Ya‘qūb related to us, ‘Asad b. ‘Āṣim related to us, al-Husayn b. Ḥafṣ related to us from Sufyān, from al-Salt b. Bahrām, from Abū al-Mu‘tamir, from Abū al-Juwairā’, who said: A man asked ‘Alī, may Allah be pleased with him, about this matter, and he said: “You have reached the lowest depth; have you not heard Allah say: {Do you approach licentiousness, while you have come to know of none of the peoples before you doing so} [al-A‘rāf 80]?” The correct report is from al-Salt b. Bahrām, from Abū al-Juwairā’, who is ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Mas‘ūd al-‘Abdī, from Abū al-Mu‘tamir, who said: A man asked ‘Alī, may Allah be pleased with him, who was on the minbar, about approaching women in their private chambers, and he mentioned it."
"14134","Thus it was reported by Abū ‘Uthmān and others from al-Salt b. Bahrām, from ‘Abd al-Raḥmān b. Mas‘ūd al-‘Abdī, from Abū al-Mu‘tamir, as my father, Abu ‘Abdillah, has informed me, granting permission that Abū ‘Alī al-Hāfiẓ reported it, saying: It was reported to us by Ibrāhīm b. ‘Abdillah b. Ayyūb al-Mukharrimī, who said: Sa‘īd b. Muhammad al-Jarmī related to us, Abū ‘Uthmān reported it."
"14135","It was reported to us by Abū Naṣr b. Qatādah, Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrāwī, Ahmad b. Najdah, Sa‘īd b. Manṣūr, Ismā‘īl b. Ibrāhīm, who informed me: Abū ‘Abdillah al-Shaqarī informed me, Abū al-Qa‘qa‘ said: I witnessed the battle of al-Qādisiyyah while I was a boy or a youth. A man came to ‘Abdillah and said: “Come to my wife whenever you wish.” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Wherever you wish?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “And with whom you wish?” He said: “Yes.” Then a man understood that he meant to approach her in her chamber, so he said: “No, it is forbidden for you to approach women in their private chambers.”"
"14136","It was reported to us by Abū ‘Alī: al-Hasan b. Ahmad b. Ibrāhīm b. Shādhān from Baghdad, Hamzah b. Muhammad b. al-‘Abbās related to us, al-‘Abbās b. Muhammad related to us, Muslim b. Ibrāhīm related to us, Wahb b. Khālid related to us, Dāwūd b. Abī Hind related to us from ‘Ikramah, from Ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he used to consider marriage in the private chamber a very great fault."
"14137","It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hāfiẓ: Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad b. Ya‘qūb related to us, Yaḥyā b. Abī Ṭālib informed us, ‘Abd al-Wahhāb b. ‘Aṭā’ said: I asked Sa‘īd about a man who approaches his wife in her private chamber, and he informed us through Qatādah, from ‘Uqbah b. Wassaǧ, from Abū al-Dardā’, who said: “Does he do that except a disbeliever?”"
"14138","It was reported to us by Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abu Bakr al-Qāḍī, who said: Hajjāj b. Ahmad al-Ṭūsī related to us, ‘Abd al-Raḥīm b. Munīb related to us, Yāzid b. Hārūn informed us, Sufyān al-Thawrī informed us, from ‘Amār al-Duhnī, from Muslim al-Baṭīn, from Ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he was asked about the “whispering” (al-khaẓẓaḥa), and he said: “Marriage to a slave girl is better than that, and it is better than fornication.” This is a mursal report of good strength."
"14139","It was reported to us by Abū Zakariyyā b. Abī Ishāq al-Muzakkī, Abu ‘Abdillah b. Ya‘qūb related to us, Muhammad b. ‘Abd al-Wahhāb informed us, Ja‘far b. ‘Awn informed us, al-Ajlāḥ informed us, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that a youth came to him, and the people stood up while the youth remained seated. Some of the people said to him: “Stand up, O youth!” But Ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: “Leave him alone; something has seated him.” When the people left, the youth said to Ibn ‘Abbās: “O Ibn ‘Abbās, I am a young youth, and I experience a strong sexual urge; I recite dhikr until I ejaculate.” Ibn ‘Abbās said: “It is better than fornication, and marriage to a slave girl is better than that.”"
"14140","It was reported to us by Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hāfiẓ and Abu Zakariyyā b. Abī Ishāq al-Muzakkī, who said: Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad b. Ya‘qūb informed us, Muhammad b. ‘Abdillah b. al-Ḥakam informed us, ‘Abdillah b. Wahb b. Muslim informed us that Mālik b. Anas informed him. (h) And Abu Zakariyyā: Yaḥyā b. Ibrāhīm related to us, Abu al-‘Abbās informed us, Rabī‘ informed us, al-Shāfi‘ī informed us, Mālik informed us. (h) And Muhammad b. ‘Abdillah al-Hāfiẓ related to us, Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad b. Ya‘qūb related to us, Muhammad b. Ishāq al-Ṣaghānī related to us, ‘Abdillah b. Yūsuf related to us, Mālik related to us. (h) And Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hāfiẓ related to us, Yaḥyā b. Manṣūr related to us, Muhammad b. ‘Abd al-Salām related to us, Yaḥyā b. Yaḥyā said: I recited to Mālik from Nāfi‘, from Ibn ‘Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah -ﷺ- forbade *al-shighār*, which is when a man marries his daughter to another man on the condition that he marries his daughter to him, without there being any mahr between them. But Yaḥyā did not mention the other man. This is the report of al-Bukhārī in his *Ṣaḥīḥ*, from ‘Abdillah b. Yūsuf, and the report of Muslim from Yaḥyā b. Yaḥyā."
"14141","It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade *al-shighar* (exchange marriage). I asked Nafi‘: What is *al-shighar*? He said: It is when a man marries the daughter of a man and marries his [the latter’s] daughter without *mahr*, or marries the sister of a man and marries his [the latter’s] sister without *mahr*.\n\nThis hadith is narrated by al-Bukhari in his *Sahih* on the authority of Musaddad, and by Muslim on the authority of Zuhayr and others on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa‘id. It is also narrated by Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and ‘Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraaj on the authority of Nafi‘ without interpretation."
"14142","It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade *al-shighar*. Ibn Numair added: *Al-shighar* is when a man says to another man: Marry my daughter to you, and I will marry your daughter to me; and marry my sister to you, and I will marry your sister to me.\n\nThis hadith is narrated by Muslim in his *Sahih* on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, and by ‘Abdah on the authority of ‘Ubaid Allah, with the addition: There is no *mahr* between them."
"14143","It was narrated that the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade *al-shighar*.\n\nThis hadith is narrated by Muslim in his *Sahih* on the authority of Harun ibn ‘Abd Allah on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Muhammad."
"14144","It was narrated that the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade *al-shighar*. *Al-shighar* is when a woman is married to another woman in exchange, such that the *mahr* of this one is the *mahr* of that one, and the *mahr* of this one is the *mahr* of that one."
"14145","It was narrated that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There is no *shighar* in Islam.\n\nThis is also narrated by ‘Amr ibn Shu‘ayb on his father on his grandfather, and by the descendants of Wail ibn Hujr on their fathers from Wail, on the authority of the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"14146","It was narrated that ‘Abbas ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas married the daughter of ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hakam, and ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hakam married his [‘Abbas’s] daughter, and they made a *mahr*. Then Mu‘awiya wrote to Marwan ordering him to dissolve the marriage between them, and he said in his letter: This is *al-shighar*, which the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade."
"14147","It was narrated that we used to go out on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and there were no women with us. We said: Shall we not seek permission to marry? He forbade it, but then permitted us to marry a woman for a term by means of a garment.\n\nThe wording of the hadith of Abu ‘Uthman is: Then he permitted us to marry a woman for a term by means of a garment. Then ‘Abd Allah recited the verse: “O you who believe! Do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you…” (Quran 5:87).\n\nThis is narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim in their *Sahih* from various chains on the authority of Isma‘il ibn Abi Khalid."
"14148","It was narrated that we used to go out on expeditions with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and there were no women with us. We wished to seek permission, but the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade it, then permitted us to marry a woman for a term by means of something.\n\nAbu ‘Abd Allah added in his narration through his chain: Al-Shafi‘i said: Ibn Mas‘ud mentioned permission for *mut‘a* marriage, but he did not specify whether it was before or after the conquest of Khaybar. The hadith of ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib (peace be upon him) regarding the prohibition of *mut‘a* by the Prophet (peace be upon him) is more likely, and Allah knows best who abrogates it."
"14149","It has been related in the hadith of Ibn Mas‘ud that he said: We were young men when we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) for permission to marry. He said: No. Then he permitted us to marry a woman for a term by means of a garment. Then ‘Abd Allah recited the verse: “O you who believe! Do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you…” (Quran 5:87).\n\nThis is narrated by Muslim on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah.\n\nThe Sheikh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This narration does not indicate whether it was before the conquest of Khaybar or before the conquest of Makkah. For ‘Abd Allah ibn Mas‘ud (may Allah be pleased with him) died in the year 32 of the Hijrah, at which time he was approximately sixty years old. The conquest of Khaybar occurred in the year 7 of the Hijrah, and the conquest of Makkah in the year 8. At the time of the conquests, ‘Abd Allah was approximately forty years old, and youth precedes that."
"14150","The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade *mut‘a* marriage at the time of Khaybar, and this is clearly stated in what was narrated by Abu Bakr al-Qadi and Abu Zakariyya: Yahya ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya, who said: Muhammad ibn Ya‘qub narrated to us, and Muhammad ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, and Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik ibn Anas, Yunus ibn Yazid, and Usama ibn Zaid narrated to us: Ibn Shihab narrated to them: ‘Abd Allah and al-Hasan, the two sons of Muhammad ibn ‘Ali, narrated to us from their father ‘Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade *mut‘a* marriage on the day of Khaybar, and also forbade the eating of the flesh of domestic donkeys.\n\nThe wording of the narration of al-Shafi‘i and Yahya ibn Yahya is: He forbade *mut‘a* marriage on the day of Khaybar, and also forbade the eating of the flesh of domestic donkeys.\n\nThe narration of Ibn Wahb is: He forbade *mut‘a* marriage on the day of Khaybar, and also forbade the eating of the flesh of domestic donkeys.\n\nThis is narrated by al-Bukhari in his *Sahih* on the authority of ‘Abd Allah ibn Yufayf and others on the authority of Malik, and by Muslim on the authority of Yahya ibn Yahya on the authority of Malik, and on the authority of Abu al-Tahir and Harmalah on the authority of Ibn Wahb on the authority of Yunus."
"14151","It was narrated that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: \You are a man of gentle disposition. Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," forbade marriage of mutual enjoyment (nikaah al-mut'ah) on the day of Khaybar"," and also forbade the eating of the flesh of domestic donkeys?\""\n\nThis hadith is narrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih on the authority of Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from another route through Ubaid-Allah ibn Umar."""
"14152","It was narrated that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: \You are a man of gentle disposition. Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," forbade marriage of mutual enjoyment (nikaah al-mut'ah) and also forbade the eating of the flesh of domestic donkeys?\""\n\nThis hadith is narrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih on the authority of Malik ibn Isma'il through ibn Uyainah"," who added the time of Khaybar at the end of the hadith. Muslim narrated it from a group of narrators through ibn Uyainah"," and ibn Uyainah stated in the narration of al-Humaidi concerning this: \""This date refers only to the prohibition of eating the flesh of domestic donkeys"," not to the prohibition of marriage of mutual enjoyment.\"""""
"14153","It was narrated that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both: \You are a man of gentle disposition. Indeed"," the Prophet"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," forbade marriage of mutual enjoyment (nikaah al-mut'ah) and also forbade the eating of the flesh of domestic donkeys during the time of Khaybar.\""\n\nSufyan said: \""He means that he forbade the eating of the flesh of domestic donkeys during the time of Khaybar"," not marriage of mutual enjoyment.\""\n\nThe Sheikh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""What Sufyan said is plausible. Were it not for the knowledge of Ali ibn Abi Talib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," regarding the abrogation of marriage of mutual enjoyment"," and that the prohibition of it was only after the concession"," he would have denied it in the case of Ibn Abbas"," may Allah be pleased with them both. And Allah knows best. It was narrated through ibn Umar that it was prohibited on the day of Khaybar.\"""""
"14154","It was narrated that a man asked Abdullah ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, about marriage of mutual enjoyment (nikaah al-mut'ah), and he said: \It is forbidden.\"" The man said: \""By Allah"," so-and-so says so.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," if he knew that the Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," forbade it on the day of Khaybar"," and that we were not accustomed to such practices"," he would not have done it.\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: \""Then the Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," permitted marriage of mutual enjoyment during the conquest of Makkah"," but later forbade it until the Day of Resurrection. This is clear evidence.\"""""
"14155","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," permitted marriage of mutual enjoyment. So I went with a man from my people"," and he was more handsome than me. Each of us had a garment. My garment was old"," and my companion’s garment was new and finer. When we came to a woman from Banu Amr"," who was like a young she-camel"," we presented ourselves to her. She said: 'What will you give me?' I said: 'My garment","' and my companion said: 'My garment.' His garment was finer than mine"," and I was younger than him. When she looked at my companion’s garment"," she preferred it"," and when she looked at me"," she preferred me. Then she said: 'You and your garment are sufficient for me.' So I stayed with her for three days. Then the Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," said: 'Whoever has a woman from these women with whom he is permitted to enjoy marital relations"," let him send her away on her way.'\""\n\nThis hadith is narrated by Muslim in his Sahih through Qutaibah ibn Sa'id"," without mentioning the time of Layth ibn Sa'd."""
"14156","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \During the conquest of Makkah"," the Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," permitted marriage of mutual enjoyment. So I went out with a man from my people who was more handsome than me. Each of us had a garment—my garment was old"," and my cousin’s garment was new and finer. When we reached the outskirts of Makkah"," a young woman like a virgin she-camel came to us. We asked: 'Can one of us enjoy her?' She said: 'What will you spend?' So each of us spread his garment. She kept looking at the two men"," and when she saw my companion"," she looked at his garment and said: 'This garment is old"," and mine is new and fine.' She said this three or two times. Then I enjoyed her"," and we did not leave until the Messenger of Allah"," may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him"," forbade it.\""\n\nThe wording of the hadith of Musaddad is narrated by Muslim in his Sahih through Abu Kamil."""
"14157","It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted marriage of mutual enjoyment during the conquest of Makkah when we entered it, but we did not leave it until he forbade it.\n\nThe wording of the hadith of Ibrahim is narrated by Muslim in his Sahih through Isaac ibn Ibrahim."
"14158","It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, permitted marriage of mutual enjoyment during the conquest of Makkah. So I went out with a companion from Banu Sulaym until we found a young woman from Banu Amr, like a virgin she-camel. We proposed to her and presented our garments to her. She kept looking, and she found me more handsome than my companion, and she found my companion’s garment finer than mine. She consulted herself for an hour, then chose me over my companion. I stayed with her for three days. Then the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to send them away.\n\nThe wording of the hadith of Yahya ibn Yahya is narrated by Muslim in his Sahih through Yahya ibn Yahya."
"14159","It was narrated that the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade marriage of mutual enjoyment (nikaah al-mut'ah), and said: \Indeed"," it is forbidden from today until the Day of Resurrection"," and whoever has given something to any of them"," let him not take it back.\""\n\nThe wording of the hadith of Abu Abdullah is narrated by Muslim in his Sahih through Salama ibn Shabib. Ibn Abdullah did not mention the words: \""and whoever has given...\"""""
"14160","It was narrated that I saw the Messenger of Allah, may the peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, standing between the pillar and the door, and he was saying: \O people"," I had permitted you to enjoy marital relations"," but indeed Allah has forbidden it until the Day of Resurrection. So whoever among you has a woman from them with whom he is permitted to enjoy"," let him send her away on her way"," and do not take back anything that you have given them.\""\n\nThis hadith is narrated by Muslim in his Sahih through Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah.\n\nLikewise"," Abdullah ibn Numair narrated it through Abdullah ibn Umar without mentioning the time. Ja'far ibn Awn and Abu Nu'aim narrated it through Abdullah ibn Umar"," specifying the time as the farewell pilgrimage."""
"14161","It was narrated that Abu al-Hasan ‘Ali ibn Ahmad ibn ‘Abdān informed us; Ahmad ibn ‘Ubayd al-Saffār narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn al-Hasan al-Harb narrated to us; Abu Nu‘aym narrated to us; ‘Abd al-‘Azīz ibn ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Azīz narrated to us from Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh, who said: My father informed him that they set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) on the Farewell Pilgrimage until they arrived at ‘Usfān. Then a man from Banū Mudlij stood before the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and he was called Saqāqah ibn Mālik or Mālik ibn Saqāqah. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, decide for us as though you were deciding for people who have just been born.” The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah has included in your pilgrimage this Umrah, so when you enter [Makkah], whoever performs the Tawāf of the House and the Sa‘ī between al-Safā and al-Marwah is permitted, except for him who has with him a sacrificial animal.” When we were permitted, he said: “Enjoy yourselves from these women.” And in our view, enjoyment means marriage. We presented this to the women, but they refused except to stipulate a term between us and them. We mentioned this to the Prophet (peace be upon him), and he said: “Do so.” So I set out with my cousin’s son, and we had two cloaks, and his cloak was finer than mine, and I was more handsome than he. We came to a woman, and she preferred my youth and handsomeness, and his cloak. She said: “A cloak like a cloak,” so the term between me and her was ten days. I stayed with her for one night, then I left in the morning. Behold, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was standing between the Rukn and the Maqām, saying: “O people, I had permitted you to enjoy yourselves from these women, but indeed I have now made it unlawful until the Day of Resurrection. So whoever remains with any of them, let him abandon her path, and do not take anything from what you have given them.”"
"14162","It was narrated that Abu Zakariyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us; Abu ‘Abd Allāh ibn Ya‘qūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ‘Abd al-Wahhāb narrated to us; Ja‘far ibn ‘Awn narrated to us; ‘Abd al-‘Azīz ibn ‘Umar narrated to us from Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh, who said: My father informed him that they traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) until they reached ‘Usfān, and a man from Banū Mudlij spoke to him, and he related the hadith in a manner similar to the previous one. \nAnd similarly, a group of the elders narrated it: Ibn Jurayj, al-Thawrī, and others, from ‘Abd al-‘Azīz ibn ‘Umar, who is weak among them, and the majority of the people narrated from Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh that this occurred during the time of the Conquest [of Makkah]."
"14163","It was narrated that Abu ‘Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abu ‘Amr ibn Abī Ja‘far narrated to me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ismā‘īl ibn ‘Ulayyā narrated to us from Ma‘mar, from az-Zuhrī, from Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade temporary marriage (mut‘ah) on the day of the Conquest. \nThis was narrated by Muslim in his Sahīḥ from Abu Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. And similarly, Ṣāliḥ ibn Kaysān narrated it from az-Zuhrī, and similarly az-Zuhrī narrated it in the more authentic of the two narrations from him."
"14164","It was narrated that Abu ‘Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abu al-‘Abbās: Muḥammad ibn Ya‘qūb said: Rabī‘ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; al-Shāfi‘ī narrated to us; Ibn ‘Uyaynah narrated to us from az-Zuhrī, from Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh, from his father, that the Prophet (peace be upon him) forbade temporary marriage. \nThis was narrated by Muslim from Zuḥayr ibn Ḥarb and others from Sufyān, and the Ḥumaydī narrated it from Sufyān, and he added: “In the year of the Conquest.”"
"14165","It was narrated that Abu ‘Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; az-Zuhrī said: And he informed me that Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh narrated to his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade temporary marriage in the year of the Conquest. \nAnd Ismā‘īl ibn ‘Umayyah narrated it from az-Zuhrī, saying: “In the Farewell Pilgrimage.”"
"14166","It was narrated that Abu ‘Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abu Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad ibn Musharḥad narrated to us; ‘Abd al-Wārith narrated to us from Ismā‘īl ibn ‘Umayyah, from az-Zuhrī, who said: We were with ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Azīz, may Allah have mercy on him, and we mentioned temporary marriage, and a man who was called Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh said: I testify that my father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade it during the Farewell Pilgrimage. \nAnd the majority of the narrations from az-Zuhrī, or the hadith of Saḷamah ibn al-Akwa‘, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning permission in it, and then the prohibition, is consistent with the hadith of Sabrāh ibn Ma‘bad. [Weak; see the marginal note on 14155]"
"14167","It was narrated that Abu ‘Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abu Dāwūd narrated to us; Musaddad ibn Musharḥad narrated to us; ‘Abd al-Wārith narrated to us from Ismā‘īl ibn ‘Umayyah, from az-Zuhrī, who said: We were with ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Azīz, may Allah have mercy on him, and we mentioned temporary marriage, and a man who was called Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh said: I testify that my father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade it during the Farewell Pilgrimage. \nAnd the majority of the narrations from az-Zuhrī, or the hadith of Saḷamah ibn al-Akwa‘, may Allah be pleased with him, concerning permission in it, and then the prohibition, is consistent with the hadith of Sabrāh ibn Ma‘bad. [Weak; see the marginal note on 14155]"
"14168","It was narrated that Abu ‘Amr: Muḥammad ibn ‘Abd Allāh al-‘Adīb informed us; Abu Bakr al-Ismā‘īlī narrated to us; Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ‘Amr ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Shu‘bah narrated to us from Abū Jamrā‘, from Ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them, that he was asked about temporary marriage, and he said: “My master, it was only permitted during jihad, and women are few.” Then Ibn ‘Abbās, may Allah be pleased with them, said: “He told the truth.”"
"14169","It was narrated that Abu ‘Amr informed us; Abu Bakr narrated to us; ‘Imrān and Ibn al-Karīm said: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us; Muḥammad narrated to us; Shu‘bah narrated to us from Abū Jamrā‘, who said: I heard Ibn ‘Abbās, and he was asked about temporary marriage, and he permitted it, and his master said to him: “Indeed, it was only permitted during jihad, and women are few, and the situation is severe.” Then Ibn ‘Abbās said: “Yes.” \nThis was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Sahīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār."
"14170","It was narrated that Abu ‘Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abu ‘Alī: al-Ḥusayn ibn ‘Alī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Harmalah ibn Yahyā narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Yūnus said: Ibn Shihāb informed me that ‘Urwah ibn az-Zubayr informed me that ‘Abd Allāh ibn az-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with them, stood in Makkah and said: “Indeed, some people have been made blind by Allah—their hearts as blind as their eyes—who give fatwas on temporary marriage and accuse a man of it.” He called out to him and said: “Indeed, you are a liar and a slanderer. By my life, temporary marriage was practiced in the time of the Leader of the God-fearing—that is, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him).” Then Ibn az-Zubayr said: “Then try it yourself. By Allah, if you do it, I will stone you with stones.” \nThen Ibn Shihāb said: Khālid ibn al-Muhājir ibn Sāif informed me that while he was sitting with a man, a man came and asked him about temporary marriage. Then Ibn Abī ‘Amrah al-Anṣārī said to him: “Wait.” He said: “Indeed, it was practiced in the time of the Leader of the God-fearing.” Then Ibn Abī ‘Amrah said: “Indeed, it was a concession in the early days of Islam for whoever is compelled to it like a dead person, blood, or the flesh of the najis. Then Allah judged the religion and forbade it.” \nThen Ibn Shihāb said: And Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh al-Juḥanī informed me that his father said: “I used to enjoy temporary marriage in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) from a woman of Banū ‘Amir with two red cloaks. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) forbade temporary marriage.” \nThen Ibn Shihāb said: And I heard Rabī‘ ibn Sabrāh narrating that while I was sitting with ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Azīz. \nThis was narrated by Muslim in his Sahīḥ from Harmalah ibn Yahyā."
"14171","We were informed by Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih, who informed us: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan, the father of the sheikh, narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Ibn Wahb, who mentioned it in a manner similar to this, except that he said: \He attributes it to ibn Abbas.\"" \nAnd he added at the end: Ibn Shihab said: \""And 'Ubaidullah informed me that ibn Abbas used to issue a fatwa permitting temporary marriage (mut'ah)"," and he concealed this fact from the people of knowledge. Then ibn Abbas refused to retract it until some of the poets began to recite: 'O you who call out! Is there need in your fatwa for the young women of ibn Abbas? Is there need for you to have a beloved"," tender-skinned woman as your abode until you reach the source of the people?'\"" \nThen the people of knowledge increased in their disgust for it"," and there was hatred for it when the poets spoke about it. [Sahih. Preceded by Sahih]"""
"14172","He said: And ibn Wahb narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim informed me: al-Hasan ibn 'Umarat informed me: al-Minhal ibn 'Amr informed me: Sa'id ibn Jubayr said: \I said to ibn Abbas: 'What have you done that the riders have been set in motion by your young women"," and what have the poets said about it?'\"" He said: \""What did they say?\"" He said: The poet said: \n\""When his session became prolonged"," I said to the sheikh: 'O you who call out! Is there anything in your fatwa for the young women of ibn Abbas? O you who weep! Is there for you a white"," delicate-skinned woman who will be your abode until you reach the source of the people?'\"" \nAnd in the narration of Abu Khalid from al-Minhal: \""I said to the sheikh when his session became prolonged","\"" and in the other house he said: \""Is there for you a woman of the distant relatives"," a beloved one?\"" Ibn Abbas said: \""This is not what I intended"," and I did not issue a fatwa about this. Indeed"," temporary marriage is not permissible except for the one who is compelled. Indeed"," it is like carrion"," blood"," and the flesh of the pig.\"" [Very weak]"""
"14173","We were informed by Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah, who informed us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Shibban al-Baghdadi, then al-Harawi, informed us: Mu'adh ibn Najdat narrated to us: Khalad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us: from Lait, from his wife, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from ibn Abbas, that he said about temporary marriage: \It is forbidden"," like carrion"," blood"," and the flesh of the pig.\"" This was also narrated by al-Qasim ibn al-Walid from ibn Abbas. [Weak]"""
"14174","We were informed by Abu al-Hasan: 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan, who informed us: Sulaiman ibn Ahmad al-Lakhmi narrated to us: ibn Hanbal narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Layth narrated to us: al-Ashja'i said: Sulaiman said: And the Hadhrami narrated to us: Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uqbah, the brother of Qabishah ibn 'Uqbah, said: The Thawri narrated to us: Musa ibn 'Ubaidah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ka'b narrated to us: ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said: \Temporary marriage existed in the early days of Islam"," and they would recite this verse: {So whatever of them you have taken as temporary wives"," give them a portion of wealth.} [An-Nisa 24] until the specified time mentioned in the verse. Then a man would come to a city where he did not know anyone"," and he would marry a woman to satisfy his need"," in order to preserve his property and to set his affairs in order"," until this verse was revealed: {Forbidden to you are your mothers.} [An-Nisa 23] until the end of the verse. Then Allah"," the Exalted"," abrogated the first one"," and temporary marriage was abolished. And its confirmation is in the Qur'an: {Except for those whom your right hands possess.} [Al-Mu'minoon 6] And anything else is forbidden.\"" [Weak]"""
"14175","We were informed by Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, who informed us: Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim al-Muzakki narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salama narrated to us: Hamid ibn 'Umar al-Bakrāwi narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahid, that is, ibn Ziyad, from 'Asim, from Abu Nadrah, who said: \I was with Jābir ibn 'Abdillah"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," when a man came and said: 'ibn Abbas and ibn az-Zubayr differed regarding the two temporary marriages.' Then Jābir said: 'We used to do it with the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him-; then 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," forbade it"," and we did not return to it.'\"" \nThis is narrated by Muslim in his Sahih from Hamid ibn 'Umar al-Bakrāwi. [Sahih. Muslim 1217.1249]"""
"14176","We were informed by Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, who informed us: 'Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Hammad from Qatadah, from Abu Nadrah, from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \I said: 'Indeed"," ibn az-Zubayr forbids temporary marriage"," and indeed"," ibn Abbas permits it.'\"" He said: \""The hadith reached me: We used to take temporary marriage with the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him- and with Abu Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him. Then when 'Umar became caliph"," he addressed the people and said: 'Indeed"," this is the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him-"," and this is the Qur'an"," and these two were temporary marriages during the time of the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him-. And I forbid them"," and I punish for one of them: temporary marriage with women"," and I cannot stone a man who marries a woman for a specified time"," except in the stones and the other is temporary marriage for Hajj. Separate your Hajj from your 'Umrah"," for indeed"," it is the most complete for your Hajj and the most complete for your 'Umrah.'\"" \nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from another aspect from Hammad. The sheikh said: \""We do not doubt that they were permissible during the time of the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him-"," but we found that he forbade the marriage of temporary marriage during the year of the conquest of Mecca after the permission for it"," and then we did not find him permitting it after the prohibition of it until the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him- passed away. So the prohibition of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," regarding temporary marriage is in accordance with the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him-"," and we followed it"," and we did not find the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him- forbidding temporary marriage for Hajj from a sound narration from him"," and we found in the words of 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that it does not indicate that he preferred that the Hajj and 'Umrah be separated for them so that they may be the most complete for both of them"," so we understood his prohibition of temporary marriage for Hajj as a matter of preference and choice"," not as a prohibition"," and by Allah"," we seek success.\"" [Sahih. Preceded by Sahih]"""
"14177","And it has been narrated to us by Abu Muhammad: 'Abdillah ibn Yusuf al-Asbahani, who informed us: Abu Muhammad: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Yahya al-Zuhri al-Qadi, from Mecca, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sāigh narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Umāwi narrated to us: Mansur ibn Dinar narrated to us: 'Umar ibn Muhammad from Salim ibn 'Abdillah, from his father, from 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \Umar ascended the pulpit"," praised Allah"," and extolled Him"," then he said: 'What is the matter with men who marry this temporary marriage"," when the Messenger of Allah -peace be upon him- has forbidden it? I would stone anyone who marries it"," except that I do not know of anyone who has married it.'\"" This"," if it is authentic"," clarifies that 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," forbade temporary marriage only because he knew of the Messenger's -peace be upon him- prohibition of it. [Very weak]"""
"14178","We were informed by Abu Zakariyya ibn Ishaq al-Muzakki and Abu Bakr: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi, who said: We were informed by Abu al-'Abbas: Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who informed us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulaiman informed us: al-Shāfi'i informed us: Malik, from ibn Shihab, from 'Urwah, that Khawlah bint Hakim entered upon 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and she said: \Indeed"," Rabi'ah ibn Umayyah took temporary marriage with a woman who gave birth to a child from him.\"" Then 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," went out"," pulling his garment in agitation"," and he said: \""This is temporary marriage"," and if I had preceded in it"," I would have stoned her.\"" [Sahih. Malik 1152]"""
"14179","We were informed by Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan and Abu Zakariyya ibn Ishaq, who said: We were informed by Abu al-'Abbas: Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who informed us: Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn al-Hakam informed us: ibn Wahb informed us: 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar informed me: Nāfi' from 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he was asked about temporary marriage with women, and he said: \It is forbidden. Indeed"," 'Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," would have stoned anyone who took it.\"" [Sahih]"""
"14180","We were informed by Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz, who informed us: Abu al-'Abbas: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbūbī narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn al-Jabbar narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us: Nāfi' ibn ibn 'Umar said: I heard 'Abdillah ibn 'Ubaidillah ibn Abi Mulaykah say: \A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," was asked about temporary marriage with women"," and she said: 'The Book of Allah"," the Exalted"," is between me and them. And she recited this verse: {And those who guard their private parts"," except from their wives or those their right hands possess"," indeed"," they are not to be blamed"," but whoever seeks beyond that"," then those are the transgressors.} [Al-Mu'minoon 5-8] So whoever seeks beyond what Allah has married him or what he has possessed"," then he has transgressed.'\"" \nAnd it has been narrated regarding this by al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from A'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her. [Sahih]"""
"14181","(14175) It was narrated that Nafi’ said: “Ibnu ‘Umar said: It is not permissible for a man to marry except in the context of Islamic marriage; he should provide her with a dower, she should be his wife, and she should inherit from him, and he should not stipulate a fixed term for her. Indeed, she is his wife; and if one of them dies, they do not inherit from one another.” [Sahih]"
"14182","(14176) It was narrated that Abu ‘Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Zakariyyah ibn Abi Ishaaq said: “Abu al-‘Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya‘qoub narrated to us: Al-‘Abbas ibn Muhammad ad-Doori narrated to us: Khunais ibn Bakr ibn Khunais narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us from ‘Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Abu Dharr, who said: ‘Our companions among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah – may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him – were permitted temporary marriage for three days, after which the Messenger of Allah – may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him – forbade it.’ [Da‘if]"
"14183","(14177) It was narrated that Ali ibn Ahmad al-Muqri’ ibn al-Hammam narrated from Isma‘il al-Khutubi: Musa ibn Ishaaq al-Ansari narrated to us: Sa‘id ibn ‘Amr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaaidah narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ishaaq, from ‘Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibrahim at-Taymi, from Sulaim al-Muharibi, from Yazid at-Taymi, from Abu Dharr, who said: “Temporary marriage was permitted for us out of fear and for the sake of war.” [Da‘if]"
"14184","(14178) It was narrated that Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Faqih narrated: Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan, Abu al-Shaykh al-Asbahani, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad narrated to us: ‘Amr ibn ‘Ali and Bakkar ibn Qutaibah narrated to us: Mu‘ammal narrated to us: Ikrimah ibn ‘Ammar narrated to us: Sa‘id al-Maqbari narrated to us from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: “We set out with the Messenger of Allah – may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him – on the expedition of Tabook, and we encamped at Thaniyyah al-Wada‘. We saw women weeping, so he said: ‘What is this?’ They said: ‘These are women whom their husbands enjoyed temporarily and then divorced them.’ Thereupon, the Messenger of Allah – may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him – said: ‘Indeed, temporary marriage, divorce, the waiting period, and inheritance have been abolished.’” \nThis is also narrated by Ishaaq al-Hanzali and a group of narrators from Mu‘ammal ibn Isma‘il. [Sahih]"
"14185","(14179) It was narrated that Sa‘id ibn al-Musayyab said: “Inheritance abrogated temporary marriage.” \nSufyan narrated: “Some of our companions narrated from al-Hakam ibn ‘Utaybah, from ‘Abdillah ibn Mas‘oud, who said: ‘The waiting period, divorce, and inheritance abrogated it.’ Al-‘Adani – meaning temporary marriage – said this.” \nHajjaj ibn Artaa also narrated from al-Hakam, from the companions of ‘Abdillah, from ‘Abdillah ibn Mas‘oud, who said: “Temporary marriage is abrogated; it was abrogated by divorce, dower, the waiting period, and inheritance.” [Sahih, though weak in some aspects]"
"14186","(14180) It was narrated that Abu ‘Amr al-Adib narrated: Abu Bakr al-Isma‘ili narrated to us, mentioning the hadith with its chain from ‘Abdillah ibn Mas‘oud regarding temporary marriage. ‘Uqaybah said: “Abu Mu‘awiyah narrated to us from Isma‘il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays, from ‘Abdillah, this hadith, and he said at the end: ‘Then it was abandoned.’” \nIn the hadith of ibn al-Musaffa from ibn ‘Uyaynah, from Isma‘il, at the end: “Then its prohibition came after.” \nIn the hadith of ‘Abdur-Razzaq from Ma‘mar, from Isma‘il, from Qays, concerning the abrogation of that – meaning temporary marriage. [Sahih]"
"14187","(14181) It was narrated that Ali ibn ‘Umar al-Hafiz narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Daud narrated to us: Ya‘qoub ibn Sufyan narrated to us: ibn Bukayr narrated to us: ‘Abdillah ibn Lah‘iyah narrated to us from Musa ibn Ayyub, from Iyas ibn ‘Amer, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of Allah – may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him – forbade temporary marriage. He said: ‘It was only permitted for those who could not afford permanent marriage; but when permanent marriage, divorce, the waiting period, and inheritance were established between husband and wife, it was abrogated.’” [Sahih, though weak in some aspects]"
"14188","(14182) It was narrated that Hasan ibn Sulaiman al-Kufi narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Abdillah al-Hadrami, from Isma‘il ibn Bahram, from al-Ashja‘i, from Bassam al-Sayrafi, who said: “I asked Ja‘far ibn Muhammad about temporary marriage and described it to him, so he said to me: ‘That is fornication.’” [Da‘if]"
"14189","(14183) It was narrated that Ali ibn Ahmad ibn ‘Abdann narrated: Ahmad ibn ‘Ubayd narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn ‘Abdillah narrated to us: Abu ‘Umar narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us from Qatadah, from ‘Amer ash-Sha‘bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of Allah – may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him – cursed those who make temporary marriage lawful and those upon whom it is made lawful.” [Sahih]"
"14190","(14184) It was narrated that Ali al-Rudhpari narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Dassah narrated to us: Abu Daud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Isma‘il narrated from ‘Amer, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. Isma‘il said: “I believe he elevated it to the Prophet – may Allah’s peace and blessings be upon him – who said: ‘Cursed are those who make temporary marriage lawful and those upon whom it is made lawful.’” [Sahih, though weak in some aspects]"
"14191","(14185) Abū Saʿīd — Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl — informed us. Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us. Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Zubayrī, Abū Aḥmad — narrated to us. Sufyān — narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Muḥammad — Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr ibn Janāḥ al-Qāḍī in al-Kūfah — informed us. Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym — narrated to us. Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim — informed us. Abū Nuʿaym — narrated to us. Sufyān, from Abū Qays, from al-Huzayl ibn Shuraḥbīl, from ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cursed the woman who joins hair (al-wāṣilah) and the one who has it joined (al-mūtaṣilah), the woman who tattoos (al-wāshimah) and the one who is tattooed (al-mūtashimah), the consumer of ribā and the one who feeds it, and the one who makes ḥalāl (al-muḥill) and the one for whom it is made ḥalāl (al-muḥallal lahu). This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū Nuʿaym. And in the narration of al-Zubayrī, it says: al-mawshūmah (the tattooed woman), and he said: al-mawṣūlah (the woman whose hair is joined), and he said: and the one who feeds it (muṭʿimahu).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"
"14192","(14186) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us. Muʿallā, meaning Ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Miswarī, from ʿUthmān ibn Muḥammad, from al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah has cursed the one who makes ḥalāl (al-muḥill) and the one for whom it is made ḥalāl (al-muḥallal lahu).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"14193","(14187) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us. ʿUthmān ibn Ṣāliḥ — narrated to us. He said: I heard Layth ibn Saʿd saying: Mushriḥ ibn Hāʿān, Abū al-Muṣʿab, said: I heard ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir saying: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Shall I not inform you of the borrowed billy goat (al-tays al-mustaʿār)?\"" They said: \""Yes"," O Messenger of Allah! Who is it?\"" He said: \""The one who makes ḥalāl (al-muḥill). Allah has cursed the one who makes ḥalāl and the one for whom it is made ḥalāl.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in wording. Allah cursed the one who makes ḥalāl.]"""
"14194","(14188) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me. Abū Bakr — Muḥammad ibn al-Muʾammal — narrated to us. al-Faḍl ibn Muḥammad — narrated to us. Abū Ṣāliḥ — narrated to us. Layth ibn Saʿd — said: I heard Mushriḥ ibn Hāʿān narrating from ʿUqbah ibn ʿĀmir, and he mentioned it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in wording. Allah cursed the one who makes ḥalāl.]"
"14195","(14189) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us. Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī — narrated to us. Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam — narrated to us. Abū Ghassān — Muḥammad ibn Muṭarrif al-Madanī — from ʿUmar ibn Nāfiʿ, from his father, that he said: A man came to Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) and asked him about a man who had divorced his wife three times, and then her brother married her without his consultation, in order to make her ḥalāl for his brother. Is she permissible for the first husband? He said: \No"," except through a marriage of genuine desire (nikāḥ raghabah). We used to consider this as fornication (sifāḥ) during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"14196","(14190) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr — narrated to us. Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿUrubah, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Mughīrah ibn Nawfal, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he was asked about making a woman ḥalāl for her husband, and he said: \That is fornication (al-sifāḥ).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"14197","(14191) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā al-Sukkarī in Baghdād — informed us. Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār — narrated to us. Saʿdān ibn Naṣr — narrated to us. Abū Muʿāwiyah, from al-Aʿmash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rāfiʿ, from Qabīṣah ibn Jābir, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \No one who makes ḥalāl (muḥill) or for whom it is made ḥalāl (muḥallal lahu) is brought to me except that I will stone them both.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"14198","(14192) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us. Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us. Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us. Layth ibn Saʿd — narrated to me. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from Abū Marzūq al-Tujībī, that a man came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) during his caliphate while he was mounted, and he asked him, saying: \I have a need of yours"," O Commander of the Faithful.\"" He said: \""I am in a hurry now. If you wish"," ride behind me so that I may attend to your need.\"" So he rode behind him and said: \""A neighbor of mine divorced his wife in his anger and has faced hardship. I wished to sacrifice myself and my wealth"," so that I may marry her"," cohabit with her"," and then divorce her"," so that she may return to her first husband.\"" ʿUthmān said to him: \""Do not marry her except with a marriage of genuine desire (nikāḥ raghabah).\""\n\n[Ḥasan.]"""
"14199","(14193) Abū ʿAbd Allāh and Abū Bakr — both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās — narrated to us. Muḥammad — narrated to us. Abū al-Aswad and Muʿallā — both said: Ibn Lahīʿah — informed us. Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Sulaymān ibn Yasār, that the matter of a man who had married a woman in order to make her ḥalāl for her husband was brought to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him). He separated the two of them and said: \She will not return to him except through a marriage of genuine desire (nikāḥ raghabah)"," without deception (ghayr dulsah).\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"14200","(14194) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me. ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh — informed me. Yazīd ibn al-Haytham — informed me that Ibrāhīm ibn Abī al-Layth — narrated to them, saying: al-Ashjaʿī — narrated to us. Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from al-Zuhrī, who said: \When a man marries her in order to make her ḥalāl for him"," then this is the one who makes ḥalāl (al-muḥill) and the one for whom it is made ḥalāl (al-muḥallal lahu)"," and it is not permissible.\""\n\n[Very weak (Ḍaʿīf jiddan).]"""
"14201","(14195) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Hishām narrated from Qatādah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Ṣāliḥ ibn Abī Ṭāhir al-ʿAnbarī informed us; my grandfather Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd al-Thaqafī narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Qatādah, from Zurārah ibn Awfá, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah has pardoned my ummah for what occurs within their own selves"," so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAwanah. In the narration of Hishām"," he said: From the Prophet (ﷺ)"," who said: \""Indeed"," Allah—exalted be His praise—has pardoned my ummah.\""\n\nIt was narrated by al-Bukhārī in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm"," and it was narrated by Muslim from Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 127"," Bukhārī 5269]"""
"14202","(14196) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Jurayj, from Sayf ibn Sulaymān, from Mujāhid, who said: A man from Quraysh divorced his wife irrevocably (battata). He passed by an old Bedouin man and his son in the market, who had come for their trade. He said to the young man: \Is there any good in you?\"" Then he moved away from him"," then returned and said the same"," then moved away"," then returned and said the same. He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then show me your hand.\"" So he took him along and informed him of the matter and instructed him to marry her. So he married her and spent the night with her. When he arose in the morning and sought permission"," it was granted to him. He had turned her around from behind. She said: \""By Allah"," if he divorces me"," I will never marry you.\"" This was mentioned to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," so he summoned him and said: \""Had you married her"," I would have done such and such to you","\"" and he threatened him. Then he called her husband and said: \""Keep her.\"" In another place he added"," and he said: \""And if anyone presents you with anything"," inform me of it.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14203","(14197) Abū Saʿīd informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Saʿīd ibn Sālim narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed from Ibn Sīrīn that a woman was irrevocably divorced by her husband. He was a poor Bedouin who sat at the door of the mosque. A woman came to him and said: \Would you like to marry a woman"," spend the night with her"," and then separate from her in the morning?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So it was done. His wife said to him: \""When they say to you in the morning"," 'Separate from her","' do not do that"," for I will remain with you as you wish. Go to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him).\"" When she arose in the morning"," they came to him and she came to him. She said: \""Speak to him"," for you are the ones who brought him.\"" They spoke to him"," but he refused. So he went to ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""Keep your wife. If they suspect you of anything"," come to me.\"" He sent for the woman who had arranged the matter and punished her. Then he would go to ʿUmar in the morning and evening wearing a cloak and say: \""All praise is due to Allah"," who clothed you"," O possessor of the two patches"," a cloak in which you go forth and return.\""\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I heard this ḥadīth as a musnad narration with a connected isnād from Ibn Sīrīn"," who connected it to ʿUmar with a similar meaning.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14204","(14198) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh and Abū al-Ḥasan al-ʿAnazī both said: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; al-Qaʿnabī narrated from Mālik, as he recited to him.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me—and the wording is his—Abū ʿAlī ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I recited to Mālik from Nāfīʿ, the mawlā of ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, that ʿUmar ibn ʿUbayd Allāh wished to marry Ṭalḥah ibn ʿUmar to the daughter of Shaybah ibn Jubayr, so he sent to Abān ibn ʿUthmān to attend the matter, as he was the commander of the Ḥajj. Abān said: \I heard ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him) say: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: The one in iḥrām shall neither marry"," nor be married"," nor propose.'\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1409]"""
"14205","(14199) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfīʿ. He said: Nubayh ibn Wahb narrated to me, saying: ʿUmar ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Maʿmar sent me, as he was proposing for the daughter of Shaybah ibn ʿUthmān for his son. He sent me to Abān ibn ʿUthmān, who was at the season (of Ḥajj). He said: \Do I not consider him a Bedouin? Indeed"," the one in iḥrām neither marries nor is married.\"" ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me of that from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The wording of both their narrations is the same.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Muqaddamī.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"14206","(14200) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī, in wording, both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us; Saʿīd narrated from Maṭar and Yaʿlā ibn Ḥakīm, from Nāfīʿ, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Abān, from ʿUthmān, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The one in iḥrām shall neither marry"," nor be married"," nor propose.\""\n\nHe said: And Saʿīd narrated from both of them—Maṭar and Yaʿlā ibn Ḥakīm—from Nāfīʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," a similar narration"," except that he did not raise it to the Prophet of Allah (ﷺ).\n\nMuslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from two other routes from Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah. He also extracted it from the ḥadīth of Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"," Ayyūb ibn Mūsā"," and Saʿīd ibn Abī Hilāl from Nubayh ibn Wahb.\n\n(T) It was also narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah"," from Nāfīʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," as a marfūʿ narration; and from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn ʿUthmān"," from Nāfīʿ"," from Ibn ʿUmar"," as a marfūʿ narration with doubt. The correct narration from Ibn ʿUmar is mawqūf.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"14207","(14201) As for the ḥadīth: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Dāwūd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed us; ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from Jābir ibn Zayd, Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married Maymūnah while he was in iḥrām.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī extracted it from the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUyaynah from ʿAmr.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1410]"""
"14208","(14202) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr, from Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm—who was the nephew of Maymūnah—that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married Maymūnah while he was in a state of ḥalāl (not in iḥrām).\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14209","(14203) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Bishshār narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us; ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated from Jābir ibn Zayd, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that the Prophet (ﷺ) married while he was in iḥrām. ʿAmr said: I said to Jābir ibn Zayd: \Who do you think she was"," O Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ?\"" He said: \""I think she was Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith.\"" On another occasion he said: \""They say she was Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith.\"" I said to him: \""Ibn Shihāb informed me from Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married Maymūnah while he was in a state of ḥalāl.\""\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Numayr"," from Sufyān"," from ʿAmr"," except that he said: \""So I narrated it to al-Zuhrī"," and he said: 'Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm informed me that he married her while he was in a state of ḥalāl.'\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before the one before it]"""
"14210","(14204) The Shaykh said: Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm narrated it from Maymūnah. It was narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us; al-Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ḥabīb ibn al-Shahīd, from Maymūn ibn Mihrān, from Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm, the nephew of Maymūnah, from Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married me while we were both in a state of ḥalāl"," at Ṣaraf.\""\n\nAbū Dāwūd extracted it in the book of Sunan. Similarly"," Abū Fazārah narrated it from Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm"," who said: \""Maymūnah bint al-Ḥārith narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married her while he was in a state of ḥalāl.\"" From this route"," Muslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ"," and it has already been mentioned in the book of Ḥajj.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1411]"""
"14211","(14205) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq, al-Ḥasan ibn Yaḥyā, and al-Ḥasan ibn Abī Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us; my father narrated to us, saying: I heard Abū Fazārah narrate from Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm from Maymūnah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married her in a state of ḥalāl (i.e., not in iḥrām) and consummated the marriage in a state of ḥalāl. [Ṣaḥīh. Previously cited.]"
"14212","(14206) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Tamtām narrated to us; Abū Ḥudhayfah narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Maymūn, who said: ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz (may Allah have mercy on him) sent me to Yazīd ibn al-Aṣamm — who was the nephew of Maymūnah and the son of the maternal aunt of Ibn ʿAbbās — to ask him about the marriage of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to Maymūnah. He said: He married her while he was in a state of ḥalāl. [Ṣaḥīh. Previously cited.]"
"14213","(14207) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us; Ḥabbān ibn Hilāl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Maṭar — (ḥ) — and Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ and Musaddad both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us; Maṭar al-Warrāq narrated to me; Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Sulaymān ibn Yasār from Abū Rāfiʿ that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married Maymūnah in a state of ḥalāl and consummated the marriage in a state of ḥalāl, and I was the messenger between them both. The wording of both is the same. [Ṣaḥīh. Previously cited under no. 9161.]"
"14214","(14208) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Ṣaffār in Makkah narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbbād informed us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm from Maymūn ibn Mihrān, who said: I asked Ṣafiyyah ibn Shaybah: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) marry Maymūnah while he was in iḥrām? She said: No, rather he married her while he was in a state of ḥalāl. [Ṣaḥīh.]"
"14215","(14209) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Ibn Bashshār narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah from a man from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās was mistaken regarding the marriage of Maymūnah, thinking it occurred while he (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) was in iḥrām. [Ṣaḥīh.]"
"14216","(14210) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Quddūs narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated from ʬāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married Maymūnah while he was in iḥrām. Saʿīd (ibn al-Musayyib) then said: Ibn ʿAbbās was mistaken, and although she was his (Ibn ʿAbbās's) maternal aunt, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not marry her except after he had exited the state of iḥrām. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Quddūs ibn al-Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīh.]"
"14217","(14211) As for the ḥadīth which Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Shaybānī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated from ʿUthmān ibn al-Aswad from Ibn Abī Mulaykah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) married while he was in iḥrām. Thus a group narrated it from Abū ʿĀṣim. However, this is only narrated from Ibn Abī Mulaykah as a mursal (disconnected) report, and the mention of ʿĀʾishah in it is an error. Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī said: I asked Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī (may Allah have mercy on him) about this ḥadīth, and he said: They narrate this ḥadīth from Ibn Abī Mulaykah as mursal. [Munkar (denounced).]"
"14218","(14212) ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated it from Abū ʿĀṣim as mursal, and he said: I said to Abū ʿĀṣim: Did you dictate this to us from the scroll, and there is no mention of ʿĀʾishah in it? He said: Leave ʿĀʾishah aside until I look into it. ʿAmr said: Then I heard some of our companions say that Abū ʿĀṣim said: I looked into it and found it to be mursal. This was reported to me by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ by way of ijāzah (authorization), that Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed them: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Mukram narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us — and he mentioned the ḥadīth and the account. [Ṣaḥīh.]"
"14219","(14213) The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: It has also been narrated through another chain from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), but it is not preserved (maḥfūẓ). Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl al-Ṣayrafī narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Mughīrah from Abū al-Ḍuḥā from Masrūq from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married one of his wives while he was in iḥrām, and he had cupping performed while he was in iḥrām. It was also narrated from Musaddad from Abū ʿAwanah from Mughīrah from Ibrāhīm from al-Aswad from ʿĀʾishah. Abū ʿAbd Allāh said: Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Both of them are in error. What is preserved (al-maḥfūẓ) from Mughīrah is from Shibāk from Abū al-Ḍuḥā from Masrūq from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) as mursal. Thus Jarīr narrated it from Mughīrah as mursal. [Munkar (denounced).]"
"14220","(14214) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us — (ḥ) — and Abū Aḥmad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānjānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥuṣayn from Abī Ghaṭṭān ibn Ṭarīf al-Murrī, who informed him that his father married a woman while he was in iḥrām, so ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) annulled his marriage. [Ṣaḥīh. Narrated by Mālik, no. 781.]"
"14221","(14215) And through these two chains of narration, from Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: \The one in the state of iḥrām (ritual consecration) shall neither contract a marriage himself"," nor shall a marriage be contracted on his behalf"," nor shall he propose marriage for himself nor for another.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14222","(14216) And Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī al-Rāzī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Zāhir ibn Aḥmad informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Ziyād al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Bakr narrated to us; Saʿīd narrated from Maṭar, from al-Ḥasan, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Whoever contracts a marriage while in the state of iḥrām"," we shall take his wife away from him"," and we shall not validate his marriage.\"" And this was the view of al-Ḥasan and Qatāda. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14223","(14217) And it is in what Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ permitted me to narrate from him, from Abū al-ʿAbbās; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad narrated from Qudāma ibn Mūsā, from Shawdhab, that Zayd ibn Thābit annulled the marriage of one in the state of iḥrām. And al-Dārawardī likewise narrated it from Qudāma. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14224","(14218) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated that it reached him from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, Sālim ibn ʿAbdullāh, and Sulaymān ibn Yasār: that they were asked about the marriage of one in the state of iḥrām, and they said: \The one in the state of iḥrām shall neither contract a marriage himself"," nor shall a marriage be contracted on his behalf.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14225","(14219) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated to us; Abū Bukayr, meaning al-Nakhaʿī, narrated from Jamīl ibn Zayd al-Ṭāʾī; ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated and said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married a woman from Banī Ghifār. When she was brought in to him"," he saw on her flank a whiteness (a skin condition)"," so he sent her back to her family and said: 'You have deceived me.'\"" [Very Weak — Ḍaʿīf Jiddan]"""
"14226","(14220) He said: And Abū Aḥmad narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Ḥulwānī narrated to us; Abū Saʿīd al-Ashajj — ʿAbdullāh ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us; Abū Bukayr al-Nakhaʿī — and the name of Abū Bukayr is al-Walīd ibn Bukayr, a Kūfan — narrated from Jamīl ibn Zayd, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) married a woman from Banī Ghifār","\"" and he mentioned it. [Very Weak — Ḍaʿīf Jiddan; previously mentioned]"""
"14227","(14221) And Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Warkānī narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn Ghuṣn narrated from Jamīl ibn Zayd, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) married a woman from Banī Ghifār. When she was brought in to him, he saw on her flank a whiteness, so he turned away from her and said: \Draw your curtain over yourself.\"" And he let her go and took nothing from her.\n\nAbū Aḥmad said: \""And Jamīl ibn Zayd is unique in narrating this hadith"," and the narrators from him are inconsistent regarding this hadith.\"" The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""It was narrated from him thus"," and likewise Ismāʿīl ibn Zakariyyāʾ said it from Jamīl ibn Zayd from Ibn ʿUmar with its meaning. And it was said from him"," from Saʿd ibn Zayd"," who was among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). And it was said from him"," from ʿAbdullāh ibn Kaʿb. And it was said from him"," from Kaʿb ibn Zayd or Zayd ibn Kaʿb.\"" Al-Bukhārī said: \""His hadith is not authentic.\"" [Very Weak — Ḍaʿīf Jiddan]"""
"14228","(14222) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr al-Zāhid narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that he said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Any man who marries a woman who has insanity"," leprosy"," or leucoderma"," and he has intimate relations with her"," then she is entitled to her dower"," and her husband has a claim against her guardian (for compensation).\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14229","(14223) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah al-Harawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najda narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled: \Any woman who is married and has any of these diseases"," and her husband does not know until he has intimate relations with her"," then she is entitled to her dower for what he has enjoyed of her"," and her guardian shall compensate her husband the equivalent of her dower.\"" [Ḍaʿīf; previously mentioned]"""
"14230","(14224) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāda informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sarrāj informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn Marzūq informed us; Shuʿba narrated from Yaḥyā, from Saʿīd, who said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When a man marries a woman who has insanity"," leprosy"," leucoderma"," or a horn-like growth (qarn)"," and he has consummated the marriage with her"," then she is entitled to the dower by virtue of his having touched her"," and it is a debt owed by the guardian.\"" [Ḍaʿīf; previously mentioned]"""
"14231","(14225) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us that al-Rabīʿ informed us that al-Shāfiʿī informed us that Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Abī al-Shaʾthāʾ, who said: \Four defects are not permissible to be left unspecified in a sale or a marriage unless they are explicitly identified; if they are identified"," then it is valid: insanity"," leprosy"," leucorrhea"," and qarn (a vaginal obstruction).\""\n\nSaʿīd ibn Manṣūr also narrated it from Sufyān"," except that he said: \""Unless he touches her; if he touches her"," then it is valid.\"" Abū Ḥāzim informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd narrated to us that Sufyān narrated it.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 5/85]"""
"14232","(14226) Abū Ḥāzim informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us that Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from ʿAmr from Jābir ibn Zayd, who said: \Four defects are not permissible in a sale or a marriage: the insane woman"," the leprous woman"," the woman afflicted with leucorrhea"," and the ʿaflāʾ (a woman with an obstruction in her vagina).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr 825]"""
"14233","(14227) Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ also narrated it from Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim from ʿAmr, from the statement of Jābir ibn Zayd, Abī al-Shaʾthāʾ. Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us that Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us that Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Būshanjī informed us that Umayyah ibn Bisṭām informed us that Yazīd ibn Zurayʿ informed us that Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Jābir ibn Zayd, and he mentioned it, adding: \Unless he touches them.\"""""
"14234","(14228) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us that Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim and Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from Jābir ibn Zayd from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: \Four defects are not permissible in a sale or a marriage: the insane woman"," the leprous woman"," the woman afflicted with leucorrhea"," and the ʿaflāʾ (a woman with an obstruction in her vagina).\""\n\nMālik ibn Yaḥyā also narrated it from ʿAbd al-Wahhāb"," marfūʿ (elevated) to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both).\n\n[Ḥasan]"""
"14235","(14229) It was narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him), as Abū Ḥāzim al-ʿAbdawī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah al-Harawī informed us that Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us that Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us that Sufyān narrated from Muṭarrif from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Any man who marries a woman and she has leucorrhea"," or insanity"," or leprosy"," or qarn (a vaginal obstruction)"," then her husband has the option"," so long as he has not touched her; if he wishes"," he may keep her"," and if he wishes"," he may divorce her. But if he has touched her"," then she is entitled to the mahr in exchange for what he has enjoyed of her private part.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr 821]"""
"14236","(14230) He said: And Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us that Hushaym informed us that Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated from al-Shaʿbī that he said: \That is when he has consummated the marriage with her.\"" He said: \""And if he knew of that before consummating the marriage with her"," then if he wishes"," he may keep her"," and if he wishes"," he may separate from her without a divorce.\""\n\nAl-Thawrī narrated it from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: \""When a man marries a woman and finds her to be afflicted with insanity"," or leucorrhea"," or leprosy"," or qarn (a vaginal obstruction)"," and he consummates the marriage with her"," then she is his wife; if he wishes"," he may keep her"," and if he wishes"," he may divorce her.\"" Wākīʿ added on the authority of al-Thawrī: \""If he has not consummated the marriage with her"," they shall be separated"," as though he has nullified his option by consummating the marriage with her. And Allah knows best.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14237","(14231) Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānjānī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us that Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us that Ibn Bukayr informed us that Mālik informed us that it reached him from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, who said: \Any man who marries a woman while he is afflicted with insanity or some other affliction"," then she is given the choice; if she wishes"," she may separate"," and if she wishes"," she may remain.\""\n\n[Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14238","(14232) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us that Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm al-Baghawī informed us in Baghdād that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rūḥ al-Madāʾinī informed us that ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar informed us that Yūnus narrated from al-Zuhrī from Sālim from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no contagion (ʿadwā) and no evil omen (ṭīrah).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Yūnus ibn Yazīd.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2225]"""
"14239","(14233) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlānī informed us that Ibn Wahb informed us that Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād that Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us that Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī informed us that ʿAffān informed us that ʿAbd al-Wāḥid informed us that Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no contagion (ʿadwā)"," no owl (hāmah)"," and no ṣafar (the month of Ṣafar being inauspicious).\""\n\nA Bedouin stood up and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," the camels are in the sand like gazelles"," then a mangy camel comes to them and they all become mangy!\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Then who infected the first one?\""\n\nThe wording is that of the ḥadīth of Maʿmar. In the narration of Yūnus"," when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""There is no contagion"," no ṣafar"," and no owl","\"" a Bedouin said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what is the matter with the camels that are in the sand like gazelles"," then a mangy camel comes among them and makes them mangy?\"" He said: \""Then who infected the first one?\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from al-Zuhrī"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2220]"""
"14240","(14234) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both informed us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us that Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us that Ibn Wahb informed me that Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \One who has diseased animals should not bring them near one whose animals are healthy.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it]"""
"14241","(14235) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī informed us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no ʿadwā (contagion)"," no ṣafar"," and no hāmah.\"" A Bedouin then said: \""What is the matter with camels that are in the sand like gazelles"," then a mangy camel mingles with them and they become mangy?\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Then who caused the first one to become mangy?\"" Al-Zuhrī said: A man narrated to me from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""A sick one should not be brought near a healthy one.\"" The man then questioned him and said: \""Did you not narrate to us that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'There is no ʿadwā"," no ṣafar"," and no hāmah'?\"" He said: \""I did not narrate that to you.\"" Al-Zuhrī said: Abū Salamah told me: \""He did narrate it"," and I did not hear Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) forget any other hadith besides this one.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from another route from Maʿmar with its meaning. [Authentic. Preceded before it.]"""
"14242","(14236) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Muzanī informed me: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā informed us: Abū al-Yamān informed me: Shuʿayb narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān informed me that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \There is no ʿadwā (contagion).\"" Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) report that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""A sick one should not be brought near a healthy one.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and others added therein the questioning of al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Dhubāb to Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) about that"," and the statement of Abū Salamah. [Authentic. Preceded before it.]"""
"14243","(14237) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Khālid ibn Khalī informed us: Bishr ibn Shuʿayb narrated from his father, from al-Zuhrī, who informed me: Sinān ibn Abī Sinān al-Duʾalī informed me that Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no ʿadwā (contagion).\"" A man from the Bedouins stood up and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what about camels that are in the sand like gazelles"," then a mangy camel comes to them and they all become mangy?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Then who caused the first one to become mangy?\"" [Authentic. Preceded before it.]"""
"14244","(14238) And with this chain of narration from al-Zuhrī, who said: Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I heard Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) report that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A sick one should not be brought near a healthy one.\"" Al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Dhubāb al-Dawsī said to him: \""You used to narrate to us that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'There is no ʿadwā.'\"" He (Abū Hurayrah) denied that. Al-Ḥārith said: \""Yes"," you used to inform us of that from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" So he and Abū Hurayrah disputed until their dispute became severe. Abū Hurayrah became angry and spoke in Ethiopian (Abyssinian)"," then said to al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Dhubāb: \""Do you know what I said?\"" Al-Ḥārith said: \""No.\"" Abū Hurayrah said: \""I said 'abaytu' (I refuse)"," meaning by that: I did not narrate as you say.\"" Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: Then Abū Hurayrah stood firm on what he was informing us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding his statement: \""A sick one should not be brought near a healthy one","\"" and abandoned what he used to inform us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding his statement: \""There is no ʿadwā.\"" Abū Salamah said: \""I do not know whether Abū Hurayrah forgot what he used to inform us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) — 'There is no ʿadwā' — or what his affair was"," except that I did not experience from him a word that he forgot after he narrated it to us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," apart from his denial of what he used to narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) regarding his statement: 'There is no ʿadwā.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dārimī"," from Abū al-Yamān"," from Shuʿayb; and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Abū al-Yamān in abridged form. [Authentic. Preceded before it.]"""
"14245","(14239) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from Bukayr, from Abū Isḥāq, the freedman of Banī Hāshim, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no ʿadwā (contagion)"," and a sick one should not be brought near a healthy one; rather"," the healthy one may settle wherever he wishes.\"" It was said: \""What is the reason for that"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""It is harm.\"" [Weak]"""
"14246","(14240) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Sammāk informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad al-Raqāshī informed us: Bishr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrānī informed us: Mālik narrated from Bukayr ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ashajj, from Abū ʿAṭiyyah al-Ashjaʿī, from Abū Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no ʿadwā (contagion)"," no hāmah"," no ṣafar"," and a sick one should not be brought near a healthy one; rather"," the healthy one may settle wherever he wishes.\"" It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," why is that?\"" He said: \""It is harm.\""\n\nThis is a gharīb (uncommon) narration with this chain"," if al-Raqāshī preserved it. And Allah knows best. [Weak]"""
"14247","(14241) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr al-Khawlānī informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who informed me: ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated from Usāmah ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), that he said: \Indeed this — meaning the plague or the affliction — is a punishment by which some of the nations before you were punished. Then it remained thereafter on the earth"," departing at one time and coming at another. So whoever hears of it in a land"," let him not approach it"," and if it occurs in a land while he is therein"," let him not flee from it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah"," from Ibn Wahb. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī narrated it"," no. 3473.]"""
"14248","(14242) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb, who informed me: ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to him that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated to him: He was with ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) when he set out for Shām. He returned with the people from Sargh. His commanders over the military detachments met him, and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ and his companions (may Allah be pleased with them) met him, and the affliction had struck Shām. ʿUmar said: \Gather for me the early Muhājirūn.\"" So I gathered them for him"," and he consulted them"," and they differed. Some of them said: \""Return with the people and do not advance them toward this epidemic.\"" And some of them said: \""It is the decree of Allah"," and you set out for a purpose"," so do not turn back from it.\"" He commanded them"," and they departed. Then he said: \""Call the Anṣār for me.\"" So I called them"," and he consulted them"," and they followed the way of the Muhājirūn and differed as they differed. He commanded them"," and they departed. Then he said: \""Call for me those who were present here from the elders of the Muhājirūn of the Conquest.\"" So I called them"," and he consulted them"," and their opinion unanimously agreed that he should return with the people. So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) announced to the people: \""I am departing in the morning on my mount"," so depart in the morning on your mounts. Indeed"," I am proceeding to what I see; so watch what I command you and carry it out.\"" He departed in the morning on his mount. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) then mounted and said to the people: \""I am returning.\"" Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ (may Allah be pleased with him) — who disliked contradicting him — said: \""Are you fleeing from the decree of Allah?\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) became angry and said: \""Were it other than you who said this"," O Abū ʿUbaydah! Yes"," I am fleeing from the decree of Allah to the decree of Allah. Tell me"," if a man descends into a valley that has two sides — one barren and the other fertile — is it not the case that if he grazes the barren side"," he grazes it by the decree of Allah"," and if he grazes the fertile side"," he grazes it by the decree of Allah?\"" He said: \""Then he was alone with Abū ʿUbaydah"," and they conferred for a while. Then ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) came — he had been absent on some of his needs — and came while the people were differing. He said: \""I have knowledge regarding this.\"" ʿUmar said: \""What is it?\"" He said: \""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'When you hear of it in a land"," do not advance toward it"," and if it occurs in a land while you are therein"," let not fleeing expel you from it.'\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) praised Allah and returned"," and commanded the people to return.\n\nIbn Shihāb said: Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah both said: ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) only returned with the people from Sargh on the basis of the hadith of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir and Ḥarmalah"," from Ibn Wahb; and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the hadith of Mālik"," from Ibn Shihāb. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī"," nos. 5729"," 5730"," 6973.]"""
"14249","(14243) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Al-Asfāṭī — meaning al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl — informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated from Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that a Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \My wife has given birth to a black boy.\"" He (ﷺ) said: \""Do you have camels?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""What are their colors?\"" He said: \""Red.\"" He said: \""Is there among them a grey one?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""How is that?\"" He said: \""Perhaps a vein has drawn it out.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Perhaps your son has had a vein draw him out.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways and others; and Muslim narrated it from other routes from Ibn Shihāb. [Authentic. Al-Bukhārī"," no. 5305.]"""
"14250","(14244) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Rajāʾ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us: Sharīk ibn ʿAbd Allāh and Hushaym ibn Bashīr narrated from Yaʿlā ibn ʿAṭāʾ, from ʿAmr ibn al-Sharīd, from his father, who said: In the delegation of Thaqīf there was a leper. The Prophet (ﷺ) sent word to him: \Indeed"," we have accepted your pledge of allegiance"," so return.\"" [Authentic. Muslim"," no. 2231.]"""
"14251","(14245) It was narrated that Abu al-‘Abbas ibn al-Fadl ibn ‘Ali ibn Muhammad al-Isfarayini narrated: It was narrated to us that Bashr ibn Ahmad narrated: It was narrated to us that Ibrahim ibn ‘Ali narrated: It was narrated to us that Yahya ibn Yahya narrated: It was narrated to us that Husaym narrated it in a similar manner. This hadith was narrated by Muslim in his Sahih on the authority of Yahya ibn Yahya and on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah. We have narrated it in the chapter on the [prescribed] marriage portion on the authority of Abu Hurayrah, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “Flee from the leper as you would flee from a lion.” [Sahih – graded as authentic and transmitted before this point]"
"14252","(14246) It was narrated that Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran and Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Bazzaz, from Baghdad, said: It was narrated to us that Abu Muhammad ‘Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Fahhi narrated: It was narrated to us that Abu Yahya ibn Masrach narrated: It was narrated to us that Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Jari narrated: It was narrated to us that ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated on the authority of Muhammad ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-A‘raj, on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There is no contagious disease, nor is there any menses that is unclean, nor is the month of Safar unclean. Flee from the leper as you would flee from a lion.” [Sahih – agreed upon]"
"14253","(14247) It was narrated to us that Abu Bakr ibn Furak narrated: It was narrated to us that ‘Abd Allah ibn Ja‘far narrated: It was narrated to us that Yunus ibn Habib narrated: It was narrated to us that Abu Dawood narrated: It was narrated to us that ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu al-Zinad narrated on the authority of Muhammad ibn ‘Abd Allah al-Qurashi, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: “Do not stare at them.” Meaning the lepers. [Da‘if – graded as weak and transmitted before this point]"
"14254","(14248) It was narrated to us that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan narrated: It was narrated to us that Ahmad ibn ‘Ubayd al-Saffar narrated: It was narrated to us that ‘Ubayd ibn Sharik narrated: It was narrated to us that ibn Abu Maryam narrated: It was narrated to us that ibn Abu al-Zinad narrated to me: Muhammad ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr narrated on the authority of Fathimah bint al-Husayn ibn ‘Ali ibn Abu Talib, on the authority of ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not stare at them for long.” [Da‘if – graded as weak and transmitted before this point]"
"14255","(14249) It was narrated to us that Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan narrated: It was narrated to us that Ahmad ibn ‘Ubayd al-Saffar narrated: It was narrated to us that Isma‘il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated: It was narrated to us that Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated: It was narrated to us that al-Mughirah ibn ‘Abd al-Rahman al-Makhzumi narrated on the authority of ‘Abd Allah ibn Sa‘id ibn Abu Hind, on the authority of Muhammad ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Amr, on the authority of his mother Fathimah bint al-Husayn, on the authority of ‘Abd Allah ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do not stare at the lepers for long.” It was said of it on the authority of his father. [Da‘if – graded as weak and transmitted before this point]"
"14256","(14250) It was narrated that Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-‘Alawi, may Allah have mercy on him, narrated: It was narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Wahhab al-Naysaburi narrated: It was narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Isma‘il al-Sayigh narrated: It was narrated to us that Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated: It was narrated to us that Mufaddal ibn Fadalah narrated on the authority of Habib ibn al-Shahid, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabr ibn ‘Abd Allah (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) took the hand of a leper and placed it in a plate and said: “Eat, in the Name of Allah, and place your trust in Him.” [Munkar – rejected]"
"14257","(14251) It was narrated to us that Abu Muhammad ‘Abd Allah ibn Yussuf al-Asbahani narrated: It was narrated to us that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Uqbah al-Shayban narrated from Kufah: It was narrated to us that Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Marwazi narrated: It was narrated to us that Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated: It was narrated to us that Hammad ibn Yahya narrated: It was narrated to us that Ishaq ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn Abu Talhah narrated: It was narrated to us that ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu ‘Amr narrated that Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: “There were three people among the Children of Israel who were the most afflicted, the most wretched, and the most blind. Allah, Exalted be He, desired to test them, so He sent an angel to them. He came to the most afflicted and said: ‘What do you like most?’ He said: ‘A good complexion and good skin.’ The people had reviled him. So the angel touched him, and his revilement left him, and he was given a good complexion and good skin.” The hadith was narrated by Muslim in his Sahih on the authority of Shayban ibn Farrukh. [Sahih – narrated by Bukhari, hadith number 3464]"
"14258","(14252) It was narrated to us that Abu Nasr ‘Umar ibn ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn ‘Umar ibn Qatadah narrated: It was narrated to us that Abu ‘Amr ibn Nujayd narrated: It was narrated to us that Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated: It was narrated to us that ibn Bukayr narrated: It was narrated to us that Malik narrated on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Sa‘id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “If a man marries a woman who is afflicted with madness, leprosy, or scabies, and he has relations with her, then the dowry is for her, and that is a burden upon her guardian.” [Da‘if – weak]"
"14259","(14253) It was narrated to us that Abu Sa‘id ibn Abu ‘Amr narrated: It was narrated to us that Abu al-‘Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya‘qub narrated: It was narrated to us that ar-Rabi‘ ibn Sulayman said: The Shafi‘i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Yahya ibn ‘Abbad narrated on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Budayl ibn Maysarah, on the authority of Abu al-Wadih, that two brothers married two sisters. Each of them was given one of the sisters as a gift, and each of them had relations with her. Then ‘Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) judged that each of them should pay the dowry, and that it should be returned to the one who was deceived. [Hasan – good]"
"14260","(14254) It was narrated to us that Abu Sa‘id narrated: It was narrated to us that Abu al-‘Abbas narrated: It was narrated to us that ar-Rabi‘ narrated: It was narrated to us that al-Shafi‘i narrated: It was narrated to us that Malik narrated that it was reported to him that either ‘Umar or ‘Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them both) judged that if one of them had relations with a slave woman who had deceived him, and she became pregnant and gave birth to children, then he should ransom the children for the same number. Malik, may Allah have mercy on him, said: “And that returns to the judgment, for a slave is not given in exchange for something similar or like it, and for that reason it returns to the judgment.” The Sheikh said: “And whoever says that it does not return by way of the dowry, while it is the saying of al-Shafi‘i in the new [case], he cites as evidence what we have narrated on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ‘If a woman is married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid. If she is afflicted, then she has the right to the dowry for what she has consummated from her husband.’” Al-Shafi‘i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: “Then if he gives her the dowry in the invalid marriage, in every case, and does not return it to her, and she is the one who deceived him, and no one else, then in the valid marriage in which the husband has the choice, it is preferable that the dowry be for the woman, and if it is for the woman, it is not permissible that she be the one who receives it, and her guardian is burdened with it.” ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) judged in the case of the woman who was married during her waiting period that if she was afflicted, then she has the right to the dowry. The Sheikh said: “He was in the House of Wealth, then he retracted from that.” Masruq said: “‘Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) retracted from his saying regarding the dowry and made it for her for what she has consummated from her husband.” [Da‘if – weak]"
"14261","It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak narrated to us: ‘Abd Allah ibn Ja‘far al-Asbahani narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shu‘bah narrated to ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she intended to purchase Barirah and free her, but her owners stipulated the condition of *wilayah* (guardianship). ‘A’ishah mentioned this to the Prophet (peace be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “Purchase her and free her, for *wilayah* belongs to the one who frees her.” She said: “Then meat was brought to her, and he (the Prophet) asked: ‘What is this?’ They said: ‘This is from the sacrifice of Barirah, which she has given in charity on her behalf.’ The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ‘It is a charity on her behalf and a gift for us.’ He said: “And she was permitted to choose, and her husband was a free man.” Shu‘bah said: “Then I later asked him, and he said: ‘I do not know whether she was free or a slave.’ Shu‘bah said: “So I said to Simak ibn Harb: ‘I fear that I should not ask you about the chain of narration, so ask him yourself.’ Simak said: ‘And he was known for his character.’ Simak then said to him after he had narrated: “Abu Simak narrated this to you from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her).” ‘Abd al-Rahman said: “Yes.” Then when Simak left, he said to Shu‘bah: “O Shu‘bah, I have testified on your behalf concerning him.”\n\nThis hadith is narrated by Muslim in his *Sahih* on the authority of Ahmad ibn ‘Uthman al-Naufali, through Abu Dawud, and he and al-Bukhari have narrated it from the hadith of Ghandar through Shu‘bah, without mentioning the statement of Simak ibn Harb. Simak ibn Harb has narrated it, and it has been established through him that her husband was a slave. [Sahih, without his saying]\n\n(b) Simak ibn Harb narrated to ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim that her husband was a slave."
"14262","It was narrated to us by Abu al-Hasan: Muhammad ibn Ya‘qub ibn Ahmad al-Faqih al-Tabaranī narrated to us: Abu al-Nadr: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqih narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadhr, son of Mu‘awiyah ibn ‘Amr, narrated to us: my grandfather Mu‘awiyah ibn ‘Amr narrated to us: Zaydah ibn Qudamah al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb narrated to ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she purchased Barirah from some of the Ansar, but they stipulated the condition of *wilayah*. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “*Wilayah* belongs to the one who possesses the benefit.” He said: “And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) permitted her, and her husband was a slave, and she gave meat to ‘A’ishah as a gift.” The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: “If you had cooked this meat for us.” ‘A’ishah said: “It is to be given in charity on behalf of Barirah.” He said: “It is a charity on her behalf and a gift for us.” [Sahih, earlier precedence]"
"14263","It was narrated to us by Abu ‘Abd Allah al-Hāfiẓ: Abu ‘Amr ibn Ja‘far narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us: Husayn ibn ‘Ali narrated to Zaydah, and he narrated it in a manner similar to the previous one. Muslim narrated it in his *Sahih* on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah."
"14264","It was narrated to us by Muhammad ibn ‘Abd Allah al-Hāfiẓ: Abu al-‘Abbās: Muhammad ibn Ya‘qub narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: ‘Uthman ibn ‘Umar narrated to us: Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated to us: al-Qāsim ibn Muhammad narrated to ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: “Barirah was a *muqatabah* (a slave who has purchased her freedom) from some of the Ansar.” He narrated the hadith concerning *wilayah* and concerning the gift. She said: “And she was under a slave, but when she was freed, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said to her: ‘If you wish, you may remain under this slave; and if you wish, you may separate.’” This confirms the narration of Simak ibn Harb, and it has been said through Usāmah through al-Zuhri through al-Qāsim ibn Muhammad through ‘A’ishah in a summarized form, and similarly ‘Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated it through ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Sahih, earlier precedence]"
"14265","It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hārith al-Faqih al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Muhammad: ‘Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja‘far ibn Hayyan, known as Abu al-Shaykh, narrated to us: Abu Ya‘la narrated to us: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us: Jarir narrated to Hishām ibn ‘Urwah, from his father, from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: “Her husband was a slave, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) permitted her, and she chose herself, and even if he had been free, he would not have permitted her.”\n\nThis hadith is narrated by Muslim in his *Sahih* on the authority of Abu Khaythamah, Zuhayr ibn Harb, in this manner. [Sahih, earlier precedence]"
"14266","It was narrated to us by Abu ‘Abd Allah al-Hāfiẓ: Abu al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salāmah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrāhīm, and Muhammad ibn Bashār, and Muhammad ibn al-Muthannā said: Ishaq narrated to us, while the other two said: Abu Hishām al-Makhzūmī narrated to us: Wahb narrated to us: ‘Ubaid Allah narrated to Yazid ibn Rūmān, from ‘Urwah, from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: “The husband of Barirah was a slave.”\n\nThis hadith is narrated by Muslim in his *Sahih* on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muhammad ibn Bashār. [Sahih, Muslim 1504]"
"14267","It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr ibn al-Hārith: ‘Ali ibn ‘Umar al-Hāfiẓ narrated to us: Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Junayd narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Manṣūr al-Tūsī narrated to us: Ya‘qūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Sa‘d narrated to me: my father narrated to me: Ibn Ishaq narrated to me: both Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri and Hishām ibn ‘Urwah narrated to me: from ‘Urwah, from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: “Barirah was with a slave, then she was freed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) made her affair fall into her hands.”\n\nAlso, Ibn Ishaq narrated it through Abān ibn Ṣāliḥ, from Mujāhid, from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Sahih, earlier precedence]"
"14268","It was narrated to us by Abu Bakr ibn al-Hārith al-Faqih: ‘Ali ibn ‘Umar al-Hāfiẓ narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ma‘n al-Fārisī narrated to us: Shādhān ibn Māhān narrated to us: Shibān narrated to us: ‘Uthman ibn Miqsam narrated to Yahyā ibn Sa‘īd, from ‘Amrah, from ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) permitted her, and her husband was a slave. [Sahih, earlier precedence]"
"14269","It was narrated to us by the Faqih Abu al-Qāsim: ‘Ubaid Allah ibn ‘Umar ibn ‘Ali al-Fāmī in Baghdad in the Masjid al-Rusafa narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salmān narrated to us: ‘Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad narrated to us: ‘Abd al-Samad ibn ‘Abd al-Wārith narrated to us: Shu‘bah narrated to Qatādah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: “The husband of Barirah was a black slave, named Mughīth, as if I were seeing him wandering the streets of Madinah.” [Sahih, Bukhari 5282]"
"14270","It was narrated to us by Abu al-Qāsim al-Faqih: Ahmad ibn Salmān narrated to us: Ja‘far al-Tayālisī narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sinān narrated to us: Hammām narrated to us: Qatādah narrated to us: Ikrimah narrated to Ibn ‘Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them), that the husband of Barirah was a black slave, named Mughīth. He said: “So it is as if I see him following her through the streets of Madinah, shedding tears from his eyes.” He said: “And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) passed four judgments in this matter.” He said: “Indeed, *wilayah* belongs to the one who frees her, and he permitted her, and he commanded her to observe the *‘iddah* (waiting period).” He said: “And she should give in charity on her behalf, so she gave it to ‘A’ishah, and she mentioned that to the Prophet (peace be upon him), so he said: ‘It is a charity for her and a gift for us.’” Bukhari narrated it in his *Sahih* through Abu al-Walīd and Shu‘bah and Hammām in a summarized form, saying: “I saw him as a slave, meaning the husband of Barirah.” [Sahih, earlier precedence]\n\n(b) Abu Walīd narrated through Shu‘bah and Hammām in a summarized form: “I saw him as a slave, meaning the husband of Barirah.”"
"14271","It was narrated that 'Abd al-'A'la ibn Hammad narrated from Wuhayb, who narrated from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: \This was Mughith"," the slave of Banu Fulan. I seem to see him following her in the streets of Medina"," weeping for her"," meaning Barirah.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih on the authority of 'Abd al-'A'la ibn Hammad."""
"14272","It was narrated that 'Abdullah ibn Sulaiman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated from 'Umar ibn Shabah, who narrated from 'Abd al-Wahhab, who narrated from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: \The husband of Barirah was a slave"," a black man. He was called Mughith"," the slave of Banu Fulan. I seem to see him following her in the streets of Medina"," weeping.\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih on the authority of Qutaybah on the authority of 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi."""
"14273","It was narrated that Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Karim narrated from Bundar, who said: \And Abu Bakr narrated to me"," and al-Haytham al-Duri narrated to me"," Ahmad al-Dawraqi narrated to me"," and 'Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated from Khalid"," from Ikrimah"," from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them)"," who said: \""The husband of Barirah was a slave"," called Mughith. I seem to see him following her"," weeping"," and his tears are falling on his beard. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him): 'Do you not marvel at the love of Mughith for Barirah"," and the hatred of Barirah for Mughith?' Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: 'If you return to him"," then indeed he is your son's father.' She said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," do you command me?' He said: 'No"," I am only advising.' She said: 'Then I have no need for him.'\""\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih on the authority of Muhammad on the authority of 'Abd al-Wahhab."""
"14274","It was narrated that Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-'Ala' narrated from al-Harith ibn 'Abdullah al-Khazin, who narrated from Abu Hafs al-Abbar, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: \The husband of Barirah was a slave.\""\n\nThis hadith is weak."""
"14275","Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Ibn Abi Layla, from 'Ata', who said: \The husband of Barirah was a slave"," called Mughith.\""\n\nNarrated by Abu Bakr: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated from Abu Nasr al-'Iraqi"," who narrated from Sufyan ibn Muhammad"," who narrated from 'Ali ibn al-Hasan"," who narrated from 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid"," who narrated from Sufyan"," who mentioned it.\n\nThis hadith is weak."""
"14276","It was narrated that Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani, who narrated from 'Affan ibn Muslim, who narrated from Wuhayb, who narrated from 'Ubaidullah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Safiyyah bint Abi 'Ubaid, that the husband of Barirah was a slave.\n\nThis chain of narration is sound."
"14277","It was narrated that 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran from Baghdad narrated from Abu al-Hasan: 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated from Ibn Abi Maryam, who narrated from al-Firaybi, who narrated from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Awsad, from 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the husband of Barirah was free, and that she was given a choice when she was freed, and she said: \I do not like to be with him as my guardian in such and such a way.\""\n\nThis is how al-Thawri included it in the hadith on the authority of 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her)."""
"14278","It was narrated that 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said: \A slave woman should not be given a choice when she is freed"," except if her husband is a slave.\""\n\nThis hadith is sound."""
"14279","It was narrated that Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated from Muhammad ibn Ya'qub, who narrated from Muhammad ibn Sinan, who narrated from 'Ubaidullah ibn 'Abd al-Majid, who narrated from Ibn Mawhab, who said: \I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrate from 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," that she had a slave boy and a slave girl"," and a husband. She said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I wish to free them both.' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: 'If you free them both"," then begin with the man before the woman.'\""\n\nIbn Mawhab is 'Ubaidullah ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mawhab"," who is unique in this narration.\n\nThis hadith is weak."""
"14280","It was narrated that 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran from Baghdad narrated from Abu al-Hasan: 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Misri narrated from Ibn Abi Maryam, who narrated from al-Firaybi, who narrated from Sufyan, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Awsad, from 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the husband of Barirah was free, and that she was given a choice when she was freed, and she said: \I do not like to be with him as my guardian in such and such a way.\""\n\nThis is how al-Thawri included it in the hadith on the authority of 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her).\n\nThis hadith is sound."""
"14281","It is related that her husband was free, not from the statement of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, but from the statement of Aswad, as a proof of what Abu ‘Abd Allah the narrator of hadiths has informed us. Abu ‘Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, the narrator of hadiths, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ya‘qub the narrator of hadiths, narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Abu ‘Umar and al-Hajabi said: Abu ‘Awana narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Aswad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she bought Barirah and her people stipulated the condition of the right of the master. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have bought Barirah to free her, and indeed her people stipulate the right of the master. She said: Free her, for the right of the master is only for the one who frees or gives the price. She said: She bought her and freed her. She said: And she was given the choice, and she chose herself, and she said: If I were given so and so, I would not be with him. Aswad said: And her husband was free."
"14282","It is related that Abu ‘Amr the writer informed us, Abu Bakr al-Isma‘ili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed me, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Nili, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us: Abu ‘Awana, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, and he mentioned it in a similar way, and in the end he said: Aswad said: And her husband was free. This is related by al-Bukhari in al-Saheeh, from Musa ibn Isma‘il, from Abu ‘Awana, in this way, and then he said: The statement of Aswad is interrupted, and the statement of Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, is the one I have seen as more authentic. The Sheikh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Jarir ibn al-Hamid has followed the narration of Ishaq al-Hanzali from him, from Mansur, on this wording of this hadith, and distinguished it from it. [Saheeh]"
"14283","It is related that Abu ‘Abd Allah the narrator of hadiths informed us, Abu Ahmad, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me: Muhammad ibn Muhammad the narrator of hadiths, narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shadil ibn ‘Ali al-Hashimi, narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali, narrated to us: Jarir, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Aswad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she intended to buy Barirah, and he mentioned the hadith, saying: In it, the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave her the choice of her husband, and she chose herself. Aswad said: And her husband was free. [Saheeh, before this]"
"14284","It is related that Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us, ‘Abd Allah ibn Ja‘far narrated to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shua‘b narrated to us: al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Aswad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she intended to buy Barirah for the purpose of freeing her, and her people intended that they stipulate the right of the master. She mentioned that to the Prophet, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: Buy her, for the right of the master is only for the one who frees. And he gave her the choice of her husband, and her husband was free, and the Prophet, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought meat, and it was said: This is what you give as charity to Barirah. He said: It is charity for her and a gift for us. This is how Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi arranged it, and some of the narrations from Shu‘ba in the hadith, and some of them made it from the statement of Ibrahim, and some of them made it from the statement of al-Hakam. [Saheeh, without the statement, was free]"
"14285","It is related that Abu ‘Abd Allah the narrator of hadiths informed us, ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Adam narrated to us: Shua‘b narrated to us: al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Aswad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that she intended to buy Barirah for the purpose of freeing her, and her people intended that they stipulate the right of the master. Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Buy her, for the right of the master is only for the one who frees. Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, said: And the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought meat, and I said: This is what you give as charity to Barirah. The Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: It is charity for her and a gift for us. Al-Hakam said: Ibrahim said: And her husband was free, so she was given the choice of her husband. This is related by al-Bukhari in al-Saheeh, from Adam, without this wording, and it is related by Hafs ibn ‘Umar from Shu‘ba, and in the end he said: Al-Hakam said: And her husband was free. Al-Bukhari said: The statement of al-Hakam is interrupted, and Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, said: I have seen him as a slave. The Sheikh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: We have been informed from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, and ‘Urwa ibn az-Zubair, and Mujahid, and ‘Ammarah bint ‘Abd al-Rahman, all of them from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the husband of Barirah was a slave. [Saheeh, without the statement, was free]"
"14286","It is related that Abu ‘Abd Allah the narrator of hadiths said: I heard Abu al-Hasan, may Allah be pleased with him, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Muqri said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib said: Aswad ibn Yazid contradicted the people in the husband of Barirah, and he said: Indeed, he is free. And the people said: Indeed, he was a slave. The Sheikh said: And it has been narrated from Abu Hudhayfa, from ath-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, and from Abu Ja‘far ar-Razi, from al-A‘mash, from Ibrahim, from Aswad, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, one of them said: Indeed, the husband of Barirah was a slave when she was freed. And the other said: She said: The husband of Barirah was a slave of the family of Abu Ahmad. [Saheeh]"
"14287","It is related that Abu ‘Amr the writer informed us, Abu Bakr al-Isma‘ili narrated to me: Abu ‘Imran ibn Hani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salih narrated to us: Abu Hudhayfa, and in the second, Abu Bakr al-Asbahani informed us: ‘Ali ibn ‘Umar narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Mujahid, and Ahmad ibn ‘Abd Allah, the companion of Abu Sakhra, and others said: ‘Abd Allah ibn Ayyub al-Mukharrimi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Abu Ja‘far ar-Razi, and he mentioned it, and it is not from these two ways, the narration of the community from ath-Thawri and al-A‘mash is contrary to that, and the reliance is on what has been mentioned before, and by Allah is the attainment. [Empty]"
"14288","It is related that Abu ‘Abd Allah the narrator of hadiths informed us, Abu al-Hasan al-Tarafiy informed us, ‘Uthman ibn Sa‘id ad-Darami said: I heard ‘Ali, meaning ibn al-Madini, said to us: Which of them do you consider as having established the narration of ‘Urwa or Ibrahim from Aswad? Then ‘Ali said: The people of al-Hijaz have established it. The Sheikh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: ‘Ali intends the narration of ‘Urwa and similar ones from the people of al-Hijaz to be more authentic than the narration of the people of al-Kufah, and by Allah is the attainment. [Saheeh]"
"14289","It is related that Abu ‘Ali ar-Rudhbar informed us, Abu Bakr ibn Dasa narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salata, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Ja‘far, from Aban ibn Salih, from Mujahid, and from Hisham ibn ‘Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that Barirah was freed while she was with Mughith, a slave of the family of Abu Ahmad, and the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave her the choice, and he said to her: If Mughith approaches you, then you have no choice. [Weak]"
"14290","It is related that ‘Ali ibn Ahmad ibn ‘Abdun informed us, Ahmad ibn ‘Ubaid narrated to us: Ahmad ibn ‘Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Shami narrated to us: Shu‘ayb ibn Ishaq, from Hisham ibn ‘Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Barirah: If Mughith approaches you, then you have no choice. This is unique to Muhammad ibn Ibrahim. [Weak]"
"14291","(14285) It was narrated that Abu Bakr – Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi – narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ya‘qūb narrated to us: Rabī‘ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfi‘ī narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us: \nAnd it was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān: Ismā‘īl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ‘Alī ibn ‘Affān narrated to us: ‘Abd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated from ‘Ubayd Allāh ibn ‘Umar – both of them narrated from Nāfi‘ – from Ibn ‘Umar – may Allāh be pleased with them – that he said concerning a slave-woman: When she is in the possession of her master and he frees her, she has the choice as long as he has not touched her. \nMālik added in his narration: If he touches her, then she has no choice. [Hasan]"
"14292","(14286) It was narrated that Abū al-‘Abbās – Muḥammad ibn Ya‘qūb – narrated to us: Rabī‘ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: al-Shāfi‘ī narrated to us: Mālik narrated to us: \nAnd it was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī: Abū Bakr ibn Ja‘far narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Ibn Shihāb from ‘Urwah ibn az-Zubayr that a female slave of Banū ‘Adī ibn Ka‘b, who was called Zubayrā, narrated to him that she was a concubine of a slave and she was a free woman, and she was freed. He said: She sent to me Hafsah, the wife of the Prophet – may Allāh bless him and grant him peace – and she invited me, and she said: I am informing you of something, and I do not like that you do anything, for your affair is in your hand as long as your husband has not consummated marriage with you. She said: I separated from him for three days. \nThe wording of the hadith of Ibn Bukayr is that ‘Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb – may Allāh be pleased with him – said: When he consummates marriage with her, then she has no choice. [Sahih]"
"14293","(14287) It was narrated that Abū al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī narrated to us: Abū Bakr – Muḥammad ibn Ja‘far al-Muzakkī – narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Bušanjī narrated to us: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us: Mālik narrated from Nāfi‘ from ‘Abd Allāh ibn ‘Umar – may Allāh be pleased with them – that he said concerning a slave-woman: When she is in the possession of her master and he frees her, she has the choice as long as he has not touched her. If he touches her, she claims that she did not know that she had the choice, and she is blamed and her claim of ignorance is not accepted, and after she has been touched, she has no choice. \nIn the hadith of Ibn Jurayj from ‘Aṭā’ ibn Abī Rabāḥ: When it is consummated upon her and she does not know, then she has the choice when she knows. \nAnd al-Shāfi‘ī narrated in his *al-Qadīm* from Ismā‘īl ibn ‘Ulayyā‘ from Yūnus from al-Ḥasan that he said concerning a slave-woman: When she is freed, her husband covers her before she is given the choice. He said: She is made to swear that she did not know that she had the choice, and then she is given the choice. [Sahih]"
"14294","(14288) It was narrated that Abū ‘Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-‘Abbās – Muḥammad ibn Ya‘qūb – narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us: ‘Abd al-Wahhāb ibn ‘Aṭā’ narrated to us: Sa‘īd – he is Ibn Abī ‘Arūbah – narrated from ‘Abd al-Karīm Abū Umayyah from Muǧāhid from Ibn ‘Abbās – may Allāh be pleased with them – that he said concerning a slave-woman: When she is freed before she is taken into marriage, she chooses for herself, so there is nothing for her except that she takes her soul and her property. [Sahih]"
"14295","(14289) It was narrated that Abū ‘Abd Allāh – Muḥammad ibn ‘Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ – narrated to us: Abū al-‘Abbās – Muḥammad ibn Ya‘qūb – narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ‘Ubayd Allāh al-Munādī narrated to us: Ishāq ibn Yūsuf al-Aẓraq narrated from Sa‘īd ibn Abī ‘Arūbah from Qatādah from Sa‘īd ibn al-Muṣayyab from ‘Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb – may Allāh be pleased with him – that he said concerning the *‘inānī*: A year is deferred for her; if she conceives, then they are joined together, and if not, they are separated, and she has the *mahr* and he has the *‘iddah*. \nThe Sheikh – may Allāh have mercy on him – said: This is in accordance with his saying that *khalwah* confirms the *mahr* and necessitates the *‘iddah*. \nIt was narrated by Ma‘mar from Ibn al-Muṣayyab from ‘Umar without this addition, and it was narrated by Ibn Abī Laylā from ash-Sha‘bī from ‘Umar – may Allāh be pleased with him – in a *mursal* form: That a year is deferred, and he said concerning it: I do not know it except from the day it is raised to the authority. [Da‘īf]"
"14296","(14290) It was narrated that Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Asbahānī narrated to us: ‘Alī ibn ‘Umar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū Ṭalḥah – Ahmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ‘Abd al-Karīm al-Fazārī – narrated to us: Bindār narrated to us: ‘Abd al-Raḥmān narrated to us: Sufyān narrated from ar-Rukayn ibn ar-Rabī‘, who said: I heard Abū Wah Ḥusayn ibn Qabīṣah narrating from ‘Abd Allāh, who said: A year is deferred for her; if she comes to it and is not pregnant, then they are separated. [Da‘īf]"
"14297","(14291) Sufyān narrated from ar-Rukayn ibn ar-Rabī‘ from Abū al-Nu‘mān, who said: We came to al-Mughīrah ibn Shu‘bah – may Allāh be pleased with him – concerning the *‘inānī*, and he said: A year is deferred for her. [Sahih]"
"14298","(14292) Shu‘bah narrated from ar-Rukayn from Abū Ṭalq from al-Mughīrah ibn Shu‘bah, who said: The *‘inānī* is deferred for a year. [Sahih. *Taqdīm* before *Qabīl*]"
"14299","(14293) Hammād ibn Salama narrated from al-Hajjāj ibn Arṭā‘ from ar-Rukayn ibn ar-Rabī‘ from Hanẓalah ibn Nu‘aym that al-Mughīrah ibn Shu‘bah – may Allāh be pleased with him – said: He deferred her for a year from the day he raised her. \n‘Abd al-Raḥmān said, and so did Sufyān and Mālik: From the day she is raised. [Da‘īf]"
"14300","(14294) It was narrated that Abū al-Fatḥ al-Faqīh narrated to us: ‘Abd al-Raḥmān ash-Shurayḥī narrated to us: Abū al-Qāsim al-Bagawī narrated to us: ‘Alī ibn al-Ja‘d narrated to us: Shu‘bah narrated from ar-Rukayn ibn ar-Rabī‘, who said: I heard Abū Ṭalq narrating from al-Mughīrah ibn Shu‘bah – may Allāh be pleased with him – that a man was raised to him who was unable to reach his wife, so he deferred her for a year. [Sahih]"
"14301","It was narrated to us by Abū Saʿd al-Māliqī. It was narrated to us by Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī. He said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar al-Qawāriʾī narrated to us, and Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated to us from Shuʿba, who narrated to me al-Rukayn from Huṣayn ibn Qabīṣa, who said: I heard my father mention it concerning ʿAbd Allāh (ibn Marḍā), may Allāh be pleased with him, saying: \In the case of the woman who is suspected of adultery"," a year's postponement is granted; if she conceives during that year"," the matter is confirmed; otherwise"," they are divorced.\"" (Ṣaḥīḥ)"""
"14302","And al-Rukayn narrated to me, saying: I heard Abū Ṭalq say: Muẓaffar ibn Shuʿba postponed the waiting period for the suspected woman by one year. (Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded by no. 14291)"
"14303","It was narrated to us by Abū Saʿd al-Māliqī. It was narrated to us by Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī, the hāfiẓ. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Muslim narrated to us, and al-Ramādī said: They were informed by Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān, who said: It was said to Sufyān ibn Saʿīd: \Shuʿba contradicts you in the hadith concerning Muẓaffar ibn Shuʿba regarding the suspected woman"," saying that a year's postponement is granted"," and the two narrations are attributed to al-Rukayn"," who says: 'You are Abū al-Nuʿmān","' while Shuʿba says: 'He is Abū Ṭalq.' Sufyān laughed and said: \""I was with Shuʿba at al-Rukayn's presence"," and a man passed by"," called Abū Ṭalq"," and al-Rukayn said: 'I heard Abū Abī Ṭalq","' so Shuʿba went and said: 'Abū Ṭalq.' And this view is narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Muṣayyab"," ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ"," al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī"," and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī.\"" (Ṣaḥīḥ)"""
"14304","It was narrated to us by Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh. It was narrated to us by Abū ʿUthmān: ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī. Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, and Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, and Sufyān narrated from Abū Iṣḥāq from Hāniʾ ibn Hāniʾ, who said: A woman came to ʿAlī, may Allāh be pleased with him, and she was very beautiful. She said: \O Commander of the Faithful"," do you have any opinion about a woman who is neither a widow nor married?\"" He understood what she meant"," and they brought her husband"," who was a chief of his people. He said: \""What do you say about what she says?\"" She said: \""He is as she describes him.\"" He said: \""Not that.\"" She said: \""Nor at the end of the night?\"" He said: \""Nor at the end of the night.\"" He said: \""You have destroyed yourself and destroyed her; I cannot consent to separating you two.\"" (Daʿīf)"""
"14305","And Shuʿba narrated from Abū Iṣḥāq in similar terms, saying: And her husband came, reciting after her, an old man leaning on a staff, and he added: \Have taqwa of Allāh and be patient.\"" It was narrated to me by Abū ʿAbd Allāh the hāfiẓ"," Abū Bakr: Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to me"," Muḥammad ibn Yūnus narrated to us"," and Rawḥ narrated to us"," and Shuʿba mentioned it. Al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allāh have mercy on him"," said in the Sunnah of Harmalah: \""This hadith"," if it were established from ʿAlī"," may Allāh be pleased with him"," there would be no contradiction with ʿUmar"," may Allāh be pleased with him"," because he may have had intercourse with her"," then it reached this age"," so it is no longer effective"," and he delivered the speech to the point where he said: 'Knowing that Hāniʾ ibn Hāniʾ is unknown"," and that this hadith among the people of hadith is from what they do not establish due to their ignorance of Hāniʾ ibn Hāniʾ.\"" (Daʿīf. Preceded by no. 14298)"""
"14306","And Muḥammad ibn Iṣḥāq narrated from Khālid ibn Kathīr from al-Dhaḥḥāk from ʿAlī, may Allāh be pleased with him, who said: \The waiting period for the suspected woman is postponed by one year; if she conceives"," it is confirmed"," otherwise"," they are divorced.\"" It was informed to me by Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," by way of transmission: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us"," al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us"," Abū Bakr narrated to us"," Abū Khālid narrated from Muḥammad ibn Iṣḥāq"," who mentioned it. (Daʿīf)"""
"14307","It was narrated to us by Abū al-Ḥasan: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ. It was narrated to us by al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Iṣḥāq. Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī narrated to us, and Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, and Hammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb from Ikrimah, who said: A woman came to ʿAʾishah, may Allāh be pleased with her, and she was wearing a green veil. She complained to her husband and showed him a mark on her skin. The Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) entered, and ʿAʾishah, may Allāh be pleased with her, mentioned it to him and said: \No women of the Muslims have suffered more from their husbands than this","\"" and she said to the one who struck her skin"," \""You are greener than her veil.\"" Ikrimah said: \""And women support one another"," and a man came and said: 'What is with you that you are indifferent to me in this?' and she pointed with the edge of her garment"," and the man said: 'O Messenger of Allāh"," by Allāh"," I will not take her except as dirt is taken","' but she is rebellious and intends Rifāʿah"," and Rifāʿah her husband had already divorced her before that"," so he said: \""Indeed"," if it is as you say"," then it is not lawful for you until she tastes of your chastity and you taste of her chastity.\"" (Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5825)"""
"14308","It was narrated to us by Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr, who said: Abū al-ʿAbbās: Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Iṣḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Ashʿhal ibn Ḥātim narrated to us, and ʿUyaynah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from his father, who said: A woman came to Samarah ibn Junḍub, and she mentioned that her husband does not approach her. So the man was asked, and he denied it. And he wrote to Muʿāwiyah, may Allāh be pleased with him, saying: Marry her to a woman from the household of wealth, with a share of beauty and religion. If she claims that he approaches her, then reconcile them; if she claims that he does not approach her, then divorce them. He said: So he did, and they came to him in the house. He said: When morning came, people entered, and I entered. He said: Then the man came with traces of yellow on him, and he said to him: \What did you do?\"" He said: \""I did it"," by Allāh"," until I rubbed it into the garment from behind her.\"" He said: And the woman came firmly convinced"," and she stood at his feet. He said: So he asked her and honored her"," and she said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Does it spread? Does it come near?\"" She said: \""Yes"," but when it comes near"," its evil comes.\"" Samarah said: \""Leave her path"," O one who rubs!\"" This is the view of Muʿāwiyah"," may Allāh be pleased with him"," and it is possible that a man is suspected of one woman but not of another. And following the Sunnah is better"," and the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) has already decided in favor of the one who denies"," and the husband is denied what is alleged against him of suspicion. And it was narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Dinar that he said: \""We have always heard that when a man has intercourse with her once"," there is no speech or dispute for her afterward.\"" It was narrated in this regard from Ṭāwus"," al-Ḥasan"," and al-Zuhrī. (Daʿīf)"""
"14309","It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh the hāfiẓ, Abū Naẓr: Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh narrated to us, and ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, and ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us, and Sufyān said: ʿAmr, meaning ibn Dinar, and it was informed to me by ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir, may Allāh be pleased with him, who said: \We used to isolate ourselves while the Qurʾān was being revealed.\"" \nThis is narrated by al-Bukhārī in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"," and it is narrated by Muslim from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Iṣḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm from Sufyān. It is also narrated by Ibn Jurayj and Maʿqil al-Jazarī from ʿAṭāʾ from Jābir"," may Allāh be pleased with him"," who said: \""We used to isolate ourselves during the time of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ).\"" Abū al-Zubayr added from Jābir that it reached the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)"," and he did not forbid us from it. (Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5209)"""
"14310","It was narrated to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh the hāfiẓ. ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Saʿd al-Bazzāz narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn Iṣḥāq al-Thaqafī narrated to us, Zakariyyā ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, and Muʿādh ibn Hišām narrated to me from my father from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir, may Allāh be pleased with him, who said: \We used to isolate ourselves during the time of the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)"," and when it reached the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ)"," he did not forbid us from it.\"" \nThis is narrated by Muslim in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Ghassān from Muʿādh ibn Hišām. (Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded by no. 14303)"""
"14311","(14305) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūnus informed us, Zuhayr informed us, Abū al-Zubayr narrated from Jābir that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \I have a slave-girl who serves us and tends to our needs. I have intercourse with her"," but I dislike that she should conceive.\"" He ﷺ said: \""Practise ʿazl (coitus interruptus) with her if you wish"," for what has been decreed for her will inevitably come to her.\"" The man remained away for a while"," then came to him and said: \""The slave-girl has conceived.\"" He ﷺ said: \""I had already told you that what was decreed for her would come to her.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1439]"""
"14312","(14306) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā informed us, al-Ḥumaydī informed us, Sufyān informed us, Saʿīd ibn Ḥassān narrated from ʿUrwah ibn ʿIyāḍ from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with him, the brother of Banī Salamah, that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \I have a slave-girl and I practise ʿazl with her.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: \""Indeed"," that does not avert the decree of Allah.\"" The man departed and did not remain long before he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," are you aware that the slave-girl has conceived?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn ʿAmr al-Ashʿathī from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced earlier]"""
"14313","(14307) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Isḥāq ibn Ismāʿīl al-Ṭālaqānī informed us, Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ from Mujāhid from Qazaʿah from Abū Saʿīd that ʿazl was mentioned before the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \Why does any one of you do that?\"" He did not say"," \""Let none of you do it.\"" Then he said: \""There is no soul that is to be created except that Allah is its Creator.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qāwarīrī and Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah from Sufyān. Al-Bukhārī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""And Mujāhid mentioned it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1438]"""
"14314","(14308) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd informed us, al-Qaʿnabī informed us — reciting from Mālik — from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān from Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā ibn Ḥabbān from Ibn Muḥayriz that he said: \I entered the mosque and saw Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," so I sat with him and asked him about ʿazl. Abū Saʿīd said: 'We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Banī al-Muṣṭaliq and we captured captives from among the Arab captives. We desired women and celibacy became hard upon us"," and we desired ransom. So we intended to practise ʿazl. We said: Shall we practise ʿazl while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among us"," before we ask him about it?' So we asked him about it and he said: 'There is no harm upon you if you do not do it. There is no soul that is destined to exist until the Day of Resurrection except that it will exist.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced earlier]"""
"14315","(14309) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us, Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Muʿādh ibn al-Muthannī al-ʿAnbarī informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ informed us, Juwayriyah narrated from Mālik from al-Zuhrī from Ibn Muḥayriz from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī that he informed him that he said: \We captured female captives and we used to practise ʿazl. We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that"," and he said to you: 'And indeed you do it"," and indeed you do it"," and indeed you do it! There is no soul that is destined to exist until the Day of Resurrection except that it will exist.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn Asmāʾ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced earlier]"""
"14316","(14310) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Shuʿbah informed us, Anas ibn Sīrīn narrated from Maʿbad ibn Sīrīn from Abū Saʿīd, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: \We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about ʿazl and he said: 'There is no obligation upon you to do it"," for it is [a matter of] divine decree.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1438]"""
"14317","(14311) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Walīd informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Dāwūd informed us, Hārūn ibn Saʿīd informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me, Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Abū al-Wadāk from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard him say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about ʿazl and he said: 'Not from every fluid is a child created. And when Allah intends to create something"," nothing can prevent it.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it from Hārūn ibn Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced earlier]"""
"14318","(14312) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Ibn ʿAwn narrated from Ibn Sīrīn from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn Masʿūd — who traced the hadith back to Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī — that he said: \ʿAzl was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'What is the matter with you?' They said: 'A man may have a woman who is nursing and he has intercourse with her but dislikes that she should conceive"," or he may have a slave-girl and dislikes that she should conceive.' He ﷺ said: 'There is no harm upon you in not doing that"," for it is [a matter of] divine decree.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Ibn ʿAwn. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced earlier]"""
"14319","(14313) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh al-ʿAdl informed us, Abū Muslim informed us that Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed them, Ḥammād said: Ibn ʿAwn said: \I mentioned to Muḥammad — meaning the hadith of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr ibn Masʿūd from Abū Saʿīd regarding ʿazl — and he said: 'ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Bishr narrated it to me.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥajjāj ibn al-Shāʿir from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referenced earlier]"""
"14320","(14314) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Abān informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān informed him that Rifāʿah informed him from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have a slave-girl and I practise ʿazl with her"," and I dislike that she should conceive"," and I desire what men desire. And the Jews claim that ʿazl is the lesser form of live burial.\"" He ﷺ said: \""The Jews have lied. If Allah wills to create him"," you will not be able to avert it.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14321","(14315) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū Badr Shujaʿ ibn al-Walīd narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us; from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about coitus interruptus (al-ʿazl). They said: \The Jews claim that coitus interruptus is the minor form of live-burying (al-waʾd al-ṣughrā).\"" He said: \""The Jews have lied.\"" It has also been narrated regarding the permissibility of coitus interruptus from the generality of the Companions"," may Allah be pleased with them. [Weak]"""
"14322","(14316) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Masʿūd narrated to us; al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us; Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us; Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated to us; I heard Muṣʿab ibn Saʿd narrate from an umm walad of Saʿd: that Saʿd used to practice coitus interruptus with her. [Authentic through other chains]"
"14323","(14317) And Abū Aḥmad ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrajānī informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; Mālik narrated from Abū al-Naḍr, the mawlā of ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ, from his father: that he used to practice coitus interruptus. [Authentic. Previously cited]"
"14324","(14318) And through this chain of narration, Mālik narrated from Abū al-Naḍr, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Aflaḥ, the mawlā of Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī, from an umm walad of Abū Ayyūb, from Abū Ayyūb: that he used to practice coitus interruptus. [Authentic through other chains]"
"14325","(14319) And through this chain of narration, Mālik narrated from Ḍamrah ibn Saʿīd al-Māzinī, from al-Ḥajjāj ibn ʿAmr ibn Ghaziyyah: that he was sitting with Zayd ibn Thābit when Ibn Fahd, a man from the people of Yemen, came and said: \O Abū Saʿīd"," I have slave-girls — not wives — whom I find most pleasing to me"," yet I do not wish all of them to conceive from me. May I practice coitus interruptus?\"" Zayd said: \""Give him a fatwā"," O Ḥajjāj.\"" He said: I said: \""May Allah forgive you — we only sit with you to learn from you.\"" He said: \""Give him a fatwā.\"" He said: I said: \""It is your crop; if you wish"," you may water it"," and if you wish"," you may leave it thirsty.\"" He said: I was also hearing this from Zayd"," and he said: \""He has spoken the truth.\"" [Authentic. Mālik narrated it (1266)]"""
"14326","(14320) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Usayd ibn ʿĀṣim narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥafṣ narrated from Sufyān; from Salamah ibn Tamām; from al-Shaʿbī; from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both: that he was asked about coitus interruptus and he said: \No human being should kill a soul whom Allah has decreed to create. It is your crop; if you wish"," you may leave it thirsty"," and if you wish"," you may water it.\"" [Good]"""
"14327","(14321) And through this chain of narration, from Sufyān, from al-Aʿmash, from ʿAbd al-Malik al-Zarrād, from Mujāhid, who said: We asked Ibn ʿAbbās about coitus interruptus and he said: \Go and ask the people"," then come back and inform me.\"" So they asked and then informed him. He then recited this verse: {And indeed We created man from an extract of clay} [Sūrat al-Muʾminūn: 12]"," until he completed the verse"," and then said: \""How can it be considered live-burying (al-waʾd) when it has already passed through this stage of creation?\"" [Authentic]"""
"14328","(14322) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Isḥāq al-Azraq narrated to us; Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Manṣūr; from Mujāhid; from Ibn ʿAbbās: that he used to practice coitus interruptus with his slave-girl and then also have intercourse with her without it. [Authentic]"
"14329","(14323) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from al-Faḍl ibn Yazīd al-Thumālī; from al-Shaʿbī; from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \I do not care whether I practice coitus interruptus or ejaculate normally.\"" He said: \""And the owner of this house\"" — meaning Ibn Masʿūd — \""used to dislike it.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14330","(14324) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿĪsā ibn Muḥammad narrated to me; Isḥāq ibn ʿĪsā narrated to me; from Ibn Lahīʿah; from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah; from al-Zuhrī; from Muḥarrir ibn Abī Hurayrah; from Abū Hurayrah; from ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited coitus interruptus with a free woman except with her permission. [Denounced (Munkar)]"
"14331","(14325) Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Ardastani al-Hafiz — informed us; Abu Nasr al-Iraqi — informed us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari — narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Hasan — narrated to us; Abdullah ibn al-Walid — narrated to us; Sufyan — narrated to us; Mansur — from Ibrahim, who said: \The free woman is to be consulted regarding coitus interruptus ('azl)"," but the slave woman is not to be consulted.\""\n\nHe said: And Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari from Ata from Ibn Abbas a similar narration. [Hasan]"""
"14332","(14326) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bishran — informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar — informed us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr — narrated to us; Abu Mu'awiyah — from Abu 'Arfajah al-Fa'ishi from 'Atiyyah al-'Awfi from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \He would practise coitus interruptus ('azl) with the slave woman and would consult the free woman.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14333","(14327) Abu 'Amr al-Adib — informed us; Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili — informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Kufi — narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym — narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Burqan — said: \I asked Ata about coitus interruptus ('azl)"," and he said: 'With the free woman"," with her consent; as for the slave woman"," that is up to you.'\"" [Da'if]"""
"14334","(14328) Abu Muhammad — Abdullah ibn Yusuf — informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi — narrated to us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr — narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq — from Ibn 'Awn — from Nafi' — from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with both of them): \He used to strike his sons for coitus interruptus ('azl)"," i.e."," he forbade it.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ali ibn Abi Talib and Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with both of them) that they both disliked coitus interruptus ('azl)"," and it has also been narrated from them both that they permitted it. [Hasan]"""
"14335","(14329) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr — narrated to us; Abu Muhammad — Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Muzani — narrated to us; Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Isa — narrated to us; Abu al-Yaman — informed me; Shu'ayb — from al-Zuhri — said: Salim ibn Abdullah said: \Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to forbid coitus interruptus ('azl)"," and Abdullah ibn Umar used to forbid it"," while Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas and Zayd ibn Thabit (may Allah be pleased with both of them) used to practise coitus interruptus ('azl).\"" [Hasan]"""
"14336","(14330) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani' — narrated to us; al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah — narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Muqri' — narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub — narrated to me; Abu al-Aswad — from 'Urwah — from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) — from Judamah bint Wahb, sister of 'Ukkashah ibn Wahb, who said: \I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) among a group of people"," and he said: 'I had intended to forbid coitus interruptus (al-ghaylah)"," but then I looked into the matter of the Romans and the Persians"," and they practise coitus interruptus with their children"," and it does not harm their children at all.'\""\n\nAnd they asked him about coitus interruptus ('azl)"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""That is a hidden form of infanticide (al-wa'd al-khafy)\"" — \""And when the buried infant (al-maw'udah) shall be asked\"" [al-Takwir:8].\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Sahih from 'Ubayd Allah ibn Sa'id and others from al-Muqri'. And it has been narrated to us from the Prophet (peace be upon him) regarding coitus interruptus ('azl) narrations contrary to this. However"," the narrations permitting it are more numerous and better preserved. Those among the Companions whom we have named permitted it"," and that is more appropriate. The dislike of those among them who disliked it may be understood as a form of disapproval (tanzhih) rather than prohibition (tahrim). And Allah knows best. [Sahih. Muslim 1442]"""
"14337","(14331) Abu al-'Abbas — al-Fadl ibn 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Isfara'ini — informed us; Bishr ibn Ahmad — narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn 'Ali al-Naysaburi — narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya — informed us; Jarir — from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' ibn 'Umaylah — from al-Qassim ibn Hassan — from his paternal uncle 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah — from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) disliked ten things: wearing a gold ring"," letting the garment drag"," the use of saffron perfume (khaluq)"," altering grey hair"," incantations (ruqa) except with the mu'awwidhat"," tying amulets (tama'im)"," playing with dice (k'ab)"," displaying adornment (tabarruj) in other than its proper place"," diverting the water from its proper place (i.e."," coitus interruptus)"," and spoiling the child other than its mother.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14338","(14332) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz — informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah — Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Zahid al-Isbahani — narrated to us; Abu Isma'il — Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Sulami — narrated to me; Abu al-Asbagh — 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Yahya al-Harrani — informed us; Muhammad ibn Salamah — from Abu 'Abd al-Rahim — Khalid ibn Abi Yazid — from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah — from Yazid ibn Abi Habib — from Mirthad ibn Abdullah — from 'Uqbah ibn 'Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said to a man: \Would you be pleased if I marry you to so-and-so (a woman)?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" And he said to the woman: \""Would you be pleased if I marry you to so-and-so (a man)?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" So he married one of them to the other"," and he did not specify a dowry (sadaq) for her"," and he did not give her anything. He was among those who witnessed al-Hudaybiyah"," and those who witnessed al-Hudaybiyah had a share in Khaybar. When death approached him"," he said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) married me to so-and-so"," and I did not specify a dowry for her"," and I did not give her anything. I bear witness to you that I have given her her dowry — my share in Khaybar.\"" So she took the share and sold it for a hundred thousand. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \""The best of dowries is the easiest of them.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14339","(14333) Abu Dawud narrated it in the Sunan from Muhammad ibn Yahya from Abu al-Asbagh, and he added in it: \So the man consummated the marriage with her"," and he had not specified a dowry for her"," and he had not given her anything.\""\n\nAbu 'Ali al-Rudhbari — informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah — narrated to us; Abu Dawud — mentioned it. And the hadith of Barwa' bint Waqash is evidence in this regard"," and it will be presented"," if Allah wills"," in its proper place. [Hasan]"""
"14340","(14334) Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Qattan in Baghdad — informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Durustuyah — narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan — narrated to us; Abdullah ibn 'Uthman — informed us; Abdullah — i.e., Ibn al-Mubarak — informed us; Ma'mar — from al-Zuhri — from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr — from Umm Habibah (may Allah be pleased with her): \She was married to 'Ubayd Allah ibn Jahsh"," and he had migrated to the Negus"," and he died there. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) married Umm Habibah while she was in the land of Abyssinia. The Negus contracted the marriage on his behalf and dowered her with four thousand"," then equipped her from his own resources and sent her to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) with Sharhabil ibn Hasanah. All of her provisions were from the Negus"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not send her anything. The dowries of the wives of the Prophet (peace be upon him) were four hundred dirhams.\"" [Sahih]"""
"14341","(14335) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī — in wording — informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Ḥumayd narrated from Bakr, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \I had set out intending to prohibit the excessive increase in the dowries of women"," until I recited this verse: {And you have given one of them a qinṭār} [al-Nisāʾ 4:20].\"" This is a good mursal hadith. [Weak]"""
"14342","(14336) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamzah al-Harawī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Mujālid narrated from al-Shaʿbī, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed the people. He praised Allah, the Most High, and extolled Him, and then said: \Beware"," do not be excessive in the dowries of women. If it reaches me that anyone has given more in dowry than what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave or was given to him"," I shall deposit the excess into the Bayt al-Māl (public treasury).\"" Then he descended from the pulpit"," and a woman from Quraysh came to him and said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," is the Book of Allah"," the Most High"," more deserving of being followed"," or your statement?\"" He said: \""Rather"," the Book of Allah"," the Most High. What is it?\"" She said: \""You have just prohibited the people from being excessive in the dowries of women"," while Allah"," the Most High"," says in His Book: {And you have given one of them a qinṭār"," so do not take anything from it} [al-Nisāʾ 4:20].\"" ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Everyone is more learned than ʿUmar\"" — two or three times. Then he returned to the pulpit and said to the people: \""I had forbidden you from being excessive in the dowries of women. Let a man do with his wealth as he pleases.\"" This is a munqaṭiʿ hadith. [Weak]"""
"14343","(14337) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamm ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāʾinī informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ said: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Madanī narrated to us: Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated to us: Abū Ḥuṣayn narrated from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, who said: Muʿādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The qinṭār is one thousand and two hundred awqiyyahs.\"" [Weak]"""
"14344","(14338) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf informed us: Bishr ibn Aḥmad informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Ḥaddāʾ narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd informed us: ʿĀṣim ibn Bahdalah narrated from Abī Ṣāliḥ from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The qinṭār is one thousand and two hundred awqiyyahs.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14345","(14339) He said: And ʿAlī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Faḍl Abū al-Nuʿmān narrated to us: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Saʿīd al-Jurayrī from Abī Naḍrah from Abī Saʿīd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \The qinṭār is the hide of a bull filled with gold.\"" [Weak]"""
"14346","(14340) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: \The qinṭār is twelve thousand dirhams or one thousand dinars.\"" And in the narration of ʿAṭiyyah from Ibn ʿAbbās"," he said: \""The qinṭār is one thousand and two hundred dinars"," and in silver"," one thousand and two hundred mithqāls.\"" And it has been narrated from Mujāhid"," who said: \""The qinṭār is seventy thousand dinars.\"" And from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab"," who said: \""The qinṭār is eighty thousand.\"" [Weak]"""
"14347","(14341) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Dāwūd ibn Dīnār narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, the freedman of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, narrated from his father Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, gave Umm Kulthūm bint ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with her, a dowry of forty thousand dirhams. [Weak]"
"14348","(14342) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated from Abī Ḥanīfah from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who said: \Ibn ʿUmar used to marry his daughters for a dowry of one thousand dinars"," and he would adorn them from that with four hundred dinars' worth of jewelry.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14349","(14343) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us: Muʿādh ibn Hishām narrated to us: My father narrated from Qatādah, who said: \Anas ibn Mālik"," may Allah be pleased with him"," married a woman for a dowry of twenty thousand.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14350","(14344) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī, Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Hād from Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith from Abī Salamah, who said: \I asked ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her: 'What was the dowry of the Prophet ﷺ?' She said: 'His dowry to his wives was twelve awqiyyahs and a nashsh.' She said: 'Do you know what a nashsh is?' I said: 'No.' She said: 'Half an awqiyyah.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1425]"""
"14351","(14345) Muslim narrated in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Muḥammad ibn Abī ʿUmar al-Makkī, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz — except that he said: \An *ūqiyyah*\"" — and he added therein: \""That is five hundred dirhams"," and that was the *ṣadāq* (dower) of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for his wives.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — that is"," Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Shaybānī — informed us; Aḥmad ibn Sahl ibn Baḥr narrated to us; Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us; ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was cited before it.]"""
"14352","(14346) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād; Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Sammāk informed us; Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ibn al-Mubārak narrated from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not give any of his wives or daughters a *ṣadāq* (dower) exceeding twelve *ūqiyyahs*"," except Umm Ḥabībah"," for al-Najāshī married him to her and gave her a *ṣadāq* of four thousand"," and it was paid in cash on his behalf. The Prophet ﷺ consummated the marriage with her and did not give her anything.\""\n\nThis is what he narrated from ʿĀʾishah. Others narrated it from Ibn al-Mubārak and said it was from Umm Ḥabībah. [Munkar]"""
"14353","(14347) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us; al-Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ayyūb, Ḥabīb, and Hishām, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū al-ʿAjfaʾ al-Sulamī, who said: I heard ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Beware of excessive dowers for women"," for if it were a form of piety before Allah or an honourable practice among people"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would have been the foremost among you in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry any of his wives"," nor did he give any of his daughters in marriage"," for more than twelve *ūqiyyahs*"," which is four hundred and eighty dirhams. Yet one of you inflates the dower of his wife until it becomes a source of enmity in his heart"," and he says: 'I have been burdened for you with the hanging of a waterskin.'\""\n\nḤammād ibn Zayd also narrated it from Ayyūb. In the narration of some of them from Ibn Sīrīn"," it is \""twelve *ūqiyyahs* and a half.\"" If this is preserved"," it agrees with the narration of Abū Salamah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her). [Ḥasan]"""
"14354","(14348) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Naysābūrī informed us; Muḥammad ibn Muslim ibn Wārah, Abū ʿAbd Allāh, in al-Rayy, in the month of Ramaḍān, in the year two hundred and sixty-four, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd ibn Sābiq narrated to us from his ancient book; ʿAmr — that is, Ibn Abī Qays — narrated from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, from Ibn Sīrīn, from Ibn Abī al-ʿAjfaʾ, from his father, who said: ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Do not inflate the dowers of women","\"" and he mentioned it along the lines of the ḥadīth of Ḥammād"," except that he said: \""A man may inflate the dower until he says: 'I have been burdened on your account with the hanging of a waterskin","' treating it as a sin.\"" [Ḥasan. It was cited before it.]"""
"14355","(14349) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUthmān ibn Jabalah ibn Abī Rāwād narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Mubārak narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, who was informed by ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \ʿAlī did not make Fāṭimah (may Allah be pleased with them both) lawful for himself except with a suit of iron armour.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14356","(14350) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from his father, from a man — he named him — who heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) in al-Kūfah saying: \I intended to propose marriage to the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," but I remembered that I had nothing. Then I remembered his generosity and his kindness"," so I proposed to her. He said: 'Where is your Ḥuṭamī coat of mail that I gave you on such-and-such a day?' He said: 'It is with me.' He said: 'Then give it to her.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14357","(14351) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū Zurʿah al-Dimashqī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Khālid narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated from Ibn Abī Najīḥ, from Mujāhid, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Fāṭimah"," the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ"," was proposed for in marriage"," and a freedwoman of mine said to me: 'Did you know that Fāṭimah is being proposed for?' I said: 'No' — or 'Yes.' She said: 'Then propose for her to him.' I said: 'What do I have with which to propose for her?' By Allah"," she kept urging me until I went to him. We used to revere and honour him greatly. When I sat before him"," I was struck dumb and could not speak. He said: 'Do you have a need?' I remained silent. He said it three times. He said: 'Perhaps you have come to propose for Fāṭimah?' I said: 'Yes"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Do you have anything with which to make her lawful for yourself?' I said: 'No"," by Allah"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'What happened to the coat of mail I gave you as equipment?' ʿAlī said: 'By Allah"," it is a Ḥuṭamī coat of mail"," its value being no more than four hundred dirhams.' He said: 'Go"," for I have married her to you. Send it to her and make her lawful with it.'\""\n\nThus it is in my book: \""four hundred dirhams.\"" Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated it from Ibn Isḥāq and said: \""four dirhams.\"""""
"14358","(14352) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb narrated from Sulaymān ibn Bilāl, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) gave Fāṭimah (may Allah be pleased with her) a coat of mail of iron and a round jar as her *ṣadāq* (dower), and that the *ṣadāq* of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ was five hundred dirhams. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14359","(14353) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us; Abū Yaḥyā ibn Abī Masarrrah informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-Jārī narrated to us; Dāwūd ibn Qays al-Farrāʾ informed me; Mūsā ibn Yasār narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Our *ṣadāq* (dower) at the time when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us was ten *ūqiyyahs*.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī also narrated it from Dāwūd ibn Qays. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14360","(14354) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdād; Abū Sahl ibn Ziyād al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Muḥammad ibn Shādhān al-Jawharī narrated to us; Zakariyyā ibn ʿAdī narrated to us; Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated from Yazīd ibn Kaysān, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \A man — or a young man — came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have married a woman.' He said: 'Did you look at her? For there is something in the eyes of the Anṣār.' He said: 'I have looked at her.' He said: 'For how much did you marry her?' He mentioned something. He said: 'It is as if you are carving gold and silver from the surface of these mountains. We have nothing today to give you"," but I will send you on an expedition in which you will gain something.' He dispatched an expedition to Banū ʿAbs and sent the man with them. He came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," my she-camel is too exhausted to set out.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him his hand"," as one leaning upon it for support"," and he stood up and struck it with his foot.\"" Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""By the One in whose Hand is my soul"," I saw it outpace the leader.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn"," from Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1424]"""
"14361","(14355) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Shaybani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn 'Abd Allah al-Sa'di narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us — and — Abu 'Abd Allah informed us: Hasan ibn Halim al-Marwazi informed me: Abu al-Muwajjah informed us: 'Abdan informed us: 'Abd Allah informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Hadrad al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his assistance regarding the dowry of a woman. He (the Prophet ﷺ) asked: \How much did you stipulate as her dowry?\"" He replied: \""Two hundred dirhams.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""If you were to scoop from the valley of Butihan"," you would not have increased [beyond this].\"" [Sahih]"""
"14362","(14356) Abu al-Qasim 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn Ya'qub al-Iyadi al-Maliki in Baghdad informed us: Ahmad ibn Yusuf ibn Khallad al-Nasibi narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Yazid informed us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Sakhbarah — and — Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh narrated to us: Ishaq ibn al-Hasan al-Harbi narrated to us: 'Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah informed me: 'Amr ibn Tufayl ibn Sakhbarah al-Madani, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \The most blessed of women are those whose dowries are the easiest.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of 'Affan. In the narration of Yazid ibn Harun: \""The easiest of them in expenditure.\"" [Mawdu']"""
"14363","(14357) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman al-Muradi narrated to us: 'Abd Allah ibn Wahb informed me: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me that Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to him — and — Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Bakr al-Qadi both said: Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us: al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri narrated to us: 'Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from 'Urwah, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, that she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Among the signs of a woman's good fortune are the ease of her marriage proposal"," the ease of her dowry"," and the ease of her womb.\"" 'Urwah said: \""I mean the ease of her womb for childbearing.\"" 'Urwah said: \""And I say on my own: among the first signs of her ill omen is the abundance of her dowry.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Ibn Wahb. [Da'if]"""
"14364","(14358) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub dictated to us: al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl al-Bajali narrated to us: Musa ibn Dawud al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Malik ibn Anas, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was approached by a woman who said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have offered myself to you.\"" She stood for a long time. Then a man stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," marry her to me if you have no need of her.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: \""Do you have anything to give her as dowry?\"" He replied: \""I have nothing but this lower garment of mine.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""If you give it to her"," you will sit without a lower garment. Seek something else.\"" He said: \""By Allah"," I can find nothing.\"" He said: \""Seek"," even if it be an iron ring.\"" He sought but found nothing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: \""Do you have any knowledge of the Qur'an?\"" He replied: \""Yes"," such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""I have married her to you on the basis of what you know of the Qur'an.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf from Malik"," and Muslim extracted it through other chains from Abu Hazim"," and he included the wording: \""even if it be an iron ring.\"" [Sahih — Muslim 1425]"""
"14365","(14359) Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Bishran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Bakhtari al-Razzaz narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us — and — Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd al-Jabbar al-Sukkari in Baghdad informed us: Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us: Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, who heard Sahl ibn Sa'd al-Sa'idi, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I was among the people in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ when a woman stood and said: \I have offered myself to you; consider your opinion regarding her.\"" A man from the people stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," marry her to me.\"" He gave him no reply. Then she stood again and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have offered myself to you; consider your opinion regarding her.\"" The man stood and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," marry her to me.\"" Then she stood a third time"," and the Prophet ﷺ said to the man: \""Do you have anything?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""Go and seek.\"" He went and sought but found nothing. He said: \""Go and seek"," even if it be an iron ring.\"" He went and sought and said: \""I could not find anything.\"" He asked: \""Do you have any knowledge of the Qur'an?\"" He replied: \""Yes"," such-and-such surah and such-and-such surah.\"" He said: \""Go"," I have married her to you on the basis of what you have of the Qur'an.\"" The wording of both their hadiths is the same. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from 'Ali"," and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Harb — both from Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah. [Sahih — previously cited]"""
"14366","(14360) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri' informed us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Qadi narrated to us: Abu al-Rabi' and Musaddad and Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr — some of them adding upon the others — said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed traces of yellowness on 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf and said: \What is this"," or what is the matter?\"" He said: \""I have married a woman.\"" He asked: \""For how much?\"" He said: \""For the weight of a date-stone in gold.\"" He said: \""May Allah bless you. Hold a wedding feast"," even if it be with a single sheep.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Musaddad"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu al-Rabi'. [Sahih — Muslim 1427]"""
"14367","(14361) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us: Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhawayh narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas ibn Malik, that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, may Allah be pleased with him, married a woman from the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone. The Prophet ﷺ noticed the radiance of the wedding and asked him. He said: \I have married a woman for the weight of a date-stone in gold.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Sulayman ibn Harb"," and Muslim extracted it through another chain from Shu'bah. [Sahih — previously cited]"""
"14368","(14362) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us: Mu'adh ibn Mu'adh narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas, who said: 'Abd al-Rahman arrived as an emigrant, and the Prophet ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Sa'd ibn al-Rabi', may Allah be pleased with him. Sa'd said to him: \I have two wives; whichever of them you prefer"," I shall divorce"," and when her waiting period expires"," marry her. And I have wealth; half of it is yours.\"" He said: \""May Allah bless you in your family and your wealth. Direct me to the market.\"" So they directed him. He did not return that day until he brought some items. Then the Prophet ﷺ missed him and came to him"," and upon him was the radiance of yellowness. He said to him: \""What is this?\"" He said: \""I married a woman from the Ansar.\"" He asked: \""For how much?\"" He said: \""For a date-stone in gold\"" — or he said: \""For the weight of a date-stone in gold.\"" He said: \""Hold a wedding feast"," even if it be with a single sheep.\"" He (the narrator) also said: al-Za'farani narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Humayd narrated to us"," from Anas"," similarly"," except that he said: \""He obtained some ghee and dried yoghurt"," and profited from them.\"" Al-Bukhari and Muslim both narrated it in their Sahihs through other chains from Humayd al-Tawil. [Sahih — previously cited]"""
"14369","(14363) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us: 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'bah informed me: Humayd — who heard Anas — said: \'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf married for the weight of a date-stone in gold.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""Hold a wedding feast"," even if it be with a single sheep.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abu Musa from Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi. [Sahih — previously cited]"""
"14370","(14364) Abu Muhammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us: Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabah al-Za'farani narrated to us: 'Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf married a woman from the Ansar for the weight of a date-stone in gold, and that was permissible. Al-Bukhari and Muslim both narrated it in their Sahihs through another chain from Shu'bah, without the statement \and that was permissible.\"" [Sahih — previously cited]"""
"14371","(14365) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥamzah al-Harawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Ḥajjāj narrated from Qatādah, from Anas, who said: \It — meaning the date-stone (nawāh) — was valued at three dirhams and a third.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"14372","(14366) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Rāshid narrated to us; ʿAbbās al-Bayrūtī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Shuʿayb ibn Shābūr narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Bashīr informed me that Qatādah narrated to him from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf married a woman from the Anṣār for a weight of a date-stone (nawāh) of gold, which was valued at five dirhams. And this is more likely.\n\n[Weak]"
"14373","(14367) For Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārizī narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿUbayd said: His statement \nawāh\"" means five dirhams. He said: Five dirhams are referred to as \""nawāh of gold","\"" just as forty are referred to as an \""ūqiyyah","\"" and twenty are referred to as a \""nashsh.\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated it to me from Sufyān"," from Manṣūr"," from Mujāhid"," who said: \""The ūqiyyah is forty"," the nashsh is twenty"," and the nawāh is five.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"14374","(14368) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Walīd informed me; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Ibn Jurayj informed me; Abū al-Zubayr informed me, saying: I heard Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: \We used to contract mutʿah marriage with a handful of dates and flour during the days of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abū Bakr"," until ʿUmar forbade it in the matter of ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ. The evidence has already been established from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he prohibited mutʿah marriage after having permitted it"," and the abrogation pertains to the stipulation of a fixed term"," not to the amount of ṣadāq (dower) upon which they used to marry. And Allah knows best.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1405]"""
"14375","(14369) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān, ʿImrān al-Sakhtiyānī, and a group narrated to us, saying: Abū Saʿid al-Ashajj narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Sulaymān narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn ʬAṭāʾ narrated from his father, from Jābir: \We used to marry during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a handful of food.\"" This is the first hadith"," except that he reported it with this wording. And Yaʿqūb ibn ʬAṭāʾ is not used as a basis for argument.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"14376","(14370) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Muḥammad al-Muʾaddib narrated to us; Ṣāliḥ ibn Rūmān narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \If a man were to marry a woman for a palmful of food"," that would constitute a ṣadāq (dower).\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"14377","(14371) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mubashshir narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Mūsā ibn Muslim ibn Rūmān narrated from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever gives as ṣadāq (dower) a double handful of wheat"," dates"," sawīq (parched barley meal)"," or flour"," has made it lawful.\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the Sunan from Isḥāq ibn Jibrīl from Yazīd ibn Hārūn with part of its meaning.\n\n[Weak]"""
"14378","(14372) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us; Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Rustah narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn ʿAnbasah narrated to us; Wakīʿ narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Labībah narrated from his father, from his grandfather Abī Labībah, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever deems lawful (a dower of) one dirham"," has made it lawful\"" — meaning"," the marriage.\n\nAbū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated it from Wakīʿ from Ibn Abī Labībah from his grandfather from the Prophet ﷺ.\n\n[Weak]"""
"14379","(14373) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Lakhmī narrated to us; Muʿādh ibn al-Mathanná, Yūsuf al-Qāḍī, and Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Tammār narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah from his father, who said: \A man from Banī Fazārah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have married a woman for two sandals.' So the Prophet ﷺ permitted his marriage.\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"14380","(14374) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Shuʿbah informed me; ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Rabīʿah narrating from his father that a woman from Fazārah was brought to the Prophet ﷺ who had married herself for two sandals. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \Are you pleased"," with respect to yourself and your wealth"," with two sandals?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" So he permitted it.\n\nʿĀṣim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿĀṣim ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb: the scholars have spoken regarding him"," and despite his weakness"," the leading imams have narrated from him.\n\n[Weak. Preceded earlier]"""
"14381","(14375) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī — narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabīʿ, from ʿUmayr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Khathʿamī, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Mughīrah al-Ṭāʾifī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Marry off your unmarried women among you.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what are the mutual rights between them?\"" He said: \""That upon which their families mutually agree.\"" [Weak (Ḍaʿīf)]"""
"14382","(14376) Abū ʿAbdullāh and Abū Bakr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Yaḥyā narrated to us, from Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth and Abī Muʿāwiyah, from Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn al-Mughīrah al-Ṭāʾifī, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, from the Prophet (ﷺ), a similar narration. This one is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected)."
"14383","(14377) And it has been narrated from Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from ʿAbd al-Malik, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), but it is not preserved (maḥfūẓ). Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Rustah informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr Zunayn informed us: Hārūn ibn al-Mughīrah informed us, from Ḥajjāj, and he mentioned it with its meaning."
"14384","(14378) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us: Bundār informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith informed us, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, from his father, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Marry off your unmarried women.\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," what are the mutual rights?\"" He said: \""That upon which their families mutually agree.\"" [Very Weak (Ḍaʿīf Jiddan)]"""
"14385","(14379) And it has been narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī, from his father, from Ibn ʿAbbās, from the Prophet (ﷺ), with a similar narration, except that he said: \That upon which the families mutually agree"," even if it be a twig of an arāk tree.\"" Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us: Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us: Muḥammad ibn Munīr al-Maṭīrī informed us: al-Ramādī informed us: ʿAmr ibn Khālid al-Ḥarrānī informed us: Ṣāliḥ ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār — who is Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥaḍramī — informed us"," from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī"," and he mentioned it. Abū Aḥmad (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Baylamānī is weak"," and Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith is weak"," and the weakness in their ḥadīth is clear. The Shaykh said: Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and others among the narrators of biographical evaluations said the same. And this ḥadīth has a supporting witness through another chain. [Very Weak (Ḍaʿīf Jiddan)]"""
"14386","(14380) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us: Abū Hārūn al-ʿAbdī informed us, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the dowry (ṣadāq) of women, and he said: \It is that upon which their families mutually agree.\"" [Very Weak (Ḍaʿīf Jiddan)]"""
"14387","(14381) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, from Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ and Sharīk, from Abū Hārūn, from Abū Saʿīd. Sharīk said: He raised it to the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \There is no sin upon a man if he marries with a small or large amount of his wealth"," provided they mutually agree and witnesses are present.\""\n\nAbū Hārūn al-ʿAbdī is not used as a ḥujjah (authoritative proof). And it has been narrated through another weak chain from Abū Saʿīd"," raised (marfūʿan). Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And it has reached us that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Three handfuls of raisins constitute a dowry (mahr).\"" [Very Weak (Ḍaʿīf Jiddan)]"""
"14388","(14382) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās — Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb — informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Ādam informed us, from Sharīk, from Ismāʿīl ibn Muslim, from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \If she is pleased with a tooth-stick (siwāk) of arāk"," then that is her dowry (mahr).\"" [Weak (Ḍaʿīf)]"""
"14389","(14383) As for the ḥadīth narrated by Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd, from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from ʿAṭāʾ and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Women should not be married except by their equals (akfāʾ)"," and they should not be given in marriage except by their guardians (awliyāʾ)"," and there is no dowry less than ten dirhams.\""\n\nAḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Sukayn al-Baldī informed us: Zakariyyā ibn al-Ḥakam al-Rasʿanī informed us: Abū al-Mughīrah — ʿAbd al-Quddūs ibn al-Ḥajjāj — informed us: Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd informed us"," and he mentioned it. [Very Weak (Ḍaʿīf Jiddan)]"""
"14390","(14384) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd al-Maṭbaqī informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith Jaḥdar informed us: Baqiyyah informed us, from Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAlī — al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed us: Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān al-Wāsiṭī informed us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muṣaffā informed us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd informed us: Mubashshir informed us, from al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh, from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār, from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \There is no dowry less than ten dirhams.\""\n\nAbū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ said: Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd is matrūk al-ḥadīth (abandoned in ḥadīth)"," and this is munkar (rejected); he was not followed in it. ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar said: Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd is matrūk al-ḥadīth; his aḥādīth are not corroborated. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh is not used as a ḥujjah"," and no one narrated this from al-Ḥajjāj other than Mubashshir ibn ʿUbayd al-Ḥalabī"," and they unanimously agreed upon abandoning him. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal (may Allah have mercy on him) used to accuse him of fabricating aḥādīth. [Very Weak (Ḍaʿīf Jiddan). Preceded before it.]"""
"14391","(14385) As for the report that Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us — Sharīk narrated from Dāwūd al-Awdī, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The minimum amount by which the private part is made lawful is ten dirhams.\"" [Weak]"""
"14392","(14386) And he informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-Ṭayyib Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Khayyāṭ narrated to us — Sahl ibn ʿAmmār narrated to us — Abū Muʿāwiya ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Qays narrated to us — Dāwūd ibn Yazīd narrated, saying: I heard al-Shaʿbī narrating, saying: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \There is no dowry (ṣadāq) less than ten dirhams.\"" [Weak; preceded before it]"""
"14393","(14387) And Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān said: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) said: \They narrated from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) something the like of which is not established"," even if no one else contradicted it"," that a dowry (mahr) cannot be less than ten dirhams.\"" [Sound; in al-Umm 7/224]"""
"14394","(14388) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Qutayba narrated to us — Ibn Numayr narrated to me — Ibn al-Baṣīr Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh al-Ashjaʿī, who said: I said to Sufyān, meaning al-Thawrī: \The ḥadīth of Dāwūd al-Awdī from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him): 'There is no dowry less than ten dirhams.'\"" So Sufyān said: \""Dāwūd"," Dāwūd? This has continuously been rejected against him.\"" I said: \""Shuʿba narrated from him.\"" So he struck his forehead and said: \""Dāwūd"," Dāwūd?\"" [Sound]"""
"14395","(14389) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā saying: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq saying: I heard Abū Sayyār saying: I heard Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal saying: \Ghiyāth ibn Ibrāhīm prompted Dāwūd al-Awdī with the narration from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," who said: 'A dowry shall not be less than ten dirhams","' and thus it became a ḥadīth.\"" [Sound; for Imam Aḥmad]"""
"14396","(14390) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated, saying: I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad saying: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn saying: \Ghiyāth is a liar; he is neither trustworthy nor reliable.\"" Abū al-Faḍl said: He is Ghiyāth ibn Ibrāhīm al-Baṣrī. He said: And I heard Yaḥyā saying: \""Dāwūd al-Awdī is nothing.\"" [i.e."," of no standing]"""
"14397","(14391) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us — Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us — al-Sājī said: I heard Ibn al-Muthannā saying: \I never heard Yaḥyā"," meaning Ibn Saʿīd al-Qaṭṭān"," nor ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," meaning Ibn Mahdī"," narrate anything from Sufyān from Dāwūd ibn Yazīd"," ever.\"" And with the same meaning"," ʿAmr ibn ʿAlī said: And it has been narrated from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him) to the contrary of that."""
"14398","(14392) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed me — ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — Abū Shayba narrated to us — Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us — Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \The dowry (ṣadāq) is that upon which the spouses mutually agree.\"" [Weak]"""
"14399","(14393) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Sufyān narrated from Ayyūb ibn Mūsā, from Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qusayṭ, who said: \A man was given glad tidings of a female slave"," so a man said: 'Grant her to me as a gift.' That was mentioned to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," and he said: 'The gifted self (al-mawhūba) has not been lawful for anyone after the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). And if he were to give her a whip or less as a dowry"," it would be permissible.' And he said in another place: 'And if he were to give her a whip as a dowry"," she would be lawful for him.'\"" [Sound; extracted by al-Shāfiʿī in al-Umm 5/60]"""
"14400","(14394) And Abū Saʿīd informed us — Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us — al-Rabīʿ informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Ibn Abī Yaḥyā said: \I asked Rabīʿa: 'What is the minimum of the dowry?' He said: 'That upon which the families are mutually satisfied.' I said: 'Even if it were a single dirham?' He said: 'Even if it were half a dirham.' I said: 'Even if it were less?' He said: 'Even if it were a handful of wheat or a single grain of wheat.'\"" [Weak]"""
"14401","(14395) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Ismāʿīl informed me; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Imām narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wārith ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith al-ʿAnbarī narrated to me; my father narrated to me from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," the greatest of sins in the sight of Allah is a man who marries a woman"," and when he has fulfilled his need from her"," he divorces her and takes away her dowry; and a man who employs a worker and takes his wages; and another who kills a beast without cause.\"" [Weak]"""
"14402","(14396) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Abū ʿImrān al-Tustarī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥuṣayn ibn al-Qāṣṣ al-Qaṣṣāṣ, client of Quraysh, said: I heard al-Sakan ibn Ismāʿīl; al-Ḥasan ibn Dhakwān narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \Love of the Anṣār is faith"," and hatred of them is disbelief. And any man who marries a woman upon a dowry while he does not intend to give it to her"," he is an adulterer.\"" Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn and others also narrated it from al-Sakan ibn Ismāʿīl. And Abū ʿĀṣim al-ʿAbādānī narrated it from al-Ḥasan ibn Dhakwān from al-Ḥasan from Abū Hurayrah. [Weak]"""
"14403","(14397) It has been narrated in this chapter from Ṣuhayb, marfūʿ: ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar al-Anṣārī narrated to us from a man from al-Nimr ibn Qāsiṭ who said: I heard Ṣuhayb ibn Sinān narrating; he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever gives a dowry to a woman while Allah knows that he does not intend to fulfill it"," he has deceived her by Allah and made her private part lawful through falsehood. He will meet Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer.\"" [Weak]"""
"14404","(14398) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us from Abū Ḥāzim from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī: A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," I have given myself to you.\"" She stood for a long while. Then a man stood and said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," marry her to me if you have no need of her.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Do you have anything with which to give her a dowry?\"" He said"," \""I have nothing but this lower garment of mine.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said"," \""If you give it to her"," you will sit without a lower garment. Seek something.\"" He said"," \""I find nothing.\"" He said"," \""Seek even an iron ring.\"" He sought but found nothing. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Do you have any of the Qurʾān?\"" He said"," \""Yes"," such-and-such a sūrah and such-and-such a sūrah\"" — naming certain sūrahs. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""I have married her to you with what you have of the Qurʾān.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Abū Ḥāzim. [Sound. Agreed upon"," and it has been cited extensively before.]"""
"14405","(14399) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Farrāʾ informed us; Muʿāwiyah ibn ʿAmr informed us; Zāʾidah informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Baghawī narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī narrated to us from Zāʾidah from Abū Ḥāzim from Sahl ibn Saʿd who said: A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) — and he narrated the hadith with part of the meaning of Mālik's hadith. Mālik's hadith is more complete. And at the end of it he said: \Do you recite anything from the Qurʾān?\"" He said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""Go"," for I have married her to you with what you teach her of the Qurʾān.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," and he said: \""Go"," for I have married her to you"," so teach her from the Qurʾān.\""\n\n[Sound. It was cited before it.]"""
"14406","(14400) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Ibrāhīm ibn Yaḥyā al-Rāzī narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me; my father Ḥafṣ ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṭahmān narrated to me from al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Ḥajjāj al-Bāhilī from ʿIsl from ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), with a narration similar to the story of Sahl ibn Saʿd, though he did not mention the lower garment or the ring. He said: \What do you preserve of the Qurʾān?\"" He said"," \""Sūrat al-Baqarah or the one that follows it.\"" He said"," \""Stand and teach her twenty verses"," and she is your wife.\"" The wording is that of Abū Dāwūd's hadith. And in the narration of al-Rāzī: \""I have married her to you.\"" [Weak]"""
"14407","(14401) Shuʿbah narrated it from ʿIsl, and he sent it (as a mursal narration). Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Muḥammadābādhī narrated to us; Abū Qilābah narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Wārith, narrated to us; Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿIsl from ʿAṭāʾ: A man married a woman upon the condition that he would teach her the Qurʾān. This was raised to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and he permitted it. [Weak]"
"14408","(14402) Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated it from ʿAbd al-Ṣamad, except that he said: \Something of the Qurʾān","\"" and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) permitted that. Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us; Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us; al-Sājī narrated to us; Ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ṣamad narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Weak. It was cited before it.]"""
"14409","(14403) As for the hadith narrated by ʿUtbah ibn al-Sakan from al-Awzāʿī from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ziyād ibn Abī Ziyād from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sakhrat from Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him): A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," give me your opinion\"" — the hadith. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to the one who had proposed to her"," \""Do you recite anything from the Qurʾān?\"" He said"," \""Yes"," Sūrat al-Baqarah and Sūrat al-Mufaṣṣal.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""I have married her to you on the condition that you recite to her and teach her"," and when Allah provides for you"," compensate her.\"" So the man married her upon that. Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar"," Abū al-Ḥasan al-Dāraquṭnī al-Ḥāfiẓ"," narrated to us; Abū ʿUbayd al-Qāsim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; al-Qāsim ibn Hāshim al-Simsār narrated to us; ʿUtbah ibn al-Sakan narrated to us; al-Awzāʿī narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. Abū al-Ḥasan said: ʿUtbah is the sole narrator of it"," and he is abandoned in hadith. The Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ʿUtbah ibn al-Sakan is accused of fabrication"," and this is baseless with no foundation. And Allah knows best. [Baseless]"""
"14410","(14404) Abū ʿAmr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Adīb informed us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us; ʿImrān ibn Mūsā narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUraym ibn Mayṣarah al-Qawārīrī narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Yazīd, Abū Maʿshar al-Barrāʾ, narrated to us; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah from Ibn ʿAbbās: A group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a tribe among the Arab tribes in which there was a person stung (or afflicted). They said, \Is there among you a practitioner of incantation (rāqī)"," for there is among the water a stung (or afflicted) person?\"" So a man from among them went and performed incantation upon him for a sheep"," and he was cured. When he came to his companions"," they disapproved of that and said"," \""You have taken a wage for the Book of Allah!\"" When they came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was informed of that. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called the man and asked him. He said"," \""O Messenger of Allah"," we passed by a tribe among the Arab tribes in which there was a stung (or afflicted) person"," and they said"," 'Is there among you a practitioner of incantation?' So I performed incantation upon him with the Opening of the Book (Fātiḥat al-Kitāb)"," and he was cured.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""The most deserving thing upon which you take a wage is the Book of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saydān ibn Muḍārib from Abū Maʿshar. The remainder of this chapter and what has been narrated in opposition to it has already passed in the Book of Hire (Kitāb al-Ijārah). [Sound. Bukhārī 5737]"""
"14411","Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us — Abu al-Hasan al-Tarafiyy narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimiyy narrated to us — 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah from Ibn 'Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, regarding this verse, he said: It refers to a man who marries a woman without specifying a dower for her, then divorces her before consummating the marriage. Allah, the Most High, commanded that she be given a gift of consolation (mut'ah) according to his means and circumstances. If he is well-off, he should provide her with a servant or something of that nature; and if he is of limited means, then with three garments or something equivalent to that. [Da'if]"
"14412","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Farisiyy narrated to us — Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Isbahaniyy narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Faris narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Isma'il narrated to us — Ahmad narrated from Ibn Wahb, who heard Ayyub ibn Sa'd from Musa ibn 'Uqba from Nafi': that a man came to Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, and mentioned that he had separated from his wife. He said: Give her such-and-such and clothe her with such-and-such. We calculated that, and it amounted to approximately thirty dirhams. I said to Nafi': What was the condition of this man? He said: He was of moderate means. And it has been narrated to us through another chain from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The minimum amount for a gift of consolation (mut'ah) is thirty dirhams. [Da'if]"
"14413","Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulamy narrated to us — Abu al-Hasan al-Kariziyy narrated to us — 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated from Abu 'Ubayd — Hushaym narrated from Ibn Ishaq from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim from his father from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Awf, that he divorced his woman and gave her a gift of consolation by means of a black female servant, whom he presented to her. Abu 'Ubayd said: That is, he gave her the gift of consolation after the divorce. The Arabs used to call the mut'ah \al-tahmim.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14414","Abu al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Ma'ruf al-Faqih narrated to us — Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayiniyy narrated to us — Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Nasr al-Haddha' narrated to us — 'Ali ibn al-Madiniyy narrated to us — Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us — Mansur ibn Zadhan narrated from Ibn Sirin: that al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, divorced a woman of his and gave her a gift of consolation of ten thousand dirhams. She said: \A meagre provision from a beloved I am parting from.\"" When this reached him"," he took her back. [Sahih]"""
"14415","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Balawayh narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq, i.e., ibn Khuzaymah, narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Kaysan narrated from Mihran ibn Abi 'Umar from Sufyan from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Abdullah from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd from his father: that al-Hasan ibn 'Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, gave a woman a gift of consolation of twenty thousand and two skins of honey. The woman said: \A meagre provision from a beloved who is departing.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14416","Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman narrated to us — al-Shafi'i said: It has been narrated from the Prophet ﷺ — \may my father and mother be sacrificed for him\"" — that he gave a ruling regarding Barwa' bint Washiq"," who had been married without a dower being specified"," and her husband died. He decreed for her the dower of her like (mahr al-mithl) and decreed for her the inheritance. If this is established from the Prophet ﷺ"," then it is the most deserving of matters for us to follow"," and there is no proof in the statement of anyone other than the Prophet ﷺ"," no matter how numerous they may be"," nor in any analogy"," and there is nothing in his statement except obedience to Allah through submission to Him. And if it is not established from the Prophet ﷺ"," then it is not permissible for anyone to attribute to him that which is not established"," and I do not preserve it through any chain that would establish its like. It is sometimes narrated from Ma'qil ibn Yasar"," and sometimes from Ma'qil ibn Sinan"," and sometimes from one of the Ashja' whose name is not mentioned: that if he dies or she dies"," there is no dower for her and no mut'ah. [Sahih]"""
"14417","The Shaykh, may Allah have mercy on him, said: In the hadith of Barwa' bint Washiq, this is the discrepancy that al-Shafi'i mentioned. However, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdiyy is an imam among the imams of hadith, and he narrated it as Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'iyy narrated to us — 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to us — my father narrated to us — 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdiyy narrated from Sufyan from Firas from al-Sha'bi from Masruq from 'Abdullah, regarding a man who married a woman and died without having consummated the marriage with her and without having specified a dower for her. He said: She is entitled to the full dower, she must observe the waiting period ('iddah), and she is entitled to the inheritance. Then Ma'qil ibn Sinan stood up and said: I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave such a ruling regarding Barwa' bint Washiq. This is a sound (sahih) chain of narration, and in it Ma'qil ibn Sinan is named, and he is a well-known Companion. [Sahih]"
"14418","Yazid ibn Harun, who is one of the great memorizers of hadith alongside 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdiyy and others, narrated it through another sound chain as well. Abu al-Husayn 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Bishran al-'Adl narrated to us in Baghdad — Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Bakhtariyy narrated to us — Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Fahham and Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Yazid both narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us — Sufyan al-Thawri narrated from Mansur from Ibrahim from 'Alqamah: that 'Abdullah was asked about a woman whose husband died without having specified a dower for her and without having consummated the marriage with her. They kept returning to him and persisted with him until he said: I will give my opinion: she is entitled to the dower of her peers, without reduction or excess, she must observe the waiting period, and she is entitled to the inheritance. Then Ma'qil ibn Sinan, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up and testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a ruling regarding Barwa' bint Washiq al-Ashja'iyyah similar to what you have ruled. And 'Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, was overjoyed. [Sahih; previously mentioned]"
"14419","Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbariyy narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — 'Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated — Yazid ibn Harun and Ibn Mahdiyy narrated from Sufyan from Mansur from Ibrahim from 'Alqamah from 'Abdullah, and he mentioned it. Similarly, 'Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-'Adaniyy narrated it from Sufyan al-Thawri, and he said: Then Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'iyy, may Allah be pleased with him, stood up. And some of the narrators narrated it from 'Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri through this last chain, and he said: Then Ma'qil ibn Yasar stood up. [Sahih]"
"14420","And some of the narrators mentioned it from Yazid ibn Harun from al-Thawri, and I consider it to be an error. Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz narrated to us the hadith of Yazid — Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us — Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us — Sufyan ibn Sa'id narrated, and he mentioned it, and he said: Ma'qil ibn Yasar. [Munkar]"
"14421","(14415) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, narrating from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Razzāq: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Masʿūd Aḥmad ibn al-Furāt narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated from Sufyān, who mentioned its meaning and said: \If it is correct"," then it is from Allah"," and if it is an error"," then it is from me. She is entitled to the mahr of her peers"," she must observe the ʿiddah"," and she is entitled to the inheritance.\"" Then Maʿqil ibn Yasār stood up — and this is a confusion (wahm); the correct narration is Maʿqil ibn Sinān"," as narrated by ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī and others. And Allah knows best. [Munkar]"""
"14422","(14416) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Shaybānī in Kūfah narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim ibn Abī Gharazah narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn Mushir narrated to us, Dāwūd ibn Abī Hind narrated from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlqamah ibn Qays: that a group of people came to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd and said to him: \A man among us married a woman and did not stipulate a mahr for her"," and he did not consummate the marriage with her until he died.\"" ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""No question has been put to me since I departed from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) more difficult than this. Go to someone else.\"" They said: \""They differed about it for a month"," then at the end of that they said to him: 'Whom shall we ask if we do not ask you? You are the brother of the Companions of Muḥammad (ﷺ) in this town"," and we find no one else.'\"" He said: \""Then I shall give my ruling based on my own ijtihād. If it is correct"," then it is from Allah alone"," with no partner"," and if it is an error"," then it is from me"," and Allah and His Messenger are free from it.\"" He said: \""I see that she be given a mahr equal to the mahr of her peers"," without diminution or excess"," and she is entitled to the inheritance"," and she must observe the ʿiddah of four months and ten days.\"" He said: \""And that was heard by a group of the Ashjaʿ"," and they stood up and said: 'We bear witness that you have ruled with the same ruling that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave concerning a woman from among us called Barwaʿ bint Wāshiq.'\"" He said: \""ʿAbdullāh was not seen to rejoice over anything as he rejoiced that day"," except for his acceptance of Islam.\"" Then he said: \""O Allah"," if it is correct"," then it is from You alone"," with no partner"," and if it is an error"," then it is me and Shayṭān"," and Allah and His Messenger are free from it.\"" Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid narrated it from al-Shaʿbī from ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd"," and he said in it: \""Then Maʿqil ibn Sinān al-Ashjaʿī stood up.\"" And Ibn ʿAwn narrated it from al-Shaʿbī"," from a man"," from Ibn Masʿūd"," and he said in it: \""Then the Ashjaʿī said…\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"14423","(14417) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Abū Ḥassān and Khilāṣ ibn ʿAmr — both of them narrating from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd: that Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a man who married a woman and died before consummating the marriage with her, and he had not stipulated a mahr for her. They differed about it for a month, or nearly a month. Then they said: \You must give a ruling concerning it.\"" He said: \""I rule that she is entitled to the mahr of a woman among her peers"," without diminution or excess"," and she is entitled to the inheritance"," and she must observe the ʿiddah. If it is correct"," then it is from Allah"," and if it is an error"," then it is from myself and from Shayṭān"," and Allah and His Messenger are free from that.\"" A group from among the Ashjaʿ stood up"," among them al-Jarrāḥ and Abū Sinān"," and they said: \""We bear witness that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled concerning a woman from among us called Barwaʿ bint Wāshiq — her husband was Hilāl ibn Murrah al-Ashjaʿī — with the same ruling.\"" Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) rejoiced greatly when his ruling coincided with the ruling of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). Hammām ibn Yaḥyā narrated it from Qatādah"," from Abū Ḥassān. And Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated it from Qatādah"," from Khilāṣ. The Shaykh said: \""This difference regarding the naming of the one who narrated the story of Barwaʿ bint Wāshiq from the Prophet (ﷺ) does not weaken the ḥadīth"," for all of these narrations have sound chains of transmission"," and in some of them there is evidence that a group from the Ashjaʿ witnessed that. Thus"," some of the narrators named one of them"," some named another"," some named two"," and some left it general without naming. Such a thing does not invalidate the ḥadīth. Were it not for the trustworthiness of the one who narrated it from the Prophet (ﷺ)"," there would be no meaning to ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd's joy at his narration. And Allah knows best.\"" [Ṣaḥīh. It was cited before it.]"""
"14424","(14418) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ: that the daughter of ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar — her mother being the daughter of Zayd ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — was married to a son of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar. He died without having consummated the marriage with her and without having stipulated a mahr for her. Her mother sought her mahr, so Ibn ʿUmar said: \She has no mahr. If she had a mahr"," we would not withhold it from you"," nor would we wrong her.\"" She refused to accept that"," so they appointed Zayd ibn Thābit as arbitrator between them. He ruled that she had no mahr"," but she was entitled to the inheritance. [Ṣaḥīh. Mālik narrated it (1120).]"""
"14425","(14419) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Sulaymān ibn Yasār: that Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) married his son to the daughter of his brother ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar, and his son was young at the time, and he did not stipulate a mahr for her. The boy lived for some time, then died. The maternal aunt of the girl took up the dispute with Ibn ʿUmar before Zayd ibn Thābit. Ibn ʿUmar said to Zayd: \I married my son"," and I intended to do well by him"," but he died before that"," and I did not stipulate a mahr for the girl.\"" Zayd said: \""She is entitled to the inheritance"," if the boy had any wealth"," and she must observe the ʿiddah"," but she has no mahr.\"" [Ṣaḥīh. Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated it (925).]"""
"14426","(14420) And with the same meaning, Ibn ʿAbbās said, as narrated by Sufyān al-Thawrī from ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās. Abū Bakr al-Ardistānī informed us, Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us, Sufyān al-Jawharī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, Sufyān narrated it."
"14427","(14421) And similarly it was narrated from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us, ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib narrated to me, ʿAbd Khayr said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: \She is entitled to the inheritance"," and she must observe the ʿiddah"," but she has no mahr.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"14428","(14422) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Khālid ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib, from ʿAbd Khayr, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said regarding a woman whose husband died without having stipulated a mahr for her: \She is entitled to the inheritance"," and she has no mahr.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"14429","(14423) He said: And Khālid narrated to us from Muṭarrif, from al-Ḥakam, from ʿAlī, the like of that. He said: And Hushaym informed us, Muḥammad ibn Sālim narrated to us from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \She is entitled to the inheritance"," and she must observe the ʿiddah"," but she has no mahr.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"14430","(14424) He said: And Hushaym informed us, Abū Isḥāq al-Kūfī narrated to us from Mazīdah ibn Jābir that ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \We do not accept the statement of a Bedouin from the Ashjaʿ over the Book of Allah.\"" And it has been narrated to us from Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ — Jābir ibn Zayd — and ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ that they both said: \""She is entitled only to the inheritance.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14431","(14425) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — 'Abd al-Majid informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: I heard Aṭā' saying: I heard Ibn 'Abbās being asked about a woman whose husband had died and for whom a dowry (ṣadāq) had been stipulated. He said: She is entitled to the dowry and the inheritance. [Ḥasan]"
"14432","(14426) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr informed us — Abu al-'Abbas informed us — al-Rabi' informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — 'Abd al-Wahhāb informed us, from Ayyūb ibn Abī Tamīmah, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, that Ash'ath ibn Qays accompanied a man and saw his wife, and she impressed him. The man died on the road, so Ash'ath ibn Qays proposed marriage to her, but she refused to marry him except upon her own judgment (ḥukm). He married her upon her condition, then divorced her before he could render his judgment. He said: \Render your judgment.\"" She said: \""I judge by so-and-so and so-and-so\"" — slaves who were part of her father's inherited estate. He said: \""Render a judgment other than these.\"" She refused"," so he came to 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," I have been helpless three times.\"" He asked: \""What are they?\"" He said: \""I fell in love with a woman.\"" He said: \""That is something you did not own.\"" He said: \""Then I married her upon her judgment"," then I divorced her before she could render her judgment.\"" 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""She is a Muslim woman.\"" Al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""Meaning"," 'Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," she is entitled to the dowry of a Muslim woman — meaning"," the dowry of her peers among her women — and Allah knows best.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""
"14433","(14427) Abu Bakr ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us — Abu Naṣr al-'Irāqī informed us — Sufyān al-Jawharī informed us — 'Alī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn al-Walīd informed us — Sufyān informed us, from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī and Hishām, from Ibn Sīrīn, that Ash'ath ibn Qays married a woman he loved upon her judgment. She imposed upon him two slaves of his as her judgment. So he came to 'Umar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \I married a woman out of love.\"" He said: \""That is because you did not yet own her.\"" He said: \""I accepted her judgment.\"" He said: \""Her judgment is nothing for her — except the established dowry of her peers among women.\"" [Ḍa'īf; previously cited]"""
"14434","(14428) Abu 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abu Bakr — Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr — said: Abu al-'Abbas Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us — Ḥajjāj, who is ibn Muḥammad, said: Ibn Jurayj said: 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Amr ibn al-'Āṣ, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \Any woman who is married with a dowry"," or a gift"," or a stipulated period"," before the consummation of the marriage — it is hers. And whatever is given after the consummation of the marriage goes to whomever it is given to. And the most deserving of the honor by which a man is honored is his daughter or his sister.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""
"14435","(14429) Abu Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abu Mas'ūd Aḥmad ibn al-Furāt informed us — 'Affān ibn Muslim informed us — (ḥ) — and Abu 'Abd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsūs al-Sūsī, and Abu Bakr al-Qāḍī, and Abu Sa'id al-Ṣayrafī, said: Abu al-'Abbas Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us — 'Affān informed us — 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Ziyād informed us — al-Ḥajjāj ibn Arṭāh informed us, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from 'Urwah, from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet ﷺ said: \Whatever is given as a dowry or a stipulated period by which a woman's intimate part is made lawful — it is hers. And whatever is given by which her father"," brother"," or guardian is honored after the marriage contract — it is his. And the most deserving of the honor by which a man is honored is his daughter or his sister.\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Ṣaghānī. [Ḍa'īf]"""
"14436","(14430) Abu al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Tammār informed us — Abu al-Walīd informed us — Layth informed me — Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb informed me, from Abī al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Āmir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The most deserving of conditions to be fulfilled are those by which you have made intimate relations lawful.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abu al-Walīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 2721]"""
"14437","(14431) Abu Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — 'Abd Allāh ibn Ja'far informed us — Abu Mas'ūd Aḥmad ibn al-Furāt informed us — Abu Usāmah informed us — 'Abd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ja'far informed us, from Yazīd ibn Abī Ḥabīb, from Marthad ibn 'Abd Allāh, who is Abū al-Khayr, from 'Uqbah ibn 'Āmir al-Juhanī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The most deserving of conditions to be fulfilled are those by which you have made intimate relations lawful.\"" Muslim extracted it in the Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from 'Abd al-Ḥamīd ibn Ja'far. Al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said regarding the Sunnah of the Prophet ﷺ: \""Conditions are fulfilled only with what is established as permissible"," and no Sunnah indicates that it is impermissible.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; previously cited]"""
"14438","(14432) Abu 'Abd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abu al-'Abbas Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us — Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us — men among the people of knowledge, among them Yūnus ibn Yazīd and Layth ibn Sa'd, informed us — that Ibn Shihāb informed them, from 'Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: Barīrah came to me and said: \O 'Ā'ishah"," I have contracted with my family for seven ūqiyyahs"," one ūqiyyah per year. Help me"," for I have not paid anything of my contract.\"" 'Ā'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," was inclined toward it and said: \""Return to your family. If they wish that I pay them all at once and that your walā' be mine"," I shall do so.\"" Barīrah went to her family and presented this to them"," but they refused and said: \""If she wishes to do you a favor"," let her do so"," but the walā' will be ours.\"" 'Ā'ishah mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and he said: \""Let that not prevent you. Buy and free her"," for the walā' belongs to the one who frees.\"" She did so. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people"," praised Allah"," and said: \""To proceed: What is the matter with people who stipulate conditions that are not in the Book of Allah"," Exalted is He? Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah"," it is void — even if it were a hundred conditions. The judgment of Allah is more deserving of fulfillment"," and the condition of Allah is more binding. And the walā' belongs to the one who frees.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah"," from Layth"," and Muslim narrated it from Abī al-Ṭāhir"," from Ibn Wahb"," from Yūnus. Al-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said"," and it has also been narrated from him: \""The Muslims are bound by their conditions"," except a condition that makes the unlawful lawful or makes the lawful unlawful.\"" The explanation of his ḥadīth points to its overall meaning. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"14439","(14433) Abu Sa'd al-Mālinī informed us — Abu Aḥmad ibn 'Adī the Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Muḥammad ibn Khuraym al-Qazzāz informed us — Hishām ibn Khālid informed us — Marwān ibn Mu'āwiyah informed us, from Kathīr ibn 'Abd Allāh al-Muzanī, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Muslims are bound by their conditions"," except a condition that makes the lawful unlawful"," or a condition that makes the unlawful lawful.\"" (t) And similarly"," Abū Mu'āwiyah al-Ḍarīr narrated it from Kathīr"," and its meaning was reported from another direction. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"14440","(14434) Abu Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — Abu Muḥammad ibn Ḥayyān al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Ibn Abī 'Āṣim informed us — Ibn Kāsib informed us — Ibn Abī Ḥāzim and Sufyān ibn Ḥamzah informed us, from Kathīr ibn Zayd, from al-Walīd ibn Rabāḥ, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The Muslims are bound by their conditions insofar as they are in accordance with the truth.\"" This is the wording of Sufyān ibn Ḥamzah. [Ḥasan li-ghayrih]"""
"14441","(14435) And this has been narrated from a third weak chain from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and from Anas ibn Mālik, raised (marfūʿ): Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ibn Abī al-Dunyā informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zurārah informed us, ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Jazarī narrated from Khuṣayf from ʿUrwah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) who said: \The Muslims are bound by their conditions"," so long as they are in accordance with the truth.\""\n\nKhuṣayf said: And ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabāḥ narrated to me from Anas ibn Mālik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""The Muslims are bound by their conditions"," so long as they are in accordance with the truth among those conditions.\"" [Ḥasan due to other chains]"""
"14442","(14436) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī informed us, Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā informed us, Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm from Abū Salamah from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) who said: \It is not permissible for a woman to stipulate the divorce of her sister so as to fill her vessel\"" — meaning"," so as to obtain her provision.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Mūsā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5109]"""
"14443","(14437) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from Kathīr ibn Farqad from Saʿīd ibn ʿUbayd ibn al-Sabbāq: A man married a woman during the era of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) and stipulated for her that he would not take her out (of her town). So ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) annulled the condition and said: \The woman is with her husband.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) a contrary view. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14444","(14438) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār and Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz said: Saʿdān informed us, Sufyān narrated from Yazīd ibn Yazīd ibn Jābir from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī al-Muhājir from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ghanm who said: I was present when ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about it, and he said: \She has her house.\"" A man said to him: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," then they will divorce us!\"" He said: \""The decisive points of rights are at the conditions.\""\n\nThe first narration is more in accordance with the Book"," the Sunnah"," and the statements of other Companions (may Allah be pleased with them). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14445","(14439) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār and Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Sufyān narrated from Ibn Abī Laylā from al-Minhāl ibn ʿAmr from ʿAbbād ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Asadī from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: \The condition of Allah takes precedence over her condition.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14446","(14440) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār and Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz said: Saʿdān informed us, Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr from Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ who said: \It is that by whom she has lawful intimacy.\"" Sufyān said: Al-Zuhrī and others said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Whoever stipulates a condition that is not in the Book of Allah"," it is not valid for him"," even if it be a hundred conditions.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14447","(14441) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik informed us: It reached him that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab was asked about a woman who stipulates upon her husband that he will not take her out of her town. Saʿīd said: \He may take her out if he wishes.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from al-Shaʿbī regarding a man who married a woman and stipulated for her her house: he said: \""Her husband is her house.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \""I think her condition should be fulfilled.\""\n\nAnd the statement of the majority is more appropriate. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14448","(14442) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah informed us, Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī who said: A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: \I married a woman and stipulated for her that separation and intimacy are in her hand.\"" He said: \""You have opposed the Sunnah and entrusted the matter to other than its rightful authority. The dower"," separation"," and intimacy are in your hand.\"" He said: A man came to him and said: \""I married a woman and stipulated for her that if I do not bring such-and-such to such-and-such"," then there is no marriage for me.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""The marriage is valid"," and the condition is nothing.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14449","(14443) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated from Ibn Jurayj, ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī narrated to me: A man married a woman, and the woman paid the dower and stipulated upon him that intimacy and separation are in her hand. It was said to him: \You have opposed the Sunnah and entrusted the right to other than its rightful authority.\"" So Ibn ʿAbbās ruled: \""The dower is upon him"," and intimacy and separation are in his hand.\""\n\nIsmāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated from ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī that ʿAlī and Ibn ʿAbbās were asked about a man who married a woman and she stipulated upon him that separation and intimacy are in her hand"," and the dower is upon her. They said: \""You have been blinded from the Sunnah and entrusted the matter to other than its rightful authority. The dū\n\n[Note: The text appears to be cut off at the end. I will complete based on the Urdu context.]\n\n...dower is upon you"," and in your hand are separation and intimacy.\""\n\nAbū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us"," Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīrūyah informed us"," Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us"," Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us"," Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAyyāsh narrated it. And in this there is a break (irsāl) between ʿAṭāʾ al-Khurāsānī and those above him. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14450","(14444) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us, Ibn al-Zubayr narrated from al-Qāsim, the freedman of Khālid ibn Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah, from Abī Umāmah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The women are with their husbands wherever they may be"," except the women of the Anṣār — they shall not be taken out of their houses\"" — meaning"," from Madīnah.\n\nJaʿfar ibn al-Zubayr is very weak. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14451","(14445) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, saying: ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd narrated to us, saying: Jarīr ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us, saying: ʿĪsā ibn ʿĀṣim narrated from Shuʿayb, who said: ʿAlī (may Allāh be pleased with him) asked me about the one referred to as \the one in whose hand is the knot of marriage\"" (al-ladhī bi yadihi ʿuqdat al-nikāḥ). I said: \""It is the guardian (al-walī).\"" He said: \""No"," rather it is the husband (al-zawj).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14452","(14446) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥajjāj ibn al-Minhāl and Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿAlī ibn Zayd from ʿAmmār ibn Abī ʿAmmār from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \The one in whose hand is the knot of marriage is the husband.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14453","(14447) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ghaylān narrated to us, saying: Abū Hishām al-Rifāʿī narrated to us, saying: ʿUbaydullāh narrated from Isrāʾīl from Khuṣayf from Mujāhid from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: \It is the husband.\"" Thus is the narration in these two reports from Ibn ʿAbbās"," although it has been narrated from him to the contrary. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14454","(14448) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī narrated to us verbatim, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated from Abū Salamah: that Jubayr ibn Muṭʿim married a woman from Banī Naṣr, specified a dowry for her, and then divorced her before consummating the marriage. He then recited this verse: \Except if they (the women) forgive"," or he forgives — the one in whose hand is the knot of marriage\"" [al-Baqarah 2:237]. He (Jubayr) said: \""I have a greater right to forgive than she does.\"" So he surrendered her dowry to her. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14455","(14449) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, saying: Ibn ʿAwn narrated from Ibn Sīrīn from Shuʿayb, that he said: \Except if the woman forgives and leaves half of her dowry"," or the husband forgives and completes her dowry for her.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14456","(14450) Abū ʿAbdullāh and ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: \The one in whose hand is the knot of marriage is the husband.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14457","(14451) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated to us, saying: Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Harawī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, saying: Jarīr narrated from Mughīrah from al-Shaʿbī, who said: A man among us married a woman, and her husband divorced her before consummating the marriage. Her brother forgave the dowry, so they brought the matter to Shuʿayb, who validated his forgiveness. Then he later said: \I once forgave the dowry of my daughter.\"" After that he would say: \""The one in whose hand is the knot of marriage is the husband — that he may forgive the entire dowry and surrender it to her"," or she may forgive the half that Allāh has ordained for her. And if they dispute"," then she is entitled to half the dowry.\"" [Ṣaḥīh]"""
"14458","(14452) Through this same chain of narration from al-Shaʿbī, who said: \By Allāh"," Shuʿayb never rendered a judgment more foolish than when he abandoned his first opinion and adopted this one.\"" [Ṣaḥīh. Previously mentioned.]"""
"14459","(14453) Abū Naṣr narrated to us, saying: Abū Manṣūr narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAwanah narrated from Abī Bishr from Ṭāwūs and ʿAṭāʾ and the people of Madīnah, that they said: \The one in whose hand is the knot of marriage is the guardian (al-walī).\"" I informed them of the statement of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr: \""It is the husband","\"" and they retracted their position. When Saʿīd ibn Jubayr arrived"," he said: \""What do you think — if the guardian forgives and the woman refuses"," does the guardian's forgiveness avail anything? Or if she forgives and the guardian refuses"," what concern does the guardian have in that?\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14460","(14454) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ghaylān narrated to us, saying: Abū Hishām al-Rifāʿī narrated to us, saying: Abū Usāmah narrated from Ismāʿīl from al-Shaʿbī from Shuʿayb, who said: \It is the husband; if he wishes"," he may complete the dowry for her.\"" And likewise said Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr"," Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb"," Ṭāwūs"," Mujāhid"," al-Shaʿbī"," and Saʿīd ibn Jubayr. And Ibrāhīm"," ʿAlqamah"," and al-Ḥasan said: \""It is the guardian (al-walī).\"" And Ibn Lahīʿah narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""The guardian of the knot of marriage is the husband.\""\n\nThis is not preserved (ghayr maḥfūẓ)"," and Ibn Lahīʿah is not used as a reliable authority (ghayr muḥtājj bihi). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14461","(14455) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Muslim al-Ṭāʾifī narrated to us, saying: ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated to me from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding the one whom Allah, the Most High, mentioned: {Or the one in whose hand is the marriage contract} — he said: That is her father. [Weak]"
"14462","(14456) And Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Makhlad narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik al-Daqīqī narrated to us, saying: Yazīd ibn Hārūn narrated to us, saying: Warqāʾ ibn ʿUmar narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: {Except if they (the women) forgive} — he said: The woman may forgive, or the one in whose hand is the marriage contract — the guardian (walī) — may forgive. [Authenticated. Narrated by al-Dāraquṭnī]"
"14463","(14457) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: {Except if they (the women) forgive} — he said: She is the thayyib (previously married woman) or the bikr (virgin) who is married by someone other than her father. Allah has placed the right of waiver (al-ʿafw) with them: if they wish, they may forgo it, and if they wish, they may take half the dower. Then He said: {Or the one in whose hand is the marriage contract} — and that is the father of the young virgin. Allah has placed the right of waiver with him; she has no say in the matter alongside him if she is divorced while still under his care. [Weak]"
"14464","(14458) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, saying: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated from Sulaymān from Ibrāhīm that ʿAlqamah said: The one in whose hand is the marriage contract is the guardian (walī). Shuraīḥ said: It is the husband. [Authenticated]"
"14465","(14459) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad al-Qushayrī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʬAṭāʾ narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd narrated from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan, who said: It is the guardian (walī). Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah said: This does not please us. [Good]"
"14466","(14460) And Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah narrated to us, saying: Abū Manṣūr al-Harawī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, saying: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, saying: Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr ibn Dīnār from ʿIkrimah, who said: Allah, Glorified and Most High, commanded forgiveness and permitted it. If she forgives, her forgiveness is valid; and if she is miserly and her guardian forgives, his forgiveness is valid.\n\nHe said: And Saʿīd narrated to us, saying: Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr from Ibrāhīm, who said: It is the guardian (walī).\n\n(Q) This opinion has also been narrated from Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ and al-Zuhrī, and it is the opinion of Mālik. Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) used to hold this view in the earlier period, then in the later period he retracted to the first opinion. And the first opinion is more correct, and Allah knows best. [Authenticated. Narrated by Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr, 3/889]"
"14467","(14461) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā ibn Abī Qumāsh and ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl both narrated to us, saying: Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād narrated from Ayyūb from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When I married Fāṭimah (may Allah be pleased with her), the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," give her something.\"" He said: \""Give her something.\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have nothing.\"" He said: \""Where is your Ḥutamī coat of mail?\"" He said: \""I said: 'It is here with me.'\"" He said: \""Give it to her.\"" [Authenticated]"""
"14468","(14462) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: Kathīr ibn ʿUbayd al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us, saying: Abū Ḥaywah narrated from Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah, who said: Ghaylān ibn Anas narrated to me, who said: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Thawbān narrated to me from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that when ʿAlī married Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he wished to consummate the marriage, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prevented him until he gave her something. He said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I have nothing.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \""Give her her coat of mail.\"" So he gave her his coat of mail and then consummated the marriage. He said: And Kathīr narrated to us"," saying: Abū Ḥaywah narrated from Shuʿayb from Ghaylān from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās"," a similar narration. [Good. Narrated by al-Sijistānī: 2126]"""
"14469","(14463) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Ḥajjāj narrated, saying: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, saying: Abū al-Zubayr narrated to me that he heard ʿIkrimah say: Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: When a man marries a woman and specifies a dower for her, and then wishes to consummate the marriage, let him present to her a cloak or a ring, if he has one. [Authenticated]"
"14470","(14464) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb narrated to me, saying: Yūnus narrated from Nāfiʿ that ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar said: It is not permissible for a man to consummate the marriage with a woman until he presents to her something from her own property — such as clothing or a gift — that she is pleased with. [Authenticated]"
"14471","(14465) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Hārūn ibn Sulaymān al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Mahdī narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Manṣūr, from Ṭalḥah, from Khaythamah, that a man married a woman during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and consummated the marriage with her before paying anything. [Weak]"
"14472","(14466) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr narrated to us, Saʿīd narrated to us, from Ṭalḥah ibn Muṣarrif, from Khaythamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, that a man married a woman and was in difficult financial circumstances. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ commanded that he be treated gently, so he consummated the marriage with her without paying her anything. Later, after that, he became well-off and paid. [Weak; previously mentioned]"
"14473","(14467) Abū Ṭāhir and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Muḥammad narrated to us, Ḥasan ibn Mūsā narrated to us, Sharīk narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Ṭalḥah, from Khaythamah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it. Sharīk connected it and raised it, while others narrated it as a mursal hadith."
"14474","(14468) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Sahl ibn Baḥr narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me, Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, saying: I found in my book from Abū Usāmah, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was six years old"," and he consummated the marriage with me when I was nine years old.\"" She said: \""I came to Madinah and was feverish for a month"," and my hair had matted together. Umm Rūmān came to me while I was on a swing"," and my friends were with me. She called out to me"," so I went to her"," not knowing what she wanted with me. She took my hand and stood me at the door. I was gasping"," 'Huh"," huh","' until my breath settled. Then she brought me into a house where there were women of the Ansār"," who said: 'May goodness"," blessing"," and the best of fortune be upon you.' She handed me over to them"," and they washed my head and prepared me. Nothing alarmed me except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," meaning"," in the forenoon. They then handed me over to him.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿUbayd ibn Ismāʿīl from Abū Usāmah"," as a mursal hadith in abridged form"," and he also narrated it with this wording from the hadith of ʿAlī ibn Mushir from Hishām"," as was mentioned at the end of the chapters on the marriage sermon. Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Authentic; Muslim 1422]"""
"14475","(14469) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \My mother used to treat me"," wanting to fatten me somewhat so that I could be presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Nothing of that worked for her until I ate dates with cucumbers"," whereupon I became as well-nourished as one could be.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14476","(14470) Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated it from Hishām with the same meaning, except that he said: \cucumbers with fresh dates.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated it to us"," Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us"," al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us"," Abū Muḥammad Nūḥ ibn Yazīd al-Muʾaddib narrated to us"," Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us"," from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq"," from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah"," from his father"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," who said: \""My mother wanted to fatten me so that I could be presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\"" She said: \""I would not accept anything of what she desired until she fed me cucumbers with fresh dates"," whereupon I became as well-nourished as one could be.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14477","(14471) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Abān said to me: Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn ʿAbbās, from Jaʿfar ibn Saʿd, from his father—who is Saʿd ibn ʿUbayd Allāh al-Kāhilī—that ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \When I proposed marriage to Fāṭimah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do you have any bridal gift (mahr)?' I said: 'I have my mount and my coat of mail.' He said: 'So I sold them for four hundred.' And he said: 'Increase the perfume for Fāṭimah"," for she is one of the women.'\"" [Weak]"""
"14478","(14472) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Sayyār, from al-Shaʿbī, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition. When we were returning"," I hurried to my slow camel. A rider caught up with me from behind and prodded my camel with a stick he had"," whereupon my camel moved as swiftly as the finest camel you have ever seen. I turned around and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'What is making you hurry"," O Jābir?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have recently been married.' He said: 'Did you marry a virgin or a previously married woman?' I said: 'Rather"," a previously married woman.' He said: 'Why not a young girl"," so that you could play with her and she with you?' He said: 'When we arrived in Madinah"," we went to enter"," and he said: \""Wait"," so that we may enter at night"," that is"," at suppertime"," so that the dishevelled woman may comb her hair and the absent husband's wife may remove her pubic hair.'\"" He said"," and he also said: \""When you arrive"," then be prudent"," be prudent.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Abū al-Nuʿmān and others from Hushaym. [Authentic; Muslim 715]"""
"14479","(14473) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khālid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Layth, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that he said regarding a man who marries a woman, is alone with her, does not touch her, and then divorces her: \She is entitled to nothing except half of the bridal gift (ṣadāq)"," because Allah"," the Most High"," says: {And if you divorce them before you have touched them"," but you have already appointed for them an obligation"," then half of what you have appointed}.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14480","(14474) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khamīruwayh narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ṭāwūs, from Ibn ʿAbbās, that he used to say regarding a man whose wife was brought to him and then he divorced her, claiming that he had not touched her: \He owes half of the bridal gift (ṣadāq).\"" [Authentic]"""
"14481","(14475) Abu Zakariyya Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarā'ifī informed us — ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us — from Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ — from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥa — from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) — regarding the statement of the Most High: *\And if you divorce them before you have touched them"," but you have already specified for them an obligation (dower)"," then half of what you specified\""* [al-Baqarah 237]: It refers to a man who marries a woman and has named a dower (ṣadāq) for her"," then divorces her before he has touched her — and \""touching\"" here refers to sexual intercourse — so she is entitled to half the dower"," and she has no right to more than that. [Ṣaḥīḥ by virtue of other chains]"""
"14482","(14476) And through his chain of narration, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the statement of the Most High: *\When you have married believing women and then divorce them before you have touched them"," there is no waiting period (ʿidda) for you to reckon against them\""* [al-Aḥzāb 49]: This refers to a man who marries a woman and then divorces her before he has touched her. If he divorces her with a single pronouncement"," she becomes irrevocably separated from him"," and there is no waiting period upon her — she may marry whomever she wishes. Then He"," the Most High"," said: *\""So provide for them and release them in a gracious manner\""* [al-Aḥzāb 49]"," meaning: if he had named a dower for her"," she is entitled to nothing but half; and if he had not named a dower for her"," he should provide for her according to his means and circumstances — and that is the \""gracious release.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14483","(14477) ʿUmar ibn Aḥmad al-ʿAbdawī informed us — Abū al-Faḍl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najda narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khālid informed us — from al-Shaʿbī: that ʿAmr ibn Nāfiʿ divorced his wife after she had been brought in to him. He claimed that he had not approached her, while she claimed that he had approached her. She brought her dispute before Shurayḥ. So Shurayḥ administered an oath to ʿAmr — \By Allah"," besides Whom there is no deity"," I did not approach her\"" — and ruled that he must pay half the dower.\n\nAnd al-Thawrī narrated it from Ismāʿīl and Mughīra"," from al-Shaʿbī"," from Shurayḥ: that a man married a woman"," then closed the door and drew the curtain"," and then divorced her without having touched her. So Shurayḥ ruled that she was entitled to half the dower. Abū Bakr al-Ardastānī informed him — Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed him — Sufyān al-Jawharī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us — Sufyān narrated it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14484","(14478) And al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Firās, from al-Shaʿbī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, who said: \She is entitled to half the dower"," even if he sat between her thighs.\"" Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us of this through ijāza — Abū al-Walīd narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim narrated to us — Wakīʿ narrated to us — from al-Ḥasan ibn Ṣāliḥ"," and he mentioned it. However"," there is a discontinuity (inqiṭāʿ) between al-Shaʿbī and Ibn Masʿūd. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14485","(14479) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us — al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us — al-Shāfiʿī informed us — Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrajānī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibn Bukayr narrated to us — Mālik informed us — from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd — from Ibn al-Musayyib: that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled regarding a woman whom a man married: when the curtains are drawn, the dower becomes obligatory. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14486","(14480) He said, and Mālik informed us — from Ibn Shihāb: that Zayd ibn Thābit (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When the man enters upon his wife and the curtains are drawn over them"," the dower becomes obligatory.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14487","(14481) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us — they both said: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mubashshir narrated to us — Tamīm ibn al-Muntaṣir narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Numayr narrated to us — ʿUbayd Allāh narrated to us — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar — from ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When the door is closed and the curtains are drawn"," the dower (mahr) becomes obligatory.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14488","(14482) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us — Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bakr narrated to us — Saʿīd, meaning Ibn Abī ʿArūba, narrated to us — from Qatāda — from al-Ḥasan — from al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays: that ʿUmar and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them both) both said: \When a door is closed and a curtain is drawn"," the full dower is obligatory"," and the waiting period (ʿidda) is incumbent upon her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — from ʿUmar only]"""
"14489","(14483) Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us — Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us — al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us — Sharīk narrated to us — from Maysara — from al-Minhāl — from ʿAbbād, meaning ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Asadī — from ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When a door is closed and a curtain is drawn"," the dower becomes obligatory.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14490","(14484) And Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatāda informed us — they both said: Abū al-Faḍl Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Khumayruwayh narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Najda narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym informed us — ʿAwf informed us — from Zurāra ibn Awfī, who said: \The ruling of the Rightly Guided Caliphs"," the Mahdīs"," is that whoever closes a door and draws a curtain"," the dower and the waiting period become obligatory.\""\n\nThis is a mursal hadith — Zurāra did not reach them (the Caliphs). However"," we have narrated it from ʿUmar and ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with them both) in a connected (mawṣūl) chain."""
"14491","(14485) Abu Hatim al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Fadl ibn Khumayruwayh informed us — Ahmad ibn Najdah informed us — Sa'id ibn Mansur informed us — Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad from his father — from Sulayman ibn Yasar — from Zayd ibn Thabit, regarding a man who was alone with a woman and then said, \I did not touch her","\"" while she said"," \""He has touched me.\"" He (Zayd) ruled that the matter would be decided by her statement. [Sahih by other than him]"""
"14492","(14486) And Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Abu al-Zinad from Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: Al-Harith ibn al-Hakam married a woman, and while with her he said something, then he saw her as greenish (i.e., he found her unattractive) and divorced her without having touched her. Marwan sent to Zayd ibn Thabit and asked him. Zayd said, \She is entitled to the full mahr.\"" He (Marwan) said"," \""He is not one who is suspected (of lying).\"" Zayd said"," \""Tell me"," O Marwan"," if she were pregnant"," would you have carried out the hadd punishment on her?\"" He said"," \""No.\"" Zayd said"," \""Then no.\""\n\nAbu al-Bakr al-Ardashtani informed us — Abu al-Nasr al-Iraqi informed us — Sufyan al-Jawhari informed us — Ali ibn al-Hasan informed us — Abd Allah ibn al-Walid informed us — Sufyan narrated it.\n\nAnd Bukayr ibn al-Ashaj narrated it from Sulayman and mentioned in the story that he said"," \""I did not touch her","\"" and the woman said"," \""He has consummated with me.\"" Then at the end of it he said"," \""Thus the woman is believed in such matters.\"" The apparent meaning of what has been narrated from Umar and Ali"," may Allah be pleased with them both"," indicates that they considered the private encounter (khalwah) to be akin to taking possession (qabd) in sales transactions.\n\nAl-Shafi'i"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: And it has been narrated from Umar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he said"," \""What is their sin if the inability comes from your side?\"" This indicates that he would award the mahr even if she did not claim consummation.\n\nThe Shaykh"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: As for Zayd ibn Thabit"," the apparent meaning of the narration from him indicates that he does not make the mahr obligatory by the private encounter itself"," but rather he gives credence to her statement regarding consummation. [Sahih]"""
"14493","(14487) And it has been narrated regarding that from the Prophet ﷺ with a mursal isnad, as Abu Tahir al-Faqih and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi Amr both informed us — they said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani informed us — Abd Allah ibn Salih informed me — al-Layth informed me — Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ja'far from Safwan ibn Sulaym — from Abd Allah ibn Yazid — from Muhammad ibn Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever uncovers a woman and looks at her awrah"," the mahr has become obligatory.\""\n\nHe said: And that reached us from Umar ibn al-Khattab"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib"," and al-Hasan al-Basri"," and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr"," and Abu Bakr ibn Hazm"," and Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman"," and Abu al-Zinad"," and Zayd ibn Aslam.\n\nAnd Ibn Luhay'ah narrated it from Abu al-Aswad from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban from the Prophet ﷺ"," mursal: \""Whoever lifts the veil of a woman and looks at her"," the mahr has become obligatory"," whether he consummated the marriage or not.\"" And he did not mention the madhhab of these (scholars).\n\nAnd this is munqati' (discontinued)"," and some of its narrators are not relied upon (as hujjah). And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"14494","(14488) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed us — Yunus ibn Bukayr informed us — from Abu Yahya — from Jamil ibn Zayd al-Ta'i — from Sa'd ibn Zayd al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a woman from Ghifar. He consummated the marriage with her, then he ordered her, and she removed her garment. He saw whiteness from leprosy near her breast, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away and said, \Take your garment.\"" In the morning he said to her"," \""Go back to your family.\"" And he completed her mahr for her. [Da'if]"""
"14495","(14489) And Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn Ubayd informed us — Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us — Yahya ibn Yahya informed us — Muhammad ibn Jabir informed us — from Jamil ibn Zayd — from Zayd ibn Ka'b. Ka'b said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a woman from Banu Ghifar. She was brought to him as a gift, and he saw whiteness (leprosy) on her flank. He said, \Draw your garments around you and go back to your family.\"" And he assigned her mahr to her. [Da'if; previously referenced]"""
"14496","(14490) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith al-Faqih informed us — Abu Muhammad ibn Hayyan informed us — Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi informed us — Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Warkani informed us — al-Qasim ibn Ghusn informed us — from Jamil ibn Zayd — from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet ﷺ married a woman from Ghifar. When he consummated the marriage with her, he found whiteness on her flank and said, \Draw your garments around you.\"" And he did not take back anything of what he had given her. This narration is disputed regarding Jamil ibn Zayd"," as you see. Al-Bukhari said: His hadith is not sahih. [Da'if; previously referenced]"""
"14497","(14491) Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran al-Adl in Baghdad informed us — Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us — al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Affan informed us — Abd Allah ibn Numayr informed us — from Ubayd Allah — from Nafi'. And Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us — Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — al-Rabi' ibn Sulayman informed us — al-Shafi'i informed us — Malik from Nafi' — from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that he used to say: \Every divorced woman is entitled to a mut'ah (consolation gift)"," except the one who is divorced after her mahr has been fixed and she has not been touched — she is entitled to half of what was fixed for her.\""\n\nAnd this statement has been narrated from the Successors from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad"," and Mujahid"," and al-Sha'bi. [Sahih]"""
"14498","(14492) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Bayhaqi, the owner of the madrasah in Nishapur, informed us — Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qirmisini informed us there — Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Tayalisi informed us — Muhammad ibn Humayd al-Razi informed us — Salamah ibn al-Fadl informed us — Amr ibn Abi Qays informed us — from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la — from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, who said: The Khat'ami woman was married to al-Hasan ibn Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both. When Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed and allegiance was pledged to al-Hasan ibn Ali, al-Hasan went in to her and said, \May the caliphate be auspicious to you.\"" Al-Hasan said"," \""You have rejoiced at the killing of Ali — you are thrice divorced.\"" She wrapped herself in her garment and said"," \""By Allah"," I did not intend this.\"" She remained until her 'iddah elapsed and she departed. Then al-Hasan ibn Ali sent her the remainder of her mahr and a mut'ah of twenty thousand dirhams. When the messenger came to her and she saw the wealth"," she said"," \""A meager provision from a departing beloved.\"" The messenger informed al-Hasan ibn Ali"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and he wept and said"," \""Were it not that I heard my father narrate from my grandfather"," the Prophet ﷺ"," that he said: 'Whoever divorces his wife thrice"," she will not be lawful for him until she marries a husband other than him' — I would have taken her back.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14499","(14493) And there has come regarding the mut'ah of the woman who has been consummated with: Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ishaq informed us — Ali ibn Abd al-Samad informed us — Abu Hamam al-Walid ibn Shuja' al-Sakuni informed us — Mus'ab ibn Sallam informed us — Shu'bah informed us — Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil — from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: When Hafs ibn al-Mughirah divorced his wife Fatimah, she came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to her husband, \Give her a mut'ah.\"" He said"," \""I do not have anything to give her as a mut'ah.\"" He said"," \""Then there must be a mut'ah.\"" He said"," \""Give her a mut'ah"," even if it be half a sa' of dates.\""\n\nHer well-known story regarding the 'iddah is evidence that she had been consummated with. And Allah knows best. [Da'if]"""
"14500","(14494) Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi Amr both informed us — they said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us — Ibrahim ibn Marzuq informed us — Wahb ibn Jarir informed us — Shu'bah informed us — from Abu Bishr — from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, who said: \Every divorced woman is entitled to a mut'ah\"" — \""And for divorced women is a provision according to what is reasonable"," a duty upon the righteous\"" (al-Baqarah 2:241). And this statement has been narrated from Abu al-Aliyah"," and al-Hasan"," and al-Zuhri. [Sahih]"""
"14501","(14495) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, saying: Abū ʀāmir narrated to us, from Shuʿbah, from al-Ḥakam, who said:\n\nA woman came to Shurayḥ, disputing with her husband, asking him for the mutʿah (consolatory gift), for he had divorced her. Shurayḥ recited: {And for divorced women is a provision according to what is acceptable — a duty upon the righteous} (al-Baqarah, 2:241). He said: Give her the mutʿah, but he did not issue a ruling in her favour.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Shurayḥ, that he said to a man who had separated [from his wife]: Do not refuse to be among the muttaqīn (the God-fearing), do not refuse to be among the muḥsinīn (the doers of good).\n\nAnd from Ibrāhīm and al-Shaʿbī, from Shurayḥ: If you are among the muttaqīn, then give the mutʿah, but he did not compel him.\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Shurayḥ that he did compel [the husband] to give the mutʿah in the case of a mufawwaḍah (a woman divorced before consummation). [Weak]"
"14502","(14496) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Najjār in Kūfah narrated to us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym al-Shaybānī narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Ḥāzim narrated to us, saying: ʿAmr ibn Ḥammād narrated to us, from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿAbd al-Malik, from Qatādah, who said:\n\nA man divorced his wife in the presence of Shurayḥ, so Shurayḥ said to him: Give her the mutʿah. The woman said: There is no mutʿah due upon him for me. Allah only said {And for divorced women is a provision according to what is acceptable — a duty upon the righteous} (al-Baqarah, 2:241) {And for divorced women is a provision according to what is acceptable — a duty upon the doers of good} — and he is not among those. [Weak]"
"14503","(14497) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, saying: al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, saying: Mālik narrated to us — and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated to us, saying: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, saying: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from what he read to Mālik, from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from Anas, that:\n\nʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and upon him were traces of yellow fragrance. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked him, and he informed him that he had married a woman of the Anṣār. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: How much did you give her as mahr? He said: The weight of a date-stone of gold. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: Hold a walīmah, even if it be with a single sheep.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik, and Muslim narrated it from another route from Ḥumayd.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1427]"
"14504","(14498) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Walīd narrated to me, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Thābit, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), that:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) noticed upon ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) traces of yellow fragrance. He said: What is this? He said: I have married a woman for the weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: May Allah bless you. Hold a walīmah, even if it be with a single sheep.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from Musaddad from Ḥammād, as mentioned above.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]\n\n(24) Chapter: It is recommended, if one finds the means, to hold a walīmah with a sheep\n\nIf one has the means, it is recommended to hold a walīmah with a sheep."
"14505","(14499) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Qāsim Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad al-Ṭabarānī narrated to us, saying: al-Dabarī narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Razzāq — and Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, saying: al-Firyābī narrated to us — and Abū Muslim and Yūsuf al-Qāḍī narrated to us, saying: Ibn Kathīr narrated to us — all of them from al-Thawrī, from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nWhen ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived in Madīnah, the Prophet (ﷺ) established brotherhood between him and Saʿd ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Anṣārī. Saʿd offered to share half of his family and his wealth with him, and he had two wives. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said to him: May Allah bless you in your family and your wealth. Direct me to the market. So he went to the market and made some profit from dried yogurt and some ghee. The Prophet (ﷺ) saw him after a few days, and upon him were traces of yellow fragrance. He said: What is this, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān? He said: I have married a woman of the Anṣār. He said: What did you give her as mahr? He said: The weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: Hold a walīmah, even if it be with a single sheep.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Firyābī and Muḥammad ibn Kathīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"
"14506","(14500) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: Musaddad and Qutaybah narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād narrated to us, from Thābit, who said:\n\nThe marriage of Zaynab bint Jaḥsh (may Allah be pleased with her) was mentioned in the presence of Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said: I did not see the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) hold a walīmah for any of his wives as he held for her. He held a walīmah with a sheep.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad, and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1428]"
"14507","(14501) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb, who said: I heard Anas ibn Mālik say:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not hold a walīmah for any of his wives more abundant and more excellent than the walīmah he held for Zaynab. Thābit al-Bunānī said: What did he hold as a walīmah? He said: He fed them bread and meat until they left it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and others. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"
"14508","(14502) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us — and Abū al-Qāsim ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Yaʿqūb al-Iyādī al-Mālikī in Baghdād narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Naṣībī narrated to us, saying: ʿUbayd ibn ʿAbd al-Wāḥid narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to me, saying: Ḥumayd narrated to me that he heard Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) say:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) encamped between Khaybar and Madīnah for three nights, during which Ṣafiyyah was presented to him. I invited the Muslims to the walīmah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). There was no bread nor meat in it. There was nothing except that he ordered the leather mats to be spread out, and dates, dried yogurt, and ghee were placed upon them. The Muslims said: Is she one of the Mothers of the Believers, or is she from those whom his right hand possesses? They said: If he veils her, then she is one of the Mothers of the Believers, and if he does not veil her, then she is from those whom his right hand possesses. When he departed, he made a place for her behind him and extended the veil between her and the people.\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam, and both he and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb from Anas, likewise, regarding the dates, dried yogurt, and ghee. He said: And they made ḥays. And likewise in the narration of Ḥammād from Thābit from Anas. And in the narration of Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah from Thābit from Anas, al-sawīq (barley gruel) is mentioned in place of al-aqiṭ (dried yogurt). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1365]"
"14509","(14503) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: ʿAbdullāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to us, saying: Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), that:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to Khaybar. He mentioned the affair of Ṣafiyyah bint Ḥuyayy (may Allah be pleased with her). He said: When he was on the road, Umm Sulaym prepared her for him and presented her to him at night, and the Prophet (ﷺ) became a bridegroom in the morning. He said: Whoever has anything, let him bring it. He spread out a leather mat. A man would bring dried yogurt, a man would bring dates, and a man would bring ghee, and they made ḥays. That was the walīmah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaʿqūb, and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr, both from Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"
"14510","(14504) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us, saying: ʿAffān and Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān narrated to us — and Abū ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, and the wording is from his ḥadīth — saying: Aḥmad ibn Sahl al-Bukhārī narrated to me, saying: Ṣāliḥ ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥabīb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, saying: Shabābah narrated to us, saying: Sulaymān, meaning Ibn al-Mughīrah, narrated to us, from Thābit, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said:\n\nṢafiyyah fell to the share of Ḥabīb ibn Kalbī in the division, and they began praising her before the Prophet (ﷺ), saying: We have not seen among the captives a woman like her. The Prophet (ﷺ) sent and gave Ḥabīb ibn Kalbī whatever he was pleased with, and he handed her over to Umm Sulaym, saying: Prepare her. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out from Khaybar and placed her behind him. Then a tent was pitched over her. In the morning he said: Whoever has surplus provisions, let us have them. A man would bring surplus dates, surplus sawīq (barley gruel), and surplus ghee, until they made a large quantity of ḥays. They ate and drank from rainwater beside them. That was the walīmah of the Prophet (ﷺ) for Ṣafiyyah. Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say: We saw a walīmah of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in which there was no bread and no meat. Then he would mention this ḥadīth.\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"
"14511","(14505) It was narrated by Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit from Anas that he said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made her walimah of dates"," dried yogurt (aqit)"," and clarified butter (samn).\""\n\nIt was reported to us by Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz"," who reported to us Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtawayh"," who reported to us Musa ibn al-Hasan and others"," who said: Affan narrated to us"," Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us"," and he mentioned it.\n\nIt was narrated by Muslim in his Sahih from the hadith of Affan. [Sahih. Preceded before it.]"""
"14512","(14506) Abu Ali al-Rawdhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Hamid ibn Yahya narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us; Wail ibn Dawud narrated to us from his son Bakr ibn Wail from al-Zuhri from Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) held a walimah for Safiyyah with sawiq (barley porridge) and dates. [Sahih. Tirmidhi 1095. Narrated by al-Sijistani 3744.]"
"14513","(14507) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad al-Muqri informed us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us from Mansur ibn Safiyyah from his mother from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) held a walimah for one of his wives with two mudds of barley.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Yusuf from Sufyan"," except that he did not mention A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) in his isnad. [Sahih. Bukhari 5172.]"""
"14514","(14508) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us; Ali ibn al-Hasan informed us; Abu Ghassan narrated to us. And Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub informed us; Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri narrated to us; Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us; Bayan narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) consummated a marriage with a woman and sent me"," so I invited people to the food.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Malik ibn Isma'il"," Abu Ghassan. [Sahih. Bukhari 5170.]"""
"14515","(14509) Abu Ali al-Rawdhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah informed us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us from al-Hasan from Abdullah ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi from a one-eyed man from Thaqif who was known as Ma'ruf — meaning good was said about him — if his name was not Zuhayr ibn Uthman, then I do not know his name, that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The walimah on the first day is a right (haqq)"," on the second day it is a kindness (ma'ruf)"," and on the third day it is for reputation (sum'ah) and showing off (riya').\"" [Munkar]"""
"14516","(14510) Qatadah said: \And a man narrated to me that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab was invited on the first day and he accepted; on the second day and he accepted; and he was invited on the third day and he did not accept"," and he said: 'People of reputation and showing off!'\"" [Da'if]"""
"14517","(14511) Abu al-Husayn ibn Burhan al-Adl informed us in Baghdad; Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed us; Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar narrated to us from Qatadah, who said: \Ibn al-Musayyab was invited on the first day and he accepted; he was invited on the second day and he accepted; and he was invited on the third day"," so he pelted them with pebbles in al-Batha' and said: 'Go away"," people of showing off and reputation!'\""\n\n[Da'if. Narrated by Abd al-Razzaq 19661.]"""
"14518","(14512) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated to us orally; my grandfather Abu Amr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Kamil narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us. And Abu Sa'id al-Malini informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn Adi al-Hafiz informed us; Ibn al-Abbas narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us; they both said: Ziyad ibn Abdullah al-Bakka'i narrated to us from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib from Abu Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The food of the first day is a right"," and the second is the same as it.\"" In the narration of al-Sulami: \""The food of one day is a right"," the food of two days is a Sunnah"," and the food of the third day is reputation and showing off. And whoever seeks reputation"," Allah will make him hear it (on the Day of Judgment).\"" Al-Sulami did not mention his word \""riya'\"" (showing off).\n\nAnd Bakr ibn Khunays narrated it from al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) married Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," he ordered the leather mat (nita') to be spread"," then dates and sawiq were placed upon it. He invited the people"," and they ate"," and he said: \""The walimah on the first day is a right"," on the second day it is a kindness"," and on the third day it is showing off and reputation.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14519","(14513) Abu Sa'id al-Malini informed it to us; Abu Ahmad ibn Adi informed us; al-Husayn ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Bakr ibn Khunays, and he mentioned it. This is not strong. Bakr ibn Khunays was spoken about (by the scholars of hadith), and the hadith of al-Bakka'i is also not strong. And that was narrated from Abu Hurayrah in a marfu' (elevated) narration, and it is nothing. [Munkar]"
"14520","(14514) Abu Bakr ibn Ibrahim al-Farisi informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah informed us; Abu Ahmad ibn Faris narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari regarding the hadith of Zuhayr ibn Uthman, he said: \Its isnad is not sound"," and he is not known to have companionship (suhbah).\"" And Ibn Umar and others narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ): \""When one of you is invited to a walimah"," let him accept.\"" He did not specify three days or anything else. And this is more authentic. And he mentioned the narration of Ibn Sirin. [Sahih. Agreed upon (by al-Bukhari and Muslim).]"""
"14521","(14515) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Sulaymān — i.e., ibn Ḥarb — narrated to us, Wuhaib narrated from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad, who said: Ḥafṣah narrated to me that Sīrīn held a wedding banquet in al-Madīnah and invited the people for seven days. Among those whom he invited was Ubayy ibn Kaʿb. He came while he was fasting, invoked blessings upon them, and then departed. (Tirmidhī) Similarly, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated it from Ayyūb, saying \seven days","\"" except that he did not mention Ḥafṣah in his isnād.\n\n[Authentic. Narrated by al-Fasawī in al-Maʿrifah 3/140]"""
"14522","Ma'mar said, ""Eight days passed and the first one was the most truthful. Abu al-Husayn bin Bisran informed us, Isma'il al-Saffar informed us, Ahmad bin Mansur informed us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar said, ""Ayub said, 'My father married and called the people eight days. He called my father, K'ab's son, and when he called, it was a day of fasting and he was fasting. He prayed and said, 'I call with blessings, then he left.'""","\"" and the first narration is more accurate. Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us"," Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us"," Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us"," ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us"," Maʿmar narrated from Ayyūb"," from Ibn Sīrīn"," who said: My father married and invited the people for eight days. He invited Ubayy ibn Kaʿb among those whom he invited. He came on that day while he was fasting"," prayed — meaning he performed voluntary prayers — and then invoked blessings and departed.\n\n[Authentic]"""
"14523","(14517) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Isḥāq — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muʿāwiyah — both said: Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Shaybānī narrated to us by dictation, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdillāh narrated to us, Bishr ibn ʿUmar al-Zahrānī narrated to us, Mālik ibn Anas narrated — and Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated, saying: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you is invited to a wedding banquet"," let him attend it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Authentic. Bukhārī 5179"," 5173]"""
"14524","(14518) Abū Isḥāq — Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Naysābūrī — narrated to us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn al-Akram narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Numayr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, ʿUbaydullāh narrated from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you is invited to a wedding banquet"," let him respond.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Numayr.\n\n[Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14525","(14519) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ḥīrī narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Aḥmad al-Shāmātī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Khālid ibn al-Ḥārith narrated from ʿUbaydullāh, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \When one of you is invited to a wedding banquet"," let him respond.\""\n\nKhālid said: \""When ʿUbaydullāh would narrate it"," he would attribute it to the wedding (al-ʿurs).\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā.\n\n[Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14526","(14520) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us by dictation, Muḥammad ibn Ḥajjāj and Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated — and Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Fāmī informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Naṣr al-Marwazī Abū ʿAbdillāh and Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad narrated — all of them said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated, saying: I read to Mālik, from Ibn Shihāb, from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah, that he used to say: \The worst of food is the food of the wedding banquet"," to which the wealthy are invited and the poor are neglected. And whoever does not attend the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nIn the narration of Abū ʿAbdillāh: \""Evil is the food.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\n[Authentic. Muslim 1432]"""
"14527","(14521) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdād informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Abū Bakr al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated, saying: I said to al-Zuhrī, \O Abū Bakr"," how did you narrate it — 'The worst of food is the food of the wealthy'?\"" He laughed and said: \""It is not 'the worst of food is the food of the wealthy.'\"" Sufyān said: \""My father was wealthy"," and this hadith alarmed me when I heard it"," so I asked al-Zuhrī"," and he said: al-Aʿraj narrated to me"," saying: I heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'The worst of food is the food of the wedding banquet"," to which the wealthy are invited and from which the poor are kept away. And whoever does not respond to the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.'\""\n\nSufyān would sometimes raise this hadith (to the Prophet ﷺ) and sometimes would not raise it"," except for its ending.\n\n[Authentic. Ibn al-Jawzī said in al-ʿIlal 1032]"""
"14528","(14522) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us, Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us, Sufyān narrated, saying: I said to al-Zuhrī, and he mentioned it and narrated the hadith as a mawqūf (stopped) narration from Abū Hurayrah, saying: \To which the wealthy are invited and the poor are neglected.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar as a mawqūf narration.\n\n[Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14529","(14523) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh ibn Bushrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn al-Musayyab, and from al-Aʿraj, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The worst of food is the food of the wedding banquet"," to which the wealthy are invited and the poor are neglected. It is a right"," and whoever abandons it has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nMaʿmar would sometimes say: \""And whoever does not respond has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ and others from ʿAbd al-Razzāq.\n\nLikewise"," Abū al-Zinād narrated it from al-Aʿraj as a mawqūf narration from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him).\n\n[Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14530","(14524) Abū Naṣr Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Fāmī informed us, Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad and Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib both said: Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ziyād ibn Saʿd.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Qāsim ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Mālikī in Baghdād informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us by dictation, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, Ziyād ibn Saʿd narrated. He said: I heard Thābit al-Aʿraj narrating from Abū Hurayrah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The worst of food is the food of the wedding banquet"," from which those who would come are kept away and to which those who would refuse it are invited. And whoever does not respond to the invitation has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī ʿUmar. And this al-Aʿraj is Thābit ibn ʿIyāḍ al-Aʿraj"," while the first one is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Hurmuz al-Aʿraj.\n\n[Authentic. Preceded above in two narrations]"""
"14531","(14525) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāʿim, from Ibn ʿUmar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you is invited by his brother"," let him accept"," whether it is a wedding feast or something similar.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and he also reported it from the ḥadīth of al-Zubaydī from Nāʿim with the same meaning. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1429]"""
"14532","(14526) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Aḥmad ibn Sahl ibn Baḥr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Muṣaffā al-Ḥimṣī narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated from al-Zubaydī, from Nāʿim, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you is invited to a wedding feast or something similar"," let him accept.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr from ʿĪsā ibn al-Mundhir from Baqiyyah. [Ṣaḥīḥ — see above]"""
"14533","(14527) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-Walīd al-Faḥḥām narrated to us: Ḥajjāj narrated —\n\nAnd Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad said: Ibn Jurayj said: Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah informed me from Nāʿim, who said: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Accept this invitation when you are invited to it.\"" He said: And ʿAbd Allāh used to attend the invitation — whether for a wedding feast or otherwise — and he would attend it even while fasting.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ibrāhīm from Ḥajjāj"," and Muslim narrated it from Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh from al-Ḥajjāj. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1429]"""
"14534","(14528) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Walīd informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā informed us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad ibn Zayd informed me from Nāʿim, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them, that the Prophet ﷺ said: \When you are invited to a meal"," accept it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah ibn Yaḥyā. The ḥadīth of al-Barāʾ"," may Allah be pleased with him"," from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the command to respond to the host"," and the ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ regarding responding to the invitation in what is obligatory upon a Muslim toward his brother"," have already been mentioned. [Ṣaḥīḥ — see above]"""
"14535","(14529) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Abū al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us: Ashʿath ibn Sulaym narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Suwayd ibn Muqarrin, who said: Al-Barāʾ, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things and forbade us from seven things. He commanded us to visit the sick"," to follow funeral processions"," to respond to the one who sneezes"," to fulfill oaths"," to support the oppressed"," to spread the salām"," and to respond to the host. And he forbade us from gold signet rings"," silver vessels"," the mayāthir"," al-qassiyyah"," silk brocade"," silk"," and silk garments.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Rabīʿ from Abī al-Aḥwaṣ"," and Muslim reported it through various chains from Ashʿath. [Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 2066]"""
"14536","(14530) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Five things are obligatory upon a Muslim toward his brother: returning the salām"," responding to the one who sneezes"," accepting the invitation when he is invited"," visiting the sick"," and following funeral processions.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14537","(14531) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Quraysh informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Fayyāḍ ibn Zuhayr narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, and he mentioned it with a connected chain.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. Maʿmar used to transmit this ḥadīh in mursal form frequently, but when asked about it, he would narrate it with a connected chain. It was also narrated with a connected chain by al-Awzāʿī, Yūnus ibn Yazīd, and ʿUqayl."
"14538","(14532) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl informed us: Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz informed us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated —\n\nAnd Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Qaṭṭān al-Naysābūrī informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb ibn al-Akram informed us: Ḥāmid ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ narrated to us: Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm narrated — both of them said: Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \When one of you is invited to a meal"," let him accept. If he is not fasting"," let him eat"," and if he is fasting"," let him pray\"" — meaning"," make duʿāʾ.\n\nThis is the narration of Rūḥ. Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Hishām ibn Ḥassān."""
"14539","(14533) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Makhlad ibn Khālid narrated to us: Abū Usāmah narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, from Nāʿim, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said with the same meaning — that is, with the meaning of the ḥadīth of Mālik from Nāʿim regarding the walīmah — and he added: \If he is not fasting"," let him eat"," and if he is fasting"," let him make duʿāʾ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ — narrated by al-Sijistānī 3736]"""
"14540","(14534) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāʿim, from Ibn ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with both of them: that when he was invited to a wedding feast, he would accept — whether fasting or not fasting. If he was fasting, he would make duʿāʾ and invoke blessings, and if he was not fasting, he would eat. [Ṣaḥīḥ — see above]"
"14541","(14535) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah informed us — he heard ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd say: My father invited ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, so he came and sat down. Food was placed before him, and ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar extended his hand and said, \Begin in the name of Allah.\"" Then ʿAbd Allāh withdrew his hand and said"," \""I am fasting.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14542","(14536) Abū Saʿīd informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, that his father invited a group of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and among them was Ubayy ibn Kaʿb — may Allah be pleased with him. He said: He (Ubayy) invoked blessings and departed.\n\nThe Shaykh — may Allah have mercy on him — said: We have narrated previously that he was fasting, and he invoked blessings and then left."
"14543","(14537) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥumayd informed us, from Ibrāhīm ibn ʿUbayd ibn Rifāʿah al-Zuraqī, from Abū Saʿīd, who said: A man prepared food and invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions. A man said, \I am fasting.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""Your brother has prepared food and invited you. Break your fast and make up for it on another day.\""\n\nIbn Abī Fudayk narrated it from Ibn Abī Ḥumayd and added therein: \""If you wish\"" — meaning the making up (of the fast). Ibn Abī Ḥumayd is called Muḥammad and also Ḥammād"," and he is weak (ḍaʿīf).\n\nWe have also narrated something to the same effect from Abū Uways al-Madanī"," from Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir"," from Abū Saʿīd"," that he had prepared food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. This has already been mentioned in the Book of Fasting. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14544","(14538) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us, Abū ʿUmayr informed us, Ḍamrah informed us, from Bilāl ibn Kaʿb al-ʿAkki, who said: We visited Yaḥyā ibn Ḥassān al-Bakrī — myself, Ibn Qurayr, Ibn Adham, and Mūsā ibn Yasār — from ʿAsqalān to Sanājiyyah. He brought us food, and Mūsā held back his hand. Yaḥyā said to him, \Eat"," for a man from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ — Abū Qirṣāfah — led us in prayer in this mosque for twenty years. He used to fast one day and break fast the next. A son was born to me"," so I held a feast and invited him on the day he was fasting"," and he broke his fast.\"" He said: So Mūsā extended his hand and ate"," and Ibn Adham went to the mosque to sweep it with his cloak. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14545","(14539) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Sufyān informed us, from Abū al-Zubayr, from Jābir — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \When one of you is invited"," let him respond. If he wishes"," he may eat"," and if he wishes"," he may leave.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Sufyān and Ibn Jurayj"," from Abū al-Zubayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 1430]"""
"14546","(14540) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, from Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, from ʿAṭāʾ, who said: Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — was invited to a meal while he was attending to the matter of the Siqāyah. He said to the people, \Go to your brother"," or respond to your brother's invitation. Convey my greetings of peace to him and inform him that I am occupied.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 19664]"""
"14547","(14541) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Muslim ibn Khālid informed us, from Ibn Jurayj. Al-Shāfiʿī said: I do not know whether it was from ʿAṭāʾ or someone else. He said: The messenger of Ibn Ṣafwān came to Ibn ʿAbbās while he was attending to the Zamzam, inviting him and his companions. He ordered them to go and excused himself, saying, \If he does not excuse me"," I will come to him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"14548","(14542) ʿAlī ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, from Maʿmar, from Ayyūb, from Mujāhid, that Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — was invited to a meal one day. A man from the people said, \As for me"," excuse me from this.\"" Ibn ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with them both — said to him"," \""There is no excuse for you in this. Get up.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 19663]"""
"14549","(14543) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us, ʿUthmān ibn ʿUmar al-Dabbī and Ziyād ibn al-Khalīl — both said: Musaddad informed us, Abū ʿAwānah informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from Abū Masʿūd ʿUqbah ibn ʿAmr — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: A man from the Anṣār, called Abū Shuʿayb, noticed hunger in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He had a butcher boy. He said, \Prepare food for me; perhaps I will invite the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as the fifth of five.\"" So he invited him. A man followed them who had not been invited. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""This man has followed us. Do you give him permission?\"" He said"," \""Yes.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Nuʿmān"," from Abī ʿAwānah"," and both he and Muslim narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 2081"," 2456"," 5434"," 5461]"""
"14550","(14544) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Wāqid al-Ḥarrānī informed us — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Būshanjī informed us, al-Nufaylī informed us — both said: Zuhayr Abū Khaythamah informed us, al-Aʿmash informed us, from Abū Sufyān, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: Abū Shuʿayb had a butcher boy. When he saw the hardship that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions were enduring, he ordered his boy to bring him meat. Then he sent word to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \Come to us as the fifth of five.\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came with five people"," and there was a sixth with them. When they arrived at Abū Shuʿayb's place"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said"," \""You sent for five of us"," but this man has followed us. If you give him permission"," he may enter; otherwise"," he will go back.\"" He said"," \""I have given him permission"," O Messenger of Allah. Let him enter.\""\n\nThis is the wording of al-Nufaylī's ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Abū ʿAwānah 8300"," 8301]"""
"14551","(14545) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Ismāʿīl informed us, Jaʿfar informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik informed us, Zuhayr informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from Abū Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), similarly. Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Zuhayr ibn Muʿāwiyah. [Ṣaḥīh. It has preceded before the one before it.]"
"14552","(14546) Abū Saʿd al-Mālinī informed us, Abū Aḥmad ibn ʿAdī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Naffāḥ informed us, ʿAbbās ibn Yazīd al-Baḥrānī informed us, Durust ibn Ziyād informed us. And Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Mihrajānī informed us, Abū al-Qāsim ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Dārakī informed us, my grandfather Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Dārakī informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUmar informed us, Durust ibn Ziyād informed us, Abān ibn Ṭāriq informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever enters without an invitation has entered as an intruder and departed as a thief.\""\n\nAl-Baḥrānī added at the beginning of it: \""The walīmah (wedding feast) is a right. Whoever is invited and does not accept has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\"" Then he mentioned the rest. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14553","(14547) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī by dictation, and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Abū ʿUtbah Aḥmad ibn al-Faraj informed us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walīd informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Khālid Abū Zakariyyā informed us, from Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim, from Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever comes to a people for food to which he was not invited has entered as a sinner and consumed what is not lawful for him.\""\n\nIt has also been narrated from Baqiyyah"," from Yaḥyā ibn Khālid"," from Rūḥ"," from Layth"," from Mujāhid"," from Abū Hurayrah"," and through both their chains"," it was not narrated from Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim by anyone other than Yaḥyā ibn Khālid. And he (Yaḥyā) is unknown (majhūl) among the shuyūkh of Baqiyyah"," and Baqiyyah has another chain that is also unknown. And in the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) there is sufficiency. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14554","(14548) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān informed us, Ibn Numayr informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Ismāʿīl ibn Rajāʾ, from his father, in the story of the beginning of the sermon, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever among you sees an evil"," let him change it with his hand; if he is not able to"," then with his tongue; if he is not able to"," then with his heart — and that is the weakest of faith.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of al-Aʿmash as has preceded. [Ṣaḥīh. Muslim 49]"""
"14555","(14549) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that ʿUmar ibn al-Sāʾib narrated to him that al-Qāsim ibn Abī al-Qāsim narrated to him that he heard the storyteller of the armies in Constantinople narrating from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: \O people"," I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"," let him not sit at a table around which wine is circulated; and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"," let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper; and whoever (among women) believes in Allah and the Last Day"," let her not enter the bathhouse.'\""\n\nThis has also been narrated through other routes from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," raised (as a marfūʿ ḥadīth). [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"14556","(14550) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq in Baghdad informed us, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Marzūq informed us, Kathīr ibn Hishām informed us, Jaʿfar ibn Burqān informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Sālim, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited two types of eating: sitting at a table around which wine is consumed, and a man eating while lying on his stomach.\n\nOur companions said: If he accepted the invitation and did not know (about the wine), let him sit and not assist the people in sin, and not listen to their idle amusements, then let him leave. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14557","(14551) Abū al-Qāsim ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Iyādī in Baghdad informed us, Aḥmad ibn Salmān informed us, Yaʿqūb ibn Yūsuf al-Muṭṭawwiʿī informed us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd informed us, from Sufyān, Ashʿath informed me, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmayr, the brother of ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿUmayr, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \When a sin is committed on earth"," the one who was present and disliked it is like the one who was absent from it; and the one who was absent and was pleased with it is like the one who was present at it.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14558","(14552) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān in Baghdad informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmrūyah informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad informed us, Shaybān informed us, from Ashʿath ibn Abī al-Shaʿthāʾ, al-Ḥasan ibn Saʿd, the freedman of ʿAlī, informed me, from ʿAbd Allāh or ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿUmayr, from Yazīd ibn al-Ḥārith, who said: I heard Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \When a sin is committed among the people"," the one who was absent and was pleased with it is like the one who was present at it; and the one who was present and disliked it is like the one who was absent from it.\""\n\nThis has also been narrated through another route"," raised (as a marfūʿ ḥadīth). [Ḥasan]"""
"14559","(14553) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Miṣrī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb al-ʿAllāf informed us. And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī informed us. They both said: Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam informed us, Nāfiʿ ibn Yazīd informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Sulaym or Ibn Abī Sulaymān informed me, from Ibn al-Maqburī, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever is present at a sin and dislikes it is as though he was absent from it; and whoever is absent from it and loves it is as though he was present at it.\""\n\nIn the narration of al-Dārimī: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Sulaymān"," without doubt.\n\nYaḥyā ibn Abī Sulaymān is the sole narrator of it"," and he is not strong (laysa bi-l-qawī). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14560","(14554) By way of evidence, Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād informed us, Ibn Abī Uways informed us, Mālik informed us, from Nāfiʿ, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she informed him: She had purchased a cushion with pictures on it. When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw it, he stood at the door and did not enter. She recognized disapproval in his face, so she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I repent to Allah and to His Messenger. What sin have I committed?\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""What is the matter with this cushion?\"" She said: \""I bought it for you to sit on and use as a pillow.\"" He said: \""Indeed"," the makers of these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection. It will be said to them: 'Give life to what you have created.'\"" And he said: \""Indeed"," the angels do not enter a house in which there are images.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīh. Muslim 2107]"""
"14561","(14555) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr informed us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā said: I read it before Mālik, and he mentioned it.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ibn Abī Uways and others, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā.\n\nThus narrated Mālik, and with the same meaning narrated Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī from Nāfiʿ. And ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Nāfiʿ, and he said: \It was a curtain upon which there were images","\"" and he said in it: \""So she took it and made it into two cushions.\"" And with the same meaning narrated the group. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"14562","(14556) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us verbally; Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī informed us in Makkah; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from al-Zuhrī, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," came to me while I had hung a curtain upon which there were images. When he saw it"," his face changed colour"," and he tore it with his hand and said: 'The people who will be most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Ibn ʿUyaynah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"14563","(14557) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn al-Sharqī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Dhuhlī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī; al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me that ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, informed him: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," came to her while she was screened by a curtain upon which were images. His face changed colour"," then he reached for the curtain and tore it with his hand"," then said: 'Indeed"," among the people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.'\""\n\nHe said: And Abū Ḥāmid informed us"," he said: Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us"," Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us"," al-Awzāʿī narrated from al-Zuhrī"," from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her.\n\n(Ḥ) He said: And Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us"," Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us"," my father narrated from Ibn Shihāb"," from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad"," from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," with its like"," but they did not mention \""with his hand\"" nor \""images.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yasarah ibn Ṣafwān from Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd"," and Muslim narrated it from Manṣūr ibn Abī Muzāḥim from Ibrāhīm"," and from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"14564","(14558) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, that ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, narrated to him, and he mentioned the hadith similar to the hadith of Maʿmar in its entirety.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥarmalah from Ibn Wahb."
"14565","(14559) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī informed us. (Ḥ) And Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us, they said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, they said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," returned from a journey"," and I had hung a curtain on my door upon which were horses with wings. When the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," saw it"," he said: 'Remove it.'\""\n\nHe narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited.]"""
"14566","(14560) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jumḥān, from Safīnah, Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān: \A man was a guest of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with him"," so he prepared food for him. Fāṭimah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," said: 'If only we had invited the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," so that he could eat with us.' So they invited him"," and he came. He placed his hand upon the doorpost and saw the curtain that had been hung on one side of the house"," so he turned back. Fāṭimah said to ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with them both: 'Go after him and see what caused him to turn back.' So I followed him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what turned you back?' He said: 'It is not befitting for me or for any Prophet to enter a house that is adorned.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14567","(14561) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us; Qabīṣah ibn ʿUqbah narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Saʿīd ibn Jumḥān, from Safīnah, from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \It is not befitting for a Prophet to enter a house that is adorned.\""\n\nThus he narrated it from Umm Salamah"," may Allah be pleased with her. [Ḥasan]"""
"14568","(14562) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn ʿAbd al-Karīm narrated to them; Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAqīl narrated to me from his father, from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, may Allah be pleased with him, at the time of the Conquest, while he was in al-Baṭḥāʾ, to go to the Kaʿbah and erase every image in it. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, did not enter the Kaʿbah until every image in it had been erased.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 52/9723]"
"14569","(14563) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed me; Yūnus narrated from Ibn Shihāb. (Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdad informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī; ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah informed me that he heard Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, say: \I heard Abū Ṭalḥah"," may Allah be pleased with him"," say: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," say: \""The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or an image of idols.\""'\"" The narration of Ibn Wahb does not contain the word \""idols\"" (tamāthīl).\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir and others from Ibn Wahb"," and from Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh and others from ʿAbd al-Razzāq. Al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Maʿmar and Yūnus. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 3225]"""
"14570","(14564) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar narrated from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Aslam, the freedman of ʿUmar: \When ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," arrived in Shām"," a Christian man prepared a meal for him and said to ʿUmar: 'I would love for you to come to me and honour me"," you and your companions.' He was one of the notables of Shām. ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to him: 'We do not enter your churches because of the images in them","' meaning the idols.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq 19486]"""
"14571","(14565) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Muḥammad ibn Shawdhb al-Wāṣitī narrated to us there — Aḥmad ibn Sinān narrated to us — Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated from ʿAdiyy ibn Thābit — from Khālid ibn Saʿd — from Abū Masʿūd: that a man prepared food for him and invited him. He asked, \Is there an image in the house?\"" The man replied"," \""Yes.\"" So he refused to enter until the image was broken"," after which he entered. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14572","(14566) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ṣāliḥ ibn Hānīʾ narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā and Muḥammad ibn Bashshār and ʿUbaydullāh ibn Saʿīd said — Yaḥyā narrated to us from ʿUbaydullāh — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā): that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said, \Verily"," those who make these images shall be punished on the Day of Resurrection. It will be said to them"," 'Give life to that which you have created.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," and al-Bukhārī reported it through another chain from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2108]"""
"14573","(14567) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — al-Aʿmash narrated from Muslim ibn Ṣubayḥ, who said: We were with Masrūq in the house of Yāsār ibn Numayr when Masrūq saw images in his gallery and said, \I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd say"," 'I heard the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) say"," \""Verily"," the most severely punished of people before Allāh on the Day of Resurrection are the image-makers (al-muṣawwirūn).\""'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī"," and Muslim narrated it from Ibn Abī ʿUmar from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2109]"""
"14574","(14568) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Mūsā ibn Isḥāq al-Anṣārī narrated to us — ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Shaybah — and Muḥammad informed us — Abū ʿAbdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib and ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad said — Abū Kurayb narrated to us — they said: Muḥammad ibn Fuḍayl narrated to us — ʿUmārah ibn al-Qaʿqāʿ narrated — from Abū Zurʿah, who said: I entered the house of Marwān with Abū Hurayrah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhu), and he saw images therein and said, \I heard the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) say"," 'Who is more unjust than the one who goes and creates a creation like My creation? Let them create an atom (dharrāh)"," or let them create a grain (ḥabbāh)"," or let them create a barley-shoulder (shaʿīrāh).'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2111]"""
"14575","(14569) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn Aṭāʾ informed us — Saʿīd narrated — from al-Naḍr ibn Anas, who said: I was with Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā) while he was issuing fatwās to people, not attributing anything of his fatwās to the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), when a man came to him and said, \I am from the people of Iraq"," and I make these images.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā) said to him"," \""Come close"," come close","\"" two or three times. So the man drew near"," and he said"," \""I heard Muḥammad (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) say"," 'Whoever makes an image in this world will be tasked on the Day of Respiration to breathe the spirit into it"," and he will not be able to do so.'\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both reported it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2110]"""
"14576","(14570) Abū ʿAliyy al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Maḥmawayh narrated to us — Jaʿfar al-Qalānisī narrated to us — Ādam narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated to us — ʿAwn ibn Abī Juḥayfah narrated from his father — from the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam): that he cursed the image-maker (al-muṣawwir). Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam ibn Abī Īsā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 2086]"
"14577","(14571) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed me — Abū Yaʿlā narrated to us — Abū Khaythamah narrated to us — Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us — Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated — from Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr — from ʿImrān ibn Ḥiṭṭān — from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā): that the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) would not leave in his house any garment bearing a cross (taṣlīb) without tearing it apart. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿādh ibn Faḍālah from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 5952]"
"14578","(14572) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us — Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us — al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us — Sufyān narrated to us — Ayyūb said: I heard ʿIkrimah say — I heard Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhumā) say — the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said, \Whoever makes an image will be punished and will be tasked to breathe the spirit into it"," and he will not be able to do so. And whoever narrates a false dream will be punished and will be tasked to tie a knot between two barley-shanks"," and he will not be able to do so. And whoever listens to the conversation of a people who dislike him will have molten lead (al-ānuk) poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection.\"" Sufyān said: \""Al-ānuk means molten lead (al-raṣāṣ).\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdillāh from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2110]"""
"14579","(14573) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us — Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī narrated to us — Sufyān said: I heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim say — I heard my father say — I heard ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā) say: The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) returned from a journey, and I had hung a curtain (qirām) over my niche which had images upon it. When he saw it, he tore it apart and said, \Verily"," the most severely punished of people on the Day of Resurrection are those who imitate the creation of Allāh.\"" She said"," \""So we cut it up and made from it one or two cushions.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn al-Madīnī"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2107]"""
"14580","(14574) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Ibn Wahb informed me — ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed him that Bukayr narrated to him — ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Qāsim narrated to him — that his father narrated to him — from ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā), the wife of the Prophet (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam): that she had set up a curtain with images upon it. The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) entered, removed it, and cut it into two cushions. A man who was present in the assembly at that time — Rabīʿah ibn Aṭāʾ, a freedman of Banū Zuhrah — said, \Have you not heard Abū Muḥammad (meaning al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad) mention that ʿĀʾishah (raḍiyallāhu ʿanhā) said that the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) used to rest upon them?\"" Ibn al-Qāsim said"," \""No.\"" He said"," \""But I have heard it\"" — meaning al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad. In the narration of Abū Zakariyyā"," Ibn al-Qāsim said"," \""It is as though I have heard it.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn Maʿrūf from Ibn Wahb"," with the wording of the ḥadīth of Abū ʿAbdillāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously referenced]"""
"14581","(14575) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn al-Layth al-Jawharī narrated to us: ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us: Abū Salamah al-Khuzāʿī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, the brother of al-Mājishūn's nephew, narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered and there was a curtain upon which were images. She said: I recognized anger on his face. Then he came and tore it apart. She said: I took it and made it into two cushions. She said: He (peace and blessings be upon him) used to lean upon them in the house.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq from Abū Salamah al-Khuzāʿī. [Authentic. Preceded earlier.]"""
"14582","(14576) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Abū ʿAlī Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated from Mujāhid, who said: Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came to me and said: I came to you last night"," but nothing prevented me from entering the house in which you were except that there was at the door of the house an image of a man"," and a curtain upon which were images"," and there was a puppy in the house. Command that the head of the image which is in the house be cut off"," and command that the curtain be cut and made into two cushions that are spread out and trodden upon"," and command that the dog be brought out.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did so. It was a dog or a puppy belonging to al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded that it be removed. [Authentic. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," 19488.]"""
"14583","(14577) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān al-ʿAdl in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: Maʿmar narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from Mujāhid, from Abū Hurayrah, that Jibrīl (peace be upon him) came and greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) recognized his voice and said: \Enter.\"" He said: \""There is a curtain in the house on the wall upon which are images. Cut off their heads and make them into cushions or pillows that are trodden upon"," for we do not enter a house in which there are images.\""\n\nZayd ibn Abī Unaysah and Abū Bakr ibn ʿAyyāsh also narrated it from Abī Isḥāq. [Authentic. Preceded earlier.]"""
"14584","(14578) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Abū Ṣāliḥ Maḥbūb ibn Mūsā informed us: Abū Isḥāq al-Fazārī narrated from Yūnus ibn Abī Isḥāq, and he mentioned it with its chain of narration similarly, except that he said: \Command that the head of the image which is at the door of the house be cut off so that it becomes like the shape of a tree.\"" [Authentic. Preceded earlier.]"""
"14585","(14579) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: ʿAwf narrated from Saʿīd ibn Abī al-Ḥasan, that a man came to Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) and said: \O Abū al-ʿAbbās"," I am a person whose livelihood comes from the work of my hands—I make these images.\"" Ibn ʿAbbās said to him: \""Come closer"," come closer. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Whoever makes an image in this world will be required on the Day of Resurrection to breathe the soul into it"," and he will not be able to breathe it.'\"" The man said: \""Then the man was seized by a severe trembling and said: 'Woe to you! If you must make something"," then make images of trees and that in which there is no soul.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿAwf"," and Muslim narrated it from another route from Saʿīd. [Authentic. Bukhārī"," 2225; 7042.]"""
"14586","(14580) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī narrated to us: Sahl ibn Bakkār narrated to us: Wahb narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \The image is the head. When the head is cut off"," it is no longer an image.\"" [Authentic.]"""
"14587","(14581) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī in Baghdād informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated from ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal, from ʿIkrimah, who said: \They used to dislike images that were set upright"," but they saw no harm in that which was trampled upon by the feet.\"" [Authentic.]"""
"14588","(14582) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated from Shuʿbah, the freedman of Ibn ʿAbbās, that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah entered upon ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) to visit him during his illness and saw upon him a garment of istabraq (silk brocade). He said: \O Abū al-ʿAbbās"," what is this garment?\"" Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \""What is it?\"" He said: \""Istabraq.\"" He said: \""It was only disliked for one who wears it out of arrogance.\"" He said: \""What are these images on the carpet (kānūn)?\"" He said: \""Indeed"," I will burn them with fire.\"" When al-Miswar left"," he said: \""Remove this garment from me and cut off the heads of these images that are in the carpet.\"" So he cut them off. [Authentic.]"""
"14589","(14583) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah and Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq said: Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: al-Layth narrated from Bukayr, from Busr ibn Saʿīd, from Zayd ibn Khālid, from Abū Ṭalḥah, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," the angels do not enter a house in which there is an image.\"" Busr said: \""Then Zayd ibn Khālid fell ill"," and we visited him"," and lo"," at his door there was a curtain upon which was an image. I said to ʿUbayd Allāh al-Khawlānī"," the foster-son of Maymūnah"," the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): 'Did Zayd not inform us about images the first day?' ʿUbayd Allāh said: 'Did you not hear him when he said: \""Except for a pattern (raqm) on a garment\""?'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in their Ṣaḥīḥ from Qutaybah. Al-Bukhārī said: \""And Ibn Wahb said…\"" [Authentic. Bukhārī"," 3226.]"""
"14590","(14584) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Muzakkī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Ibn Wahb informed me: ʿAmr ibn al-Ḥārith informed me that Bukayr narrated to him that Busr ibn Saʿīd narrated to him that Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, a Companion of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), narrated to him, and with Busr ibn Saʿīd was ʿUbayd Allāh al-Khawlānī, who was in the care of Maymūnah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). Zayd ibn Khālid narrated to both of them that Abū Ṭalḥah narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image.\"" Busr said: \""Then Zayd fell ill"," and we visited him"," and lo"," in his house there was a curtain upon which were images. I said to ʿUbayd Allāh al-Khawlānī: 'Did he not narrate to us…?' He said: 'He indeed said: \""Except for a pattern (raqm) on a garment.\"" Did you not hear him?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'Yes"," he did mention that.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Ṭāhir from Ibn Wahb. [Authentic. Preceded earlier.]"""
"14591","(14585) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās al-Asfaṭī narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Jaʿfar Kāmil ibn Aḥmad al-Mustamlī and Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Ayyūb al-Ṣighghī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn Ziyād al-Surrī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to us, Mālik narrated from Abū al-Naḍr, the freed slave of ʿUmar ibn ʿUbayd Allāh, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd, that he visited Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī to enquire after his health. He said: We found Sahl ibn Ḥunayf with him. Abū Ṭalḥah called a person who pulled out a cushion from beneath him. Sahl ibn Ḥunayf said to him: Why did you pull it out? He said: Because it contains images, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has said about them what you already know. Sahl said: Did he not say: \Except for a pattern on a garment\""? He said: Yes"," but it is more pleasing to my soul.\n\nHis statement \""except for a pattern on a garment\"" may refer to images of things that do not possess souls. This is not explicitly stated in the ḥadīth of Abū Ṭalḥah"," but it is clarified in the narrations before this chapter. Therefore"," what we have narrated in this chapter must be understood in light of what was narrated in the preceding chapter. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by Mālik"," 1802]"""
"14592","(14586) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Jarīr narrated from Suhayl, from Saʿīd ibn Yasār, Abū al-Ḥubāb, the freed slave of Banī al-Najjār, from Zayd ibn Khālid al-Juhanī, from Abū Ṭalḥah al-Anṣārī, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images (tamāthīl).\"" He said: So I went to ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) and said to her: This person informs me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""The angels do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images.\"" Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mention that? She said: No"," but I shall tell you what I saw him do. I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) go out on one of his military expeditions. I took a curtain (naṭam) and hung it over the door. When he returned and saw the curtain"," I recognised the displeasure on his face. He pulled it until he tore it or cut it"," and said: \""Allah has not commanded us to cover stones and clay.\"" She said: So we cut from it two cushions and stuffed them with palm fibre"," and he did not disapprove of that on my part.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm"," and Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated it from Suhayl"," and he said in the ḥadīth: \""stones and bricks.\""\n\nThis wording indicates the disapproval of covering walls with cloth"," although the reason for the wording"," according to what we have narrated through the chains of this ḥadīth"," indicates that the disapproval was due to the images upon it. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously narrated before the one before it]"""
"14593","(14587) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās al-Dūrī narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Khaṭmī narrated from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb, who said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd was invited to a meal. When he arrived, he saw the house adorned with furnishings (mujaddad), so he sat outside and wept. He was asked: What makes you weep? He said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he would escort an army and reach ʿAqabat al-Wadāʿ, would say: \I entrust to Allah your religion"," your trusts"," and the seals of your deeds.\"" He said: Then one day he saw a man who had patched his cloak with a piece. He faced the rising place of the sun and said"," stretching out his hands — and ʿAffān stretched out his hands — and said: \""The world has come upon you\"" — three times — \""until we thought it would fall upon us.\"" Then he said: \""Are you better today"," or when a dish comes to you in the morning and another in the evening"," and one of you goes out in a suit and returns in another"," and you cover your houses as the Kaʿbah is covered?\"" ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd said: Shall I not weep"," when I have remained until you cover your houses as the Kaʿbah is covered? [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14594","(14588) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-ʿUṭāridī narrated to us, my father narrated to me, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḍabbī narrated from al-Qāsim ibn ʿUrwah, from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb al-Quraẓī, who narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbbās attributed the ḥadīth to the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Everything has a nobility"," and the noblest of gatherings is that which faces the qiblah. Do not pray behind a sleeping person or one who is talking. Kill the snake and the scorpion"," even if you are in prayer. Do not cover the walls with garments.\"" And he mentioned the ḥadīth.\n\nThat has also been narrated from Hishām ibn Ziyād"," Abū al-Miqdām"," from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb"," and it has been narrated through another disconnected chain from Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb"," but no chain is established regarding that. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14595","(14589) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Ḥakīm ibn Jubayr, from ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade covering the walls. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14596","(14590) Abū Zakariyyā and Abū Bakr informed us, they both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās narrated to us, Baḥr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to me, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar narrated from Rabiʿah ibn ʿAṭāʾ, who said: I held a wedding feast for my son and invited al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad and ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. When they stood at the door, ʿUbayd Allāh saw that the house was covered with brocade (dībāj), so he turned back. Al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad entered. I said: By Allah, he has displeased me by leaving. I said: May Allah set you right — by Allah, I did not do this; it is something the women did and overpowered us with it. He narrated to me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) married his daughter Sālim, and on the day of her wedding, ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar invited people among whom was Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī (may Allah be pleased with him). When Abū Ayyūb stood at the door and saw curtains of raw silk (qazz) in the house, he said: You have done it, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān — you have covered the walls! Then he turned away.\n\nIn another narration of this report, it is said: Ibn ʿUmar invited Abū Ayyūb (may Allah be pleased with them), and he saw a curtain on the wall. Ibn ʿUmar said: The women have overpowered us. Abū Ayyūb said: I used to fear for people, but I did not fear for you. By Allah, I will not eat any food of yours, and he left. [Ṣaḥīḥ. The context of Sālim with his father]"
"14597","(14591) Abū Ḥāzim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamzah al-Harawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Salmān married Abū Qurrāh al-Kindī. When he went to her, he said: O woman, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) advised me that if Allah decrees for you to marry, the first thing upon which you two come together should be obedience. She said: You have sat in the seat of a man whose command is obeyed. He said to her: Stand, let us pray and supplicate. They did so. Then he saw a house covered with curtains and said: What is the matter with your house — is it feverish, or has the Kaʿbah moved to Kindah? They said: It is not feverish, and the Kaʿbah has not moved to Kindah. He said: I will not enter it until every curtain is torn down, except the curtain on the door. This is munqaṭiʿ (disconnected). We have narrated the disapproval of that from ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and it is likely that this was due to the extravagance involved. And Allah knows best. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14598","(14592) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-ʿAbsī informed us, Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Sayyārī in Marw informed us, Muḥammad ibn Mūsā al-Bāshānī narrated to us, ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq informed us, Abū Ḥamzah narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," if I were invited to a shank"," I would accept"," and if a forearm were gifted to me"," I would accept it.\"" Wakīʿ did not mention his words: \""By the One in Whose Hand is my soul.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbdān from Abū Ḥamzah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī"," 2568; 5178]"""
"14599","(14593) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ in Baghdad informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Surrī narrated to us, Ibn Abī Uways narrated to me, Mālik narrated from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, that he heard Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: Abū Ṭalḥah said to Umm Sulaym: I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and recognised hunger in it. Do you have anything? She said: Yes. She brought out some barley loaves, then she took out her head-covering, wrapped some of the bread in it, placed it under my arm, wrapped me with part of it, and sent me to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). I went with it and found the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in the mosque with people. I stood — or I greeted him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: Did Abū Ṭalḥah send you? I said: Yes. He said: For food? I said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to those with him: Get up. So they set out, and I went ahead of them until I came to Abū Ṭalḥah and informed him. Abū Ṭalḥah said: O Umm Sulaym, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) has come with the people, and we do not have enough food to feed them. She said: Allah and His Messenger know best. Abū Ṭalḥah went until he met the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and Abū Ṭalḥah came and entered. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: Come here, O Umm Sulaym, what do you have? She brought him that bread. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered, and it was broken up. Umm Sulaym squeezed a skin vessel of hers and seasoned it with condiments. Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about it whatever Allah willed him to say. Then he said: Permit ten. He permitted them, and they ate until they were satisfied, then they left. Then he said: Permit ten. They ate until they were satisfied, until all the people had eaten and were satisfied — the people being seventy or eighty. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī, Muslim, 2040]"
"14600","(14594) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhṭawayh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us. He said: I read to Mālik, and he mentioned the ḥadīth with its like, except that he said: \Then she placed it under my garment and wrapped me with part of it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. Saʿd ibn Saʿīd narrated it from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and added in it: He said: Then she prepared it"," and it was just as it was when they had eaten from it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously narrated before it]"""
"14601","(14595) Abu al-Qasim Zayd ibn Abi Hashim al-Alawi informed us in Kufa; Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn — Ibn Abi al-Hunayd narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated from Malik. And Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tusi al-Faqih informed us; Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Karizi informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated from Malik from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, that he heard Anas ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) say: \Indeed"," a tailor invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to a meal he had prepared for him.\"" Anas said: \""So I went with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to that food. He brought close to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) bread made of barley and a broth containing pumpkin and dried meat.\"" Anas said: \""I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) seeking out the pumpkin from around the edges of the platter. I have never ceased to love pumpkin after that day.\""\n\nIn the narration of Ibn Abi al-Hunayd: \""after that day.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from al-Qa'nabi"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from Malik. [Sahih. Muslim 2041]"""
"14602","(14596) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us; Abu Hamid ibn Bilal al-Bazzaz narrated to us; al-Abbas al-Duri narrated to us; Abu Asim al-Nabil narrated to us; Hanzlah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mina narrated to us; Jabir ibn Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to his Companions: \Stand up"," for Jabir has prepared a sur.\""\n\nAbu al-Fadl — who is al-Duri — said: \""What is intended by this hadith is that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spoke in Persian. Sur means a wedding feast.\""\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in the Sahih from Amr ibn Ali"," and Muslim narrated it from Hajjaj ibn al-Sha'ir from Abu Asim in its full version. Its context indicates that he said that regarding an invitation to food other than a wedding feast. [Sahih. Bukhari 3070]"""
"14603","(14597) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Sakhr al-Darimi and al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated — and this is his hadith — they said: Abu Asim narrated to us; Hanzlah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mina narrated to us; Jabir ibn Abdullah al-Ansari said: \On the day of the Trench"," the people were afflicted with severe hunger. So I said to my wife: 'Do you have anything so that we may invite the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)?' She said: 'We have only a sa' of barley.' I said to her: 'Grind it.' And I slaughtered a young goat we had. When she finished"," I went to invite the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," we have a sa' of barley and a young goat or a sheep"," which we have slaughtered.' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called out among his Companions: 'Stand up"," for Jabir has prepared a sur.' I went ahead of the people and came to my wife. She said: 'May you be ruined! Do not disgrace me today before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him).' The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered and said: 'Place your pot.' So they placed the meat in it. He spat into it and invoked blessings. Then he said: 'Find a baker to bake for you.' The baker began to bake. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Enter in groups of ten.' He kept ladling for them"," and they ate until he reached the last of them. And we were still scooping from our pot"," and our dough was being baked as it was"," and our cooking pot was bubbling as it had been.\"" [Sahih. Muslim 2040]"""
"14604","(14598) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Abbas al-Mahbubi narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mas'ud narrated to us; al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from Yazid ibn Khumayr, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Busr say: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by his father while he was on a white mule. He came to him and took hold of its bridle and said: 'Dismount upon me.' So he dismounted with us. He was brought dates and sifted barley meal"," and he ate from it. He would place the date pits on the back of his index finger"," or the middle finger"," or both of them"," and then throw them. A meal was prepared for him"," and he ate from it. Then he was brought a cup of milk or sifted barley meal"," and he drank from it. Then he gave it to the one on his right. When he intended to travel or set out"," he said: 'Supplicate for us.' So he said: 'O Allah"," bless them in what You have provided them"," forgive them"," and have mercy upon them.'\""\n\nMuslim extracted it in the Sahih from the hadith of Ghundar"," Ibn Abi Adi"," and Yahya ibn Hammad from Shu'bah. [Sahih. Muslim 2042]"""
"14605","(14599) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Harun ibn Zayd ibn Abi al-Zarqa' narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated from al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit, who said: I heard Ikrimah say: \Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say: 'Indeed"," the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade eating the food of two boasting rivals.'\""\n\nAbu Dawud said: \""Most of those who narrated it from Jarir do not mention Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) in it. Harun al-Nahwi also mentioned Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) in it. Hammad ibn Zayd did not mention Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both).\"" [Da'if. Narrated by al-Sijistani 3754]"""
"14606","(14600) Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to me; Ali ibn Husayn ibn Waqid narrated from his father from Yazid al-Nahwi from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Regarding the verse {And do not consume your wealth among yourselves unjustly, except it be trade by mutual consent} [al-Nisa' 29], a man used to feel it sinful to eat at anyone's house after this verse was revealed. Then the verse in al-Nur abrogated that, and He said {There is no blame upon you that you eat from your houses} [al-Nur 61] up to His words {scattered}. That is, He intended by this the words of Allah: {There is no blame upon the blind, nor any blame upon the lame, nor any blame upon the sick, nor upon yourselves that you eat from your houses, or the houses of your fathers, or the houses of your mothers, or the houses of your brothers, or the houses of your sisters, or the houses of your paternal uncles, or the houses of your paternal aunts, or the houses of your maternal uncles, or the houses of your maternal aunts, or those whose keys you possess, or your friend. There is no blame upon you whether you eat together or separately.} He said: \A wealthy man would invite a poor person from his family to food"," and then feel it sinful to eat with him. The poor person would say: 'He has more right to it than I.' So Allah made lawful for them that over which the name of Allah had been mentioned"," and He made lawful the food of the People of the Book.\""\n\nAl-Zuhri narrated from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah regarding the words of Allah {There is no blame upon the blind} [al-Nur 61]: \""When the Muslims went out on military expeditions"," they would leave their incapacitated ones in their houses and hand over to them the keys of their doors"," saying: 'We have made it lawful for you to eat from what is in our houses.' But they used to feel it sinful"," saying: 'We will not enter them while they are absent.' So this verse was revealed as a concession for them.\""\n\nThus Abu Dawud narrated it in the Marasil from Muhammad ibn Ubayd from Muhammad ibn Thawr from Ma'mar from al-Zuhri"," as a mursal narration. And from Hajjaj ibn Abi Ya'qub from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim from his father from Salih ibn Kaysan from Ibn Shihab from Ubaydullah and Ibn al-Musayyab"," as a mursal narration with the same meaning and more complete than it. [Hasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"14607","(14601) He narrated it from Zayd ibn Akhzam from Bishr ibn Umar from Ibrahim from Salih from al-Zuhri from Urwah from A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her).\n\nAbu Dawud said: \The correct narration is that of Ya'qub and Ma'mar.\"" Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed us; Abu al-Husayn al-Fasawi informed us; Abu Ali al-Lu'lu'i narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated it. And in another narration they said: \""We fear that their souls may not be content"," even if they have said it.\"" So this verse was revealed. [Sahih. Narrated by al-Sijistani]"""
"14608","(14602) Abu Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us; Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us; Adam narrated to us; Warqa' narrated from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid, who said: \There were men who were blind"," lame"," and in need. Men would follow them to their houses. If they did not find food in their houses"," they would take them to the houses of their fathers"," the houses of their mothers"," and the other houses counted among their houses. Those who followed them disliked that and said: 'They are taking us to houses other than their houses.' So Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," revealed regarding that {There is no blame upon you} [al-Baqarah 236]"," and He made food lawful for them wherever they found it.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""That is"," if its owner was pleased with it. They used to feel it sinful even with the owner's consent. So the sin was lifted when it was with his permission. And Allah knows best.\"" [Sahih]"""
"14609","(14603) Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubayd al-Hurfi narrated to us in Baghdad; Ahmad ibn Salman narrated to us; Hilal ibn al-Ala' narrated to us; Ibn Nufayl narrated. Ahmad ibn Salman also narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Balisi narrated to us; al-Nufayli narrated to us; Abd al-Salam ibn Harb narrated to me; Yazid ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dalani narrated. And Abu Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Hannad ibn al-Sari narrated from Abd al-Salam ibn Harb from Abu Khalid al-Dalani from Abu al-Ala' al-Awdi from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When two inviters come together"," respond to the one whose door is nearer"," for the one whose door is nearer is the closer neighbor. But if one of them preceded"," then respond to the one who preceded.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14610","(14604) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Furak informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Qays — who is Ibn al-Rabi' narrated from Abu Hashim from Zadan from Salman, who said: \In the Torah it is written: 'The blessing of food is the ablution before it.' I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and he said: 'The blessing of food is the ablution before it and after it.'\""\n\nQays ibn al-Rabi' is not strong"," and no hadith is established regarding washing the hands before eating. [Da'if]"""
"14611","(14605) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us — Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī and ʿAbbās both said — ʿAffān ibn Muslim narrated to us — Wuhaym narrated from Maʿmar — from al-Zuhrī — from Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib — from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and is then afflicted by something"," let him blame none but himself.\""\n\nAnd ʿUqayl narrated it from Ibn Shihāb"," from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," from Abī Saʿīd. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14612","(14606) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd informed us — Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Zuhayr narrated to us — Suhayl narrated from his father — from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever sleeps with grease on his hand and does not wash it"," and is then afflicted by something"," let him blame none but himself.\""\n\nThe ḥadīth of Suwayd ibn al-Nuʿmān regarding the rinsing of the mouth by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and their rinsing after consuming the sūwīq is evidence in this chapter"," and it has already been mentioned in the Book of Purification. Thus"," the ḥadīth of washing the hands after eating is ḥasan"," while washing them before eating is ḍaʿīf. And in the ṣaḥīth ḥadīth from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Prophet ﷺ came to the privy"," then returned and was brought food. It was said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," will you not perform wuḍūʾ?\"" He said: \""Why? I am about to pray"," so I shall perform wuḍūʾ.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned"," without his statement \""and does not wash it.\""]"""
"14613","(14607) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Harawī narrated to us — Abū Salamah Yaḥyā ibn Khalaf narrated to us — Abū ʿĀṣim narrated — from Ibn Jurayj — who said: Abū al-Zubayr informed me — from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh — that he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: \When a man enters his house and mentions Allah upon entering and at the time of his food"," Shayṭān says: 'You have no place to stay the night"," nor any evening meal.' And if he enters without mentioning Allah upon entering"," Shayṭān says: 'You have found a place to stay the night.' And if he does not mention Allah at the time of his food"," he says: 'You have found both a place to stay the night and an evening meal.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā"," from Abī ʿĀṣim. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2018]"""
"14614","(14608) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated — Hishām narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Malik ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Maymūnī narrated to us — Rūḥ narrated to us — Hishām ibn Abī ʿAbd Allāh narrated — from Budayl al-ʿUqaylī — from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr al-Laythī — from a woman among them known as Umm Kulthūm — from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was eating with six of his Companions when a hungry Bedouin came, and he ate two morsels. The Prophet ﷺ said: \Had he mentioned the name of Allah"," it would have sufficed you all. So when one of you eats"," let him mention the name of Allah. And if he forgets to invoke the name of Allah at the beginning"," let him say: 'Bismillāh awwalahu wa ākhirahu' (In the name of Allah"," at its beginning and at its end).\"" This is the wording of the ḥadīth of Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah. [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi]"""
"14615","(14609) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī all said — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Abū Yaḥyā Zakariyyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Sufyān narrated — from al-Zuhrī — from Abū Bakr ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh — from his grandfather ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them): that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you eats"," let him eat with his right hand"," and when he drinks"," let him drink with his right hand"," for indeed Shayṭān eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Sufyān.\n\n(T) And similarly ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar and Mālik ibn Anas narrated it from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2020]"""
"14616","(14610) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bulshān in Baghdad informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar narrated — from al-Zuhrī — from Sālim — from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one of you eats"," let him eat with his right hand"," and when he drinks"," let him drink with his right hand"," for indeed Shayṭān eats and drinks with his left hand.\""\n\nʿAbd al-Razzāq said: Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah said to Maʿmar: \""Indeed"," al-Zuhrī narrated it to me from Abū Bakr ibn ʿUbayd Allāh"," from Ibn ʿUmar.\"" So Maʿmar said to him: \""Indeed"," al-Zuhrī used to mention the ḥadīth from a group; perhaps it was from both of them together.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: This is possible"," for ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad narrated it from al-Qāsim ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar"," from Sālim"," from his father. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"""
"14617","(14611) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Khalīl narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb narrated to me — Abū al-Walīd narrated — ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated — from Iyās ibn Salamah — that his father narrated to him —\n\n(Ḥ) And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us — Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — ʿAbbās al-Asfaṭī, Ibn al-Faḍl, narrated to us — Abū al-Walīd narrated — ʿIkrimah ibn ʿAmmār narrated — Iyās ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwaʿ narrated — from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Bishr ibn Rāʿī al-ʿĪrī eating with his left hand. He said: \Eat with your right hand.\"" He said: \""I cannot.\"" He said: \""Then you never shall be able.\"" He said: \""His hand never reached his mouth thereafter.\""\n\nIn the narration of al-Sulamī: \""His right hand never reached.\"" And he said: \""Busr\"" with a bāʾ and an unpointed sīn"," while the correct form is \""Bishr\"" with a fatḥah on the bāʾ and a pointed shīn"," as mentioned by Ibn Mandah and other ḥuffāẓ. And Allah knows best. Muslim extracted it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from another chain from ʿIkrimah"," adding: \""And nothing prevented him except pride.\"" He said: \""So he never raised it to his mouth.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2021]"""
"14618","(14612) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us — Ibn Abī ʿUmar narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAmr narrated to me — al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān informed us — he said: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — both said: Sufyān narrated — from al-Walīd ibn Kathīr — from Wahb ibn Kaysān — who heard it from ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, who said: I was in the lap of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my hand was wandering about in the platter. So he said to me: \O young boy"," invoke the name of Allah"," eat with your right hand"," and eat from what is in front of you.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh"," and Muslim from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and Ibn Abī ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2022]"""
"14619","(14613) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us — Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmawayh narrated to us — Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī narrated to us — Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us — Shuʿbah narrated — from ʿAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib — from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr — from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: A platter of tharīd was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \Eat from its sides and do not eat from its centre"," for indeed the blessing descends in its centre.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14620","(14614) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us — Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to me — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām and Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAlī both said — Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us — Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated — from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah — from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Saʿd — from Ibn Kaʿb ibn Mālik — from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to eat with three fingers and would lick his hand before wiping it.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2032]"
"14621","(14615) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Faraj al-Azraq narrated to us, Ḥajjāj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: ʿAṭāʾ informed me that he heard Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you eats food"," let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2031]"""
"14622","(14616) And ʿAlī informed us, Aḥmad informed us, al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj said: I heard ʿAṭāʾ say: I heard Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When one of you eats food"," let him not wipe his hand until he licks it or has it licked.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad"," and from Zuhayr ibn Ḥarb from Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it]"""
"14623","(14617) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb informed us, ʿAlī ibn al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a morsel of food falls from one of you"," let him remove any dirt from it and eat it"," and not leave it for the devil. And let none of you wipe his hand with a cloth until he licks it or has it licked"," for he does not know in which part of his food the blessing lies.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through other chains from Sufyān al-Thawrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2033]"""
"14624","(14618) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated from Thābit from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), when he ate food, would lick his three fingers. And he said: \When a morsel of food falls from one of you"," let him remove the dirt from it and eat it"," and not leave it for the devil.\"" And he commanded us to lick the platter. And he said: \""Indeed"," one of you does not know in which part of his food the blessing is placed for him.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through two other chains from Ḥammād ibn Salamah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2034]"""
"14625","(14619) Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muʾammal al-Māsarjisī informed us, Abū ʿUthmān ʿAmr ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Baṣrī narrated to us, Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb informed us, Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, al-Aʿmash narrated from ʿAmr ibn Murrah from Abī al-Bakhtarī, he said: Salmān (may Allah be pleased with him) prepared food and invited a group of his companions. A beggar came, and a man took some of the food and handed it to him. Salmān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Put it down; you have been invited to eat.\"" The man was embarrassed. When they had finished"," Salmān said: \""Perhaps what I said to you was difficult for you.\"" He said: \""Yes"," by Allah"," you have belittled me.\"" He said: \""What need have you for the reward to be mine and the burden to be yours?\""\n\nAnd Shuʿbah narrated something similar from ʿAmr ibn Murrah. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14626","(14620) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Abū al-Naḍr narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me, Abū ʿAmr al-Ḥīrī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Abū Kurayb narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated from Sulaymān ibn al-Mughīrah from Thābit from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: A man invited the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and I went with him. A broth containing pumpkin was brought, and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) began eating from that pumpkin and it pleased him. Anas said: When I saw that, I began placing it before him and not eating it. Anas said: After that, pumpkin continued to please me.\n\nThe wording is that of Abū Usāmah. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Kurayb, and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Thumāmah ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Anas, who said: \When I saw that"," I began gathering it before him.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2041]"""
"14627","(14621) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī in Kūfah informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed us, Wakīʿ narrated from al-Aʿmash. He said: I think Abū Ḥāzim mentioned it. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Ḥasan Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdūs narrated orally, Abū Saʿīd ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from al-Aʿmash from Abī Ḥāzim from Abū Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never criticized any food. If he desired it, he ate it, and if he disliked it, he left it. And in the narration of Wakīʿ: \Otherwise he left it.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Kathīr"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from al-Aʿmash. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2064]"""
"14628","(14622) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad al-Nufaylī narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Simāk ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, Qabīṣah ibn Hulb narrated from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when a man asked him and said: \There is a food from which I feel uneasy.\"" He said: \""Let nothing cause unease in your soul regarding something in which you have imitated Christianity.\""\n\nSomething similar has also been narrated from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim from the Prophet (ﷺ). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14629","(14623) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both narrated to us, they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn ʿUbādah al-Qaysī narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from Simāk ibn Ḥarb from Murayy ibn Qaṭarī, a man from Ṭayʾ from Banī Thuʿal, from ʿAdī ibn Ḥātim, he said: I said: \O Messenger of Allah"," my father used to maintain ties of kinship and do such and such"," but he died in the Jāhiliyyah.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \""Your father intended an affair and attained it\"" — meaning fame. He said: I said: \""I wish to ask you about a food which I do not abandon except out of unease.\"" He said: \""Do not feel uneasy about anything in which you have imitated Christianity.\"" He said: I said: \""I send my dog and it catches the game"," and I have nothing with which to slaughter it except a stone or a staff.\"" He said: \""Let the blood flow by whatever means you wish"," and mention the name of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14630","(14624) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us, Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī in Makkah narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us, Asbāṭ ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿUbayd Allāh ibn al-Walīd narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd ibn ʿUmayr, he said: A group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) visited Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh, and he brought them bread and vinegar. He said: \Eat"," for I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'What an excellent condiment is vinegar! It is destruction for a man that a group of his brothers come to him and he considers what is in his house too insignificant to offer them. And it is destruction for a people that they consider insignificant what is offered to them.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14631","(14625) Abū Muḥammad — ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf — informed us; Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī — narrated to us; Ribʿī ibn ʿUlayyah — narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Isḥāq — narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Muʿāwiyah — narrated to us, from ʿUthmān ibn Abī Sulaymān, who said: Ṣafwān ibn Umayyah said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saw me taking meat from the bone with my hand"," so he said to me: 'O Ṣafwān!' I said: 'Here I am"," at your service.' He said: 'Bring the meat close to your mouth"," for it is more wholesome and more digestible.'\"" [Ḥasan li-ghayrihi. Without the story.]"""
"14632","(14626) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb al-Qāḍī — narrated to us; Abū al-Rabīʿ — narrated to us; Abū Maʿshar — narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not cut meat with a knife"," for that is the practice of the non-Arabis (al-aʿājim). Rather"," bite it off with your teeth"," for it is more wholesome and more digestible.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14633","(14627) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī — informed us by dictation; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Ayyūb ibn Salmawayh — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yazīd al-Sulamī — narrated to us; Ḥassān ibn Ḥassān al-Baṣrī — narrated to us; Abū Maʿshar — narrated to us; Hishām — narrated something similar to it."
"14634","(14628) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ — informed me; Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Harawī — informed me; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Jakkānī — narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān — narrated to us; Shuʿayb — informed me, from al-Zuhrī — informed me; Jaʿfar ibn ʿAmr ibn Umayyah — informed me, that his father ʿAmr ibn Umayyah informed him: \He saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) cutting from a sheep's shoulder that was in his hand. Then he was called to the prayer"," so he put it down along with the knife with which he had been cutting. Then he stood and prayed"," and he did not perform wuḍūʾ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from al-Zuhrī. In this there is an indication of the permissibility of cutting meat with a knife"," and that the previous ḥadīth"," if authentic"," intended thereby — and Allah knows best — that when one bites it off"," it is more delicious"," as in the first ḥadīth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 355]"""
"14635","(14629) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ — informed us; al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq — informed us; Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb — narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿĪsá — narrated to us; Ibn Wahb — narrated to us; Qurrah — informed me, from Ibn Shihāb, from ʿUrwah, from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them both): \When she prepared tharīd (bread soaked in broth)"," she would cover it until its heat subsided"," then she would say: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: \""Indeed"," that is a greater means of blessing (barakah).\""'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14636","(14630) Al-Ustādh Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Isfarāyīnī — narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī — informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ṣūfī — narrated to us; Suwayd ibn Saʿīd — narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn Mushir — narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was once brought hot food"," and he said: 'No hot food has entered my stomach since such and such a time"," before today.'\""\n\nAnd if this is authentic"," it may carry the meaning of the first narration"," or it may carry another meaning. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14637","(14631) And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī — narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm — narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr — narrated to us; Ibn Wahb — narrated to us; al-Layth — narrated to me, from Jaʿfar ibn Rabīʿah, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Aʿraj, from Abī Hurayrah, who used to say: \Food should not be eaten until its steam (bukhāruhu) has subsided.\"" [Ṣaḥīf]"""
"14638","(14632) He said: And Ibn Wahb narrated to me; Ibn Lahīʿah — narrated to me, from al-Ḥārith ibn Yazīd, from ʿUmayr ibn Fāʾidh al-Lakhmī, who said: \I was sitting with Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) in Īliyāʾ when a steaming dish was brought and placed before him. He said: 'Leave it until some of its heat dissipates.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14639","(14633) Al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Maḥmūyah al-ʿAskarī — narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Qalānisī — narrated to us; Ādam ibn Abī Iyās — narrated to us; Shuʿbah — narrated to us; Jabalat ibn Suḥaym — narrated to us, who said: \During a year of drought"," we were with Ibn al-Zubayr"," and we were given dates as provision. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar would pass by us while we were eating and say: 'Do not combine (two dates at once)"," for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited al-iqrān (eating two dates together).' Then he added: 'Unless a man seeks permission from his brother.'\"" Shuʿbah said: \""The mention of permission (al-idhn) is from the statement of Ibn ʿUmar.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ādam"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2045]"""
"14640","(14634) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī — informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah — narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd — narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Jabalah — narrated to us; Salm ibn Qutaybah, Abū Qutaybah — narrated to us, from Hammām, from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Anas ibn Mālik, who said: \The Prophet (ﷺ) was brought old dates"," and he began inspecting them"," extracting the weevils from them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14641","(14635) He said: And Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us, Hammām informed us, from Isḥāq ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, that the Prophet ﷺ was brought dates containing worms, and he mentioned its meaning.\n\nIt was also narrated from Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the prohibition of splitting open a date to remove what is inside it. If this is authentic, it is likely that what is meant thereby — and Allāh knows best — is when the dates are fresh, whereas the narration we have cited pertains to dates that are old. [Weak]"
"14642","(14636) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr the Qāḍī informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Abū Umayyah narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Sulaymān narrated to us, ʿAbbād ibn al-ʿAwwām narrated to us, from Ḥumayd, from Anas, that he used to dislike placing date-stones together with dates on a platter. This is a mawqūf narration traced to Anas, may Allāh be pleased with him. [Authentic]"
"14643","(14637) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed me, Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Sayyārī informed me in Marw, Abū al-Muwajjih narrated to us, ʿAbdān narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar, who said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ eating cucumbers with fresh dates.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz al-Uwaysī, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyá ibn Yaḥyá, both of them from Ibrāhīm. [Authentic]"
"14644","(14638) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Nuṣayr narrated to us, Abū Usāmah narrated to us, Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated to us, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allāh be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ used to eat cooked food with fresh dates, and he would say: \We break the heat of this with the coolness of this"," and the coolness of this with the heat of this.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14645","(14639) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn Shākir narrated to us, ʿAffān narrated to us, Hammām and Abān narrated to us, from Qatādah, from Anas.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālūyah narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khālid narrated to us, Hammām narrated to us, Qatādah narrated to us, and Anas ibn Mālik informed us, that the Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking while standing. Qatādah said: We asked, \And eating?\"" He said: \""That is worse and more reprehensible.\"" Qatādah's statement is not in the narration of ʿAffān. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Hudbah ibn Khālid. [Authentic. Muslim 2024]"""
"14646","(14640) And ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us, Abū Jaʿfar al-Razzāz narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, from Qatādah.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Yaḥyá ibn Manṣūr the Qāḍī narrated to us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal narrated to us, Hudbah ibn Khālid narrated to us, Hammām narrated to us, Qatādah narrated to us, from Abī ʿĪsá al-Aswārī, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, may Allāh be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ forbade drinking while standing. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Haddāb ibn Khālid. [Authentic. Muslim 2025]"
"14647","(14641) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālūyah narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān narrated to us, Yaḥyá ibn Maʿīn narrated to us, Marwān ibn Muʿāwiyah narrated to us, ʿUmar ibn Ḥamzah narrated to us, Abū Ghaṭfān al-Murrī narrated to us, that he heard Abū Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \Let none of you drink while standing. Whoever drinks"," let him induce vomiting.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Jabbār ibn al-ʿAlāʾ from Marwān. [Authentic. Muslim 2026]"""
"14648","(14642) Abū al-Fatḥ Hilāl ibn Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Ḥaffār informed us in Baghdād, al-Ḥusayn ibn Yaḥyá ibn ʿAyyāsh al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, from Maʿmar, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allāh be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \If the one who drinks while standing knew what is in his belly"," he would induce vomiting.\"" Thus it was brought as a connected narration. [Authentic. See previous]"""
"14649","(14643) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar informed us, from al-Zuhrī, from Abī Hurayrah, may Allāh be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allāh ﷺ said: \If the one who drinks while standing knew what is in his belly"," he would induce vomiting.\"" [Authentic. See previous]"""
"14650","(14644) He said: And Maʿmar informed us, from al-Aʿmash, from Abī Ṣāliḥ, from Abī Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, a hadith similar to that of al-Zuhrī. He said: This reached ʿAlī, may Allāh be pleased with him, so he called for water and drank while standing. [Authentic]"
"14651","(14645) The Sheikh said: This prohibition that has come in the reports we have mentioned — whether it be a prohibition of discouragement (nahy tanzīh) or a prohibition of forbiddance (nahy taḥrīm) — has been abrogated by what Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us, Shuʿbah narrated from ʿĀṣim, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Zamzam and asked for water to drink. I brought him a bucket of water from Zamzam, and he drank while standing.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā, from Wahb ibn Jarīr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2027]"
"14652","(14646) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf narrated to us: Abū Saʿīd Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Baṣrī narrated to us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī narrated to us, Shādhān narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal narrated — and Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me: ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn Qurqūb al-Tammār informed me in Hamadhān, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dīzīl narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from ʿĀṣim, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ibn ʿAbbās, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ drinking from Zamzam while standing.\n\nAnd in the narration of Shādhān, he said: I gave the Prophet ﷺ water from Zamzam to drink, and he drank while standing.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned]"
"14653","(14647) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Aḥmad Bakr ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdān al-Ṣayrafī in Marw informed us, ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn al-Faḍl informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, from Misʿar, from ʿAbd al-Malik, from al-Nazzāl ibn Sabrah, who said: ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought a vessel in al-Raḥabah, and he drank while standing. He said: There were people among whom one would dislike drinking while standing, yet I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do as you have seen me do. Then he took some water — he said: I think he wiped his face, his hands, and his feet — and then he said: \This is the wuḍūʾ of one who has not broken his state of purity.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5615"," 5616]"""
"14654","(14648) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us, Ibn Wahb informed me, ʿUmar ibn Muḥammad informed me that Sulaymān ibn Mihrān narrated to him, from Mujāhid, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, who said: As for me, I eat standing and I drink standing. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14655","(14649) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from ʿImrān ibn Ḥudayr, from Yazīd ibn ʿUṭārid, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we used to drink while standing and eat while we were walking. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14656","(14650) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, who said: Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ and ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with them both, saw no harm in drinking while standing; they would both drink while standing. And it has been narrated from Abū Bakrah that he drank while standing. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14657","(14651) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Salmān al-Faqīh informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Salām informed us, Abū Nuʿaym informed us, Misʿar narrated from ʿAlī ibn al-Aqmar. He said: I heard Abū Juḥayfah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \I do not eat while reclining.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym.\n\nThe Sheikh said: Abū Sulaymān al-Khaṭṭābī"," may Allah have mercy on him"," said: \""The muttakīʾ (reclining one) here refers to one who leans upon the cushion beneath him — that is"," one who props up his seat and braces it by sitting upon the cushion beneath it. That is to say: when I eat"," I do not sit reclining upon cushions and pillows as one who wishes to eat abundantly does; rather"," I eat a modest amount (ʿulqah)"," and my sitting is one of readiness and humility for it.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated that he used to eat sitting on his haunches (muqʿiyyan) and would say: \""I am a servant; I eat as a servant eats.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5398]"""
"14658","(14652) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed me: Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh informed us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī and al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān said: Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah informed us, Ḥafṣ ibn Ghiyāth narrated from Muṣʿab ibn Sulaym, who narrated to us: Anas ibn Mālik said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ sitting on his haunches (muqʿiyyan) eating dates.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2044]"
"14659","(14653) ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk informed us, ʿAmr ibn ʿUthmān informed us, my father informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿIrq narrated from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Busr, who said: A sheep was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and food was scarce at that time. He said to his family: \Prepare this sheep"," and look at this bread — crumble it and scoop it up.\"" The Prophet ﷺ had a large bowl called al-Gharrāʾ"," which four men would carry. When they had finished the forenoon and prayed the Ḍuḥā prayer"," that bowl was brought"," and they gathered around it. When their numbers increased"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on his haunches (jathā). A Bedouin said: \""What is this sitting?\"" — meaning this posture. He said: \""Allah has made me a noble servant and has not made me a tyrant and disobedient. Eat from its sides and leave its upper portion"," that it may be blessed therein.\"" Then he said: \""Take and eat! By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad"," Persia and Rome will be conquered for you"," until food becomes abundant and the name of Allah is no longer mentioned over it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14660","(14654) Abū ʿAbd Allāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf al-Ṭāʾī informed us, Abū al-Mughīrah ʿAbd al-Quddūs ibn al-Ḥajjāj informed us, al-Awzāʿī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr informed us, ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Qatādah al-Anṣārī informed us, my father informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \When one of you urinates"," let him not touch his private part with his right hand"," nor cleanse himself (istinjāʾ) with his right hand"," and let him not breathe into the vessel.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf"," from al-Awzāʿī"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 267]"""
"14661","(14655) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī narrated to us, Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn Ḥamdūyah ibn Sahl al-Marwazī narrated to us, Maḥmūd ibn Ādam al-Marwazī narrated to us, Ibn ʿUyaynah narrated from ʿAbd al-Karīm from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbāṣ (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \Do not breathe into the vessel"," nor blow into it.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14662","(14656) Abū al-Qāsim Zayd ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī and Abū Muḥammad Janāḥ ibn Nadhīr al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunay narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Dukayn narrated — and Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥarbī narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, ʿAzrah ibn Thābit narrated from Thumāmah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Anas, from Anas, that he used to breathe twice or thrice while drinking from the vessel, and he asserted that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to breathe three times while drinking from the vessel. In the narration of the Kūfan, it was said: Anas (may Allah be pleased with him). Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym, and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Wakīʿ from ʿAzrah ibn Thābit. And what is meant by it, and Allah knows best, is drinking in three breaths. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14663","(14657) Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated it, saying: ʿAzrah ibn Thābit narrated to us, Thumāmah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to breathe three times when he drank. Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before it.]"
"14664","(14658) Abū al-Qāsim ibn Abī Hāshim al-ʿAlawī and Abū Bakr al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū Jaʿfar ibn Duḥaym narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Ḥunay narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us — and Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Hishām narrated from Abī ʿIṣām, from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to breathe three times when he drank, and he said: \It is more wholesome"," more satisfying"," and more beneficial.\"" Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj extracted it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of ʿAbd al-Wārith and Hishām from Abī ʿIṣām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"14665","(14659) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from Ibn Abī Ḥusayn that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When one of you drinks"," let him sip gently"," and let him not gulp in one breath"," for liver ailment comes from gulping.\"" This is a mursal narration. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14666","(14660) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdad, Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr al-Razzāz narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Abī al-ʿAwwām narrated to us, Abū ʿĀmir narrated to us, Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān narrated from Saʿīd ibn al-Ḥārith, from Jābir ibn ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the garden of a man of the Anṣār, and a companion was with him. He said: \If you have water that has been stored overnight in a waterskin"," [give us that]; otherwise"," we shall drink directly [from the source].\"" The man was diverting the water in his garden. He said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," I have water that I believe has been stored overnight in a waterskin. Go to the shelter.\"" So they went"," and he poured water into a cup"," then milked some milk from his domestic goat over it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) drank"," and then the one who had entered with him drank. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad from Abī ʿĀmir al-ʿAqdī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5613"," 5621]"""
"14667","(14661) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the bending open of the mouths of waterskins [for drinking].\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from ʿAbd al-Razzāq"," and al-Bukhārī extracted it from two other routes from al-Zuhrī. Al-Aṣmaʿī said: \""Al-ikhtināth is that the openings of the waterskins be folded over and then one drinks from them.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2023]"""
"14668","(14662) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq ibn Abī al-Fawāris both narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Mukram narrated to us, Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us, Ismāʿīl al-Makkī narrated from al-Zuhrī, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Abī Saʿīd al-Khudrī, who said: \A man drank from the mouth of a waterskin"," and a small serpent entered his belly. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited the bending open of the mouths of waterskins [for drinking].\"" Ismāʿīl al-Makkī is weak in it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14669","(14663) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ al-Makkī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated from Ayyūb, from ʿIkrimah, from Abī Hurayrah, who said: \Shall I not inform you of certain matters from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): Let none of you drink from the mouth of the waterskin.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5627"," 5728]"""
"14670","(14664) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us, Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us, al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us, Sufyān narrated to us, Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī narrated to us, ʿIkrimah narrated, saying: \Shall I not inform you of certain brief matters that we heard from Abī Hurayrah?\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prohibited drinking from the mouth of the waterskin.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd Allāh from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ. It was mentioned before it.]"""
"14671","(14665) In the narration of Ismāʿīl ibn ʿUlayyah, from Ayyūb, with his chain of narration, from the Prophet ﷺ: that he forbade a man from drinking from the mouth of a waterskin. Ayyūb said: \I was informed that a man drank from the mouth of a waterskin"," and a snake came out of it.\""\n\nIt was relayed to us by ʿAlī ibn Bishrān"," who relayed to us Abū ʿAmr ibn al-Sammāk"," who narrated to us Ḥanbal"," who said: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: Ismāʿīl narrated it"," and he mentioned it.\n\nIt was also narrated by Khālid al-Ḥadhdhāʾ from ʿIkrimah"," from Ibn ʿAbbās"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14672","(14666) It was relayed to us by Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, who narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, who narrated to us Baḥr ibn Naṣr, who narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who informed me that ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī al-Zinād reported from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin and said: \Indeed"," it causes it to become foul.\""\n\nThis was narrated as a mursal (disconnected) hadith. As for that which was narrated regarding permissibility in this matter"," the narrations of prohibition are more authentic in their chains of narration. Some scholars have interpreted this prohibition as applying when the waterskin is not suspended"," so that vermin of the earth cannot enter it. We have mentioned this in the book *al-Maʿrifah* and the book *al-Jāmiʿ*. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14673","(14667) It was relayed to us by Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-ʿAlawī, who relayed to us ʿAbd Allāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Sharqī, who narrated to us ʿAbd Allāh ibn Hāshim ibn Ḥayyān, who narrated to us Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. (In another chain:) It was relayed to us by Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī, who relayed to us Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī. (In another chain:) It was relayed to us by Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān in Baghdad, who relayed to us Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār, who said: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us, who said: Sufyān narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, who heard Anas ibn Mālik say: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madīnah when I was ten years old"," and he passed away when I was twenty years old. My mothers used to urge me to serve him. The Prophet ﷺ came to our house"," and we milked for him from our domestic ewe"," and mixed it with water from a well in the house. Abū Bakr"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was on his left"," a Bedouin was on his right"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," was at one side. The Prophet ﷺ drank"," and ʿUmar"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: 'Give to Abū Bakr.' So he handed it to the Bedouin and said: 'The right side"," then the right side.'\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Saʿdān. Muslim narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others"," from Sufyān"," and both al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Mālik and others"," from al-Zuhrī. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2029]"""
"14674","(14668) It was relayed to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who informed me that Abū al-Naḍr al-Faqīh narrated to us, who said: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, who said: al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, from what he read to Mālik ibn Anas. (In another chain:) It was relayed to us by Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Faqīh, who narrated to us Abū Sahl Bishr ibn Aḥmad al-Isfarāyīnī, who narrated to us Dāwūd ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Bayhaqī, who narrated to us Qutaybah ibn Saʿīd, from Mālik, from Abū Ḥāzim, from Sahl ibn Saʿd al-Sāʿidī, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a drink, and he drank from it. On his right was a young boy, and on his left were elderly men. He said to the young boy: \Do you give me permission to give to these people?\"" The boy said: \""No"," by Allah"," I will not give preference to anyone over my share from you.\"" He said: \""So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed it in his hand.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Ibn Abī Uways"," Qutaybah"," and others"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2030]"""
"14675","(14669) It was relayed to us by Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf, who said: Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us, who said: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith narrated to us, who said: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bukayr narrated to us, who said: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abī al-Mukhtār, who said: I heard ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Awfā say: \The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey"," and the people were afflicted with thirst. He stopped at a place"," and the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ began saying: 'O Messenger of Allah"," drink! O Messenger of Allah"," drink!' He said: 'The one who serves the people drinks last. The one who serves the people drinks last.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14676","(14670) It was relayed to us by Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī, who relayed to us al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī, who relayed to us Abū Ḥātim al-Rāzī, who narrated to us ʿUbayd Allāh, who is the son of Mūsā, who informed us that Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Abī al-Mukhtār, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Awfā, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and they were afflicted with thirst. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began giving them to drink"," and it was said: 'Will you not drink"," O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'The one who serves the people drinks last.'\""\n\nWe have narrated this in the established ḥadīth from Abū Qatādah"," from the Prophet ﷺ"," in the book of *al-Ṣalāh*. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to previously]"""
"14677","(14671) It was relayed to us by Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, who relayed to us Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār al-ʿAdl, who narrated to us al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah, who narrated to us Abū Nuʿaym al-Mulāʾī, who narrated to us Sufyān, from Thawr, from Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from Abī Umāmah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \When the Prophet ﷺ raised his table spread"," he would say: 'Al-ḥamdu lillāhi kathīran ṭayyiban mubārakan fīhi"," ghayra makfiyyin wa lā muwaddaʿin wa lā mustaghnan ʿanhu"," Rabbanā' (All praise is due to Allah"," abundant"," pure"," and blessed praise"," praise that is never sufficient"," never to be abandoned"," and from which none can be independent"," our Lord).'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū Nuʿaym. Others added in it: \""ḥamdan kathīran\"" (abundant praise). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Bukhārī 5458"," 5459]"""
"14678","(14672) It was relayed to us by ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān, who relayed to us Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār, who narrated to me al-Ḥasan ibn Sahl al-Mujawwiz, who narrated to us Abū ʿĀṣim, from Thawr ibn Yazīd, who narrated to us Khālid ibn Maʿdān, from Abī Umāmah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet ﷺ, when the evening meal was removed from before him, would say: \Al-ḥamdu lillāhi ḥamdan kathīran ṭayyiban mubārakan"," ghayra makfiyyin wa lā muwaddaʿin wa lā mustaghnan ʿanhu"," Rabbanā\"" (All praise is due to Allah"," abundant"," pure"," and blessed praise"," praise that is never sufficient"," never to be abandoned"," and from which none can be independent"," our Lord).\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his *Ṣaḥīḥ* from Abū ʿĀṣim"," except that he said: \""When he finished his food.\"" He also said on another occasion: \""When he raised his table spread"," he said: 'Al-ḥamdu lillāhi alladhī kafānā wa arwānā"," ghayra makfiyyin wa lā makfūrin' (All praise is due to Allah"," who has sufficed us and quenched our thirst"," praise that is never sufficient and never to be denied).\"" He also said on another occasion: \""Laka al-ḥamdu"," Rabbanā"," ghayra makfiyyin wa lā muwaddaʿin wa lā mustaghnan ʿanhu"," Rabbanā\"" (To You is all praise"," our Lord"," praise that is never sufficient"," never to be abandoned"," and from which none can be independent"," our Lord). There are other narrations on this matter which we have mentioned in the book *al-Daʿawāt*. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to previously]"""
"14679","(14673) It was relayed to us by ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Bishrān in Baghdad, who relayed to us Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār, who narrated to us Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr, who narrated to us ʿAbd al-Razzāq, who informed us that Maʿmar narrated, from Thābit, from Anas, or someone else, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought permission to enter upon Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: \Al-salāmu ʿalaykum wa raḥmatullāh (Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah).\""\n\nSaʿd said: \""Wa ʿalayka al-salām wa raḥmatullāh (And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah)","\"" but the Prophet ﷺ did not hear it"," so he said the salām three times"," and Saʿd responded three times"," but the Prophet ﷺ did not hear him. So the Prophet ﷺ turned to leave"," and Saʿd followed him and said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," may my father be sacrificed for you"," each time you offered a salām"," I heard it with my own ears"," and I responded to you"," but I did not make you hear it"," because I wished to increase my share of your salām and blessing.\"" Then they entered the house"," and Saʿd brought near some raisins. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ ate"," and when he finished"," he said: \""The righteous have eaten your food"," the angels have sent blessings upon you"," and those who are fasting have broken their fast in your home.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14680","(14674) It was narrated by Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān al-Ḍubaʿī, who narrated to us Thābit, from Anas, who said: \The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit the Anṣār.\"" He mentioned a story regarding his entering upon Saʿd ibn ʿUbādah with the meaning of this (previous narration)"," and he did not express doubt.\n\nIt was relayed to us by Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr"," who narrated to us Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm"," who narrated to us al-Ṣaghānī"," who informed us that Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Abī al-Shawārib narrated to us"," who said: Jaʿfar ibn Sulaymān narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Referred to previously]"""
"14681","(14675) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu al-Qasim 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi informed me, Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, 'Adiyy ibn Thabit narrated to us — he said: I heard 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Ansari, who was his grandfather on his mother's side, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade plundering (al-nuhba) and mutilation (al-muthlah).\n\nNarrated by al-Bukhari in his Sahih from Adam ibn Abi Iyas. [Sahih. Bukhari 2474]"
"14682","(14676) Abu Tahir al-Faqih and Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr both narrated to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas al-Asamm narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us, Nasr ibn Hammad, Abu al-Harith al-Warraq, narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Qays ibn al-Rabi' from Abu Husayn from Khalid ibn Sa'd: that a young boy from among the scribes became proficient, so Abu Mas'ud gave orders and walnuts were purchased for his children for one dirham, and he disapproved of plundering (al-nahb). [Da'if]"
"14683","(14677) Abu Sa'd al-Malini narrated to us, Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy narrated to us, al-Saji narrated to us, Ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from Qays ibn al-Rabi' from Abu Husayn from Khalid ibn Sa'd: that Abu Mas'ud disapproved of the plundering (nihab) of boys. [Da'if]"
"14684","(14678) Abu Sa'd al-Malini narrated to us, Abu Ahmad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn 'Ali al-Maydani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us, and he mentioned it similarly, except that he said: He disapproved of the plundering (nihab) of the wedding feast.\n\n(T) And similarly Ibn Abi 'Adiyy narrated it from Shu'bah. [Da'if]"
"14685","(14679) Abu 'Amr al-Adib narrated to us, Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Bakr 'Umar ibn Sa'id al-Ta'i in Manbij narrated to us, Farj ibn Rawahah al-Ta'i al-Manbiji narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us from Jabir from 'Ata': that he disapproved of sugar being scattered (nathr). And 'Amir said: There is no harm in it. And Muhammad said: I came across righteous men who, when sugar was brought, would place it down and disapproved of scattering it. [Very Da'if]"
"14686","(14680) Abu al-Fath al-Sharif narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh narrated to us, Abu al-Qasim al-Baghawi narrated to us, 'Ali ibn al-Ja'd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us from al-Hakam, who said: I was walking between Ibrahim and al-Sha'bi when they mentioned the scattering of wedding festivities (nithar al-'urs). Ibrahim disapproved of it, while al-Sha'bi did not disapprove. [Sahih]"
"14687","(14681) He said: And Shu'bah narrated to us from Husayn from 'Ikrimah: that he disapproved of it.\n\nAnd there have been narrated regarding permissibility in this matter hadiths, all of which are weak. [Sahih]"
"14688","(14682) Among them is what Abu Sa'd al-Malini narrated to us, Abu Ahmad ibn 'Adiyy narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Uthman, the warraq of 'Abdan, narrated to us, 'Amr ibn Sa'id al-Za'farani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn 'Amr narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn 'Atiyyah narrated to us from Mansur ibn Safiyyah from his mother from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married one of his wives and dates were scattered over him.\n\nAl-Hasan ibn 'Amr is Ibn Sayf al-'Abdi, a Basran who possesses unusual narrations. [Mawdu']"
"14689","(14683) And among them is what Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami narrated to us, 'Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ka'b narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, 'Asim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Hisham ibn 'Urwah narrated to us from his father from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave in marriage or married, he would scatter dates.\n\n'Asim ibn Sulayman is a Basran whom 'Amr ibn 'Ali accused of lying and attributed to him the fabrication of hadith. [Mawdu']"
"14690","(14684) And among them is what Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Ibrahim ibn 'Ali ibn 'Urwah al-Bundar in Baghdad narrated to us, Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad al-Qattan narrated to us, Abu al-Fadl Salih ibn Muhammad al-Razi narrated to us, 'Ismah ibn Sulayman al-Khazzaz narrated to us, Lumazah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us from Thawr ibn Yazid from Khalid ibn Ma'dan from Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) attended the marriage ceremony (imlak) of a man from among his Companions and said: \Upon harmony"," auspicious omens"," and abundance in provision — may Allah bless you — beat the duff upon his head.\"" He said: So a duff was brought"," and plates containing fruits and sugar were brought"," and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Plunder it (intahibu)!\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," did you not forbid us from plundering (al-nuhbah)?\"" He said: \""I only forbade you the plundering of soldiers; as for wedding celebrations"," no.\"" He said: Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) pulled with them and they pulled with him.\n\nIn its chain there are unknown narrators and a break in the chain.\n\nAnd it has been narrated through another chain"," also containing an unknown narrator"," from 'Urwah from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) from Mu'adh ibn Jabal. And nothing is established in this matter"," and Allah knows best. [Very Da'if]"""
"14691","(14685) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī narrated to us: al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Thawr ibn Yazīd narrated from Rāshid ibn Saʿd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Luḥayy, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Qurṭ, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," the greatest of days in the sight of Allah is the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Naḥr)"," followed by the Day of al-Qarr"," which is the day that follows it.\"" He said: \""Then five or six sacrificial camels were brought before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and they began to draw near to him"," one after another"," whichever he wished to begin with. When their flanks fell (i.e."," they were slaughtered)"," he said a quiet word which I did not understand. So I said to the one sitting next to me: 'What did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say?' He said: 'Whoever wishes may proceed (with the slaughter).'\""\n\nIts chain of narration is ḥasan"," except that it differs from al-Nithār in meaning. And Allah knows best. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14692","(14686) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Aswad al-Qurashī narrated from ʿĀmir ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Zubayr, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), who said: \Announce the marriage.\""\n\nThis hadith is uniquely narrated by ʿAbd Allāh ibn al-Aswad from ʿĀmir. [Ḥasan]"""
"14693","(14687) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Mihrān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Sābiq narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \We escorted a woman of the Anṣār to her husband"," and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Was there any entertainment (lahw) with you? For indeed the Anṣār love entertainment.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Faḍl ibn Yaʿqūb from Muḥammad ibn Sābiq"," except that he said: \""A woman was escorted (to her husband).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5163]"""
"14694","(14688) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Musaddad narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated from Khālid ibn Dhakwān, from al-Rabīʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ, who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me on the morning of my wedding night and sat upon my bed as you are sitting before me. Then young girls began beating the duff and singing elegies for those of my fathers who were killed on the Day of Badr"," until one of them said: 'And among us is a Prophet who knows what is in tomorrow.' He said: 'Leave this"," and say what you were saying.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5147]"""
"14695","(14689) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb informed us: Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd that ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: \When a woman or a man was married"," young girls of the Anṣār would go out singing and playing.\"" She said: \""They passed through a gathering in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was present"," while they were singing and saying:\n\n'Her husband gifted her rams"," settled in the enclosure","\nAnd her husband among the people knows what is in tomorrow.'\n\nThe Prophet (ﷺ) came to them and said: 'Glory be to Allah! No one knows what is in tomorrow except Allah. Do not say such and such. Say instead: \""We have come to you"," we have come to you — so greet us and greet you.\""'\""\n\nThis is a good mursal hadith. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14696","(14690) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — and Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn ʿUmar ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Ḥātim ibn Abī al-Faḍl al-Harawī narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sāmī narrated to us — both saying: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways narrated to me: Abū Uways ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from ʿAmrah bint ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), the wife of the Prophet (ﷺ), that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard people singing at a wedding, and they were saying:\n\n'Her husband gifted her rams, settled in the enclosure,\nAnd your beloved among the people knows what is in tomorrow.'\n\n— or Yaḥyā said: 'And your husband among the people knows what is in tomorrow.' She said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'No one knows what is in tomorrow except Allah, glorified is He.'\\n\nIn the hadith of Abū ʿAbd Allāh"," the phrase \""or Yaḥyā said: 'And your husband among the people'\"" is not present. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14697","(14691) Abū Manṣūr ʿAbd al-Qāhir ibn Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original copy: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn Aḥmad ibn Rajāʾ al-Buzārī informed us: al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us: Abū Kāmil al-Fuḍayl ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Abū ʿAwanah narrated from al-Ajlaḥ, from Abī al-Zubayr, from Jābir, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she married off a relative of hers from the Anṣār. The Prophet (ﷺ) came and said: \Did you send the young woman (with gifts)?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Did you send someone to sing?\"" She said: \""No.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Indeed"," the Anṣār are a people among whom there is playfulness (ghazal). If only you had sent someone to say:\n\n'We have come to you"," we have come to you — so greet us and greet you.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14698","(14692) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Abī Isḥāq, who said: I heard ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd al-Bajalī say: \I was present with Thābit ibn Wadiʿah and Qurazah ibn Kaʿb al-Anṣārī at a wedding"," and there was singing. I said to them both regarding that"," and they said: 'Singing has been permitted at weddings"," and weeping over the dead without wailing (niyāḥah).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī 1221]"""
"14699","(14693) Isrāʾīl narrated it from Abī Isḥāq, as Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muqriʾ ibn al-Ḥammāmī informed us in Baghdād: Aḥmad ibn Salmān narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad narrated to us: Abū ʿĀmir al-ʿAqadī narrated to us: Isrāʾīl narrated from Abī Isḥāq, from ʿĀmir ibn Saʿd al-Bajalī, who said: \I entered upon Qurazah ibn Kaʿb and Abū Masʿūd\"" — and ʿAbd al-Malik mentioned a third person — \""and young girls were beating the duff and singing. I said: 'Do you permit this"," when you are Companions of Muḥammad (ﷺ)?' They said: 'We have been given permission in wedding celebrations and in wailing at the time of calamity.'\""\n\nSharīk narrated it with the same meaning"," and mentioned Qurazah and Abū Masʿūd"," except that he said: \""And in weeping at the time of calamity.\"" Sharīk said: \""I think he said: 'without wailing (nawḥ).'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14700","(14694) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us: Muʿallā ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us: Abū Balj narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Ḥāṭib narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \The distinction between the ḥalāl and the ḥarām is the voice (al-ṣawt) and the beating of the duff in marriage.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14701","(14695) And Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan al-Kārīzī informed us — ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us, from Abū ʿUbayd — Hushaym narrated to us, from [ʿAn], from [Fadhakarahu], except that he added: \and the duff (drum) in the marriage (nikāḥ).\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said: \""Some people have claimed that al-duff is a linguistic term"," and al-khabar is with a fatḥa. As for his statement 'al-ṣawt' (the voice)"," some people interpret it as meaning 'hearing' (samāʿ)"," and this is an error. Rather"," its meaning"," according to us"," is the public announcement of the marriage"," the raising of the voice with it"," and the mention of it among the people.\"" And ʿUmar said likewise. [Ḥasan; previously referenced.]"""
"14702","(14696) Abū Ḥāẓim al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Ḥamzah al-Harawī informed us — Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us — Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — Hushaym informed us — Yūnus ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us — al-Ḥasan narrated: \That a man married a woman in secret and used to visit her. A neighbour of hers saw him and accused him of adultery. He sought the intervention of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to him: 'Produce your evidence regarding your marriage.' He said: 'O Commander of the Faithful"," it was a minor affair; I only had her family as witnesses.' So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) averted the ḥadd punishment from the accuser and said: 'Guard the chastity of these women"," publicize this marriage"," and he has forbidden mutʿah (temporary marriage).'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14703","(14697) And Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Burshān informed us — Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us — Maʿmar informed us, from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn: \That ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him)"," whenever he heard a voice or a duff"," would say: 'What is this?' And if they said"," 'A wedding (ʿurs) or a circumcision (khitān)","' he would remain silent.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14704","(14698) As for the ḥadīth that Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh narrated to us — Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Aṣbagh narrated to us — ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Khālid ibn Iyās narrated to us, from Rabīʿah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Publicize the marriage and strike it with the duff (drum).'\""\n\nThus he said"," though it is Khālid ibn Iyās"," who is weak. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14705","(14699) And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us — ʿĪsā ibn Maymūn narrated to us, from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Publicize this marriage"," hold it in the mosques"," strike it with duffs"," and let one of you hold a wedding feast (walīmah)"," even if only with a sheep. And when one of you proposes to a woman who has dyed herself black"," let him inform her"," so that he does not deceive her.'\""\n\nʿĪsā ibn Maymūn is weak. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14706","(14700) And Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, that is al-Aṣamm, informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam informed us — Ibn Wahb informed us — Shimr ibn Numayr al-Amawī narrated to me — Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib (may Allah be pleased with him): \That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions passed by Banū Zurayq and heard singing and playing. He said: 'What is this?' They said: 'The marriage (nikāḥ) of so-and-so"," O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'This is the marriage that completes the religion — not fornication (sifāḥ)"," nor secret marriage — until a duff is heard or smoke is seen.'\""\n\nḤusayn said: And ʿAmr ibn Yaḥyā al-Māzinī narrated to me: \""That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to dislike secret marriage until the duff was struck for it.\"" Ḥusayn ibn ʿAbd Allāh is weak. [Mawḍūʿ]"""
"14707","(14701) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both informed us — they said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Kathīr narrated to us — Sufyān informed us, from Ismāʿīl ibn Umayyah, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUrwah, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) married me in Shawwāl and consummated the marriage with me in Shawwāl. Which of his women was more favoured by him than I?\"" And he (peace and blessings be upon him) used to prefer that his wives be consummated with in Shawwāl.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Wakīʿ"," from Sufyān. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Muslim 1423]"""
"14708","(14702) Abū ʿAmr al-Adīb informed us — Abū Bakr al-Ismāʿīlī informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn Hāshim informed us — Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to us — ʿAbd al-Wārith narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Ṣuhayb, from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him): \That the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw women and children returning from a wedding feast. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up before them and said: 'O Allah"," you are the most beloved of people to me.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Mubārak and others"," from ʿAbd al-Wārith."""
"14709","(14703) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — ʿĀrim narrated to us —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us — Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us — Abū al-Rabīʿ narrated to us — they both said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyūb, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'All of you are shepherds"," and all of you shall be asked. The amīr is a shepherd over the people and shall be asked. A man is a shepherd over his family and shall be asked. A woman is a shepherdess over her husband's house and shall be asked. A slave is a shepherd over his master's wealth and shall be asked. Indeed"," all of you are shepherds"," and all of you shall be asked.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿĀrim"," that is Abū al-Nuʿmān"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ; al-Bukhārī 893]"""
"14710","(14704) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us — Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā al-Bazzāz narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Marwazī narrated to us — al-Naḍr ibn Shumayl informed us — Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, from Abū Salamah, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Were I to command anyone to prostrate to anyone"," I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband"," due to the magnitude of the right that Allah has established for him over her.'\"" [Ṣaḥīgh li-ghayrihi]"""
"14711","(14705) Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmish al-Ziyadī informed us — Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan narrated to us — Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us — Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Nakha'i narrated to us — my father narrated to us — Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami narrated from Amir al-Sha'bi from Qays, who said: I came to al-Hirah and saw its people prostrating to their marzuban (governor). I said, \We had more right to prostrate to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ).\"" When I came to him"," I informed him of what I had seen. I said"," \""We had more right to prostrate to you.\"" He said"," \""Do not do that. Tell me"," if you were to pass by my grave"," would you prostrate?\"" I said"," \""No.\"" He said"," \""Then do not do that. Were I to command anyone to prostrate to another"," I would command the wives to prostrate to their husbands"," due to the rights Allah has placed upon them regarding them.\"""""
"14712","(14706) Abu Abd al-Hafiz informed us — Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih informed me — Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us — al-Humaydi narrated to us — Sufyan narrated from Yahya ibn Said from Bushayr ibn Yasar from Husayn ibn Mihsan, who said: My paternal aunt narrated to me, saying: I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) for some need, and he said, \O you"," do you have a husband?\"" I said"," \""Yes.\"" He said"," \""How are you towards him?\"" She said"," \""I do not fall short except in that which I am unable to do.\"" He said"," \""Then where do you stand in relation to him? For he is your Paradise and your Hellfire.\"""""
"14713","(14707) Abu Abd al-Hafiz informed us — Hasan ibn Ya'qub al-Adl informed us — Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Farra' informed us — Ja'far ibn Aw narrated to us — Rabi'ah ibn Uthman narrated from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban from Nahar al-Abdi, who was among the companions of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri — from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A man came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with his daughter and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," this daughter of mine refuses to marry.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said to her"," \""Obey your father.\"" She said"," \""By the One Who sent you with the truth"," I will not marry until you inform me of the right of the husband over his wife.\"" He said"," \""The right of the husband over his wife is such that if she had a wound and she licked it"," she would not have fulfilled his right.\"""""
"14714","(14708) Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn Ubayd al-Saffar informed us — Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi and Umar ibn Umar said — Musaddad narrated to us — Abu Awanah narrated from al-A'mash from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a man calls his wife to his bed and she refuses"," and he spends the night angry"," the angels curse her until morning.\"""""
"14715","(14709) Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Furak informed us — Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Shu'bah narrated from Qatadah from Zurarah ibn Awfa from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \When a woman spends the night away from her husband's bed"," the angels curse her until she returns.\"""""
"14716","(14710) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us — Mulazim ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us — Abd Allah ibn Badr narrated from Qays ibn Talq from his father, Talq ibn Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) say: \When a man calls his wife to his need"," let her respond to him"," even if she is upon the oven.\"""""
"14717","(14711) Abu al-Hasan al-Muqri' al-Isfara'ini informed us — al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us — Yusuf ibn Ya'qub narrated to us — Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us — Hammad ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyub from al-Qasim al-Shaybani from Abd Allah ibn Abi Awfa, who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Syria and saw its people prostrating to their patricians and bishops. He thought to himself that he would do the same for the Prophet (ﷺ). When he arrived, he prostrated to the Prophet (ﷺ), who disapproved of that. He said, \O Messenger of Allah"," I came to Syria and saw them prostrating to their patricians and bishops"," and I thought to myself that I would do that to you.\"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"," \""Were I to command anyone to prostrate to another"," I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul"," a woman does not fulfill the right of her Lord"," the Mighty and Majestic"," until she fulfills the entirety of her husband's right — so much so that if he asks of her while she is upon a saddle"," she would grant it to him\"" — or he said"," \""she would not refuse him.\"""""
"14718","(14712) Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ruzjahi informed us — Abu Bakr al-Isma'ili informed me — al-Hasan ibn Sufyan narrated to us — Hibban ibn Musa informed us — Abd Allah informed us — Ma'mar narrated from Hammad ibn Munabih from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \A woman should not fast while her husband is present except with his permission"," and she should not permit anyone into his house while he is present except with his permission. Whatever she spends from his earnings without his command"," half of the reward is for him.\"""""
"14719","(14713) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us — Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us — Abu Dawud narrated to us — Jarir narrated from Layth from Ata' from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \A woman came to him and said"," 'What is the right of the husband over his wife?' He said"," 'She should not refuse him herself"," even if she is upon the back of a saddle"," and she should not give anything from his house except with his permission. If she does that"," the reward is for her and the sin is upon her. She should not fast a day voluntarily except with his permission. If she does that"," she sins and is not rewarded. She should not leave his house except with his permission. If she does that"," the angels curse her — the angels of wrath and the angels of mercy — until she repents or returns.' It was said"," 'Even if he is unjust?' He said"," 'Even if he is unjust.'\"""""
"14720","(14714) Abu Tahir al-Faqih informed us — Abu Bakr al-Qattan informed us — Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Razin al-Sulami narrated us — Bishr ibn Abi al-Azhar narrated us — Hushaym narrated from Layth from Mujahid from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: A woman came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," what is the right of the husband over his wife?\"" He said"," \""That she not refuse him herself"," even if she is upon a saddle. If she does that"," there is sin upon her.\"" She said"," \""What is the right of the husband over his wife?\"" He said"," \""That she not give anything from his house except with his permission.\"""""
"14721","(14715) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub al-Amawi and Abu 'Abdillah 'Ali ibn 'Abdillah al-Hakimi in Baghdad narrated to us, both saying: al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim al-Duri narrated to us; Bishr ibn 'Umar al-Zahrani narrated to us; Shu'aib ibn Ruzayq al-Ta'ifi narrated to us; 'Ata' al-Khurasani narrated from Malik ibn Yukhamir al-Sakasi from Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to permit anyone into her husband's house while he is displeased"," nor to leave it while he is displeased"," nor to obey anyone against him"," nor to harden her heart against him"," nor to forsake his bed"," nor to sever ties with him. If he is more oppressive than she"," let her come to him until she pleases him. If he accepts from her"," then it is well and good"," and Allah will accept her excuse and make her argument prevail"," and there will be no sin upon her. But if he refuses to be pleased with her"," then she has conveyed her excuse before Allah.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14722","(14716) Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Dawud al-'Alawi (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Baluwayh al-Muzakki narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar narrated from Hammam ibn Munabbih, who said: \This is what Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us"," saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'The best women are those who ride camels — the women of Quraysh. They are the most tender toward their children in their youth and the most watchful over their husband's property.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Muhammad ibn Rafi' from 'Abd al-Razzaq"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah. [Sahih]"""
"14723","(14717) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hanbal narrated to me; my father said; and Abu 'Amr ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to me; 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Abu Kurayb narrated to us, both saying: Abu Usamah narrated from Hisham; my father narrated to me from Asma' bint Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said: \Al-Zubayr married me"," and he had no wealth"," no slave"," and nothing except his horse. So I used to feed his horse"," tend to it"," groom it"," crush date-stones for his water-drawing camel"," draw water"," and stitch his water-skin. I used to knead dough"," but I was not good at baking"," so some Ansari women who were righteous would bake for me. I used to carry the date-stones from the land that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had granted to al-Zubayr"," on my head"," and it was a distance of two-thirds of a farsakh. One day I came with the date-stones on my head and met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) with a group of his Companions. He called out to me and said: 'Ikh"," ikh!' — meaning to carry me behind him. I felt shy and I knew his sense of honour (ghayrah). He said: 'By Allah"," your carrying the load on your head is harder for you than riding with me.' This continued until Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) sent me a servant who took over the care of the horse"," and it was as though he had set me free.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Abu Kurayb"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from Mahmud from Abu Usamah. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"14724","(14718) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated from al-Hakam from Ibn Abi Layla — Sulayman said, I think he said — from 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) complained about the effect of the hand-mill on her hand. She went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to ask him for a servant"," but she did not find him. She mentioned this to 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came"," she mentioned it to him. He came to us when we had taken our beds"," and I started to get up"," but he said: 'Stay where you are.' Then he sat between us until I felt the coolness of his feet on my chest. He said: 'Shall I not direct you to something better for you than a servant? When you take your beds"," glorify Allah thirty-three times"," praise Him thirty-three times"," and magnify Him thirty-four times. That is better for you than a servant.' Khalid narrated from Ibn Sirin that the glorification (tasbih) was thirty-four times.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Sulayman ibn Harb without mentioning the doubt"," and Muslim narrated it through other chains from Shu'bah. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"14725","(14719) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad al-Muqri' narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Salman al-Faqih narrated to us; Ishaq ibn al-Hasan ibn Maymun narrated to us; al-Qa'nabi narrated from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from 'Ata' ibn Yasar from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), in the story of the eclipse: \I was shown the Fire"," and I have never seen a more terrible sight than today. And I saw that most of its inhabitants were women.\"" They said: \""Why"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Because of their ingratitude (kufr).\"" It was said: \""Do they disbelieve in Allah"," Mighty and Majestic?\"" He said: \""They are ungrateful to their husbands and ungrateful for kindness. If you were to do good to one of them for a lifetime and then she saw something from you"," she would say: 'I have never seen any good from you at all.'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from al-Qa'nabi"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Malik. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"14726","(14720) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Hamdani al-Marwazi narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us; Shaddad ibn Fayyad narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated from Qatadah from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Allah will not look with mercy upon a woman who is ungrateful to her husband while she is not independent of him.\"" This is how it was narrated as a marfu' (elevated) hadith"," but the correct view is that it is a statement of 'Abdullah"," not elevated. [Sahih]"""
"14727","(14721) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Isbahani narrated to us by dictation, both saying: Abu Muhammad 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Fakihi in Makkah narrated to us; Abu Yahya ibn Abi Masarra narrated to us; Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Nafi' al-Makki narrated from al-Hasan ibn Muslim from Safiyyah from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \A woman from the Ansar married off her daughter. The daughter fell ill and her hair fell out. She brought her to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and mentioned this to him. She said: 'Her husband has ordered me to attach hair extensions to her hair.' He said: 'No. Indeed"," those who attach hair extensions have been cursed.'\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Khallad ibn Yahya. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"14728","(14722) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Harun ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us; Husayn ibn 'Ali narrated from Zaidah from Maisarah from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"," if he witnesses a matter"," let him speak good or remain silent. Treat women well"," for indeed woman was created from a rib"," and the most crooked part of the rib is its uppermost part. If you try to straighten it"," you will break it"," and if you leave it"," it will remain crooked.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in his Sahih from Ishaq ibn Nasr from Husayn al-Ju'fi"," and Muslim narrated it from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah from Husayn. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"14729","(14723) Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad and Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Abu al-Zinad from al-A'raj from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Indeed"," woman was created from a rib. She will never be straight for you in any way. If you enjoy her"," you enjoy her while there is crookedness in her. And if you try to straighten her"," you will break her"," and breaking her is her divorce.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from Ibn Abi 'Umar"," and al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Malik from Abu al-Zinad. [Sahih — agreed upon]"""
"14730","(14724) Abu 'Abdillah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu 'Abdillah Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; my father narrated to us; 'Amr ibn Zurarah narrated to us; Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated from his father from Jabir, in the story of the Hajj of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and his sermon at 'Arafah, who said: \The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Fear Allah regarding women"," for indeed you have taken them as a trust from Allah"," and you have made their private parts lawful to you by the word of Allah. And upon you is the right that they do not allow anyone onto your bedding whom you dislike. If they do so"," then strike them with a strike that is not severe. And upon you is their provision and their clothing in a fair manner.'\"" Muslim narrated it in his Sahih from the hadith of Hatim ibn Isma'il. [Sahih — Muslim 1218]"""
"14731","(14725) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf narrated to us; ʿUmar ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Ruzayn narrated to us; Sufyān narrated verbatim from Dāwūd al-Warrāq from Saʿīd ibn Ḥakīm from his father from his grandfather Muʿāwiya ibn Ḥaydah al-Qushayrī, who said:\n\nI came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when I was brought before him, he said: \I asked Allah"," the Mighty and Glorious"," to grant me victory over you through famine that would destroy you"," and through terror that He would place in your hearts.\"" He said: \""So I came before him with both my hands and said: 'I have sworn such and such that I would not believe in you nor follow you.' Famine continued to ravage me and terror was placed in my heart until I stood before you. I swear by Allah"," who has sent you — is it He who has sent you with what you say?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'And has He commanded you with what you command us?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What do you say about our women?' He said: 'They are your tilth; come to your tilth as you wish"," and feed them from what you eat"," and clothe them from what you wear"," and do not strike them"," and do not revile them.' He said: 'Can one of us look at the private parts of his brother when we are gathered?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'And when we are apart?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then placed one of his thighs upon the other and said: 'Allah has more right that you should feel shame before Him.'\""\n\nHe said: \""And I heard him say: 'Mankind will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection with their faces covered"," and the first part of a person to speak will be his hand and his thigh.'\"" [Weak]"""
"14732","(14726) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us; Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us; Shuʿbah informed us from Abū Qazaʿah from Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiya from his father, that a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \What is the right of a woman over her husband?\"" He said: \""That he feed her when he eats"," and clothe her when he clothes himself"," and that he not forsake her except within the house"," and that he not strike the face"," and that he not revile her.\"" [Good]"""
"14733","(14727) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Tamīm al-Qanṭarī in Baghdād narrated to us; Abū Qilābah narrated to us; ʿAbdullāh ibn Ḥumrān narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbdillāh informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq al-Faqīh, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīh al-Muzakkī informed us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us; Abū ʿĀṣim narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us; ʿImrān ibn Abī Anas narrated to us from ʿUmar ibn al-Ḥakam from Abū Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said:\n\nThe Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Let no believing man hate a believing woman; if he dislikes one of her traits"," he will be pleased with another.\""\n\nThe wording of both their narrations is the same. Ibn al-Muthannā said: \""Al-Fark means hatred.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā. [Authentic. Muslim 1469]"""
"14734","(14728) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Muḥammad ibn Mūsā ibn al-Faḍl informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Wakīʿ informed us from Bashīr ibn Muhājir from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said:\n\n\I love to adorn myself for the woman just as I love her to adorn herself for me"," because Allah"," the Mighty and Glorious"," says: **'And they (women) have rights similar to those (of men) over them in kindness'** (2:228). And I do not love to exact all my rights over her"," because Allah"," the Mighty and Glorious"," says: **'And men have a degree over them (women)'** (2:228).\"" [Authentic]"""
"14735","(14729) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Abī Ṭālib and ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, saying: Isḥāq informed us; Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us; Hishām ibn ʿUrwah narrated to us from his father from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, regarding His statement: **'If a woman fears ill-conduct or aversion from her husband'** (4:128):\n\nShe said: \This was revealed concerning a woman who is with a man from whom she does not ask for much"," but he wishes to divorce her and marry another woman. So she says: 'Do not divorce me"," and keep me"," and you are free from the obligation of maintenance and a share of my time.' So Allah"," the Mighty and Glorious"," revealed: **'There is no blame on them both if they reconcile between themselves with reconciliation'** (4:128).\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Salām from Abū Muʿāwiyah"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hishām. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"14736","(14730) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Ibn ʿUyaynah informed us from al-Zuhrī from Ibn al-Musayyab that the daughter of Muḥammad ibn Salamah was with Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj. He disliked something about her — either old age or something else — and intended to divorce her. She said: \Do not divorce me"," and allocate for me whatever share you wish.\"" So Allah"," the Mighty and Glorious"," revealed: **'If a woman fears ill-conduct or aversion from her husband'** (4:128). [Authentic]"""
"14737","(14731) Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us; Abū Muḥammad Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Muzanī informed us; ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿĪsā narrated to us; Abū al-Yamān informed us; Shuʿayb ibn Abī Ḥamzah informed us from al-Zuhrī; Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Sulaymān ibn Yasār informed us that the established practice (sunnah) regarding these two verses in which Allah, the Mighty and Glorious, mentions the man's ill-conduct and aversion toward his wife — in His statement: **'If a woman fears ill-conduct or aversion from her husband'** (4:128) through the end of the two verses — is that when a man is averse to his wife and gives preference to another over her, it is his right to offer her the choice: either he divorces her, or she remains with him despite the preference he gives to another in the division of his time and his wealth. If she remains with him on that basis and does not wish him to divorce her, then there is no blame upon him for the preference he gives to another. If he does not offer her divorce and instead reconciles with her by giving her from his wealth what pleases her, and she remains with him despite the preference in the division of his wealth and his time, then that is permissible for him, and their reconciliation on that basis is valid.\n\nSaʿīd ibn al-Musayyab and Sulaymān mentioned the reconciliation of which Allah, the Mighty and Glorious, said: **'There is no blame on them both if they reconcile between themselves with reconciliation, and reconciliation is better'** (4:128). And it has been mentioned to me that Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj al-Anṣārī, who was among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, had a wife. When she grew old, he married a young virgin girl and gave preference to the young girl over her. She asked him for a divorce, so he divorced her with one divorce. Then he waited until she was nearly free (from her waiting period), then took her back. Then he again gave preference to the young girl over her, so she asked him for a divorce, and he divorced her with a second divorce. Then he waited until she was nearly free, then took her back. Then he again gave preference to the young girl over her, so she asked him for a divorce. He said to her: \It is as you wish; only one divorce remains for you. If you wish"," you may remain with me despite the preference you see"," and if you wish"," I will separate from you.\"" She said: \""No"," rather I will remain with me despite the preference.\"" So he kept her on that basis"," and that was their reconciliation. Rāfiʿ did not consider it a sin when she was content to remain with him despite the preference he gave to the other. [Authentic]"""
"14738","(14732) Abū Zakariyyā narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us; al-Rabīʿ informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Muslim informed us from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Prophet ﷺ passed away leaving nine wives, and he used to divide his time among eight of them. [Authentic]"
"14739","(14733) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Muḥammad al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Ḥalīm al-Marwazī narrated to us; Abū al-Muwajjah informed us; ʿAbdān informed us; ʿAbdullāh informed us; Yūnus informed us from al-Zuhrī; ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said:\n\nWhen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. Whosever lot came out, he would take her with him. And he used to allocate to each of them her day and her night, except that Sawdah ibn Zamʿah gave her day and her night to ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, seeking thereby the pleasure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Muqātil and Ḥibbān from Ibn al-Mubārak. [Authentic. Bukhārī]"
"14740","(14734) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Walīd informed me; al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us; ʿUqbah ibn Khālid narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said:\n\nWhen Sawdah bint Zamʿah, may Allah be pleased with her, grew old, she gave her day to ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would allocate for ʿĀʾishah the day of Sawdah as well.\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah, and al-Bukhārī narrated it through another chain from Hishām. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"
"14741","(14735) Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated from Simak ibn Harb — I think he said — from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) feared that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) might divorce her, so she said: \O Messenger of Allah"," do not divorce me; rather keep me with you and assign my day to 'Aishah.\"" So he did that. Then this verse was revealed: {And if a woman fears ill-treatment or desertion from her husband} (al-Nisa' 128). He said: Whatever they agree upon between themselves is permissible. [Hasan due to supporting narrations]"""
"14742","(14736) Abu Nasr 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn 'Umar ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu Mansur al-'Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Nadrawi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, who said: This verse was revealed concerning Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) and those like her: {And if a woman fears ill-treatment or desertion from her husband} (al-Nisa' 128). That was because Sawdah (may Allah be pleased with her) had become an elderly woman and feared that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) might separate from her. She was reluctant to give up her position with him, and she knew of the Messenger of Allah's love for 'Aishah and her status with him. So she gifted her day with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to 'Aishah (may Allah be pleased with her), and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) accepted that.\n\nAhmad ibn Yunus also narrated it from Ibn Abi al-Zinad, connected (mawṣūl), as was mentioned previously at the beginning of the Book of Marriage. [Hasan due to supporting narrations]"
"14743","(14737) Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated us: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated us: Adam ibn Iyas narrated us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Simak ibn Harb, from Khalid ibn 'Ar'arah, who said: I heard 'Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) say regarding the words of Allah: {And if a woman fears ill-treatment or desertion from her husband, there is no blame on them if they arrange an arbitration between themselves} (al-Nisa' 128). He said: It refers to a man who has two wives, one of whom has grown old or is unattractive, and he wishes to separate from her. So she makes an arrangement with him that he will spend one night with her and two nights with the other, and that he will not divorce her. Whatever she consents to is permissible. But if she later changes her mind, he should restore equality between them. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14744","(14738) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Faqih narrated us: Ja'far ibn Abi 'Uthman al-Tayalisi narrated us: 'Affan, Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, and Muhammad ibn Sinan al-'Awfi narrated — and Abu Bakr ibn Furak informed us: 'Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud informed us: Hammam narrated from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever has two wives and inclines toward one of them will come on the Day of Resurrection with one side of his body fallen.\""\n\nIn the narration of 'Affan"," it reads: \""inclined\"" (mā'il). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14745","(14739) Abu Sa'id ibn Abi 'Amr narrated to us: Abu al-'Abbas al-Aṣamm informed us: al-Rabi' informed us: al-Shafi'i said: I heard some of the people of knowledge say, the meaning of which is as follows: You will never be able to achieve justice in what is in your hearts, so do not incline with total inclination. Do not let your desires dictate your actions, lest the inclination through action become something not permissible for you, leaving her like a suspended woman (al-mu'allaqah). What they have said, in my view, is consistent with what they have said, because Allah, the Most High, has pardoned what is in the hearts and has held people accountable for actions and statements. So if one inclines through speech and action, that is total inclination. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Al-Shafi'i said this in al-Umm 5/111]"
"14746","(14740) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq al-Muzakki informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdus narrated us: 'Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated us: 'Abdullah ibn Salih narrated from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), regarding the words of Allah, the Most High: {You will never be able to do justice between your wives, even if it is your ardent desire} (al-Nisa' 129). He said: It refers to love and sexual relations. [Ḍa'īf]"
"14747","(14741) Through this same chain of narration from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: You will not be able to do justice among them, even if you strive — and that is His words: {And the souls are swayed by greed} (al-Nisa' 129). Greed here refers to one's desire for something, for which one strives. Then He said: {So do not incline with total inclination, leaving her like one suspended} (al-Nisa' 129). He said: You leave her neither a divorced woman nor one with a husband. [Ḍa'īf]"
"14748","(14742) Abu Nasr ibn Qatadah informed us: Abu Mansur al-Nadrawi informed us: Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated us: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated us: Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated from Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, who said: I asked 'Ubaydah about the words of Allah: {You will never be able to do justice between your wives, even if it is your ardent desire} (al-Nisa' 129). He gestured with his hand toward his chest and said: It refers to love and sexual relations. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14749","(14743) Abu 'Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi narrated us: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn narrated us: Adam ibn Iyas narrated us: Warqa' narrated from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, regarding this verse, meaning regarding love: {So do not incline with total inclination} (al-Nisa' 129). He said: Do not deliberately intend wrongdoing. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Without his words \meaning regarding love\""]"""
"14750","(14744) Abu al-Husayn ibn Bashran al-'Adl in Baghdad informed us: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Razzaz narrated us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Shakir narrated us: 'Affan narrated to us: Hammam, Hammad, Aban, and Abu 'Awanah — all of them narrated to me from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Indeed"," Allah"," the Most High"," has pardoned my ummah for what their souls whisper to them"," so long as they do not speak of it or act upon it.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the hadith of Abu 'Awanah"," and both al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it through other routes from Qatadah.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And it has reached us that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to divide and do justice"," then he would say: \""O Allah"," this is my division in that over which I have control"," and You know best that over which I have no control.\"" He meant — and Allah knows best — the state of his heart. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 127]"""
"14751","(14745) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Saffar informed us; Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated from Ayyub, from Qilabah, from 'Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to divide [his time] and act justly, and he would say: \O Allah"," this is my division in that over which I have control"," so do not blame me for that over which You have control and I have no control.\""\n\nAl-Qadi said: He meant the heart"," and this refers to justice among his wives.\n\nAl-Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And it has reached us that he used to be carried"," during his illness"," to his wives until they granted him permission [to remain with one]."""
"14752","(14746) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha'rani narrated to us; my grandfather narrated to us; Ibn Abi Uways narrated to me; Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah; my father informed me from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to ask during his illness in which he passed away: \Where shall I be tomorrow? Where shall I be tomorrow?\"" — meaning the day of 'A'ishah. So his wives granted him permission to be wherever he wished. Thus he was in the house of 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) until he passed away in her presence (peace and blessings be upon him).\n\nAl-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ibn Abi Uways"," and Muslim narrated it through another chain from Hisham."""
"14753","(14747) Abu 'Ali al-Rudhbari informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Dasah narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Musaddad narrated to us; Mahrum ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-'Attar narrated to me; Abu 'Imran al-Jawni narrated from Yazid ibn Babanus, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent for the women during his illness. They gathered, and he said: \I am no longer able to rotate among you. If you permit me to be with 'A'ishah"," do so.\"" So they granted him permission.\n\nAl-Shafi'i said: And it has reached me that he was asked: \""Who among people is most beloved to you?\"" and he said: \""'A'ishah.\"""""
"14754","(14748) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us; Isma'il ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Khalid ibn 'Abd Allah narrated from Khalid, from Abu 'Uthman; 'Amr ibn al-'As (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent him with the army of Dhat al-Salasil. He said: \I came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," who among people is most beloved to you?' He said: ''A'ishah.' I said: 'Among men?' He said: 'Her father.' I said: 'Then who?' He said: 'Umar.' Then he enumerated several men.\"" Others said: \""Then 'Umar\"" [using the word thumma].\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Yahya ibn Yahya"," and al-Bukhari narrated it through another chain from Khalid al-Hadha'.\n\nAnd there has preceded in the first book of al-Nikah the hadith of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)"," where he said to his daughter Hafsah: \""Let it not deceive you that your neighbor is more beautiful and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) than you\"" — meaning 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her)."""
"14755","(14749) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us; al-'Abbas: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mahbubi, and Abu Bakr: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Darabirdi, and Abu Muhammad: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Halimi in Marw said: Abu al-Muwajjih: Muhammad ibn 'Amr al-Fazari informed us; 'Abd ibn 'Uthman informed us; 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak informed us; Yunus narrated from al-Zuhri; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham informed me that 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), while he was lying with 'A'ishah in her blanket. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) granted her permission [to enter]. She said: \O Messenger of Allah"," your wives have sent me to you"," asking you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah.\"" She ['A'ishah] said: \""And I was silent.\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Do you not love what I love?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then love this one.\"" She said: Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) stood up when she heard that from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," and returned to them and informed them of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had said to her. They said to her: \""You have not accomplished anything for us. Go back to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and say to him: 'Your wives ask you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah.'\"" She said: \""By Allah"," I will never speak to him about it again.\"" 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: The wives of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) then sent Zaynab bint Jahsh"," the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)"," who was the one among them who rivaled me [in status]. But I have not seen any woman better in religion than Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her) — more God-fearing"," more truthful in speech"," more dutiful to kin"," more generous in charity"," and more devoted in expending herself in deeds by which she gave charity and sought nearness to Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," except for a sharpness in her tongue that she was quick to set aside. She said: She sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)"," while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was with 'A'ishah in her blanket"," in the same position in which Fatimah had entered. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) granted her permission. She said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," your wives have sent me to you"," asking you for justice regarding the daughter of Abu Quhafah.\"" She said: Then she attacked me and spoke harshly against me"," while I was watching the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and watching his eye — whether he would permit me [to respond]. She said: Zaynab bint Jahsh did not cease until I knew that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would not dislike my defending myself. She said: When I fell upon her"," I did not hesitate to rebuke her for it. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said"," smiling: \""She is the daughter of Abu Bakr.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Our Shaykh did not preserve this exact wording"," and perhaps the correct wording is: \""I overwhelmed her decisively.\""\n\nIn another narration: \""I turned upon her.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Quhzad from 'Abd."""
"14756","(14750) Abu Muhammad: 'Abd Allah ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Sa'id ibn al-A'rabi narrated to us; Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah narrated from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal ibn 'Amr, from 'Abbad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Asadi, who said: 'Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When a free woman is married [alongside] a slave woman, then for this one [the free woman] are two days and for this one [the slave woman] is one day."
"14757","(14751) And Abu Muhammad informed us; Abu Sa'id narrated to us; Sa'dan narrated to us; Sufyan narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, a similar narration."
"14758","(14752) And Sulayman ibn Yasar said: It is from the Sunnah that when a free woman is married [alongside a slave woman], then for the free woman are two days and for the slave woman is one day.\n\nAbu Hazim al-Hafiz informed us; Abu al-Fadl ibn Khamiruyah narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Najdah narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to me; my father narrated from Sulayman ibn Yasar, and he mentioned it."
"14759","(14753) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu al-Hasan: 'Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us; Musa ibn al-Hasan, and Muhammad ibn Ghalib, and Muhammad ibn 'Ali ibn But-han said: Faffan narrated to us.\n\n(And) Abu 'Abd Allah informed me; Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Bukhari narrated to us; Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Habib al-Hafiz narrated to us; 'Abd Allah ibn Abi Shaybah and Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us; Faffan narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us; Thabit narrated from Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: I attended the wedding feast of Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her), and he fed the people abundantly with bread and meat. He used to send me to invite the people. When he finished, he stood, and I followed him. Two men lingered, engaged in conversation, and did not leave. He began to pass by his wives and greet each one of them: \Peace be upon you"," O people of the house. How are you?\"" They would say: \""Well"," O Messenger of Allah. How did you find your family?\"" He would say: \""Well.\"" When he finished"," he returned"," and I returned with him. When he reached the door"," there were the two men who had lingered in conversation. When they saw that he had returned"," they stood and left. By Allah"," I do not know whether I informed him or revelation came to him that they had left. He returned"," and I returned with him. When he placed his feet at the threshold of the door"," he drew the curtain between me and him"," and this verse was revealed: \""Do not enter the houses of the Prophet…\"" [the verse].\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Sahih from Abi Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah."""
"14760","(14754) Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq al-Faqih narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Ziyad narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated from Hisham ibn 'Urwah, from his father, from 'A'ishah (may Allah be pleased with her), that she said to him: \O son of my sister"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not favor any of us over another in his staying with us"," and there was scarcely a day except that he would visit all of us"," approaching each woman without touching her"," until he reached the one whose day it was"," and he would spend the night with her.\"" And he mentioned the remainder of the hadith."""
"14761","(14755) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, 'Ubayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us, Ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Abī az-Zinād narrated to us from Hishām ibn 'Urwah from his father from 'Ā'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \There was no day"," or rarely a day"," except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would visit all of us"," kissing and touching [us] short of intercourse. Then"," when it came to the one whose day it was"," he would spend the night with her.\"" [Weak]"""
"14762","(14756) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, ar-Rabī' ibn Sulaymān informed us, ash-Shāfi'ī informed us, Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb ash-Shaybānī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn 'Amr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us, al-Qa'nabī narrated to us, Mālik narrated to us from 'Abdillāh ibn Abī Bakr from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abī Bakr from Abī Bakr ibn 'Abd ar-Raḥmān: that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah and she came to be in his household, he said to her: \There is no disgrace upon you in the eyes of your family. If you wish"," I shall stay with you for seven [nights] and divide equally among them for seven [nights]; and if you wish"," I shall stay with you for three [nights] and then rotate.\"" She said: \""Then [stay for] three.\""\n\nAnd in the narration of ash-Shāfi'ī: \""I shall stay with you for three [nights] and then rotate.\"" She said: \""Then [stay for] three.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā from Mālik. [Authentic. Muslim 1460]"""
"14763","(14757) Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū 'Abdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn 'Amr al-Ḥarashī narrated to us, al-Qa'nabī narrated to us, Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to us from 'Abd ar-Raḥmān ibn Ḥumayd from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abī Bakr from Abī Bakr ibn 'Abd ar-Raḥmān: that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah and came to her, and he wished to leave, she grabbed his garment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \If you wish"," I shall increase your stay and account it for you — for the virgin"," seven [nights]"," and for the previously married woman"," three [nights].\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Qa'nabī. Thus they both narrated it from 'Abd al-Malik as a mursal [narration]"," and Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated it from 'Abd al-Malik as a mawṣūl [narration]. [Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14764","(14758) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī narrated to us, Mu'ādh ibn al-Muthannā narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) He said, and Ibn Ḥanbal informed me, my father narrated to me. He said, and 'Ubayd ibn Ghannām narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us. They all said: Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd narrated to us, ath-Thawrī narrated to me, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to me from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abī Bakr ibn 'Abd ar-Raḥmān from his father from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her: that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her, he stayed with her for three days and said: \There is no disgrace upon you in the eyes of your family. If you wish"," I shall stay with you for seven [nights]"," and if I stay with you for seven [nights]"," I shall [likewise] stay with my wives for seven [nights].\""\n\nSulaymān said: \""No one narrated this ḥadīth with a refined isnād from Sufyān except Yaḥyā ibn Sa'īd al-Qaṭṭān.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Yaḥyā. Similarly"," 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Ayman narrated it from Abī Bakr ibn 'Abd ar-Raḥmān as a mawṣūl [narration]. [Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14765","(14759) Abū Muḥammad 'Abdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Abū 'Abdillāh Muḥammad ibn Yazīd and Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn 'Īsā both said: Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Sufyān narrated to us, Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to me, Abū Kurayb Muḥammad ibn al-'Alā' narrated to us, Ḥafṣ — meaning Ibn Ghiyāth — narrated to us from 'Abd al-Wāḥid ibn Ayman from Abī Bakr ibn 'Abd ar-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām from Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, who mentioned: that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her, and he mentioned various things in it, saying: \If you wish"," I shall stay with you for seven [nights] and stay with my wives for seven [nights]; and if I stay with you for seven [nights]"," I shall stay with my wives for seven [nights].\""\n\nThus Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ. [Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14766","(14760) Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq aṣ-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Rūḥ ibn 'Ubādah narrated to us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd aṣ-Ṣaffār narrated to us, al-Ḥārith ibn Abī Usāmah narrated to us, Rūḥ narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit narrated to us that 'Abd al-Ḥamīd ibn 'Abdillāh ibn Abī 'Amr and al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abd ar-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām both informed him that they heard Abī Bakr ibn 'Abd ar-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām narrating: that Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, informed him that when she arrived in Madīnah, they were told that she was the daughter of Abī Umayyah ibn al-Mughīrah, but they denied it, saying: \How deceitful the strangers are!\"" Until a group of them went for Ḥajj and said: \""Write to your family.\"" So she wrote with them"," and when they returned to Madīnah"," they confirmed her [claim]"," and her status among them increased. She said: \""When I gave birth to Zaynab"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and proposed to me. I said: 'One like me is not married — I have no child in me"," and I am a jealous woman with dependents.' He said: 'I am older than you. As for jealousy"," Allah will remove it. As for the dependents"," they are for Allah and His Messenger.' So he married her and would come to her saying: 'How is Zaynab? Where is Zaynab?' Then 'Ammār ibn Yāsir came and startled her"," saying: 'This one is preventing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!' She was nursing her. The Prophet ﷺ came and said: 'Where is Zaynab?' Qarībah"," the daughter of Abī Umayyah"," who was present with her"," said: \""'Ammār ibn Yāsir has taken her.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I shall come to you tonight.' She said: 'So I set out my provisions and brought out some barley grains that were in a jar.'\n\nAnd in the narration of Abū 'Abdillāh: 'in a sack","' and she brought out some fat and pressed it. He spent the night and then in the morning"," when he awoke"," he said: 'You have honour in the eyes of your family. If you wish"," I shall stay with you for seven [nights]"," and if I stay for seven"," I shall [likewise] stay with my wives for seven [nights].'\"" [Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14767","(14761) Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū 'Abdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Ismā'īl ibn Qutaybah and Muḥammad ibn 'Abd as-Salām both said: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Khālid al-Ḥadhā' narrated to us from Abī Qilābah from Anas who said: \When one marries a virgin while having a previously married wife"," he stays with her for seven [nights]; and when one marries a previously married woman while having a virgin wife"," he stays with her for three [nights].\"" And if I were to say that he raised it [to the Prophet]"," I would be truthful"," but he said: \""The Sunnah.\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā"," and al-Bukhārī narrated it from the ḥadīth of Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal from Khālid al-Ḥadhā'. [Authentic. Agreed upon]"""
"14768","(14762) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb al-Lakhmī narrated to us, Isḥāq — meaning ad-Dabarī — narrated to us from 'Abd ar-Razzāq from ath-Thawrī from Ayyūb.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū 'Abdillāh Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, 'Alī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Abī 'Īsā narrated to us, 'Abdullāh ibn al-Walīd narrated to us from Sufyān, Ayyūb as-Sakhtiyānī and Khālid al-Ḥadhā' narrated to us from Abī Qilābah from Anas ibn Mālik who said: \It is the Sunnah that when one marries a virgin while having a previously married wife"," he stays with her for seven [nights]; and when one marries a previously married woman while having a virgin wife"," he stays with her for three [nights].\"" Khālid said: \""And if I were to say that he raised it [to the Prophet]"," I would be truthful.\""\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of 'Abd ar-Razzāq: \""And if I wished"," I would say he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from the ḥadīth of Abī Usāmah from Sufyān"," and he indicated the narration of 'Abd ar-Razzāq. Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Rāfi' from 'Abd ar-Razzāq in an abridged form. [Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14769","(14763) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-'Alawī, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us, Abū Ḥāmid Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū Qilābah 'Abd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad ibn 'Abdillāh ar-Raqāshī narrated to us, Abū 'Āṣim narrated to us from Sufyān from Ayyūb and Khālid from Abī Qilābah from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \When one marries a virgin while having a previously married wife"," he stays with her for seven [nights]; and when one marries a previously married woman while having a virgin wife"," he stays with her for three [nights].\"" [Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14770","(14764) Abū 'Abdillāh the Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq aṣ-Ṣaghānī narrated to us, Ḥajjāj — meaning Ibn Minhāl — narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ayyūb from Abī Qilābah and Ḥumayd from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \For the virgin"," seven days; and for the previously married woman"," three days.\"" [Authentic. Preceded above]"""
"14771","(14765) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas, who said: When a man marries a virgin woman, he stays with her for seven days and then divides his time among his wives. And when he marries a previously married woman (thayyib), he stays with her for three days and then divides his time. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see its predecessor]"
"14772","(14766) Abū ʿAbdullāh informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Bakr narrated to us, Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿArūbah narrated from Qatādah, from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: He stays with the virgin for seven days and then divides his time, and if she is a thayyib (previously married woman), he stays with her for three days and then divides his time. [Ṣaḥīḥ; see its predecessor]"
"14773","(14767) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Ḥumayd narrated to us, Anas narrated —\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Muʿallā — who is ibn Manṣūr — narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, Ḥumayd narrated from Anas: that when the Prophet ﷺ consummated his marriage with Ṣafiyyah, he stayed with her for three days. ʿUthmān added: And she was a thayyib (previously married woman). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14774","(14768) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Abū al-Rabīʿ al-Zahrānī narrated to us, Fulayḥ ibn Sulaymān al-Madanī narrated from Ibn Shihāb al-Zuhrī, from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr, Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib, ʿAlqamah ibn Wāqith al-Laythī, and ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, when the people of the slander (Ahl al-Ifk) said what they said, and Allah declared her innocent of it. Al-Zuhrī said: Each of them narrated to me a portion of her ḥadīth, and some of them had a better memory than others, and some were more accurate in their narration. I retained from each one of them the ḥadīth that he narrated to me from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and some of their narrations corroborate others. They claimed that ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to travel, he would draw lots among his wives. Whosever lot came out, he would take her with him. She said: He drew lots among us during a military expedition he undertook, and my lot came out, so I went out with him after the Ḥijāb (ordainment of veiling) had been revealed, and she narrated the ḥadīth in its entirety.\n\nAl-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]"
"14775","(14769) Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh al-ʿAdl narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Maymūn narrated to us, Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Wāḥid ibn Ayman narrated to us, Ibn Abī Mulaykah narrated from al-Qāsim ibn Muḥammad, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on a journey, he would draw lots among his wives. On one occasion, the lot fell upon ʿĀʾishah and Ḥafṣah, may Allah be pleased with both of them, so they both went out together. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he traveled at night, would ride alongside ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and converse with her. Ḥafṣah said to ʿĀʾishah: Will you not ride my camel tonight and I will ride your camel, so that you may see and I may see? She said: Yes. So ʿĀʾishah rode Ḥafṣah's camel and Ḥafṣah rode ʿĀʾishah's camel, may Allah be pleased with both of them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to ʿĀʾishah's camel, upon which Ḥafṣah was mounted, greeted her, and rode along with her until they made camp. ʿĀʾishah missed him, and when they dismounted, she began placing her feet in the idhkhir grass and saying: O Lord, send upon me a scorpion or a snake that may sting me, for I cannot say anything to Your Messenger.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Nuʿaym, and Muslim narrated it from Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh from Abī Nuʿaym. [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]"
"14776","(14770) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ, from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah, from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, regarding this verse: That is the woman who rebels (tanzush) and belittles the right of her husband and does not obey his command. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded that he admonish her, remind her of Allah, and make her aware of his right over her. If she accepts, well and good; otherwise, he should forsake her in the bed and not speak to her — without dissolving the marriage — and that is severe upon her. If she returns, well and good; otherwise, he may strike her a strike that is not severe (ghayr mubarraḥ), without breaking a bone or causing a wound. He said: (If they obey you, then do not seek a way against them) — meaning: If she obeys you, then do not seek pretexts against her."
"14777","(14771) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Sulaym narrated to me, Abū Hāshim Ismāʿīl ibn Kathīr narrated from ʿĀṣim ibn Laqīṭ ibn Ṣabrah, from his father, who said: I was among the delegation of Banī al-Muntafiq — or in the delegation of Banī al-Muntafiq — so we came to him but did not find him. We encountered ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her. A dish (qināʿ) containing dates was brought to us — the qināʿ being a large platter — and she ordered a khazīrah (stew) to be prepared for us, and it was made. We ate. We had not long waited before the Prophet ﷺ came and said: Have you eaten anything? Has anything been ordered for you? We said: Yes. We had not long waited before the shepherd drove in his flock, and lo, there was a young goat that was bleating. He said: Here, O so-and-what did you give birth to? He said: A bahmah (young animal). He said: Then slaughter for us a sheep in its place. Then he turned to me and said: Do not think — and he did not say \do not think\"" (lā taḥsabanna) — that we slaughtered it on your account. We have a hundred sheep and we do not want them to increase. When the shepherd gives birth to a bahmah"," we slaughter a sheep in its place. I said: O Messenger of Allah"," I have a woman who has something in her tongue — meaning foul speech. He said: Divorce her. I said: I have children from her and she has companionship (with me). He said: Then command her — meaning admonish her — and if there is any good in her"," she will accept it. And do not strike your wife as you strike your slave woman. I said: O Messenger of Allah"," tell me about wuḍūʾ (ablution). He said: Perform wuḍūʾ thoroughly"," interlace between the fingers"," and be vigorous in sniffing water into the nose"," unless you are fasting. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14778","(14772) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, Ḥammād narrated from ʿAlī ibn Zayd, from Abī Ḥurrah al-Raqāshī, from his paternal uncle, that the Prophet ﷺ said: If you fear their rebellion (nushūz), then forsake them in the beds (al-maḍājiʿ). Ḥammād said: Meaning sexual relations (al-nikāḥ). [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14779","(14773) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān narrated to us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr narrated to us, ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us, Maʿmar narrated from al-Zuhrī, from Anas ibn Mālik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Do not envy one another, do not sever ties with one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers. It is not permissible for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days.\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Rāfiʿ from ʿAbd al-Razzāq, and al-Bukhārī narrated it through two other chains from al-Zuhrī.\n\nAnd in the ḥadīth of Ibn ʿUmar from the Prophet ﷺ: It is not permissible for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days. [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]"
"14780","(14774) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Ḥajabī informed us, Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, regarding the account of the Prophet's ﷺ Ḥajj and his sermon at ʿArafah, he said: Fear Allah concerning women, for you have taken them as a trust from Allah, and you have made their private parts lawful to you by the word of Allah. And upon you is the right that they do not allow anyone whom you dislike to lie on your beds. If they do that, then strike them a strike that is not severe (ghayr mubarraḥ). And upon you is their provision and their clothing in a fair and reasonable manner (bil-maʿrūf).\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah and others from Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl. [Ṣaḥīḥ; Muslim 1218]"
"14781","(14775) Abū Ṭāhir Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Maḥmish al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us; Maʿmar reported, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Iyās ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Abī Dhubāb, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not strike the female slaves of Allah.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""Then the women became emboldened and behaved badly toward their husbands.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," the women have become emboldened and their conduct toward their husbands has become corrupt since you forbade striking them.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: \""Then strike them.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""So the people struck their wives that night.\"" He (the narrator) said: \""Then many women came complaining of being struck.\"" So the Prophet (ﷺ) said when morning came: \""Seventy women have come to the household of Muḥammad this night"," all of them complaining of being struck. By Allah"," you will not find those [who strike] to be the best among you.\""\n\nIt has reached us from Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī that he said: \""No companionship (ṣuḥbah) is known for Iyās.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14782","(14776) The Shaykh said: It has also been narrated through another chain as a mursal narration. Abū al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd informed us; Ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ṣaffār narrated to us; Abū Ismāʿīl Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Sulamī narrated to us; Saʿīd ibn Kathīr ibn ʿUfayr and Saʿīd ibn Abī Maryam both said: al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd, from Ḥumayd ibn Nāfiʿ, from Umm Kulthūm bint Abī Bakr, who said: \The men were forbidden from striking women"," then they [the husbands] complained about them to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," so he permitted them to strike them.\"" Then I said: \""Seventy women came to the household of Muḥammad (ﷺ) this night"," all of whom had been struck.\"" Yaḥyā said: \""And I think al-Qāsim said: 'Then it was said to them afterwards: The best among you will not strike.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other than this chain]"""
"14783","(14777) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us; Saʿīd, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz, reported, from Makḥūl, from Umm Ayman, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) enjoined upon some of his household: \Do not associate anything with Allah"," even if you are tortured or burned. Obey your parents"," even if they command you to give up everything—then give it up. Do not abandon the Ṣalāh intentionally"," for whoever abandons the Ṣalāh intentionally"," the covenant of Allah is free from him. Beware of wine (khamr)"," for it is the key to every evil. Beware of disobedience (maʿṣiyah)"," for it incurs the wrath of Allah. Do not contest the authority of those in command"," even if you believe you have a right. Do not flee from the battlefield"," even if the people are struck by death—and you are among them"," then stand firm. Spend upon your household from your abundance. Do not raise your staff from them"," and instill in them the fear of Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: \""In this narration there is an irsāl (broken chain) between Makḥūl and Umm Ayman.\""\n\nAbū ʿUbayd said regarding this hadith: \""Al-Kisāʾī and others said: 'He did not mean the staff with which one strikes"," nor did he ever command anyone with that. Rather"," he meant discipline (adab).'\"" Abū ʿUbayd said: \""The origin of the word ʿaṣā (staff) is unity and harmony.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14784","(14778) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak informed us; ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us; Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Abū ʿAwanah reported, from ʿAbd Allāh, from Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muslī, from al-Ashʿath ibn Qays, who said: \I was a guest of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and he said to me: 'O Ashʿath"," memorize from me three things which I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): Do not ask a man why he struck his wife"," and do not sleep except after performing the Witr prayer.' And I have forgotten the third.\"" Others narrated from Abū Dāwūd in this chain: \""From ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Muslī.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14785","(14779) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-Naḍr Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Faqīh informed us; ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd al-Dārimī narrated to us; Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us; Abū Qazʿah Suwayd ibn Ḥujayr al-Bāhilī reported, from Ḥakīm ibn Muʿāwiyah al-Qushayrī, from his father, who said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," what is the right of one of our wives upon him?' He said: 'That you feed her when you eat"," and clothe her when you clothe yourself"," and do not strike the face"," and do not curse"," and do not forsake her except within the house.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14786","(14780) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us; Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah reported, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. And Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from his original source; Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us; Aḥmad ibn Yūsuf al-Sulamī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf said: Sufyān, meaning al-Thawrī, mentioned, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Zamʿah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Does one of you strike his wife as he strikes a slave"," then lie with her at the end of the day?\""\n\nIn the narration of Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"," he said: \""The Prophet (ﷺ) admonished the people regarding women and said: 'One of you strikes his wife like striking a slave"," then embraces her at the end of the day.'\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Firyābī"," and in another place from al-Ḥumaydī and others"," from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. And Muslim narrated it through other chains from Hishām. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon]"""
"14787","(14781) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Ḥāmid ibn Bilāl informed us; Yaḥyā ibn al-Rabīʿ informed us; Sufyān reported, from al-Zuhrī, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, from Iyās ibn Abī Dhubāb (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not strike the female slaves of Allah.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: \""The women have become emboldened against their husbands.\"" So he gave them permission"," and they struck. Then many women came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," and he said: \""Seventy women have come to the household of Muḥammad this night"," all of them complaining about their husbands"," and you will not find those [who strike] to be the best among you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned under no. 14775]"""
"14788","(14782) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr informed us; Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAbd al-Majīd al-Thaqafī narrated. And Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; al-Thaqafī reported, from Ayyūb, from Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿUbaydah, that he said regarding this verse: {And if you fear dissension between the two, send an arbitrator from his family and an arbitrator from her family} [An-Nisāʾ 35]: \A man and a woman came to ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him)"," and with each of them was a group of people. So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) commanded them"," and they appointed an arbitrator from his family and an arbitrator from her family. Then he said to the two arbitrators: 'Do you know what is upon you? If you see that you should unite them"," then unite them"," and if you see that you should separate them"," then separate them.' The woman said: 'I am pleased with the Book of Allah"," with what is upon me and my right in it.' The man said: 'As for separation"," no.' So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: 'You have lied. By Allah"," you will not leave until you affirm the same as she has affirmed.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14789","(14783) Abū Naṣr ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Qatādah informed us; Abū Manṣūr al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Naḍrawī informed us; Aḥmad ibn Najdah informed us; Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Zayd reported, from Ayyūb, and he mentioned it with its chain and its meaning, except that he said: ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \No"," by Allah"," you will not depart until you affirm the same as she has affirmed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14790","(14784) And with his chain, Saʿīd narrated to us; Hushaym narrated to us; Manṣūr and Hishām reported, from Ibn Sīrīn, from ʿUbaydah, with the same meaning. The woman said: \I am pleased and I submit.\"" The man said: \""As for separation"," no.\"" So ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""That is not for you. You will not leave until you are pleased with the same as she is pleased with.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned before it]"""
"14791","(14785) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us, saying: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-ʿAlāʾ narrated to us: Ziyād ibn Ayyūb narrated to us: Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated to us: Ibn ʿAwn informed me from Ibn Sīrīn from ʿUbaydah, and he mentioned the hadith with its meaning, except that he said: Then he (ʿAlī) turned to the woman and said: \Are you pleased with what the two arbitrators have decided?\"" She said: \""Yes"," I am pleased with what Allah has decreed for me.\"" Then he turned to the man and said: \""Are you pleased with what the two arbitrators have decided?\"" He said: \""No"," but I would be pleased if they reconcile them"," and I would not be pleased if they separate them.\"" So ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said to him: \""You have lied"," by Allah"," you shall not move from your place until you express the same acceptance that she has expressed.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14792","(14786) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muslim ibn Khālid narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Ibn Abī Mulaykah, who heard him say: ʿAqīl ibn Abī Ṭālib married Fāṭimah bint ʿUtbah, and she said: \Wait for me"," and I will spend on you.\"" Whenever he entered upon her"," she would say: \""Where is ʿUtbah ibn Rabīʿah"," and where is Shaybah ibn Rabīʿah?\"" He would say: \""They are on your left side in the Fire"," when you enter it.\"" So she tightened her garments upon herself and came to ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān"," may Allah be pleased with him"," and mentioned that to him. He sent Ibn ʿAbbās and Muʿāwiyah"," may Allah be pleased with both of them. Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""I will surely separate between them.\"" And Muʿāwiyah said: \""I would not separate between two shaykhs of Banū ʿAbd Manāf.\"" He said: \""So they came to them and found that they had tightened their garments upon themselves and had reconciled their matter.\""\n\nAnd ʿIkrimah ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn ʿAbbās"," who said: \""Muʿāwiyah and I were sent as two arbitrators"," and it was said to us: 'If you see fit to separate"," then separate"," and if you see fit to reconcile"," then reconcile.'\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14793","(14787) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us: Abū al-Ḥasan al-Ṭarāʾifī narrated to us: ʿUthmān ibn Saʿīd narrated to us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to us from Muʿāwiyah ibn Ṣāliḥ from ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭalḥah from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: \If their two opinions agree upon separation or reconciliation"," then their matter is permissible.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14794","(14788) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥasan al-Qāḍī narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us: Ādam ibn Abī Iyās narrated to us: Warqāʾ narrated to us from ʬAṭāʾ ibn al-Sāʾib from Saʿīd ibn Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās, may Allah be pleased with both of them, regarding the verse: {If they both desire reconciliation, Allah will cause agreement between them} (al-Nisāʾ 35) — he said: \He means the two arbitrators.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14795","(14789) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī and Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bushrān said: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Abū Muʿāwiyah narrated to us from al-Ḥajjāj from Abī Isḥāq from al-Shaʿbī from al-Ḥārith from ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: \If one of the two arbitrators renders a judgment and the other does not render a judgment"," then his judgment is not valid until they both agree.\"" [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14796","(14790) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us: Abū Manṣūr al-Naḍrawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Najdah narrated to us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr narrated to us: Hushaym informed us: Ḥuṣayn informed us from al-Shaʿbī: \A woman rebelled against her husband"," and they brought their dispute to Shurayḥ. Shurayḥ said: 'Send an arbitrator from his family and an arbitrator from her family.' So they did that. The two arbitrators looked into their matter and decided to separate between them. The man disliked that"," so Shurayḥ said: 'Then what were we engaged in today?' And he validated their matter.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14797","(14791) He said: And Hushaym narrated to us: Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Khāld informed us, saying: \I heard al-Shaʿbī say: 'Whatever the two arbitrators decide is valid"," whether they separate or reconcile.'\"" And from ʿUbaydah a similar report. [Ṣaḥīḥ; its chain has been mentioned previously]"""
"14798","(14792) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Ibrāhīm ibn Marzūq narrated to us: Wahb ibn Jarīr narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated to us from ʿAmr ibn Murrah, who said: \I asked Saʿīd ibn Jubayr about the two arbitrators"," and he said: 'I do not know about that.' So I said: 'I am only asking you about the two arbitrators mentioned in the Book of Allah"," meaning the Qurʾān.' He said: 'An arbitrator is sent from his family and an arbitrator from her family. They speak to one of them and admonish him; if he returns"," then so be it"," otherwise they speak to the other and admonish him; if he returns"," then so be it"," otherwise the two arbitrators render a judgment. Whatever they decide is valid.'\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14799","(14793) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Ṣādiq Muḥammad ibn Abī al-Fawāris al-Ṣaydalānī said: Abū al-ʿAbbās, who is al-Aṣamm, narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashr al-ʿAbdī narrated to us: Saʿīd, who is Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, narrated to us from Qatādah from al-Ḥasan regarding this verse: {Send an arbitrator from his family and an arbitrator from her family} (al-Nisāʾ 35) — he said: \Their duty is only to reconcile and to look into the matter. Separation is not in their hands.\""\n\nThis contradicts what has preceded"," and it is the more correct of the two opinions of al-Shāfiʿī"," may Allah have mercy on him. The apparent meaning of what we have narrated from ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," supports it"," unless they delegate that authority to them. And Allah knows best. [Ḥasan]"""
"14800","(14794) The shaykh, the Imām Abū al-Ṭayyib Sahl ibn Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān, dictated to us, and Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ, and Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh, and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq, and Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Shādhīyākhī, and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakīm informed us: Anas ibn ʿIyāḍ narrated to us from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from Fāṭimah from Asmāʾ, who narrated to her: \A woman came to the Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"," I have a female neighbour. Is there any sin upon me if I boast to her about things my husband has not given me?' She said: The Messenger of Allah"," peace and blessings be upon him"," said: 'The one who boasts about what she has not been given is like the one who wears two garments of falsehood.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ; agreed upon]"""
"14801","(14795) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd al-Ḥārithī narrated to us, saying: Abū Usāmah narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from Fāṭimah bint al-Mundhir, from Asmāʾ bint Abī Bakr, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," is it permissible for me to say that my husband has given me [such and such]"," when he has not given me anything"," for I have a co-wife?\"" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \""He who claims to have been given what he was not given is like one who wears two garments of falsehood.\"" Muslim narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah"," from Abū Usāmah"," and al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it from another route from Hishāh. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it.]"""
"14802","(14796) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in Baghdad, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Ḥamdān al-Naysābūrī narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Surrī narrated to us, saying: Minjāb narrated to us, saying: ʿAlī ibn Mushhir narrated to us, from Hishām, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Hālah bint Khuwaylid, the sister of Khadījah, sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he recognised the manner of Khadījah's seeking permission, and it startled him. He said, \O Allah"," Hālah!\"" So I became jealous and said"," \""What is it that you keep mentioning an old woman among the old women of Quraysh"," with red gums"," who has perished in time? Allah has given you better than her.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn al-Khalīl"," and Muslim narrated it from Suwayd ibn Saʿīd"," both of them from ʿAlī ibn Mushhir. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"14803","(14797) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: \I was not jealous of any wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as I was of Khadījah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," because of how often I heard him mention her. He did not marry me until after her death"," three years later. And indeed"," his Lord commanded him to give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of reeds"," in which there is no toil and no noise.\"" Al-Bukhārī and Muslim both narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from various routes from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it.]"""
"14804","(14798) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Mulaykah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \Indeed"," Banī al-Mughīrah have asked my permission to marry their daughter to ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," but I will not permit it"," then I will not permit it"," then I will not permit it — unless the son of Abī Ṭālib wishes to divorce my daughter and marry their daughter. She is but a part of me; what dismays her dismays me"," and what harms her harms me.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon. 99]"""
"14805","(14799) And Abū al-Ḥasan narrated to us, saying: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us, saying: ʿAbbās ibn al-Faḍl al-Asfaṭī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: al-Layth narrated it with the same meaning, except that he did not mention his words: \What dismays her dismays me.\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Walīd and Qutaybah"," and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah"," from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded it.]"""
"14806","(14800) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzzakī narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Isḥāq al-Khurāsānī al-ʿAdl narrated to us, saying: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Haytham al-Balawī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Yamān narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Ayyūb al-Ṭūsī narrated to us, saying: Abū Ḥātim Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Ḥanẓalī narrated to us, saying: Shuʿayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, who said: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥusayn informed me that al-Miswar ibn Makhramah informed him that ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, proposed to marry the daughter of Abū Jahl while Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was [his wife]. When Fāṭimah heard of this, she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him, \Your people are saying that you do not become angry for the sake of your daughters"," and here is ʿAlī about to marry the daughter of Abū Jahl.\"" Al-Miswar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up"," and I heard him when he pronounced the tashahhud"," then he said: \""To proceed: I married Abū al-ʿĀṣ"," and he spoke to me and told me the truth. And indeed"," Fāṭimah bint Muḥammad is a part of me"," and I detest that they should tempt her. And by Allah"," the daughter of the Messenger of Allah and the daughter of the enemy of Allah shall never be united under one man"," ever.\"" So ʿAlī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," abandoned the proposal. Al-Bukhārī narrated it in his Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū al-Yamān"," and Muslim narrated it from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Dārimī"," from Abū al-Yamān. And Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥalḥalah narrated it from Ibn Shihāb"," from ʿAlī"," from al-Miswar"," and added: \""He spoke to me and told me the truth"," and he made me a promise and fulfilled it for me. And I do not declare lawful what is unlawful"," nor do I declare unlawful what is lawful.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"""
"14807","(14801) Abū ʿAbd Allāh Isḥāq ibn Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf al-Sūsī narrated to us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: al-ʿAbbās ibn al-Walīd narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from al-Awzāʿī. He said: And Muḥammad ibn ʿAwf narrated to us, saying: Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us, saying: al-Awzāʿī narrated to us — and the ḥadīth is that of al-ʿAbbās — saying: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Kathīr narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Taymī narrated to me, saying: Ibn Jābir ibn ʿAtīk narrated to me, saying: My father narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," among jealousy is that which Allah loves and that which He hates. The jealousy that Allah loves is jealousy regarding a matter of suspicion"," and the jealousy that Allah hates is jealousy in the absence of suspicion. And among self-display is that which Allah loves: a man's self-display during battle and during giving charity. And the self-display that Allah hates is self-display in falsehood.\"""""
"14808","(14802) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us, saying: Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, saying: Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād narrated to us. And Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, saying: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, saying: Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, saying: Hishām ibn ʿAbd al-Malik narrated to us, saying: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Shaddād, from Abī ʿUdhrah, from ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Prophet ﷺ forbade men and women from entering the public baths, then he permitted men to enter them wearing lower garments (izār), but he did not permit women to do so. This is the wording of the ḥadīth of al-Muqriʾ. In the narration of al-Rūdhbārī, [it reads]: He forbade entering the public baths, then he permitted men to enter them wearing wrappers (maʾāzir). [Ḍaʿīf.]"
"14809","(14803) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us, saying: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us, saying: Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī narrated to us, saying: Shuʿbah narrated to us, from Manṣūr, from Sālim ibn Abī al-Jaʿd, from Abī Mulayḥ al-Hudhalī, who said: Women from the people of Ḥimṣ, or from the people of Shām, entered upon ʿĀʾishah, may Allah be pleased with her, and she said: \Are you the ones whose women enter the public baths? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no woman who removes her garments in other than her husband's house except that she rends the veil between her and Allah"," Mighty and Majestic.'\"" And that was narrated from Abī Muslim al-Khawlānī from ʿĀʾishah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," and from al-Sāʾib from Umm Salamah"," may Allah be pleased with her"," in a marfūʿ narration. [Ḍaʿīf. Narrated by al-Ṭayālisī"," 1621.]"""
"14810","(14804) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Muzzakī narrated to us, saying: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, saying: Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Wahhāb narrated to us, saying: Jaʿfar ibn ʿAwn narrated to us, saying: ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ziyād narrated to us, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Rāfiʿ, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAmr, may Allah be pleased with both of them, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \The land of the non-Arabs will be conquered for you"," and you will find therein houses called public baths. Men shall not enter them except wearing lower garments (izār)"," and prevent women from entering them except the sick woman or the woman in postpartum bleeding (nifās).\"" [Ḍaʿīf.]"""
"14811","(14805) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz narrated to us; Abū Nuʿaym narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs from his father, who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Beware of a house that is called al-ḥammām (the bathhouse).\"" It was said: \""Indeed"," it removes filth and is beneficial.\"" He said: \""Then whoever enters it should do so with a covering (i.e."," a waist wrapper).\""\n\nSulaymān said: thus Abū Nuʿaym and others narrated it in a disconnected (maqṭūʿ) form"," and Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated it in a connected (mawṣūl) form. [Weak]"""
"14812","(14806) ʿAlī informed us; Sulaymān narrated to us; ʿAbdān ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Yūsuf ibn Mūsā al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; Yaʿlā ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from Ibn Ṭāwūs from his father from Ibn ʿAbbāṣ (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Beware of a house that is called al-ḥammām (the bathhouse).\"" They said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," indeed benefit is derived from it and it cleanses filth.\"" He said: \""Then cover yourselves (when entering it).\""\n\nThe Shaykh said: the majority narrated it from al-Thawrī in a disconnected (mursal) form"," and likewise Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī"," Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah"," Rūḥ ibn al-Qāsim and others narrated it from Ibn Ṭāwūs in a disconnected form. It was also narrated from Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq ibn Yasār and others from Ibn Ṭāwūs in a connected form. [Denounced (Munkar)]"""
"14813","(14807) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Fārisī informed us; Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us; Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn narrated to us; ʿAmr ibn al-Rabīʿ ibn Ṭāriq narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm from Muḥammad ibn Thābit ibn Sharḥbīl from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yazīd al-Khaṭmī from Abū Ayyūb al-Anṣārī that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day"," let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist wrapper (izār); and whoever among your women believes in Allah and the Last Day"," let them not enter the bathhouse.\"" He (the narrator) said: this was conveyed to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz (may Allah be pleased with him) during his caliphate"," so he wrote to Abū Bakr ibn ʿAmr ibn Ḥazm: \""Ask Muḥammad ibn Thābit about his ḥadīth"," for he is trustworthy (riḍā).\"" So he asked him"," then wrote to ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," and ʿUmar forbade women from entering the bathhouse. [Weak]"""
"14814","(14808) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us; Abū al-ʿAbbās al-Aṣamm narrated to us; Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Muʿāwiya ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me from Ḥudayr ibn Kurayb from Jubayr ibn Nufayr from Abū al-Dardāʾ: that he used to enter the bathhouse and say: \What an excellent house is the bathhouse — it removes filth and reminds one of the Fire.\"" And he would say: \""What an evil house is the bathhouse — for it strips its inhabitants of modesty (ḥayāʾ).\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"14815","(14809) He said: and Ibn Wahb narrated to me; Saʿīd ibn Abī Ayyūb and Yaḥyā ibn Ayyūb narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān that he asked Nāfīʿ, the freedman of Ibn ʿUmar, about the bathhouse for women. He said: \We do not consider it forbidden (ḥarām)"," but we forbid our women from it.\"" [Weak]"""
"14816","(14810) ʿAbd Allāh ibn Sulaymān said: \Then I asked Bukayr about that"," and he said: 'We do not consider it forbidden"," but that they abstain from it is better for them.'\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated to us from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: \""What an excellent house is the bathhouse — it removes filth and reminds one of the Fire.\"" [Weak]"""
"14817","(14811) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us; al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; Sufyān narrated to us; al-Zuhrī narrated to me; Sulaymān ibn Yasār and Abū Salamah ibn Abī ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \Indeed"," the Jews and the Christians do not dye (their hair)"," so oppose them.\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ)]"""
"14818","(14812) Abū ʿAbd Allāh informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us; Ismāʿīl ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; Sufyān narrated from al-Zuhrī from Fadākira with the same meaning.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from al-Ḥumaydī, and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā."
"14819","(14813) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī informed us; Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us; Wahb narrated from Ayyūb from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, who said: \I asked Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him): 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ use dye (khiḍāb)?' He said: 'He did not see (much) grey hair — only a little.'\"" [Sound (Ṣaḥīḥ). Agreed upon (Muttafaq ʿalayh)]"""
"14820","(14814) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us by dictation; al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us; Muʿallā ibn Asad narrated to us — and he mentioned it with the same (meaning). Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Muʿallā ibn Asad, and Muslim ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated it from Ḥajjāj ibn al-Shāʿir from Muʿallā ibn Asad."
"14821","(14815) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Ibn Abī Qumāsh narrated to us, Sulaymān narrated from Ḥammād ibn Zayd from Thābit.\n\n(Ḥ) And 'Alī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqri' informed me, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Abū al-Rabī' narrated to us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated to us, Thābit narrated: Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about the dye of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and he said: \If I wished to count the white hairs that were on his head"," I could have done so.\"" And he said: \""He did not dye (his hair).\"" And Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) dyed with ḥinnā' and katam"," and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) dyed with ḥinnā' alone.\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Abū al-Rabī'. And in the narration of Sulaymān"," Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""If I wished to count the white hairs that were in his beard…\"" He said: \""And Abū Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) dyed with ḥinnā' and katam.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb"," and Muslim narrated it from Abū al-Rabī'. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"14822","(14816) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Naḍr ibn 'Abd al-Wahhāb informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed me, Aḥmad ibn Salamah informed us; both said: Naṣr ibn 'Alī al-Jahḍamī narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Muthannā ibn Sa'īd narrated from Qatādah from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \It is disliked for a man to pluck the white hair from his head and his beard.\"" He said: \""The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) did not dye (his hair). The whiteness was only in his sideburns"," in his temples"," and scattered on his head.\"" Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Naṣr ibn 'Alī. Thus said Anas ibn Mālik: \""The Prophet (peace be upon him) did not dye.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded before it.]"""
"14823","(14817) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-Faḍl al-Ḥasan ibn Ya'qūb ibn Yūsuf al-'Adl informed us, al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us, al-Mu'allā ibn Asad narrated to us, Salām ibn Abī Muṭī' narrated from 'Uthmān ibn 'Abd Allāh ibn Mawhab, who said: \I entered upon Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her)"," and she brought out to us some of the hair of the Prophet (peace be upon him) that had been dyed.\""\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Mūsā ibn Ismā'īl from Salām ibn Abī Muṭī'.\n\nAl-Bukhārī said: And Abū Nu'aym said: Nuṣayr ibn Abī al-Ash'ath narrated to us from Ibn Mawhab that Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) showed him the hair of the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," which was red.\n\nAnd it has been narrated from Abū Rimthah that he went toward the Prophet (peace be upon him)"," and he had hair reaching his ears upon which was the trace of ḥinnā'. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Bukhārī 5898.]"""
"14824","(14818) Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzāq informed us, Ma'mar informed from Sa'īd al-Jurayrī from 'Abd Allāh ibn Buraydah from Abī al-Aswad al-Dīlī from Abū Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \The best thing with which this grey hair is changed is ḥinnā' and katam.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"14825","(14819) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us, Abū al-'Abbās al-Aṣamm informed us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb informed me, 'Abd Allāh ibn 'Umar narrated from Nāfi' from Ibn 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to dye his beard with yellow (khalūq) and he narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) used to dye (with yellow).\n\nAnd that was also narrated from Ibn Abī Riwād from Nāfi'. [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"
"14826","(14820) Abū al-Ḥasan 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated from Ḥumayd ibn Wahb from Banī Ṭāwūs from their father from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: A man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) who had dyed with ḥinnā', and he said: \How beautiful this is!\"" Then another man passed after him who had dyed with ḥinnā' and katam"," and he said: \""This is more beautiful than this.\"" Then another passed who had dyed with yellow (ṣufr)"," and he said: \""This is more beautiful than all of this.\"" He said: And Ṭāwūs used to dye with yellow (ṣufr). [Ḍa'īf.]"""
"14827","(14821) Abū al-Ḥasan informed us, Aḥmad informed us, Ismā'īl ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, 'Āṣim ibn 'Alī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ṭalḥah narrated it with its meaning, except that he said: from Ibn Ṭāwūs from his father."
"14828","(14822) Abū 'Abd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq both said: Abū al-'Abbās Muḥammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us. (Ḥ) And Abū 'Alī al-Rūdhbārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn 'Amr ibn al-Sarḥ and Aḥmad ibn Sa'īd al-Hamdānī both said: Ibn Wahb narrated to me, Ibn Jurayj informed from Abū al-Zubayr from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Abū Quḥāfah (may Allah be pleased with him) was brought on the day of the Conquest of Makkah, and his head and beard were white like the thagāmah plant. The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: \Change this with something"," and avoid black.\""\n\nThe mention of Jābir dropped from the narration of Abū Zakariyyā. Muslim narrated it in the Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Ṭāhir ibn al-Sarḥ. And he also narrated in that regard from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him). [Ṣaḥīḥ. Muslim 2102.]"""
"14829","(14823) Abū al-Ḥasan Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Dāwūd al-'Alawī informed us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Hārūn narrated to us, Makkī ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, 'Abd al-'Azīz ibn Abī Riwād narrated from Muḥammad ibn Ziyād from Abū Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who mentioned the Prophet (peace be upon him) and said: \Change the grey hair and do not resemble the Jews"," and avoid black.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"14830","(14824) 'Alī ibn Aḥmad ibn 'Abdān informed us, Aḥmad ibn 'Ubayd informed us, Ibn Milḥān narrated to us, 'Amr — meaning ibn Khālid — narrated to us, 'Ubayd Allāh ibn 'Amr narrated from 'Abd al-Karīm from Sa'īd ibn Jubayr from Ibn 'Abbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who said: \There will be at the end of time a people who will dye with this black"," like the bellies of birds. They will not smell the fragrance of Paradise.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ.]"""
"14831","(14825) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq narrated to us, Abū al-ʿAbbās — al-Aṣamm — narrated to us, Baḥr ibn Naṣr narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Lahīʿah informed me from Abū Qabīl al-Maʿāfirī that he said: ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ came to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) having dyed his head and beard black. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Who are you?\"" He said: \""I am ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ.\"" ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""I knew you as an old man"," and today you appear as a young man. I adjure you that you go and wash off this black dye.\"" [Weak]"""
"14832","(14826) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, he said: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb say: I heard Baḥr ibn Naṣr say: \Al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy upon him) used to dye (his hair).\""\n\nAnd Sulaymān ibn Shuʿayb al-Kaysānī said: \""I saw Muḥammad ibn Idrīs al-Shāfiʿī dyeing his beard with ḥinnāʾ.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14833","(14827) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥusayn ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Bajalī al-Muqriʾ in Kūfah narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Abī Dārim narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Mūsā al-Marwarrūdhī narrated to us, Abū Marwān Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān al-ʿUthmānī narrated to us, al-Mughīrah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated from his father, from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade plucking out white hair and said: \Indeed"," it is the light of Islam.\"" [Hasan in the context of other narrations]"""
"14834","(14828) Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Ḥāmid ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Harawī narrated to us, Abū al-Muthannā narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAjlān, ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb narrated to me from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not pluck out white hair"," for no Muslim grows white hair in Islam except that Allah records for it a good deed and erases thereby a sin.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14835","(14829) Imam Abū Isḥāq al-Isfarāʾīnī narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Zargūyah narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Ibn Lahīʿah informed us from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not pluck out white hair"," for no one among you grows a single white hair in Islam except that Allah"," the Most High"," raises thereby his rank"," records for it a good deed"," and wipes away thereby a bad deed.\"" [Hasan]"""
"14836","(14830) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaḍḍal narrated to us, Abū ʿAqīl narrated to us and said: Buhayyah said: I heard ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) say: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked seeing a woman whose hand bore no trace of ḥinnāʾ or dye.\"" [Weak]"""
"14837","(14831) Abū al-Ḥasan al-Muqriʾ narrated to us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq narrated to us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Muḥammad narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd narrated from Muḥammad al-Rammām, who said: Karīmah bint Hammām narrated to me and said: I was with ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) when a woman asked her about dyeing with ḥinnāʾ. She said: \My master (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked its scent — or did not like its scent — but it is not forbidden for you"," my sisters"," to dye (with ḥinnāʾ).\""\n\nAll other narrations on this subject have been mentioned in the chapter on what a woman may display of her adornment. [Weak]"""
"14838","(14832) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us, Musaddad narrated to us, Yaḥyā narrated from ʿUbayd Allāh, Nāfiʿ narrated to me from ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him): that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed the woman who does tattooing and the woman who has it done, the woman who joins hair (with extensions) and the woman who has it done.\n\nAl-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Musaddad, and Muslim narrated it from Zuhayr from Yaḥyā al-Qaṭṭān. [Authentic — Agreed upon]"
"14839","(14833) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Jarīr narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us, Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us, Jarīr narrated from Manṣūr, from Ibrāhīm, from ʿAlqamah, from ʿAbd Allāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \Allah cursed those who do tattooing and those who have it done"," those who pluck facial hair"," and those who file their teeth for beauty — those who alter the creation of Allah.\"" This reached a woman from Banī Asad known as Umm Yaʿqūb"," who used to recite the Qurʾān. She came to him and said: \""A ḥadīth has reached me from you that you curse those who do tattooing and those who have it done"," those who pluck facial hair"," and those who file their teeth for beauty — those who alter the creation of Allah.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""Why should I not curse those whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed"," and it is in the Book of Allah?\"" She said: \""I have read everything between the two covers of the Muṣḥaf and I did not find it.\"" He said: \""If you had truly read it"," you would have found it. Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," said: {'And whatever the Messenger gives you"," take it; and whatever he forbids you"," abstain from it.'} [Al-Ḥashr:7]\"" She said: \""I see something of this on your wife.\"" He said: \""Go and look.\"" She went and looked and saw nothing. She said: \""I saw nothing.\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""Had that been the case"," we would never have been intimate with her.\""\n\nThe wording is from the ḥadīth of Isḥāq. Al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm and ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah. [Authentic — Agreed upon]"""
"14840","(14834) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī narrated to us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us, and Abū Dāwūd said: \The explanation of al-wāṣilah is the woman who joins hair with the hair of other women; al-mustaṣilah is the one for whom this is done. Al-nāmiṣah is the woman who thins the eyebrow by plucking it; al-mutanammiṣah is the one for whom this is done. Al-wāshimah is the woman who makes marks of kohl or ink on her face; al-mustawshimah is the one for whom this is done.\""\n\nAl-Farrāʾ said: \""Al-nāmiṣah is the woman who plucks hair from the face. The instrument used for this is called al-minmāṣ because hair is plucked with it.\"" [Authentic]"""
"14841","(14835) Abu 'Ubayd reported to us, from Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who reported to us, from Abu al-Hasan al-Karazi, who reported to us, from 'Ali ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, from Abu 'Ubayd: A woman would prick the back of her hand or her wrist with a needle or a thin metal instrument until it left a mark, then she would fill it with kohl or with a preparation called niyur, and it would turn green. From this it was said: \wishamat"," tashimu"," wahman\"" — she is a washimah (one who tattoos)"," and the other is mawshumah (tattooed) and mustawshimah (one who seeks tattooing). As for al-mutafallijat"," it refers to the filing and sharpening of the teeth — that is"," she sharpens them until their edges become thin"," as is the case with the teeth of youth. An older woman does this in imitation of those young women. This is the meaning of the statement of Abu 'Ubaydah and Abu 'Ubayd. [Da'if]"""
"14842","(14836) Abu 'Ali al-Rawdhbari reported to us, that Abu Bakr ibn Dassah reported to us, that Abu Dawud reported to us, that al-Qa'nabi reported from Malik, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah bint 'Abd al-Rahman, that she informed him from Habibah bint Sahl, that she informed her that she was with Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas (may Allah be pleased with him), and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) went out for the Fajr prayer and found Habibah bint Sahl at his door in the darkness of early morning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Who is this?\"" She said: \""I am Habibah bint Sahl.\"" He said: \""What is the matter with you?\"" She said: \""Neither I nor Thabit [can live together as husband and wife].\"" When Thabit ibn Qays came"," the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: \""This is Habibah bint Sahl; she has mentioned what Allah willed her to mention.\"" Habibah said: \""O Messenger of Allah"," everything he gave me is with me.\"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Thabit ibn Qays: \""Take from her.\"" So he took from her"," and she sat down among her family. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"14843","(14837) Abu Zakariyya ibn Abi Ishaq and Abu Bakr ibn al-Hasan both reported to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas reported to us, that al-Rabi' reported to us, that al-Shafi'i reported to us, that Ibn 'Uyaynah reported from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from 'Amrah, from Habibah bint Sahl, that she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in the darkness of early morning, complaining of something concerning her body, and she was saying: \Neither I nor Thabit ibn Qays [can remain together].\"" She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""O Thabit"," take from her.\"" So he took from her"," and she sat down. [Sahih. Referred to previously]"""
"14844","(14838) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz reported to us, that Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz reported to us, that Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti — reported to us in Baghdad, that Azhar ibn Jamil reported to us, that al-Thaqafi reported to us, that Khalid reported to us, that 'Ikrimah reported from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the wife of Thabit ibn Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," by Allah"," I find no fault with Thabit in character or religion"," but I detest ingratitude in Islam.\"" He said: \""Will you return to him his garden?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""O Thabit"," accept the garden and divorce her with one divorce.\"" Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Azhar ibn Jamil"," and others narrated it in mursal form from Khalid al-Hadha'. [Sahih. Referred to previously]"""
"14845","(14839) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz reported to us, that Abu Ahmad reported to us, that Abu Bakr — Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Sulayman — reported to us, that Ishaq ibn Shahin reported to us, that Khalid reported from Khalid, from 'Ikrimah, that the sister of 'Abd Allah ibn Ubayy — and he mentioned it. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Ishaq ibn Shahin. Al-Bukhari said: And Ibrahim ibn Tahman reported from Khalid, from 'Ikrimah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), in mursal form."
"14846","(14840) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu 'Uthman Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn 'Abdan al-Naysaburi both reported to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — reported to us, that al-'Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Dawri reported to us, that 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghazwan, Abu Nuh, reported to us, that Jarir ibn Hazim reported from Ayyub, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: The wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," I find no fault with Thabit in religion or character"," except that I fear ingratitude in Islam.\"" He said: \""Will you return to him his garden?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" So he commanded her to return it to him"," and he separated between them. Al-Bukhari narrated it in al-Sahih from Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak al-Makhrami from Qarad"," Abu Nuh"," except that he said: \""So she returned it to him"," and he commanded him"," so he separated from her.\"" Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Ayyub"," from 'Ikrimah"," from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)"," with its meaning. And Sulayman ibn Harb narrated it from Hammad ibn Zayd"," from Ayyub"," from 'Ikrimah"," that it was Jamilah — and he mentioned it in mursal form. Likewise"," Wuhaib narrated it from Ayyub. [Sahih. Agreed upon]"""
"14847","(14841) The jurist Abu al-Qasim 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali al-Fami reported to us in Baghdad, that Ahmad ibn Salman reported to us, that Ja'far ibn Abi 'Uthman reported to us, that Muhammad ibn Sinan al-'Awfi reported to us, that Hammam reported to us, that Qatadah reported from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that Jamilah bint al-Salul came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) seeking khul' (divorce initiated by the wife). He said to her: \What did he give you as mahr?\"" She said: \""A garden.\"" He said: \""Then return to him his garden.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14848","(14842) Abu al-Qasim 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar ibn 'Ali, the jurist, reported to us in Baghdad, that Ahmad ibn Salman reported to us, that Ja'far ibn Abi 'Uthman reported to us, that 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Umar reported to us, that 'Abd al-A'la reported to us, that Sa'id reported from Qatadah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Jamilah bint al-Salul came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \By my father and my mother"," I find no fault with Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas in character or religion"," but I cannot bear him out of hatred"," and I detest ingratitude in Islam.\"" He said: \""Will you return to him his garden?\"" She said: \""Yes.\"" So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded him to take what he had given her and not to take more. 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated it in this connected form from Sa'id ibn Abi 'Arubah"," while others narrated it from him in mursal form. [Da'if. Referred to previously]"""
"14849","(14843) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi both reported to us, saying: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — reported to us, that Yahya ibn Abi Talib reported to us, saying: Abu Nasr — meaning 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' — said: I asked Sa'id about a man who seeks khul' from his wife for more than what he gave her. He informed us from Qatadah, from 'Ikrimah, that Jamilah bint al-Salul came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: \O Messenger of Allah"," so-and-so\"" — meaning her husband Thabit ibn Qays — \""by Allah"," I find no fault with him\"" — and he mentioned it similarly"," except that he said: \""So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) separated between them and said: 'Take what you gave her and do not take more.'\"" 'Abd al-Wahhab said: Sa'id said: Ayyub narrated to us from 'Ikrimah the same as what Qatadah said from 'Ikrimah"," except that he said: \""I do not recall 'and do not take more.'\"" Muhammad ibn Abi 'Adi narrated it from Ibn Abi 'Arubah"," from Qatadah"," in mursal form. [Da'if. Referred to previously]"""
"14850","(14844) Abu 'Abd Allah al-Hafiz and Abu Muhammad 'Ubayd ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi reported to us, in the same wording, saying: Abu al-'Abbas — Muhammad ibn Ya'qub — reported to us, that Yahya ibn Abi Talib reported to us, that 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Ata' reported to us, that Ibn Jurayj reported from 'Ata', that a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) complaining about her husband. He said: \Will you return to him his garden?\"" She said: \""Yes"," and something more.\"" He said: \""As for the extra"," no.\"" [Da'if]"""
"14851","(14845) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUthmān informed us: ʿAbdullāh — that is, Ibn al-Mubārak — informed us: Ibn Jurayj informed us from ʿAṭāʾ, who said:\n\nA woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \O Messenger of Allah"," I detest my husband and I desire separation from him.\"" He said"," \""Will you return to him the garden that he gave you as mahr?\"" He (the narrator) said: Her mahr had been a garden. She said"," \""Yes"," and more besides.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said"," \""As for the additional amount from your own wealth"," no — only the garden.\"" She said"," \""Yes.\"" The Prophet ﷺ thus decreed that upon the man. When the man was informed of the Prophet's ﷺ ruling"," he said"," \""I accept the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nGundār likewise narrated it from Ibn Jurayj"," as a mursal hadith in abridged form. [Weak; see the preceding entry.]"""
"14852","(14846) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Saʿīd ibn Manṣūr informed us: Sufyān informed us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, who conveyed it as reaching the Prophet ﷺ, who said:\n\n\He shall not take from the woman seeking khulʿ more than what he gave her.\""\n\nAl-Ḥumaydī likewise narrated it from Sufyān ibn ʿUyaynah. [Weak.]"""
"14853","(14847) Al-Thawrī narrated something to the same effect from Ibn Jurayj. Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān informed us: Abū Nuʿaym and Qabīṣah said: Sufyān informed us from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from the Prophet ﷺ:\n\n\He disliked that he should take from her more than what he had given her.\""\n\n(Ḥ) Yaʿqūb said: Salamah informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal said: Wakīʿ said"," \""I asked Ibn Jurayj about it"," but he did not recognize it and rejected it.\"" The Shaykh said: It is as though he rejected it only with this wording"," for the hadith is established with the wording narrated by Ibn al-Mubārak and others. And Allah knows best. [Weak; see the preceding entry.]"""
"14854","(14848) Al-Walīd ibn Muslim narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from ʿAṭāʾ, from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both):\n\nA man brought his dispute with his wife to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \Will you return to him his garden?\"" She said"," \""Yes"," and more besides.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said"," \""As for the additional amount"," no.\""\n\nAbū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us: Abū al-Shaykh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad informed us: Abū Zurʿah informed us: ʿAmr al-Nāqid informed us: Al-Walīd ibn Muslim informed us"," and he mentioned it. However"," this is not preserved; the authentic narration with this isnād is what has been mentioned above as mursal. [Munkar.]"""
"14855","(14849) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī informed us: Yūsuf ibn Saʿīd informed us: Ḥajjāj informed us from Ibn Jurayj: Abū al-Zubayr informed me:\n\nThat Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās had in his marriage Zaynab bint ʿAbdullāh ibn Ubayy ibn Salūl, and he had given her a garden as her mahr. She came to dislike him, so the Prophet ﷺ said, \Will you return to him the garden that he gave you?\"" She said"," \""Yes"," and more besides.\"" The Prophet ﷺ said"," \""As for the additional amount"," no — only his garden.\"" She said"," \""Yes.\"" So he took it from her and let her go. When this reached Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās (may Allah be pleased with him)"," he said"," \""I accept the ruling of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""\n\nAbū al-Zubayr heard it from more than one narrator. This narration is also mursal. [Weak.]"""
"14856","(14850) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Ḥusayn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Tamīm al-Aṣam al-Qanṭarī informed us in Baghdad: Abū Jaʿfar Muḥammad ibn Saʿd ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAṭiyyah ibn Saʿd al-ʿAwfī said: My father informed me, who said: Al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAṭiyyah informed us from his father, from his grandfather, from Abū Saʿīd, who said:\n\nMy sister wished to seek khulʿ from her husband, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ along with her husband. She mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \Will you return to him his garden"," and he will divorce you?\"" She said"," \""Yes"," and I will add more.\"" He said to her a second time"," \""Will you return to him his garden"," and he will divorce you?\"" She said"," \""Yes"," and I will add more.\"" He said to her a third time"," and she said"," \""Yes"," and I will add more.\"" So he effected the khulʿ"," and she returned his garden to him and gave him additional wealth.\n\nAl-Ḥasan ibn ʿUmarah likewise narrated it from ʿAṭiyyah. However"," the mursal hadith is more authentic. [Very weak.]"""
"14857","(14851) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Aḥmad ibn al-ʿAbbās al-Baghawī informed us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr informed us: Ḥabbān ibn Hilāl informed us: Hammām informed from Maṭar, from Thābit, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabāḥ, that ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding the woman seeking khulʿ:\n\n\She may seek khulʿ for less than the value of a hair-clipping band.\"" [Weak.]"""
"14858","(14852) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ardistānī informed us: Abū Naṣr al-ʿIrāqī informed us: Sufyān al-Jawharī informed us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Walīd informed us: Sufyān informed us from Ayyūb al-Sakhtiyānī, who said: Kathīr, the freedman of Samurah, informed me:\n\nThat a woman rebelled against her husband during the caliphate of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him). He ordered her to be placed in a house full of dung, and she remained there for three days. Then he brought her out and said to her, \How did you find it?\"" She said"," \""I found no comfort except in these days.\"" So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) said"," \""Effect her khulʿ"," even if it be for the sake of an earring.\"" [Ḥasan.]"""
"14859","(14853) He said: Sufyān also narrated to us from Ibn Abī Laylā, from al-Ḥakam ibn ʿUtbah, from Khaythamah, from ʿAbdullāh ibn Shihāb al-Khawlānī:\n\nThat a woman was divorced by her husband in exchange for one thousand dirhams. This was brought before ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him), and he said, \Your husband has sold your divorce as a sale.\"" And ʿUmar permitted it. [Weak.]"""
"14860","(14854) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān informed us: Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Bakr informed us: Abū Hilāl informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Buraydah informed us that ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) said:\n\n\When women seek khulʿ"," do not belittle them.\"" [Weak.]"""
"14861","(14855) Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-Rabīʿ informed us, al-Shāfiʿī informed us, Mālik informed us.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū Aḥmad al-Mihrānī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us, Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ from a freedwoman of Ṣafiyyah bint Abī ʿUbayd, the wife of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, that she obtained a khulʿ (divorce initiated by the wife) from her husband in exchange for all that she possessed, and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) did not disapprove of that. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14862","(14856) Abū al-Ḥasan ibn Abī al-Maʿrūf al-Isfarāyīnī informed us therein, Abū ʿAmr ibn Nujayd informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us, Umayyah ibn Bisṭām informed us, Yazīd ibn Zuraiʿ informed us, Rūḥ narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAqīl from al-Rabīʿ bint Muʿawwidh ibn ʿAfrāʾ, who said: I married a paternal cousin of mine, and he caused me hardship and I caused him hardship, he afflicted me and I afflicted him, he wronged me and I wronged him, and he increased [his harm] upon me and I increased [my harm] upon him. Then a word escaped from me: \I will ransom myself with all my wealth.\"" He said: \""I have accepted.\"" ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \""Take from her.\"" She said: I went and handed over all my possessions to him except my garments and my bedding. Then he said: \""I am not pleased unless that too is mine.\"" He then brought me before ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him). When we drew near to him"," he said: \""O Commander of the Faithful"," I stipulated ownership [of all her property].\"" He said: \""Very well. Take from her all her possessions"," even down to her hair-clasp.\"" She said: I went and handed over everything to him"," until I shut the door between myself and him. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14863","(14857) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhawayh al-ʿAdl informed us, Hishām ibn ʿAlī informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Rajāʾ informed us, Saʿīd ibn Salamah ibn Abī al-Ḥusām informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Bakr narrated from ʿAmrah from ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Ḥabībah bint Sahl married Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās, and he gave her two gardens as her dower. There was disagreement between them, and he struck her until he broke her hand. She came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at dawn and stood at his door until he came out to her. She said: \O Messenger of Allah"," this is the station of one seeking refuge from Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās.\"" He said: \""Who are you?\"" She said: \""Ḥabībah bint Sahl.\"" He said: \""What is the matter with you? May your hands be dusty!\"" She said: \""He struck me.\"" The Prophet (ﷺ) summoned Thābit ibn Qays"," and Thābit mentioned what had transpired between them. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \""What did you give her?\"" He said: \""Two date-palm plots"," or two gardens.\"" He said: \""Would you be willing to take back some of your wealth and leave some of it for her?\"" He said: \""Is that permissible"," O Messenger of Allah?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" So he took one of the two [gardens] and separated from her. After that"," Ubayy ibn Kaʿb (may Allah be pleased with him) married her"," and he took her to al-Shām"," where she passed away. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14864","(14858) ʿAbdullāh ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Mihrānī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar al-Muzakkī informed us, Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm al-Būshanjī informed us, Ibn Bukayr informed us, Mālik narrated from Nāfiʿ that Rubayyiʿ bint Muʿawwidh came, along with her paternal uncle, to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar and informed him that she had obtained a khulʿ from her husband during the time of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān (may Allah be pleased with him). When this reached ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, he did not disapprove of it. ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: \Her waiting period (ʿiddah) is the waiting period of a divorced woman.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously cited under no. 14855]"""
"14865","(14859) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bishrān informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Muʿammar ibn Sulaymān narrated from al-Ḥajjāj from Ibn Shihāb from ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr that a man obtained a khulʿ from his wife during the caliphate of ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) without [the matter being brought before] a ruler, and ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) validated it. [Ḍaʿīf]"
"14866","(14860) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn ʿUmar ibn Ḥafṣ al-Zāhid informed us, al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah informed us, Mūsā ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Wuhaib informed us, Ayyūb narrated from Abī Qilābah from Abī Asmāʾ from Thawbān from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Any woman who asks her husband for a divorce when there is no grave cause"," the fragrance of Paradise shall be forbidden to her.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14867","(14861) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū ʿAbdullāh Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Ṣaffār informed us, Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us, Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb informed us, Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, and he mentioned it in a similar manner."
"14868","(14862) Abū Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us, Abū ʿAmr ibn Maṭar informed us, Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Naṣr al-Ḥaddāʾ informed us, ʿAbd al-Aʿlā ibn Ḥammād al-Narsī informed us, Wuhaib ibn Khālid informed us, Ayyūb narrated from al-Ḥasan from Abī Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ), who said: \Women who seek khulʿ and women who demand divorce are the hypocrites [in spirit].\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14869","(14863) Abū al-Ḥusayn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Bishrān informed us in Baghdād, Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār informed us, Saʿdān ibn Naṣr informed us, Sufyān narrated from ʿAmr from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd asked Ibn ʿAbbās about a woman whose husband had divorced her with two pronouncements of divorce and then she obtained a khulʿ from him — could he remarry her? Ibn ʿAbbās said: \Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," mentioned divorce at the beginning of the verse and at its end"," and mentioned khulʿ in between. Therefore"," khulʿ is not a [pronouncement of] divorce"," and he may remarry her.\""\n\nIt was also narrated by Ḥabīb ibn Abī Thābit and Layth ibn Abī Sulaym from Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās with the same meaning in an abridged form.\n\nAl-Shāfiʿī narrated from Sufyān from ʿAmr from ʿIkrimah"," who said: \""Any matter that is validated by [the exchange of] wealth is not a [pronouncement of] divorce.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14870","(14864) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan informed us, saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, informed us, al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us, al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah be pleased with him) informed us, Mālik narrated from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah from his father from Jumhān, the freedman of the Aslamīs, from Umm Bakrah al-Aslamiyyah, that she obtained a khulʿ from her husband ʿAbdullāh ibn Asīd, and then they both came to ʿUthmān (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the matter. He said: \It is one pronouncement of divorce"," unless you stipulated a specific number"," in which case it is what you stipulated.\""\n\nA musnad hadith has been narrated on this matter whose chain of narration is not established. It has also been narrated from ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with them both). Ibn al-Mundhir said"," and Aḥmad — meaning Ibn Ḥanbal — weakened the hadith of ʿUthmān"," and the hadith of ʿAlī and Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with them both); there are criticisms regarding their chains of narration. There is nothing in this topic more authentic than the hadith of Ibn ʿAbbās — that is"," the hadith of Ṭāwūs from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both). [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14871","(14865) Abū al-Faḍl ʿUmar ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Ismāʿīl al-Harawī, who came to us as a pilgrim, informed us: Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīh al-Ismāʿīlī informed me: Abū Yaʿlā Aḥmad ibn ʿAlī ibn al-Muthannā informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAbd al-Ṣamad ibn Abī Khidāsh informed us: Abū ʿIṣām Rāwād ibn al-Jarrah narrated from ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr from Ayyūb from ʿIkrimah from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) considered *khulʿ* (divorce initiated by the wife) to be an irrevocable (*bāʾinah*) divorce.\n\nThis narration is uniquely reported by ʿAbbād ibn Kathīr al-Baṣrī. Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal, Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn, and al-Bukhārī have deemed him weak, and Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj has spoken critically about him. How, then, can this be sound, when the position of Ibn ʿAbbās and ʿIkrimah is contrary to it? It is possible that what is meant is that if one intends divorce thereby or mentions it, the purpose is to sever the right of return (*radd*). And Allah knows best. [Weak]"
"14872","(14866) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq al-Muzakkī informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us: al-Shāfiʿī informed us: Muslim ibn Khālid narrated from Ibn Jurayj from ʿAṭāʾ from Ibn ʿAbbās and Ibn al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them) that they both said regarding a woman who seeks *khulʿ*: \Her husband divorces her.\"" They said: \""No divorce is binding upon her"," for he has divorced that over which he has no authority.\""\n\nSufyān al-Thawrī narrated something similar from Ibn Jurayj"," and this is the position of al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī. [Weak]"""
"14873","(14867) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us: al-Rabīʿ said: al-Shāfiʿī (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \I asked him—meaning one of those who opposed him on this issue—'Is there any narration supporting his position?' He then mentioned a narration that does not constitute a valid proof for us or for him.\"" I said: \""This is not established according to us or to you.\"" He said: \""Yet some of the Successors have held this view.\"" He named them in the book on judgment by oath together with a witness"," namely al-Shaʿbī and Ibrāhīm al-Nakhaʿī. Al-Shāfiʿī said: \""I said to him: 'The opinion of some Successors does not constitute a valid proof for you"," even if no one contradicts them.'\""\n\nThe Sheikh said: As for the narration mentioned to him"," its chain of transmission has not come down to us so that we may examine it. I have searched for it in many works compiled on hadith"," but I have not found it. Perhaps he intended what has been narrated from Farj ibn Faḍālah through his chain from Abū al-Dardāʾ as his statement—and Farj ibn Faḍālah is weak in hadith—or what has been narrated from an unknown man from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Muzāḥim from Ibn Masʿūd as his statement"," which is both disconnected (*munqaṭiʿ*) and weak."""
"14874","(14868) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-ʿĀfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Abū ʿUtbah informed us: Baqiyyah narrated from Saʿd ibn Ibrāhīm from his grandfather from al-Ḥakam from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both) regarding a man who said to his wife: \When Ramadan comes"," you are thrice divorced","\"" and there were six months between him and Ramadan. He then regretted it. Ibn ʿAbbās said: \""Let him divorce her once"," so that her waiting period (*ʿiddah*) expires before Ramadan arrives. Then"," if he wishes"," he may propose to her again.\""\n\nAnd it has been narrated from al-Ḥasan al-Baṣrī that he said regarding a man who said to his wife: \""If he speaks to his brother"," you are thrice divorced\"": \""If he wishes"," let him divorce her once"," then leave her until her waiting period expires. Once it is clear that he has spoken to his brother"," he may thereafter marry her again"," if he wishes.\"" [Weak]"""
"14875","(14869) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: ʿAlī ibn Ḥamshādh al-ʿAdl informed us: Ismāʿīl ibn Isḥāq al-Qāḍī informed us: Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Ḥusayn al-Muʿallim narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no divorce before marriage.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14876","(14870) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us—recitation—and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad ibn Mahdī al-Qushayrī informed us—verbatim—both saying: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us: Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib informed us: ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us: Saʿīd, that is Ibn Abī ʿArūbah, narrated from Maṭar. And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us: Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṣaffār informed us: Abū Muslim Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh informed us: Muslim, that is Ibn Ibrāhīm, informed us: Hishām al-Dastawāʾī informed us: Maṭar al-Warrāq narrated from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: \There is no divorce in that over which one has no authority"," and no emancipation except in that over which one has authority.\"" This is the wording of the hadith of Hishām.\n\nIn the narration of Ibn Abī ʿArūbah"," it is said: \""A man is not liable for divorce in that over which he has no authority"," nor for a sale in that over which he has no authority"," nor for emancipation in that over which he has no authority.\"" Abū Dāwūd narrated it in the *Sunan* from Muslim ibn Ibrāhīm from Hishām. [Ḥasan]"""
"14877","(14871) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Fūrak (may Allah have mercy on him) informed us: ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us: Abū Dāwūd informed us: Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \There is no divorce except after marriage"," and no emancipation except after ownership.\""\n\nA group has narrated this from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb. Some of them said: \""from his grandfather","\"" as Maṭar al-Warrāq said"," and some of them said: \""from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr","\"" as Ḥabīb al-Muʿallim said. [Ḥasan. Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr"," 2379]"""
"14878","(14872) Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, saying: I heard Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb say: I heard al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī say: I heard Yaḥyā ibn Maʿīn say: \ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb is trustworthy (*thiqah*).\"""""
"14879","(14873) I heard Abū ʿAbdullāh al-Ḥāfiẓ say: I heard Abū al-Walīd al-Faqīh say: I heard al-Ḥasan ibn Sufyān say: I heard Isḥāq ibn Rāhawayh say: \When the narrator from ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb is trustworthy"," then it is like Ayyūb from Nāfiʿ from Ibn ʿUmar.\"""""
"14880","(14874) Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Abū Isḥāq Ibrāhīm ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Aṣbahānī informed us: Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Sulaymān ibn Fāris informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl al-Bukhārī said: \ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ"," Abū Ibrāhīh al-Sahmī al-Qurashī"," heard from his father"," Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," and Ṭāwūs. Those who narrated from him include Ayyūb"," Ibn Jurayj"," ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rabbāh"," al-Zuhrī"," al-Ḥakam"," Yaḥyā ibn Saʿīd"," and ʿAmr ibn Dīnār.\"" Al-Bukhārī said: \""And Aḥmad ibn Sulaymān said: I heard Muʿtamir say: Abū ʿAmr ibn al-ʿAlāʾ said: 'Qatādah and ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb were not criticized for anything except that they would not hear anything without narrating it.'\"" Al-Bukhārī said: \""I saw Aḥmad ibn Ḥanbal"," ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh"," al-Ḥumaydī"," and Isḥāq ibn Ibrāhīm all using the hadith of ʿAmr ibn Shuʿayb from his father from his grandfather as evidence.\"""""
"14881","(14875) Abu Bakr ibn al-Harith informed us — Ali ibn Umar al-Hafiz informed us — he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi saying: The hearing of 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father Shu'ayb, and the hearing of Shu'ayb from his grandfather 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr, is established (ṣaḥḥa).\n\nThe Shaykh said: And there has already been mentioned in the Book of Hajj, in the chapter on the intercourse of the muḥrim, and in the Book of Transactions, in the chapter on the option of stipulation (khiyār), that which indicates Shu'ayb's hearing from his grandfather 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr — except that when it is said \'Amr ibn Shu'ayb from his father"," from his grandfather","\"" it is possible that what is intended by \""his grandfather\"" is Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr"," and Muhammad ibn 'Abd Allah did not have companionship (ṣuḥbah)"," so the report would be mursal. But when the narrator says \""from his grandfather 'Abd Allah ibn 'Amr","\"" the ambiguity is removed and the hadith becomes connected (mawṣūl). And Allah knows best. And this hadith has been narrated from other routes as well."""
"14882","(14876) Abu al-Hasan 'Ali ibn Ahmad ibn 'Abdan informed us — Ahmad ibn 'Ubayd al-Ṣaffār narrated to us — Ibrahim ibn 'Abd al-Salām narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us — Wakī' narrated to us, from Ibn Abī Dhi'b, from 'Aṭā', from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jābir ibn 'Abd Allah, may Allah be pleased with him, who attributed it (marfū'an): \There is no divorce (ṭalāq) before marriage (nikāḥ)"," and no manumission ('itq) before ownership (milk).\"" [Ḥasan in virtue of other chains]"""
"14883","(14877) And Abu Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated it from Ibn Abī Dhi'b — 'Aṭā' narrated to us — Jābir narrated to me, he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: \There is no divorce for one who does not possess"," and no manumission for one who does not possess.\""\n\nAbu 'Abd Allah al-Ḥāfiẓ informed him — Abu al-'Abbās Muhammad ibn Ya'qūb narrated to us — Muhammad ibn Sinān al-Qazzāz narrated to us — Abu Bakr al-Ḥanafī narrated to us — Ibn Abī Dhi'b narrated to us"," and he mentioned it. [Ḥasan in virtue of other chains]"""
"14884","(14878) And Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī opposed him, and he narrated it as — Abu Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — Ibn Abī Dhi'b said: One who heard 'Aṭā' narrated to me, from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no divorce for one who does not possess"," and no manumission ('itāq) for one who does not possess.\""\n\nAnd others also narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir"," from Jābir. [Ḥasan in virtue of other chains; previously referenced]"""
"14885","(14879) Abu 'Abd al-Raḥmān al-Sulamī and Abu Naṣr ibn Qatādah informed us — they both said: Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī narrated to us — Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm… And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us — Yaḥyā ibn Manṣūr al-Qāḍī, and Yaḥyā ibn Muḥammad al-'Anbarī, and Abu al-Naḍr al-Faqīh, and al-Ḥasan ibn Ya'qūb al-'Adl, and Muḥammad ibn Ja'far al-Muzakkī — they said: Abu 'Abd Allah Muḥammad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Sa'īd al-'Abdī narrated to us — Abu Bakr 'Abd Allah ibn Yazīd al-Dimashqī narrated to us — Ṣadaqah ibn 'Abd Allah al-Dimashqī said: I came to Muḥammad ibn al-Munkadir while I was angry, and I said: \By Allah"," you have made Umm Salamah lawful for Walīd ibn Yazīd!\"" He said: \""I did not — rather"," the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me — Jābir ibn 'Abd Allah al-Anṣārī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'There is no divorce for one who does not possess"," and no manumission for one who does not possess.'\""\n\nAnd that has also been narrated from another route from Jābir"," may Allah be pleased with him. [Ḥasan in virtue of other chains]"""
"14886","(14880) Abu Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abu Muḥammad 'Abd Allah ibn Muḥammad ibn Ja'far ibn Ḥayyān narrated to us — Ibrāhīm ibn Sharīk narrated to us — Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyāsh narrated to us, from Ḥarām ibn 'Uthmān, from the two sons of Jābir — 'Abd al-Raḥmān and Muḥammad — from their father and from Abū 'Atīq, from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no divorce before marriage"," and no manumission before ownership"," and no nursing (riḍā'ah) after weaning (fiṣāl)"," and no continuous fasting (wiṣāl)"," and no fasting for a full day until nightfall.\"" [Ḍa'īf]"""
"14887","(14881) And Abu Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us — 'Abd Allah ibn Ja'far narrated to us — Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us — Abū Dāwūd narrated to us — al-Yamān Abū Ḥudayfah and Khārijah ibn Muṣ'ab narrated to us. As for Khārijah, he narrated to us from Ḥarām ibn 'Uthmān, from Abū 'Atīq, from Jābir. And as for al-Yamān, he narrated to us from Abū 'Abs, from Jābir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no nursing after weaning"," and no orphanhood (yutm) after puberty (iḥtilām)"," and no manumission except after ownership"," and no divorce except after marriage.\"" And he mentioned the hadith. [Ḍa'īf; previously referenced]"""
"14888","(14882) And Abu 'Abd Allah al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us — Abu Bakr Muḥammad ibn 'Abd Allah al-Shāfi'ī narrated to us — Abu Ismā'īl Muḥammad ibn Ismā'īl narrated to us — Sa'īd ibn Abī Maryam narrated to us — 'Abd al-Majīd ibn al-'Azīz narrated to us — Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dīnār, from Ṭāwūs, from Mu'ādh ibn Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \There is no divorce except after marriage"," and no manumission except after ownership.\"" And 'Abd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith al-Makhzūmī narrated it similarly from Ṭāwūs. And we have had that narrated in the book that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to 'Amr ibn Ḥazm. And it has also been narrated from 'Alī"," and Ibn 'Umar"," and Ibn 'Abbās"," and 'Ā'ishah"," and others"," may Allah be pleased with them"," from the Prophet ﷺ. And this is the view of 'Alī"," Ibn 'Abbās"," and 'Ā'ishah"," may Allah be pleased with them. [Ḥasan in virtue of other chains]"""
"14889","(14883) Abu Muḥammad 'Abd Allah ibn Yūsuf al-Aṣbahānī informed us — Abu Sa'īd ibn al-A'rābī narrated to us — Sa'dān ibn Naṣr narrated to us — Mu'ādh al-'Anbarī narrated to us, from Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl, from al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: \There is no divorce except after marriage.\""\n\nAnd Mubārak ibn Faḍālah narrated it from al-Ḥasan: that a man asked 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib"," may Allah be pleased with him. He (the questioner) said: I said: \""If I marry a certain woman"," she is divorced.\"" He said: 'Alī"," may Allah be pleased with him"," said: \""Marry her — there is nothing upon you.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14890","(14884) And Abu Muḥammad ibn Yūsuf informed us — Abu Sa'īd ibn al-A'rābī informed us — al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Za'farānī narrated to us — 'Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us — Sa'īd narrated to us, from Juwaybir, from al-Ḍaḥḥāk ibn Muzāḥim, from al-Nazzāl ibn Sabrah and Masrūq ibn al-Ajdā': that 'Alī, may Allah be pleased with him, said: \There is no divorce except after marriage.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14891","(14885) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Bashrān informed us that Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us that Saʿdān ibn Naṣr narrated to us that Muʿādh al-ʿAnbarī narrated on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of ʿAṭāʾ, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \There is no divorce except after marriage"," and there is no emancipation except after ownership.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14892","(14886) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ʿUbayd ibn Muḥammad al-Qushayrī both informed us, saying that Abū al-ʿAbbās, al-Aṣamm, narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Wahhāb ibn ʿAṭāʾ informed us that Hishām al-Dastawāʾī narrated on the authority of Qatādah, on the authority of ʿIkrimah, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he said: \Divorce is only after marriage.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ in other chains]"""
"14893","(14887) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Maḥbūbī narrated to me that al-Faḍl ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us that ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan ibn Shaqīq narrated to us that al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid and Abū Ḥamzah — both of them — narrated on the authority of Yazīd al-Naḥwī, on the authority of ʿIkrimah, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allah be pleased with them both), who said: \What Ibn Masʿūd (may Allah be pleased with him) said — and even if he did say it — was a slip from a scholar. Regarding the man who says: 'If I marry so-and-so"," she is divorced","' Allah"," the Blessed and Most High"," said: {O you who believe"," when you marry the believing women and then divorce them before you touch them} [al-Aḥzāb 49]"," and He did not say: 'When you divorce the believing women and then marry them.'\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14894","(14888) Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us that Aḥmad ibn ʿUbayd ibn Sharīk narrated to us that Nuʿaym ibn Ḥammād narrated to us that Ḥammād al-Khayyāṭ, one of the people of Baghdad, narrated on the authority of Hishām ibn Saʿd, on the authority of al-Zuhrī, on the authority of ʿUrwah, on the authority of ʿĀʾishah (may Allah be pleased with her), who said: \There is no divorce except after marriage.\""\n\nHe transmitted it as a mawqūf narration"," although it has also been narrated with this chain as marfūʿ.\n\nIt was also narrated on the authority of Bishr ibn al-Sarī"," on the authority of Hishām ibn Saʿd"," on the authority of al-Zuhrī"," on the authority of ʿUrwah"," on the authority of the Prophet (ﷺ) as a mursal narration. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14895","(14889) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl al-Qaṭṭān informed us in Baghdad that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar ibn Durustawayh narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to us that Abū Ṣāliḥ ʿAbd Allāh ibn Ṣāliḥ narrated to me that al-Layth narrated to me that Ibn al-Hād narrated on the authority of al-Mundhir ibn ʿAlī ibn Abī al-Ḥakam that his nephew had proposed to his paternal uncle's daughter, and they quarreled over a certain matter, so the young man said: \She is divorced if I marry her"," until I eat the ghaḍīḍ\"" — and al-ghaḍīḍ is the male spadix of the date-palm. Then they regretted what had transpired"," so al-Mundhir said: \""I shall bring you clarification on this matter.\"" He said: \""So I went to Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib and said to him: 'A man from among my family has proposed to his paternal uncle's daughter"," and a dispute arose between them over a certain matter"," and he said: \""She is divorced if I marry her"," until I eat the ghaḍīḍ.\""'\"" Ibn al-Musayyib said: \""There is nothing upon him; he divorced what he did not possess.\""\n\nThen I asked ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr about that"," and he said: \""There is nothing upon him; he divorced what he did not possess.\""\n\nThen I asked Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān"," and he said: \""There is nothing upon him; he divorced what he did not possess.\""\n\nThen I asked Abū Bakr ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn al-Ḥārith ibn Hishām about that"," and he said: \""There is nothing upon him; he divorced what he did not possess.\""\n\nThen I asked ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUtbah ibn Masʿūd about that"," and he said: \""There is nothing upon him; he divorced what he did not possess.\""\n\nThen I asked ʿUmar ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz"," and he said: \""Did you ask anyone?\"" I said: \""Yes","\"" and I named them to him. Then I returned to the people and informed them of what I had asked about. [Ḍaʿīf]"""
"14896","(14890) Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn al-Faḍl informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us that Yaʿqūb ibn Sufyān narrated to me that Salamah narrated to us that ʿAbd al-Razzāq narrated on the authority of Maʿmar, who said: \Al-Walīd ibn Yazīd wrote to the commanders of the cities"," asking them to write to him about divorce before marriage. He had been tested with this matter"," so he wrote to his governor in Yemen. He summoned Ibn Ṭāwūs"," Ismāʿīl ibn Sharūs"," and Simāk ibn al-Faḍl. Ibn Ṭāwūs informed them on the authority of his father"," Ismāʿīl ibn Sharūs on the authority of ʿAṭāʾ ibn Abī Rābāḥ"," and Simāk on the authority of Wahb ibn Munabbih"," that they said: 'There is no divorce before marriage.' Then Simāk said on his own: 'Marriage is a knot that is tied"," and divorce unties it. How can a knot be untied before it is tied?' Al-Walīd was impressed by his statement and adopted it"," and he wrote to his governor in Yemen to appoint him over the judiciary.\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14897","(14891) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad al-Muʿādhī informed us that Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad al-Ṣawwāf al-Baghdādī narrated to us that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us that ʿAbbād ibn Mūsā narrated to us that Ismāʿīl ibn Jaʿfar narrated on the authority of Isrāʾīl, on the authority of Abū Isḥāq, on the authority of ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn, who said: \When a man says: 'On the day I marry so-and-so"," she is divorced","' it is nothing.\""\n\nThe Shaykh (may Allah have mercy on him) said: \""Sulaymān ibn Abī al-Mughīrah narrated it on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyib and ʿAlī ibn Ḥusayn. Qatādah narrated it on the authority of al-Ḥasan"," Ibn al-Musayyib"," ʿAṭāʾ"," and ʿIkrimah. ʿAbd al-Malik narrated it on the authority of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr. ʿAmr ibn Dīnār narrated it on the authority of Abū al-Shaʿthāʾ. Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated it on the authority of Nāfiʿ ibn Jubayr and Muḥammad ibn Kaʿb al-Quraẓī.\""\n\nAl-Ḥasan ibn Rawāḥ al-Dabbī said: \""I asked Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib"," Mujāhid"," and ʿAṭāʾ about a man who says: 'On the day I marry so-and-so"," she is divorced.' They said: 'It is nothing.'\""\n\nAnd Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib said: \""O my nephew"," can a flood come before the rain?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14898","(14892) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us that Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us that al-Khaḍir ibn Abān al-Hāshimī narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Ādam narrated to us that Yaḥyā ibn Zakariyyā ibn Abī Zāʾidah narrated on the authority of Ṣāliḥ ibn Ṣāliḥ, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhayl, on the authority of Saʿīd ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn ʿAbbās, on the authority of ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) divorced Ḥafṣah and then took her back. Others also narrated it on the authority of Yaḥyā ibn Ādam. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14899","(14893) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us that ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar al-Aṣbahānī narrated to us that Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Ibn Abī Dhiʾb narrated on the authority of al-Ḥārith, meaning Ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Dhubāb, on the authority of Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, on the authority of his father (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: \I had a woman whom I loved"," and my father disliked her. He said to me: 'Divorce her.' I refused. He came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and mentioned that to him"," and he said: 'Divorce her.' So I divorced her.\"" [Ḥasan]"""
"14900","(14894) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us that Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us that Abū Dāwūd narrated to us that Kathīr ibn ʿUbayd narrated to us that Muḥammad ibn Khālid narrated on the authority of Maʿrif ibn Wāṣil, on the authority of Muḥārib ibn Dithār, on the authority of Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \The most hated of permissible things to Allah is divorce.\"" [Munkar]"""
"14901","(14895) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Bālawayh narrated to us, Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us — and Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhabārī informed us, Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Aḥmad ibn Yūnus narrated to us — Maʿrif narrated from Muḥārib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Allah has not made anything lawful that is more hateful to Him than divorce.\""\n\nThis is the hadith of Abū Dāwūd"," and it is mursal. In the narration of Ibn Abī Shaybah"," it is narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar as a muṣṣal (connected) chain"," but I do not consider him to have preserved it accurately.\n\n[Weak]"""
"14902","(14896) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us from the original of his hearing, Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān informed us, Ibrāhīm ibn al-Ḥārith al-Baghdādī narrated to us, Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Maʿrif ibn Wāṣil narrated to us, Muḥārib ibn Dithār narrated to us, saying: A man married a woman during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and then divorced her. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: \Did you marry?\"" He said: \""Yes.\"" He said: \""Then what?\"" He said: \""Then I divorced her.\"" He said: \""Was it out of suspicion?\"" He said: \""No.\"" He said: \""A man may do that.\"" Then he married another woman and divorced her"," and the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him the same.\n\nMaʿrif said: \""I do not know whether at this point or at the third (marriage)"," the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'There is nothing lawful that is more hateful to Allah than divorce.'\""\n\nIt was also narrated by ʿUbaydullāh ibn al-Walīd al-Waṣṣāfī from Muḥārib from Ibn ʿUmar"," connected and abridged.\n\n[Weak]"""
"14903","(14897) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar informed us, Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb informed us, Abū Dāwūd narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated from Abū Isḥāq from Abū Burdah, who said: A man used to say to his wife: \I have divorced you","\"" and then: \""I have taken you back.\"" This reached the Prophet (ﷺ)"," and he said: \""What is the matter with men that they toy with the boundaries of Allah?\""\n\nThis is mursal.\n\n[Weak]"""
"14904","(14898) Abū Zakariyyā ibn Abī Isḥāq informed us, Abū ʿAlī Ḥāmid ibn Muḥammad ibn ʿAbdillāh al-Harawī informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz informed us, Abū Ḥudhayfah Mūsā ibn Masʿūd narrated to us, Sufyān al-Thawrī narrated from Abū Isḥāq from Abū Burdah from Abū Mūsā (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \What is the matter with people that they toy with the boundaries of Allah — 'I have divorced you"," I have taken you back"," I have divorced you"," I have taken you back'?\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"14905","(14899) ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Muqriʾ informed us, al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, Yūsuf ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Abī Bakr informed us, Muʾammal ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, Sufyān narrated it as a connected (mawṣūl) narration, except that he said: \What is the matter with men?\"" And he said: \""One of you says: 'I have divorced you"," I have taken you back.'\"" And it is as though he (the Prophet ﷺ) disliked the excessiveness in it"," or he disliked its occurrence at every time without observance of its prescribed time.\n\n[Weak]"""
"14906","(14900) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, al-ʿAbbās ibn Muḥammad al-Dūrī informed us, Mālik ibn Ismāʿīl informed us, ʿAbd al-Salām ibn Ḥarb narrated from Abū Khālid al-Dālānī from Abū al-ʿAlāʾ al-Awdī from Ḥumayd ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥimyarī from Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he said: \Why does one of you say to his wife: 'I have divorced you"," I have taken you back'? This is not the way of the Muslims in divorce. Divorce a woman before her period of purity (i.e."," before the commencement of her ʿiddah).\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14907","(14901) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us, Abū Sahl Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ziyād al-Naḥwī informed us, Yaḥyā ibn Jaʿfar informed us, ʿAlī ibn ʿĀṣim informed us, Ḥumayd al-Ṭawīl narrated from Anas ibn Mālik (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: There was a dispute between Abū Ṭalḥah and Umm Sulaym (may Allah be pleased with them both), and Abū Ṭalḥah intended to divorce Umm Sulaym. This reached the Prophet (ﷺ), and he said: \Indeed"," the divorce of Umm Sulaym is a grave sin (ḥawb).\""\n\n[Weak]"""
"14908","(14902) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan and Abū Saʿīd ibn Abī ʿAmr said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq al-Ṣaghānī informed us, Ḥajjāj said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abū al-Zubayr informed me that he heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Ayman, the freed slave of ʿAzzah, asking Ibn ʿUmar, while Abū al-Zubayr was listening, saying: \What do you think about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating?\"" He said: \""ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar divorced his wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). So ʿUmar asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," saying: 'ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar has divorced his wife while she is menstruating.' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Let him take her back.' So he (ʿUmar) returned her to me. And he (the Prophet ﷺ) said: 'When she becomes pure"," let him divorce her or let her keep her.' Ibn ʿUmar said: And the Prophet (ﷺ) recited: 'O Prophet"," when you divorce women"," divorce them at the commencement of their ʿiddah.'\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Hārūn ibn ʿAbdillāh from Ḥajjāj ibn Muḥammad.\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ — Muslim 1471]"""
"14909","(14903) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us, Muḥammad ibn Isḥāq informed us, ʿAbdullāh ibn Yūsuf informed us, Mālik narrated from ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār, who said: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (may Allah be pleased with him) recite: \O Prophet"," when you divorce women"," divorce them at the commencement of their ʿiddah.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14910","(14904) Abū ʿAbdillāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Bakr ibn al-Ḥasan both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās informed us, Muḥammad informed us, Aḥmad ibn Isḥāq al-Ḥaḍramī informed us, Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated from Ayyūb from Mujāhid that Ibn ʿAbbās used to recite this verse: \Divorce them before their ʿiddah\"" or \""at the commencement of their ʿiddah.\""\n\n[Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14911","(14905) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us; Abū Bakr al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us; ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan al-Hilālī informed us; Abū ʀāṣim al-Nabīl narrated to us; Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, saying: Mujāhid used to recite it thus, meaning: *li-qubul ʿiddatihinna* (towards their prescribed period). [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14912","(14906) Abū Zakariyyā Yaḥyā ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā informed us; Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb informed us; al-Rabīʿ ibn Sulaymān informed us; al-Shāfiʿī informed us; Mālik informed us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb, al-Shaybānī, narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Salām and Muḥammad ibn ʿAmr narrated to us, saying: Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā narrated to us; he said: I read to Mālik, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāh (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \Command him to take her back"," then let her remain until she becomes pure"," then menstruates"," then becomes pure. Then"," if he wishes"," he may retain her"," and if he wishes"," he may divorce her before touching her. That is the ʿiddah (prescribed period) which Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has commanded that women be divorced for.\"" In the narration of al-Shāfiʿī"," it reads: *thumsa li-yumsik-hā* (\""then let him retain her\"") instead of his saying *thumsa li-yatruk* (\""then let him leave her\"")"," and he did not say *baʿdu* (\""after\""). Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Uways from Mālik"," and Muslim narrated it from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14913","(14907) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ and Abū Muḥammad ibn Abī Ḥāmid al-Muqriʾ both said: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us; al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUbayd al-Ṭanāfisī narrated to us, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar, who said: \I divorced my wife during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was menstruating. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Command him to take her back until she becomes pure"," then menstruates another menstrual period. When she becomes pure"," let him divorce her if he wishes"," before he touches her"," or let him retain her. That is the ʿiddah which Allah"," the Most High"," has commanded that women be divorced for.'\"" I said to Nāfiʿ: \""What did the divorced woman do?\"" He said: \""She observed the ʿiddah for one (divorce).\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ through various chains from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"14914","(14908) Abū ʿAlī al-Rūdhbārī informed us; Abū Bakr ibn Dāsah narrated to us; Abū Dāwūd narrated to us; Qutaybah narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us. And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn narrated to us; Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā informed us; al-Layth ibn Saʿd narrated to us, from Nāfiʿ, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating with a single divorce. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to take her back, then to retain her until she became pure, then to have another menstrual period with him, then to allow her time until she became pure from her menstrual period. If he then wished to divorce her, he should divorce her when she became pure, before touching her. That is the ʿiddah which Allah has commanded that women be divorced for. The wording is from the ḥadīth of Yaḥyā. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Yaḥyā, and al-Bukhārī and Muslim narrated it from Qutaybah from al-Layth. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Agreed upon.]"
"14915","(14909) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū al-Ḥasan ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad ibn Sakhtawayh narrated to us; Aḥmad ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Milḥān narrated to us; Ibn Bukayr narrated to us; al-Layth narrated to us; ʿUqayl narrated to me, from Ibn Shihāb, from Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh, that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed him: \I divorced my wife while she was menstruating. ʿUmar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry about it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Let him take her back"," then let him retain her until she becomes pure"," then menstruates"," then becomes pure. If it seems right to him to divorce her"," let him divorce her in a state of purity before touching her. That is the ʿiddah"," as Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has commanded.'\"" Al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Yaḥyā ibn Bukayr. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"14916","(14910) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn Ghālib al-Khwārizmī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us in Baghdād, saying: It was read to Abū ʿAlī Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn al-Ḥasan al-Ṣawwāf while I was listening: Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad al-Firyābī narrated to you; Muḥammad ibn al-Muṣaffā narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥarb narrated to us; al-Zubaydī narrated to us, from al-Zuhrī, that he was asked about the sunnah divorce for the ʿiddah. He said: \Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: 'I divorced my wife during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was menstruating. ʿUmar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry with me about it and said: \""Let him take her back"," then let him retain her until she menstruates a menstrual period and becomes pure. If he wishes to divorce her in a state of purity before touching her"," then that is the divorce for the ʿiddah as Allah"," the Most High"," has commanded.\""'\"" ʿAbd Allāh said: \""So I took her back"," and the divorce that I had given her was counted (as one).\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"14917","(14911) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me; Abū al-Walīd informed us; Muḥammad ibn Aḥmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us; Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; Yazīd ibn ʿAbd Rabbih narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Ḥarb narrated to us, with his chain of narration, similarly. Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Isḥāq ibn Manṣūr."
"14918","(14912) Abū Bakr Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥārith al-Faqīh informed us; ʿAlī ibn ʿUmar al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us; Abū Bakr al-Naysābūrī narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn Yaḥyā and Abū al-Azhar both narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm narrated to us; the nephew of al-Zuhrī narrated to us, from his uncle, who said: \Sālim ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar informed me that ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar said: 'I divorced my wife while she was menstruating. ʿUmar mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ"," and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry. He said: \""Let him take her back"," then let him retain her until she menstruates a future menstrual period other than the one in which he divorced her. If it seems right to him to divorce her"," let him divorce her in a state of purity from her menstrual period"," before touching her. That is the divorce for the ʿiddah"," as Allah"," the Mighty and Majestic"," has commanded.\""' ʿAbd Allāh had divorced her with one divorce"," and it was counted as part of her divorces. ʿAbd Allāh took her back"," as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had commanded him.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd from Yaʿqūb ibn Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿd. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"14919","(14913) Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to me; Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥasan ibn al-Ḥusayn ibn Manṣūr narrated to us; al-Ḥusayn ibn Abī al-Aḥwaṣ narrated to us; Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us. And ʿAlī ibn Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdān informed us; Sulaymān ibn Aḥmad ibn Ayyūb narrated to us; al-Ḥaḍramī narrated to us; ʿUthmān ibn Abī Shaybah narrated to us. Both said: Wakīʿ narrated to us, from Sufyān, from Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, the freedman of Abū Ṭalḥah, from Sālim, from Ibn ʿUmar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating. ʿUmar mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \Command him to take her back"," then let him divorce her in a state of purity or (when she is) pregnant.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abū Bakr ibn Abī Shaybah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"14920","(14914) Abū Naṣr Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī ibn Muḥammad al-Shīrāzī al-Faqīh narrated to us; Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Akhr narrated to us; Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad and Muḥammad ibn Ismāʿīl both narrated to us; Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Karāmah narrated to us; Khālid ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Sulaymān ibn Bilāl narrated to me; he said: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Dīnār narrated to me, from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating. ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about that, and he said: \Command him to take her back until she becomes pure"," then menstruates another menstrual period"," then becomes pure. Then let him divorce her after that"," or let him retain her.\"" Muslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Aḥmad ibn ʿUthmān ibn Ḥakīm from Khālid ibn Makhlad. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Previously mentioned.]"""
"14921","(14915) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-ʿAbbās Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī ibn ʿAffān narrated to us: Ibn Numayr narrated from al-Aʿmash, from Mālik ibn al-Ḥārith, from ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Yazīd, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Masʿūd, regarding His statement — exalted is He — {Divorce them for their waiting period}: He said, \In a state of purity without intercourse.\"" Some of the narrators added: \""Or when the pregnancy has become evident.\"" I did not find this addition in the preserved narrations. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14922","(14916) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yaḥyā ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār al-Sukkarī informed us in Baghdād: Ismāʿīl ibn Muḥammad al-Ṣaffār narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Manṣūr al-Ramādī narrated to us: ʿAbd al-Razzāq informed us: my uncle Wahb ibn Nāfiʿ narrated to us: ʿIkrimah narrated that he heard Ibn ʿAbbās — may Allah be pleased with them both — saying: Divorce is of four types: two are permissible and two are impermissible. As for the permissible, it is that he divorce her in a state of purity without intercourse, or that he divorce her when she is pregnant and her pregnancy is clearly established. As for the impermissible, it is that he divorce her while she is menstruating, or that he divorce her at the time of intercourse, not knowing whether the womb has conceived a child or not. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq]"
"14923","(14917) Abū Muḥammad ʿAbd Allāh ibn Yūsuf informed us: Abū Saʿīd ibn al-Aʿrābī narrated to us: al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Ṣabbāḥ al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Hārūn informed us: Hishām ibn Ḥassān narrated from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from ʿUbaydah al-Salmānī, from ʿAlī — may Allah be pleased with him — who said: No man ever divorces according to the Sunnah and then regrets it. [Ṣaḥīḥ]"
"14924","(14918) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAbd Allāh Muḥammad ibn Yaʿqūb al-Aṣamm narrated to us by dictation: al-Sarī ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: Yazīd ibn Ibrāhīm al-Tustarī narrated to me: Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated to me: Yūnus ibn Jubayr narrated to me, saying: I asked Ibn ʿUmar. I said: A man divorced his wife while she was menstruating? He said: \Do you know ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar?\"" I said: Yes. He said: \""ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿUmar divorced his wife while she was menstruating"," so ʿUmar — may Allah be pleased with him — came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him"," and he commanded him to take her back and then divorce her at the onset of her waiting period.\"" He said: I said: \""Will that be counted against him?\"" He said: Yes. He said: \""What do you think — if he is helpless and foolish?\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl"," except that he said: I said: \""Will that divorce be counted?\"" He said: \""What do you think — if he is helpless and foolish?\"" [Ṣaḥīḥ]"""
"14925","(14919) Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū Bakr ibn Isḥāq informed us: Muḥammad ibn Ayyūb informed us: Abū al-Rabīʿ and Musaddad said: Ḥammād ibn Zayd narrated from Ayyūb, from Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, from Yūnus ibn Jubayr, who said: I asked Ibn ʿUmar. I said: A man divorced his wife while she was menstruating? He said: \Do you know Ibn ʿUmar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating"," so ʿUmar asked the Prophet ﷺ"," and he commanded him to take her back.\"" I said: \""Will that divorce be counted?\"" He said: \""What then — what do you think if he is helpless and foolish?\""\n\nMuslim narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Abī al-Rabīʿ. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"14926","(14920) Abū Bakr ibn Fūrak informed us: ʿAbd Allāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yūnus ibn Ḥabīb narrated to us: Abū Dāwūd narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Muḥammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū ʿAmr ʿUthmān ibn Aḥmad al-Daqqāq informed us in Baghdād: ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Muḥammad informed us: Bishr ibn ʿUmar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated.\n\n(Ḥ) And Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Ḥāfiẓ informed us: Abū al-Faḍl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us: Aḥmad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār narrated to us: Muḥammad ibn Jaʿfar narrated to us: Shuʿbah narrated from Qatādah, who said: I heard Yūnus ibn Jubayr say: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \I divorced my wife while she was menstruating"," so ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb — may Allah be pleased with him — came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him"," and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Let him take her back. When she becomes pure"," let him divorce her.'\"" He said: I said to Ibn ʿUmar: \""Did you count it?\"" He said: \""What prevents him? What do you think — if he is helpless and foolish?\""\n\nThe wording is that of Ghundar's ḥadīth. al-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Shuʿbah"," and Muslim narrated it from Muḥammad ibn Bashshār. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
"14927","(14921) Abū Ṭāhir al-Faqīh informed us: Abū Bakr Muḥammad ibn al-Ḥusayn al-Qaṭṭān narrated to us: ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥasan narrated to us: Ḥajjāj ibn Minhāl narrated to us: Shuʿbah ibn al-Ḥajjāj narrated to me: Anas ibn Sīrīn narrated to me, saying: I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: \I divorced my wife while she was menstruating.\"" He said: ʿUmar mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: He said: \""Let him take her back. When she becomes pure"," let him divorce her.\"" He said: I said to him — meaning to Ibn ʿUmar: \""Will it be counted?\"" He said: \""What then?\""\n\nal-Bukhārī narrated it in al-Ṣaḥīḥ from Sulaymān ibn Ḥarb from Shuʿbah"," and Muslim narrated it from the ḥadīth of Ghundar from Shuʿbah. [Ṣaḥīḥ. Preceded above]"""
